<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-00bcbf6a5dacd7f6> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The 'Educator Profile' page — a composite, multi-domain screen with Demographic Information/Credentials/Employment/Professional Development/Education tabs, confirmed by viewing Wireframe25_AddendumEducatorProfileEducatorTab — is referenced by name repeatedly across this FDD (25.1.2's Applicant Name hyperlink; the Approval-tab worklist's own Name hyperlink; the Candidate Tracking worklist's First Name hyperlink in 25.2.5) and, per FDD 17's own school-admin wireframe, at least one other already-reviewed FDD. No aggregate, ApiOperation, or Sequence anywhere in the mied-v3 graph models this page as a first-class thing — each tab's underlying data IS separately modeled (iam:Op_GetUser for demographics, cred:Op_GetEducatorCredentials for Credentials, presumably proflearning/profpractice feed the Professional Development/other tabs, epp itself feeds the Education tab), but nothing represents the composite profile page/navigation shell itself. Likely belongs to a cross-cutting capability (Dashboards, or a dedicated 'Educator Profile' feature) rather than any single domain — flagged here rather than forced onto EPP specifically, and worth a GAPS.md entry given it now recurs across two independently-reviewed FDDs (17 and 25)." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:epp:Req_25_1_2> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:epp:Fdd25WorklistDoc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "coverage-gap" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:impact> "M" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "open" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-01db2ac81df9b304> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "This FDD's Dependencies section states flatly: 'The appropriate credential to position mappings are defined by the MiEdWorkforce Admin (12.1)' and, separately, 'the appropriate endorsements to assignment mappings are defined by the MiEdWorkforce Admin (12.1)' — but a review comment on this exact point (comment 12, Groom: 'Maybe MiEd admin? MOECS also collects this info, this is reviewed as part of credential apps') shows the FDD's own author was unsure whether this configuration surface belongs to a system-wide Admin Users capability (FDD 12, not yet reviewed or converted into any of the 11 mied-v3 domains) or to Credentialing's own configurability (cred:CredentialDefinitionAggregate/cred:EndorsementDefinitionAggregate, which do model some of this internally per credentialing-domain.ttl). Left unresolved in the source and here — not assumed either way." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:staffing:Req_22_1_1> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:staffing:Req_22_1_2> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:staffing:Req_22_1_3> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#questioning> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:staffing:Fdd22Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "unconfirmed-assumption" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:impact> "M" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "open" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-029c30c697994652> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Req_22_6_2's acceptance criteria name 7 Data Collection Report sections. staff:Op_GetDistrictAuditReport's documented projection covers Employees Not Appropriately Placed, Employees with No Assignment, and change summaries (Employee Roster/Positions) — but TWO sections have no corresponding concept anywhere in staff:AuditWorkItemAggregate or elsewhere in staffing-domain.ttl at all: 'Required Positions with No Assignments' (positions established in the Position Roster with no staff assigned) and 'Buildings with No Appropriate Positions' (buildings 'Open' in EEM but with no assigned positions/staff — this would require cross-referencing orgs:OrganizationsContext's building data, per staffing-domain.ttl's own existing, unresolved orgs:BuildingsLookupOperation gap). Wireframe22_06 (viewed directly) independently confirms the gap from the visual side: it shows only 5 of the 7 named sections, omitting exactly these same two, AND its main chart area is literally labeled 'Power BI Charts?' — a live open question in the design itself about whether/how Power BI is even the chosen mechanism, not yet a firm decision to build against." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:staffing:Req_22_6_2> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:staffing:Fdd22CompanionDoc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "coverage-gap" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:impact> "M" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "open" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-0406825a5f0027de> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "FDD 28's review already found no Program/ProgramApplication-level audit log anywhere in proflearning-domain.ttl (described 4 separate times in that one FDD). This FDD independently names 'audit details' as an expected feature of nearly every OTHER admin capability it describes too: Alerts ('Versioning and audit details' table column), Email Templates ('Versioning and audit details' table column), historical data ('administrator processing details'), file-queue processing ('View audit details of uploaded files' — even though 14.6 excludes file-queue management from admin scope, the audit-visibility expectation is stated independently in the Business Specifications prose), Dashboards ('with audit details, ... Audit details will be stored and viewable'), Reports ('with audit details stored'), and Worklists (via the shared Coverage-Gap-re-Feature-14.3 Annotation). Across proflearning/communications/documents/reporting, only comm:AlertAggregate (via comm:AlertVersion) actually models anything resembling a change-history/versioning mechanism; everything else this FDD names has none. This extends FDD 28's finding from 'no Program-application audit log' to 'no general admin-action audit/versioning mechanism anywhere in Professional Learning's admin surface' — a materially bigger gap than FDD 28 alone would suggest, independently confirmed by a second FDD looking at a completely different set of admin screens." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:proflearning:Req_14_2_1> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:proflearning:Req_14_3_1> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:proflearning:Req_14_3_2> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:proflearning:Req_14_BizSpec_ReportsAdminConfig> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:proflearning:Fdd14Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "coverage-gap" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:impact> "H" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "open" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-04319885156de739> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Feature 4.1 (Question Sets): none of the 9 stories' admin-authoring capabilities (search, edit/copy/version, Question Set Details entry, code/provenance auto-assignment, effective-date gating, text/error-message editing, single-active-version enforcement, preview) are implemented anywhere in the 11 converted domains. qset:QuestionSetContext (minted by the proflearning v3 pass) is this content's natural conceptual home — proflearning-domain.ttl's own notes already call it 'the Question Set framework (cross-cutting capability)' — but that stub currently contains only qset:GetQuestionSetsOperation, a bare consumption-side GET for another domain (proflearning) to retrieve already-defined question sets by domain name. That is not evidence any of THIS admin-authoring surface exists; it is a downstream reader of whatever eventually implements it. No satisfiedBy is asserted on any Req_04_1_* for this reason." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:businessruleengine:Req_04_1_1> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:businessruleengine:Req_04_1_2> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:businessruleengine:Req_04_1_3> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:businessruleengine:Req_04_1_4> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:businessruleengine:Req_04_1_5> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:businessruleengine:Req_04_1_6> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:businessruleengine:Req_04_1_7> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:businessruleengine:Req_04_1_8> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:businessruleengine:Req_04_1_9> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:businessruleengine:Fdd04Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "coverage-gap" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:impact> "H" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "open" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-06fe5f9cde352fb0> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "6.3.2 asks for an HTML-capable rich text editor with image insertion (MDE/CEPI letterhead support) and font-selection UI. communications-technical-design.ttl's comm:TP_TemplateStorageAndEditing instead documents a Markdown-with-limited-extension-allowlist authoring format that explicitly rejects raw HTML, a WYSIWYG editor, custom CSS, and (by omission) any image-insertion or font-selection mechanism — the design's own stated rationale (XSS elimination, clean version diffs) is a deliberate, reasoned choice, not an oversight, which makes this a genuine architecture-vs-FDD contradiction rather than a simple gap. Unresolved which source should govern: the FDD's own letterhead/rich-text requirement, or the technical design's security-motivated Markdown-only decision." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:Req_06_3_2> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:TP_TemplateStorageAndEditing> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:Fdd06Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "discrepancy" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:impact> "H" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "open" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-0879e94f3b2d63c3> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Features 19.1.1-19.1.8 (dashboard link/widget, on-demand execution, extraction, drill-through to individual records, admin-defined violation text, acknowledge-with-justification, auto-clearing Action Items, historical/audit view) collectively describe a generic, cross-domain, admin-configurable Data Quality checking-and-reporting capability that has NO real implementation anywhere in mied-v3 — only the dq:DataQualityContext/dq:DataQualityIssueDetectedEvent/dq:GetIssuesOperation stub triad (minted from Communications' own cross-references, not from any dq: source doc) and dash:DashboardsContext (also stub-only). The closest real analogs that exist anywhere — staff:Seq_CertifyCollection's validation-before-certification workflow (acknowledge/justify/re-run/clear) and staff:Perm_CollectionValidate — are scoped entirely to Staffing's own collection-certification process, not the general capability described here; they are cited in each affected Requirement's own sd:notes rather than asserted as sd:satisfiedBy, to avoid overclaiming coverage that is real but structurally much narrower than what the story asks for. This is a genuine, still-fully-open whole-capability gap for GAPS.md." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:dataquality:Req_19_1_1> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:dataquality:Req_19_1_2> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:dataquality:Req_19_1_3> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:dataquality:Req_19_1_4> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:dataquality:Req_19_1_5> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:dataquality:Req_19_1_6> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:dataquality:Req_19_1_7> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:dataquality:Req_19_1_8> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:dataquality:Fdd19Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "coverage-gap" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:impact> "H" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "open" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-0b95bcbd62e5cf61> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Comment #38 (Sinha, 2025-11-12): 'Can we add a point for Credential Removal Request?' — Comment #39 (Dontje, 2026-03-02): '@Sinha, Yashi (DTMB-Contractor) Yes, please add the new requirement.' The product owner agreed to add a 'Credential Removal Request' capability, distinct from Suspend/Revoke/Nullify (all administrative actions on an existing credential's status, not a request to remove/delete one outright). No corresponding user story, acceptance criteria, or Requirement instance exists anywhere in the current FDD text — the agreement was made in a comment but never drafted into the document itself. A genuine 'agreed but not yet written' gap, distinct from an ordinary coverage gap. Still true in mied-v3: no Op_RemoveCredential/Op_DeleteIssuedCredential-style operation exists anywhere in credentialing-api.ttl." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Rule_CredentialStatusTransitions> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd11_16Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "coverage-gap" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:impact> "M" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:owner> "MDE (Dontje) / DTMB (Sinha)" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "open" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-0c18357e2448a28a> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "No catalog-change audit trail (who edited a ReportDefinition's name/description/workspace/permission-key, and when) exists anywhere in reporting-domain.ttl/reporting-api.ttl — only an embed-TOKEN-request audit (rpt:EmbedTokenRequestAggregate/rpt:Op_AdminListEmbedAudit) is modeled, which answers a different question (who tried to VIEW a report, not who EDITED its catalog metadata). 2.1.4 explicitly asks for the catalog-change kind. A real, confirmed gap, not a terminology quibble." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:reporting:Req_02_1_4> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:reporting:Fdd02Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "coverage-gap" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:impact> "M" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "open" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-0ef479c26639478e> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Three real, wireframed/detailed Business Specifications capabilities (MCL-code matching, the SSN/name identity-matching cascade, and search/filter) were never promoted into the Addendum's own 30.1-30.8 numbering at all — independently flagged by three separate 'I do not see user story for this requirement' / 'No user story for this requirement' review comments (Punniyamoorthy, 2026-01-26), the same kind of Addendum-omission this project's FDD 29 pass already found for three of ITS OWN Business Specifications features. Modeled here with synthetic profp:Req_30_BizSpec_* IDs rather than silently folded into the numbered scheme or dropped for lacking a number." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:profpractices:Req_30_BizSpec_IdentityMatching> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:profpractices:Req_30_BizSpec_MclMatching> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:profpractices:Req_30_BizSpec_SearchFilter> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:profpractices:Fdd30Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "discrepancy" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:impact> "M" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "open" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-10f838d22ded50ae> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Comment 51 (Groom, 2026-03-27): 'Need validation to ensure there is not a gap between the end and new effective dates.' Reply 52 (Doherty, relaying 'Yashi', 2026-04-01): 'I have updated the Acceptance Criteria to include a specific validation that checks for gaps (as well as overlaps) when a new effective date is set for an existing rule.' No such gap/overlap-check language appears anywhere in 4.2.2's visible acceptance criteria (confirmed against document.xml directly, not just the .md extraction) — the reply claims an edit that isn't reflected in the document, the same 'reviewer says content was added/removed but the visible text disagrees' pattern the FDD 29 pass found for its own cover-letter story (there, content claimed removed but still present; here, content claimed added but still absent)." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:businessruleengine:Req_04_2_2> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:businessruleengine:Fdd04Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "discrepancy" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:impact> "M" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "open" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-1403a61d1ed02a49> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "No list/search ApiOperation exists anywhere for profp:ExternalBackgroundCheckAggregate — only get-by-id (profp:Op_GetExternalCheck). This is one gap viewed from two angles: 30.1.2 is the results-table/column-display half, profp:Req_30_BizSpec_SearchFilter (below) is the filter-criteria half of the same missing list-query capability." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:profpractices:Req_30_1_2> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:profpractices:Req_30_BizSpec_SearchFilter> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:profpractices:Fdd30Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "coverage-gap" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:impact> "M" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "open" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-15ed00965f4d7f3a> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Feature 4.2 (Business Logic/Rules): none of the 11 stories' admin-authoring capabilities (rule activation by hierarchy level, on/off + effective-date scheduling, severity/justification configuration, external-data-source-backed validation, uniform online/bulk/API enforcement, message management, versioning/audit, frequency review, dry-run testing, extract publication) are implemented anywhere in the 11 converted domains, confirmed by grep before writing this entry (see this file's own header note for what was checked and ruled out: staffing's staff:TP_ValidationRuleEngine is domain-scoped to Staffing's own Collection quality-review, not a shared authoring surface; credentialing's CredentialDefinitionAggregate/EndorsementDefinitionAggregate/AssessmentDefinitionAggregate model configurability internally only). Unlike Feature 4.1, this content had NO existing stub anywhere prior to this pass — bre:BusinessRuleEngineContext is minted in this same file specifically to give it one, on the strength of 'Business Rule Engine'/'BRM' already being a named-but-unresolved participant in credentialing-sequences.ttl's and epp-sequences.ttl's own sequence diagrams. No satisfiedBy is asserted on any Req_04_2_* — the new stub carries no Aggregate/ApiOperation/Sequence of its own, deliberately, per this file's header note on why that would be a fabricated target." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:businessruleengine:Req_04_2_10> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:businessruleengine:Req_04_2_11> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:businessruleengine:Req_04_2_1> ;
