<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-169eb099ea20a675> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Bulk file upload for the Employee Roster has a Permission (staff:Perm_EmployeeRosterBulkUpload) and an admin-monitoring Permission (staff:Perm_AdminViewFileQueues/staff:Perm_AdminResetFileProcessing) but NO backing sd:ApiOperation, sd:Sequence, or processing-queue concept anywhere in the staffing conversion (a pre-existing gap, documented in staffing-permissions.ttl's own header, now independently confirmed from the FDD side). This FDD adds a second layer on top: a staging-area review-before-commit step (21.5.2) for exactly this not-yet-built pipeline, plus 'API service connections directly to HR systems' via an unspecified 'Data Hub' (21.5.1) that doesn't correspond to any bounded context or ExternalSystem in mied-v3's registry. All three pieces (bulk-upload endpoint itself, staging/review step, HR-system API integration) are open." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:staffing:Req_21_5_1> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:staffing:Req_21_5_2> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:staffing:Fdd21Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "coverage-gap" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:impact> "M" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "open" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-1b29f5c52694d581> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "All three Feature 6.5 stories describe a working communications-to-reporting data pipeline (send counts, reminder recipients, alert/notification history, audit trend analysis), but communications-capability.ttl's own asserted sd:subscribesTo edges into rpt:ReportingContext cover only comm:EmailTemplateCreatedEvent — none of the actual send/delivery lifecycle events (EmailSent, EmailDelivered, EmailBounced, EmailDeferred, EmailDropped, EmailResent) and none of the Alert lifecycle events (DashboardAlertCreated, DashboardAlertResolved) are subscribed by Reporting at all (only Audit subscribes to most of those). The underlying data (comm:EmailInstanceAggregate, comm:AlertAggregate) exists and is well-modeled; what's missing is the asserted integration path that would actually get it into the reporting platform this feature describes. High impact since all three of 6.5.1/6.5.2/6.5.3 depend on it." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:Req_06_5_1> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:Req_06_5_2> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:Req_06_5_3> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:Fdd06Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "coverage-gap" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:impact> "H" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "open" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-1ba8b5a1a0d0478d> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Worklist access from the Dashboard (32.15.8) belongs to the Dashboards capability (dash:DashboardsContext, stub-only), the same cross-cutting concern already found from FDD 29's Req_29_1_8 and FDD 11/16's Req_11_7 — a third independent FDD naming the identical gap." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:fdd32:Req_32_15_8> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:fdd32:Fdd32Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "out-of-scope" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "resolved" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-1d353a680e147d94> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "FDD 31.3's Business Specifications include a second sentence beyond the Legacy Reports rejection, easy to miss: 'The public search user support information will provide guidance to users that are not seeing expected results within the public credential search, the user will be able to request additional information for individuals.' This describes a distinct, real (if small) support/contact-request feature for the public credential search — NOT part of the Legacy Reports rejection — but like the credentialing-fdd-11-16.ttl pilot's 'Credential Removal Request' finding, this was never turned into a numbered Addendum user story (the Addendum only addresses Legacy Reports). No 'request additional information' contact-support flow exists anywhere in credentialing-api.ttl/credentialing-domain.ttl. An 'agreed-in-prose-but-never-drafted' gap, distinct from an ordinary coverage gap." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_31_3> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd31_3Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "coverage-gap" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:impact> "L" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "open" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-1dd4fd7b39ed64a7> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Feature 13.7 (Identity Management Integration for EPP) is withdrawn by both of its own source documents ('no longer needed' / 'no longer necessary'), superseded by FDD 15 (Identity Management Integration), which is not itself reviewed in this pass." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:epp:Req_13_7> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:epp:Fdd13_7Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "rejected" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "resolved" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-20675072e41f6b2e> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The FDD's own text states plainly: 'It has been determined that this feature is no longer necessary.' Taken at face value as a real, deliberate decision (not a placeholder or drafting error) — no further ADA-specific feature content exists anywhere else in either FDD 19 or FDD 20 to cross-check it against." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:dataquality:Req_19_5> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:dataquality:Fdd19Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "rejected" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "resolved" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-231a4c8f64a41d7b> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Cross-entity employee record 'push'/'send' with a receiving-entity worklist Action Item and confirmation step (21.4.5) has no counterpart anywhere in the staffing bounded context as converted — no Aggregate, Permission, Sequence, ApiOperation, or DomainEvent models sending an employee record to, or confirming receipt from, another entity in an organizational hierarchy. This is functionally a shared-staff/multi-district-employment scenario (an ISD-employed speech therapist working across several constituent districts, e.g.) that the rest of staff:EmployeeRosterAggregate's single-entity-scoped model does not appear designed for at all — worth flagging to whoever owns FDD 22 (Employee Assignment Details) or FDD 18 (Roster of Positions), since a shared/multi-entity assignment concept may belong there instead, not necessarily as new Staffing-employee-roster scope." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:staffing:Req_21_4_5> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:staffing:Fdd21Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "coverage-gap" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:impact> "H" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "open" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-2366eaab568231df> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "This FDD (22.6.4, and the Business Specifications prose's own 'SOM Auditor can request additional documentation or information from the ISD or district user') repeatedly frames SOM Auditor oversight as extending to BOTH ISD-level and district-level review, and 22.6.1's 'Appropriate Assignment Reports & Audits Worklist' is described as its own SOM-scoped worklist (not just the ISD Auditor's worklist filtered wider). But staff:AuditWorkItemAggregate — the only audit-workflow aggregate that exists — is created exclusively per-district, per staff:Rule_ISDAuditItemCreatedAfterCertification ('an audit work item is automatically created for the constituent district's ISD/RESA entity... visible to that ISD's auditors'). There is no modeled concept of an SOM-level audit item that reviews an ISD'S OWN performance/compliance (as opposed to reviewing the same district-level items an ISD Auditor already sees) — i.e. no distinct 'SOM audits an ISD' object exists, only 'ISD (and, by broader permission scope, SOM) audits a district.' This may be an accurate simplification (SOM's role may genuinely just be broader-scoped visibility into the same district-level items, not a separate ISD-performance audit), or a genuine missing concept — left open rather than guessed." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:staffing:Req_22_6_1> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:staffing:Req_22_6_4> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:staffing:Fdd22CompanionDoc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "coverage-gap" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:impact> "L" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "open" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-25454061b068a675> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Comment thread on Sponsor-application editability (comments.xml IDs 3, 4, 5) shows the FDD came close to shipping a materially different, more restrictive answer than what the visible 28.1.3 text now says: comment 3 (Ross, 2025-12-05) states edit access should be restricted to an Action + comments, with the application's own fields never editable; comment 4 (Ross, same day, later) says this was 'later discussed as potentially allowing... editable, with the interest of correcting minor typos... Need confirmation'; comment 5 (Dontje, 2026-01-28, ~2 months later) resolves it in favor of full field-level editability. The visible text reflects the final, resolved answer, so no correction was needed here — but the reversal is worth recording since it's the kind of decision a stale export/summary made before 2026-01-28 would get wrong." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:proflearning:Req_28_1_3> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#questioning> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:proflearning:Fdd28Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:impact> "L" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "resolved" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-2b2c52f5d85d2a49> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Three FDD user stories (11.1.1, 11.5.1, 16.1.4) each independently describe discrete, named, per-credential-type worklist search screens with their own filter sets and result columns, plus a recurring 'download results as Word/Excel/Pdf' export capability. Nothing in credentialing-api.ttl models per-worklist-type search (only the generic Op_ListApplications) or any export format at all. Wireframes 4/6/7 are visual evidence this is a real, designed UI, not a speculative wish-list item. Consolidated into one Annotation rather than three near-duplicates since it's the same underlying gap." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_11_1_1> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_11_5_1> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_16_1_4> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd11_16Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "coverage-gap" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:impact> "M" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "open" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-2d5161d2217b53fe> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "No page-content-management (CMS) aggregate/entity/API exists anywhere in proflearning-domain.ttl, proflearning-api.ttl, or documents-capability.ttl for the editable hyperlinks/headings/announcements/support-materials/search-result-column-config/validation-text this story describes for the public Professional Learning Resources pages. Not previously flagged by any earlier proflearning conversion pass — a new finding from this FDD." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:proflearning:Req_14_1_2> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:proflearning:Fdd14Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "coverage-gap" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:impact> "L" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "open" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-2debec4982386f2d> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "No node in mied-v3 represents a vendor exit/transition plan or a pre-launch security/configuration/smoke-test validation gate — these are engagement-management and release-QA process artifacts, not domain-model concepts, and none of the 11 domains' conversions describe them. Same category of gap as 32.1/32.2's process-shaped NFRs, grouped separately here since 32.12 is specifically about the delivery/handoff process rather than day-2 operational standards." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:fdd32:Req_32_12> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:fdd32:Fdd32Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "coverage-gap" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:impact> "L" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "open" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-2f7c7cbfdd41204b> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "cred:Rule_PublicEducatorCredentialSearch's statement describes credential-history grouping as a 2-way Active/Inactive split; this FDD's own acceptance criteria (31.2.3) and its highest-fidelity wireframe (cred:WireframeCredentialHistoryHifi, confirmed by direct viewing) describe a 3-way split — Active Credentials / Active Temporary Credentials (with a District column) / Inactive Credentials. The rule and cred:Op_GetPublicEducatorCredentialHistory's sd:projection should be updated to the 3-way shape; District is new data not modeled on any temporary-credential/permit entity today." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_31_2_3> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Rule_PublicEducatorCredentialSearch> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd31_1_2Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "discrepancy" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:impact> "M" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "open" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-33c167a7f0a5b38b> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Report dataset sourcing/provenance across MDE/CEPI systems, the historical warehouse, and integrated systems is owned by Power BI's own dataset layer and by each source domain (Staffing/Credentialing/etc.), consistent with reporting-capability.ttl's own explicit 'owns none of the underlying report data' scope statement — not a Reporting-side build item." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:reporting:Req_02_BizSpec_4> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:reporting:Fdd02Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "out-of-scope" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "resolved" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-34d111e7a3e32073> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Feature 13.3's worklist-ADMINISTRATION capability (defining/configuring which worklists exist, their task-requirement-status/deadline settings, per-user/per-role access-level assignment, item-approval workflow, and column/field customization — 13.3.1 and 13.3.2's own column-editing half) has no home anywhere in the EPP domain as modeled: epp's own 'worklist' concept is purely the existing filtered-list read pattern on CredentialApplicationReview/ApprovalApplicationReview, with zero admin-configuration surface. This is the SAME gap epp-domain.ttl's own epp:Question_WorklistAssignmentScope (Open Question #11) already flagged from FDD 5's side (citing FDD 5 Wireframe 10/Feature 5.5's per-user worklist-assignment capability) — independently reconfirmed here from FDD 13's own side, and now with concrete wireframe evidence (epp:WireframeWorklistManagement's 'Credentialing Data' breadcrumb) that the screen FDD 13 itself illustrates for 'EPP worklist management' is actually a capture of Credentialing's own admin screen. Raises confidence this whole capability belongs to Credentialing (per FDD 5), not EPP, and/or needs its own cross-domain 'worklist administration' concept neither domain currently owns outright." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:epp:Req_13_3_1> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:epp:Req_13_3_2> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:epp:Fdd13Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "coverage-gap" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:impact> "H" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "open" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-359b6a7a3933dd86> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Feature 22.5's own text explicitly defers all alert/notification generation logic to Business Specification #6 (Alerts, Emails & Communications — comm:CommunicationsContext) and all routing/timing logic to Business Specification #4 (Business Rule Management — no corresponding bounded context exists yet; already an open GAPS.md item from the FDD 29 pass, independently reconfirmed here). Nothing Staffing-specific to model beyond the existing subscribesTo claims already asserted in staffing-domain.ttl." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:staffing:Req_22_5> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:staffing:Fdd22Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "out-of-scope" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "resolved" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-36bfa15e4e23ab9a> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "No invariant on cred:CredentialApplicationAggregate or cred:IssuedCredentialAggregate enforces uniqueness of an (endorsement, grade level) combination per individual/district/academic year for permit applications. Extended Daily/Emergency Extended Daily's own FDD describes the identical rule in much more operational detail (blocking a duplicate Extended Daily Substitute Permit application for the same endorsement+grade combination), corroborating this as real, cross-permit-type business logic rather than a one-off wish-list item from Daily Substitute Permit's FDD alone." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_17_1_5> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd17DailySubDoc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "coverage-gap" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:impact> "M" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "open" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-36dff6710000a535> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "This FDD independently corroborates epp-domain.ttl's existing epp:Question_ProPrepPublicCatalogFieldGaps (Open Question #12) with concrete new evidence: a distinct 'Program search' wireframe (epp:Wireframe31_4_4) with its own results shape (Program Name/Code/Type/Classification) and its own reverse-lookup 'Available Providers' page (epp:Wireframe31_4_5), confirming Program really is meant to be a first-class, independently-searchable catalog entity — not just data nested under a provider's certificateCategories/endorsements, which is all epp:Op_SearchProPrepProviders/epp:Op_GetProPrepProviderDetail expose today. No Program-search or Program-detail ApiOperation exists in epp-api.ttl at all." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:epp:Req_31_4_2> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:epp:Req_31_4_5> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:epp:Req_31_4_6> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:epp:Fdd31_4Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "coverage-gap" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:impact> "M" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:references> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:epp:Question_ProPrepPublicCatalogFieldGaps> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "open" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-37546d021b3a5f66> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Comment thread on this exact story (1655239543, Punniyamoorthy: 'Beth/Caitlin, dont know if we need this story, as we are not going to generate cover letter and it is going to be part of email' -> 570274720, Dontje: 'Agree' -> 884312815, Sinha: 'Got it') reads as the product owner and vendor team agreeing the standalone downloadable-cover-letter-PDF capability described by 29.4.2 is NOT needed, and that cover-letter content should instead be folded into an email (Alerts & Communications territory) rather than a Credentialing-generated document. Despite that apparent agreement, the visible document was never edited to remove or descope 29.4.2 — its full acceptance criteria survive intact, AND Wireframe1 (the landing page, viewed independently) still shows a live 'Print Cover Letter' button plus a note that cover letters print 'for out-of-state applications' specifically — a scope narrower than 29.4.2's generic 'relevant to the type of certificate applied for' framing, and itself unmentioned in 29.4.2's own acceptance criteria. Three different signals (rejected-in-comments / fully-specified-in-text / narrower-scope-in-wireframe) don't agree with each other. credentialing-technical-design.ttl's existing framing of this as merely 'not enough detail specified yet' undersells the actual state: it isn't just underspecified, it's actively contested whether it should exist as a Credentialing-side document-generation feature at all, and if it does, at what scope. Recommend confirming directly with the product owner before modeling a TechnicalProcess for it." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_29_4_2> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd29Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "discrepancy" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:impact> "H" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "open" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-385c922c04bb20b0> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Req_22_6_3's Employee Details audit drawer composes fields from what should be (per staffing-domain.ttl's own explicit domain-boundary notes) Credentialing's data — Certificate Number/Type, National Board Certified, Renewal Status, Endorsements with a per-endorsement 'Nullified' flag, and a full Certificate History (App#/Issue/Expiration/Status) — alongside an 'Assignment' section and a free-form, auditor-editable 'Remarks' comment thread that exists in neither domain's model. No sd:ApiOperation, sd:Aggregate, or projection anywhere in the graph as currently converted composes this exact cross-domain shape for audit purposes; this looks like it should be a Staffing-owned audit-composition view calling into Credentialing (parallel to how staff:Op_GetDistrictAuditReport already composes cross-record staffing data), but no such operation is documented in staffing-api.yml. Also notable: the wireframe's 'Add to Investigation' button has zero backing narrative in either document's text — possibly an orphaned/future-scope UI element, possibly an undocumented capability, unresolved." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:staffing:Req_22_6_3> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:staffing:Fdd22CompanionDoc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "coverage-gap" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:impact> "M" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "open" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-38e8ce8cd67d3b30> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Both plrn:Req_28_1_5 (Sponsor application comments) and plrn:Req_28_4_2 (Program application 'internal comments'/Remarks History) need the SAME already-modeled generic comm:CommentAggregate mechanism, which explicitly does not cover either process-item type today (its invariant lists only CredentialApplication, StaffingRecord, EPPEnrollment). One coverage-gap Annotation covering both rather than two near-duplicate ones — the fix, if made, would extend comm:CommentAggregate's covered-process-item list to include proflearning's ProgramApplication (and, per Req_28_1_5's own note, a future SponsorApplication once that entity exists) rather than building a second, parallel comment mechanism inside proflearning itself." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:proflearning:Req_28_1_5> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:proflearning:Req_28_4_2> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:proflearning:Fdd28Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "coverage-gap" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:impact> "M" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "open" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-3902ce08fdeb375c> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Feature 13.2's own comment thread (ids 19/20/21, 2026-02-18 to 2026-03-16) asked what retention period applies to EPP historical data (Pathways/Certificates/Endorsements) and was resolved by DELETING the acceptance criterion rather than specifying a period ('we can remove this as it will be according to the State's retention policy per the assumptions') — i.e. deferred to a project-wide assumption, not actually answered. This is the same open question epp-domain.ttl's own epp:Question_EnrollmentRecordRetention (Open Question #7) already tracks for CandidateEnrollment specifically; not re-raised as a duplicate Annotation, just cross-referenced here since it's independent evidence the retention-period question is still open project-wide, not EPP-specific." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:epp:Question_EnrollmentRecordRetention> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#commenting> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:epp:Fdd13Doc> .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-3920f345dc032621> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Comment 49 (Groom, 2026-03-27): 'Need to discuss back dating, specifically for the rules that will be implemented at system launch, do we anticipate using a system live date?' Reply 50 (Doherty, relaying 'Yashi', 2026-04-01): confirms the current Acceptance Criteria only cover immediate (on-demand) and future-dated rules, that a rule change applies to NEW transactions going forward and won't affect pending applications, but that the strategy for 'Day 1' baseline rules at system launch is NOT yet defined ('I have added a point for the Standardized System Live Date that is to be defined yet'), and explicitly asks whether the UI needs to support manually back-dating an Effective Date at all, or whether the system should only ever look forward from the current/future date. Genuinely unresolved — no 'Standardized System Live Date' concept appears anywhere in the visible Addendum text, so either the promised addition never made it into this revision or it lives elsewhere undocumented." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:businessruleengine:Req_04_2_2> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#questioning> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:businessruleengine:Fdd04Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:impact> "M" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "open" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-3c5cfec257dda026> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Req_22_1_6's Addendum text claims the CITIZEN's evaluation-outcome appeal window is '5 years', but this FDD's own Business Specifications prose (predating the Addendum in the same document) and staffing-domain.ttl's staff:Rule_EvaluationOutcomeAppealWindow both agree citizens may appeal ANY evaluation outcome with no time limit — the 5-year window applies only to District-user appeals. The Addendum author appears to have conflated the two actor-specific rules when summarizing into a single citizen-facing user story." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:staffing:Req_22_1_6> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:staffing:Fdd22Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "discrepancy" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:impact> "L" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "open" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-3ef5329041ed621c> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "cred:Op_SearchPublicEducatorCredentials has no sd:parameters property at all — none of this FDD's Advanced Search surface (Credential Number free-text field, Credential Type multi-select filter defaulting to 'All') or its validation-message behavior ('Enter search criteria in at least one field', 'No results found') is promoted onto the ApiOperation today. The core search/matching LOGIC (cred:Rule_PublicEducatorCredentialSearch) is solidly modeled; it's specifically the request-shape/filter-parameter and UI-validation layer that's missing." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_31_1_5> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_31_1_6> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd31_1_2Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "coverage-gap" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:impact> "L" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "open" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-418bdda4c068e0d0> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Comment 715111818 (Doherty, 2026-04-06, quoting Sinha) on 14.7.2: 'The validations for the SCECH Hours have been added. Please confirm as the FDDs do not contain any references to these specific thresholds or caps.' A related comment 37 (Dontje, 2026-03-18) elsewhere in the same document — 'Added; needs more detail around not exceeding the max and rules around the decimal places, etc.' — points at the same open concern. plrn:SCECHAllocation (MaxGeneral/MaxCollege/MaxCareer/MaxMilitary) is the closest existing modeled concept for a 'maximum' cap, but neither it nor any business rule in proflearning-domain.ttl specifies decimal-place handling for awarded SCECH amounts. Recorded as an unconfirmed-assumption per the FDD's own reviewers' explicit uncertainty, not resolved by this pass." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:proflearning:Req_14_7_2> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#questioning> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:proflearning:Fdd14Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:impact> "L" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "open" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-4303f30c993c69e8> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "In-portal ad-hoc report authoring/saving (the 'ad-hoc reports' and 'save' clauses of this Business Specifications bullet) falls outside Reporting's own documented scope boundary — rpt:Rule_ReportDefinitionsOwnedOutsideApplication is explicit that report authoring requires Power BI Desktop/Pro-Premium licensing not exposed in this portal, and rpt:UT_AdHocExploration's definition explicitly distinguishes in-report exploration (in scope) from editing/creating report definitions (out of scope)." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:reporting:Req_02_BizSpec_3> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:reporting:Fdd02Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "out-of-scope" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "resolved" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-44358a1df3483f09> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Feature 28.2 (Publishing the Professional Learning Catalog) was explicitly dropped by the document's own authors, contingent on FDD 26's Feature 26.4 (Professional Learning Catalog) also having been dropped. No action needed; nothing to build, nothing missing." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:proflearning:Req_28_2> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:proflearning:Fdd28Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "rejected" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "resolved" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-4630940bf6694c4f> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "19.3.1/19.3.2's dashboard-summary content (frequency counts, communications-sent/action-item digest assembled specifically for a Data Quality Administrator) has no real implementation — dash:DashboardsContext remains stub-only and no aggregate assembles the relevant cross-cutting summary. Distinct from 19.3.3, which DOES have a real, cited partial implementation via comm:AlertAggregate (see that Requirement's own sd:satisfiedBy/notes) — grouped separately here rather than folded into the same Annotation, to avoid implying the whole Feature 19.3 is equally uncovered." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:dataquality:Req_19_3_1> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:dataquality:Req_19_3_2> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:dataquality:Fdd19Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "coverage-gap" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:impact> "M" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "open" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-46e14e33357e7c87> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Feature 14.5 explicitly defers dashboard rendering/organization to Business Specification #3 and limits its own scope to which tiles/reports are configured for Professional Learning. Correctly out-of-scope for FDD 14's own Addendum. The underlying Dashboards capability itself remains a stub (dash:DashboardsContext, sd:status \"stub\") with no real conversion anywhere in this project — consistent with, not a new instance of, the dashboard gap already on record from the FDD 29 review (see GAPS.md)." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:proflearning:Req_14_5> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:proflearning:Fdd14Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "out-of-scope" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "resolved" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-48c7314ee0146f8a> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Wireframe9 (Enrollment Information, viewed) shows a 3-row static table and was attached in direct response to an earlier 'wireframe needs to be updated' comment (964068277 -> 1600877324 'working on getting the wireframes' -> 1233352176 'new wireframe has been attached'). But a LATER comment on the same thread's target (1047102331, Punniyamoorthy, 2026-04-27 — six weeks after the wireframe was attached) says 'Still missing the wireframe for the table to list all enrollments,' with no further reply in the extracted comment set. It's unresolved whether Wireframe9 (which does show a 3-row table) was considered adequate after all, superseded by a further update not captured in this docx, or genuinely still felt incomplete by the reviewer (e.g. only shows 3 rows, doesn't visually confirm pagination/scrolling behavior for an educator with many enrollments)." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_29_4_3b> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd29Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "unconfirmed-assumption" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:impact> "L" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "open" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-495ac43da71c11e9> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "No explicit Modified By/Modified On fields exist on cred:CredentialDefinitionVersion or cred:EndorsementDefinitionVersion (credentialing-domain.ttl) despite both this FDD's Certificate/Permit-type stories (5.1.2, 5.1.4) and its Endorsement stories (5.2.4) requiring them to be captured and displayed. Comment #78 (Dontje, MDE) shows 'further discussion about audit details/history is needed' was still open on the client side too, not just a modeling gap on our end." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_05_1_4> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_05_2_4> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd05Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "coverage-gap" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:impact> "L" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "open" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-4c026afb69bd28b7> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "EPP dashboard content is explicitly deferred, by this FDD's own text, to Feature 13.5 (Educator Preparation Providers – Dashboard), owned by epp: (a real, already-converted domain). FDD 13 has not yet been reviewed in this session, so whether epp-domain.ttl/epp-sequences.ttl already model anything answering 13.5 is unconfirmed — accounting responsibility belongs to that future pass." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:dashboards:Req_03_4> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:dashboards:Fdd03Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "out-of-scope" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "open" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-4ff0d4278b36ff53> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Ongoing/on-demand revalidation of assigned employees against position requirements, with a three-state (Yes/Partially/No) outcome, a notification banner, and a detailed Recommendations modal (missing requirement + recommended actions per employee), is described in 18.1.7/18.1.8 and directly confirmed by Wireframe9 — but nothing in staffing-domain.ttl or staffing-api.ttl models it. staff:Op_ValidatePlacement only evaluates credential/endorsement fit once, at assignment-creation time, with a flat boolean outcome. This is a genuine, wireframe-confirmed gap, not a documentation artifact." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:staffing:Req_18_1_7> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:staffing:Req_18_1_8> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:staffing:Fdd18Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "coverage-gap" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:impact> "M" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "open" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-52e213a4b6919398> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Question Set admin management (add/edit/activate-deactivate questions, decision-tree authoring) has no CRUD/authoring capability anywhere — only a single read-only stub operation (qset:GetQuestionSetsOperation) exists on the already-stubbed qset:QuestionSetContext. Unlike this file's other coverage gaps, there is no partial match to point at even loosely; every part of this story is unmodeled. High confidence this is real, needed functionality: proflearning-domain.ttl's own plrn:EvaluationTemplateAggregate explicitly depends on the Question Set framework for its question content, and comment 13 (Caswell, 2025-12-04) shows this FDD's own reviewers pushed for MORE explicit CRUD/activation detail here, not less." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:proflearning:Req_14_BizSpec_QuestionSetAdmin> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:proflearning:Fdd14Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "coverage-gap" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:impact> "M" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "open" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-57805c721a0d4216> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Feature 14.6's Addendum text explicitly excludes Professional Learning Admin file-queue management (viewing/resetting/cancelling/deleting stuck files, toggling upload availability) as a 'technical management and maintenance task to be handled by developers' — not the admin's job at all. But this same document's own Business Specifications prose (and HLS rows 9-10) describes, in substantial detail, an ADMINISTRATIVE page for exactly this: 'Ability to view and manage Professional Learning File Queues including ability to cancel, reset and view uploaded files', 'View file queues with file status and details... \"Reset\" a file that is \"stuck\" in the queue... Delete a file(s) in the queue... View audit details of uploaded files.' The Addendum's later, more considered exclusion should be treated as authoritative over the earlier prose (the same 'the numbered Addendum reflects the final position' precedence FDD 28 established for its own Sponsor-editability contradiction), but the contradiction itself is worth recording since a stale export/summary reading only the Business Specifications section would build the wrong (admin-facing) capability. Note also that documents-capability.ttl's docs:StagingFileAggregate — which already models exactly this technical pipeline (functionalArea constrained to {staffing, epp, proflearning}, states Scanning/Uploaded/Processed/Failed/Infected, 7-day auto-delete) — would be the natural backing mechanism if this WERE in admin scope; it exists today purely as backend infrastructure with no admin-facing view/reset/delete surface, consistent with 14.6's own 'developer task' framing." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:proflearning:Req_14_6> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:proflearning:Fdd14Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "discrepancy" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:impact> "M" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "resolved" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-5867cfb12d7b96e5> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Feature 26.4 (Professional Learning Catalog) was explicitly dropped by the document's own authors. This is the origin decision that FDD 28's own Req_28_2/Feature-28.2 rejection is downstream of (see plrn:Req_26_4's own notes for the cross-reference). No action needed; nothing to build, nothing missing." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:proflearning:Req_26_4> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:proflearning:Fdd26Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "rejected" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "resolved" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-5a2d0aa1af2964b5> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "This file's single most significant cross-domain finding. FDD 20 describes ONE generic, reusable internal/external comment-and-flag framework meant to be defined once (per its own Description: 'All...areas of state employee interaction that requires decision-making allow for both internal...and external...comments') and reused everywhere. A real, generic implementation of roughly that shape already exists — comm:CommentAggregate, a non-stub Communications aggregate whose own invariants already draw the internal/external distinction and whose own scoping notes says Comment permissions are 'scoped to organizational hierarchy...since comments are tied to specific business process items,' i.e. designed from the start to be consumed by multiple other domains. But TWO other real domains appear to have separately, redundantly hand-rolled the identical pattern as domain-local ValueObjects/invariants instead of consuming it: Professional Practices (profp:DisclosureInternalRemarks/DisclosureExternalRemarks, directly on the Disclosure aggregate) and EPP (epp:CredentialApplicationReviewAggregate's/epp:ApprovalApplicationReviewAggregate's own 'Remarks required on Deny/Hold' invariants). Credentialing, meanwhite, has NEITHER its own local remarks fields NOR a documented integration with comm:CommentAggregate for its Deny/Cancel/Hold flows (see Req_20_0_3's own notes) — the one domain this story names by name as an equally-applicable example is the one domain where NEITHER pattern is actually built. Unresolved architectural question for the project: should ProfPractices/EPP's local remarks fields be refactored onto the shared comm:CommentAggregate (as FDD 20's own framing implies they should have been from the start), or are they intentionally separate because a Disclosure's/Application's remarks are structurally different from a general-purpose Comment (e.g. exactly one remarks field per aggregate vs. an open collection, or mandatory-on-transition vs. always-optional)? Not resolved here — flagging for the project owner." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:dataquality:Req_20_0_1> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:dataquality:Req_20_0_3> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:dataquality:Req_20_0_4> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:dataquality:Fdd20Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "discrepancy" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:impact> "M" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "open" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-5ad1d37935327edd> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Every one of Feature 28.1's five stories (28.1.1-28.1.5) depends on a SponsorApplication-shaped entity with a review-status lifecycle (New/Pending/Approved/Comment/Documentation) and admin approve/reject/edit/delete actions — none of which exists anywhere in proflearning-domain.ttl or proflearning-api.ttl. This independently confirms plrn:Question_SponsorApprovalWorkflowContradiction (raised during proflearning-domain.ttl's own v3 conversion, Open Question #9, from FDD 26's side) from the opposite direction: FDD 26 describes the SPONSOR-SIDE submission/e-signature workflow that creates such an application, and FDD 28 describes the ADMIN-SIDE worklist/review/decision workflow that consumes it — both sides of the same missing entity, now confirmed by two independent FDDs rather than one. High-impact, cross-cutting: a real SponsorApplication aggregate (parallel in shape to the already-modeled plrn:ProgramApplication) is needed before either FDD's described behavior can be built." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:proflearning:Req_28_1_1> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:proflearning:Req_28_1_2> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:proflearning:Req_28_1_3> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:proflearning:Req_28_1_5> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:proflearning:Fdd28Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "coverage-gap" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:impact> "H" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "open" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-5b9172815a127c5d> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Feature 10.14 (file/API queue management: viewing queues, resetting stuck files, deleting queued files, toggling upload availability) is explicitly and deliberately declined by the FDD itself as an ADMIN capability — 'outside scope of an administrative task... to be handled by developers.' A real decision, not a gap: staff:Perm_AdminViewFileQueues and staff:Perm_AdminResetFileProcessing remain in staffing-permissions.ttl (carried forward from the earlier permissions catalog) but are now understood to describe a developer/operations tool, not a product feature to be built for the Staffing Data Administrator persona." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:staffing:Req_10_14> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:staffing:Fdd10Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "rejected" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "resolved" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-5b9ba56e99214f4a> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "25.2.1 requires the Pending Verification and Verified Candidates worklist tables to be downloadable in Word, Excel, and PDF formats. No export/download operation for a search-results table exists anywhere in epp-api.ttl, documents-api.ttl, or reporting-api.ttl — and reporting-capability.ttl's own Rule_NotEveryDashboardIsAPowerBIReport (Power BI embedding is for complex/cross-domain/scheduled-refresh reporting, not simple UI-level table exports) argues this specific capability was never meant to live in the Reporting bounded context either. A genuine, small, EPP-side gap: nothing in the converted domains currently supports it." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:epp:Req_25_2_1> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:epp:Fdd25CandidateTrackingDoc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "coverage-gap" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:impact> "L" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "open" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-5dba3332e29ec706> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "This FDD introduces 'Professional Knowledge and Skills (PKS)' as a second named assessment type alongside MTTC (29.1.2 via comment 2095209523/1225736752 'Added'; 29.3.10 independently). Nothing in credentialing-domain.ttl's AssessmentDefinitionAggregate/AssessmentResultAggregate model, nor asp:AssessmentProviderSystem, names PKS specifically — the assumption that it's simply another configured AssessmentDefinition instance (same as any MTTC subject-area test code) rather than a structurally different kind of assessment (different provider, different scoring model, different validity rules) is plausible but unconfirmed against any source describing PKS's own data shape." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:AssessmentDefinitionAggregate> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_29_1_2> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_29_3_10> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd29Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "unconfirmed-assumption" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:impact> "L" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "open" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-5e16f432f9f4ee8e> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Dashboard tile/report configuration for EPP is explicitly deferred to Business Specification #3 (Dashboards — dash:DashboardsContext, a stub-only bounded context per abox/mied-v3/CONVENTIONS.md's registry, same stub the FDD 29 pass's own Req_29_1_8 already deferred to). Not an EPP-side build item; no new GAPS.md entry needed since this stub is already on record." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:epp:Req_13_5> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:epp:Fdd13Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "out-of-scope" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "resolved" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-5e618128d68c4c4c> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "'Needs Responses' (Y/N, distinct from ProfessionalPracticeStatus) and applicant-level In-state/Out-of-state are both referenced repeatedly across this FDD (Needs Responses: 29.1.2, 29.1.4, 29.2.1, 29.2.7, 29.2.8 all mention it; In-state/Out-of-state: 29.2.9 and the main Business Specifications section's per-certificate-type flow list) as gating/routing inputs on CredentialApplicationAggregate, but neither exists anywhere in credentialing-domain.ttl's application model. This is the SAME 'Needs Responses' gap the FDD 11/16 pass already surfaced (there, Req_11_4_1/Rule_ProfessionalPracticeClearance) — independently re-confirmed by a second, later FDD, which raises confidence this is a real, permanent field the domain model is missing, not a one-off FDD-specific quirk. In-state/Out-of-state is new to this pass; cred:EndorsementDefinitionAggregate's similarly-named 'OutOfState' field is a different, endorsement-type-scoped concept and should not be conflated with it." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_29_1_2> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_29_1_4> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_29_2_1> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_29_2_7> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_29_2_8> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_29_2_9> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd29Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "coverage-gap" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:impact> "H" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "open" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-5f7cff137bb0445f> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "No admin-configurable allowed-file-type list for document uploads exists anywhere in proflearning-domain.ttl or proflearning-api.ttl, and this FDD's own text explicitly defers that configuration's ownership to FDD 14 (Professional Learning Admin), which was not reviewed as part of this pass — genuinely cross-FDD, not resolvable from proflearning's own source material alone. Wireframe7 (plrn:Wireframe7Doc) is concrete, real evidence the behavior is expected (a live file-type-rejection UI with a specific .doc/.docx/.pdf list), not merely a paraphrased AC." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:proflearning:Req_26_3_2> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:proflearning:Fdd26Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "coverage-gap" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:impact> "L" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "open" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-635395a86b7be0d4> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Email/alert delivery logic is explicitly deferred to Business Specification #6, which already exists as comm:CommunicationsContext — and is already the target of every staff:*Event's own sd:subscribesTo assertion in staffing-domain.ttl (EmployeeAddedToRosterEvent, EmploymentStatusChangedEvent, CollectionCertifiedEvent, etc. all already list comm:CommunicationsContext as a subscriber), so this dependency direction is already fully modeled, not a gap. The second half of this feature — Business Specification #4, Business Rule Management, determining WHEN and TO WHOM alerts are sent — has no corresponding bounded context anywhere in mied-v3 at all; this is the same Business Rule Management gap FDD 29's review pass already logged in GAPS.md ('Referenced throughout FDD 29... but no bounded context or admin-facing configuration surface for it exists anywhere'), independently re-confirmed here by a second, unrelated FDD." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:staffing:Req_21_6> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:staffing:Fdd21Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "out-of-scope" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "resolved" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-65c21e01dc999bc5> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Cross-reference, not a new finding: this story's own real-world trigger (Coordinator/Assistant Coordinator reassignment) is exactly the scenario plrn:Question_MissingSponsorSequences (proflearning-domain.ttl, Open Question #10) already names — no 'Manage Sponsor Contact Information' sequence exists in proflearning-sequences.ttl, and plrn:Perm_SponsorEdit has no backing API operation. Recorded here (rather than only in plrn:Req_26_1_3's own sd:notes) so this Requirement is not left unaccounted-for by the coverage-audit query." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:proflearning:Req_26_1_3> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:proflearning:Fdd26Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "coverage-gap" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:impact> "M" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "open" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-686eea879f04e43b> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "No operation or sequence composes a single 'view educator history' screen across the four-plus domains this FDD story spans (credentialing certificates/permits/endorsements, documents uploaded files, epp enrollment, profpractices conviction/disclosure data, plus demographic/employment/education info not clearly owned anywhere). Each underlying per-domain operation now exists for real (epp:Op_SearchCandidateEnrollments, profp:Op_ListDisclosures, docs:Op_SearchDocuments) — the gap is specifically the missing aggregation/composition layer, not the absence of underlying data access." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_16_4_1> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd11_16Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "coverage-gap" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:impact> "M" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "open" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-686f68340e6e7740> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "'Duplicate/copy an existing position' is described in the FDD's Business Specifications prose with its own distinct rules (editable and deletable before submission, immutable once submitted) but was never promoted to a numbered Addendum story, and no corresponding operation exists in staffing-api.ttl. A real, if minor, coverage gap and a documentation-completeness gap in the FDD itself (a described capability with no formal story or wireframe)." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:staffing:Req_18_BizSpec_DuplicatePosition> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:staffing:Fdd18Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "coverage-gap" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:impact> "L" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "open" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-686fe3d31c04dccf> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Recurring, still-unresolved thread (at least 15 separate comments across 2025-06-26 through 2026-03-23, spanning Dontje/MDE, Groom/CEPI, Sinha/DTMB-Contractor, Caswell/DTMB-Contractor) asking who exactly holds each 'SOM Credentialing ___' / worklist-processor / guidance-manager role this FDD keeps leaving as a blank ('Define role', 'Confirming if the role has been defined'). As of the last comment on this thread (Groom, 2026-03-23): 'Need help with refining and giving more definition around user role/functions for this area' — i.e. still open at the time of this ingestion. Re-checked against mied-v3's now-real iam-domain.ttl: it models Role as a UbiquitousTerm concept ('user-facing bundled permissions... e.g. Staffing Administrator, Credential Processor') but mints ZERO actual sd:Role instances anywhere in the graph (grepped iam/*.ttl and credentialing/*.ttl for 'a sd:Role': no hits) — so this is not a gap the real IAM conversion incidentally closed; the underlying role catalog this FDD keeps deferring to still doesn't exist as data anywhere in mied-v3, only as permission definitions (Perm_ApplicationApprove/.Deny/.PlaceHold, Perm_GuidanceManage, etc.) that were never reconciled against named roles in either the FDD text or IAM's own conversion." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Perm_ApplicationApprove> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Perm_GuidanceManage> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_11_2_1> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_11_5_1> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_16_1_1> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd11_16Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "unconfirmed-assumption" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:impact> "H" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "open" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-68735b91526ab805> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "CIRCULAR DEFERRAL, not a simple pointer: Feature 3.6 defers the Credential-Admin dashboard widget catalog to 'feature 11.7 Educator Credentialing – Dashboard' — but the FDD 11/16 pass (this same session, fdd-review/11-16-educator-credentialing/11-16-educator-credentialing.ttl) already reviewed 11.7 and found the exact opposite: its own out-of-scope Annotation on cred:Req_11_7 defers Credentialing's dashboard content HERE, to 'Business Specification #3 (Dashboards)', citing a review comment ('This requirement should be moved to #3 dashboards'). Neither FDD's own text actually specifies the Credential-Admin dashboard's widget catalog — each one's Addendum entry just names the other as the source of truth. Net effect is functionally identical to a coverage gap (nothing anywhere defines this content) but the MECHANISM — two FDDs each believing the other already covers it — is the more actionable finding for the client team to resolve, hence 'discrepancy' rather than 'coverage-gap' here." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:dashboards:Req_03_6> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:dashboards:Fdd03Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "discrepancy" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:impact> "M" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "open" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-68af40411736ca55> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Report-level availability windowing (Begin/End Date, future-dated Begin Date) and aggregation-level ('building, district, ISD, statewide') are both real, review-confirmed Business Specifications features (see rpt:Req_02_BizSpec_2's own notes for the confirming comment thread) with no corresponding fields anywhere on rpt:ReportDefinitionAggregate. Grouped with rpt:Req_02_BizSpec_1's versioning gap since all three are 'ReportDefinition needs more admin-authored catalog attributes than currently modeled' findings of the same shape." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:reporting:Req_02_BizSpec_1> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:reporting:Req_02_BizSpec_2> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:reporting:Fdd02Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "coverage-gap" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:impact> "M" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "open" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-6e43569118a7ba25> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "No export/download sd:ApiOperation for Position Roster data (or any Staffing aggregate) exists anywhere in staffing-api.ttl, despite being described twice in this FDD (18.3.6 for historical rosters, 18.5.7 for an upload-compatible re-import format) and directly confirmed by a wireframe (Wireframe10's circled download icon on the Positions list). A real, wireframe-confirmed gap." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:staffing:Req_18_3_6> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:staffing:Req_18_5_7> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:staffing:Fdd18Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "coverage-gap" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:impact> "M" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "open" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-70c33fb5a5221949> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "None of the six Software-guideline Features (32.5-32.10 — frameworks, OSS approval, licensing, security updates, error reporting, integration capability) is modeled by any specific graph node: each is a solution-wide technology/vendor/process policy rather than a feature the 11 converted domains would themselves implement, and no central 'platform technology stack' or 'platform NFR register' artifact exists to hold them. This is a genuine, structural absence rather than eleven separate small gaps — worth a project-level decision on whether these belong permanently at the sd:Solution root (per sd:nonFunctionalRequirement's own comment) rather than in per-domain files, the next time any of them needs to be cited or satisfied individually." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:fdd32:Req_32_10> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:fdd32:Req_32_5> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:fdd32:Req_32_6> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:fdd32:Req_32_7> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:fdd32:Req_32_8> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:fdd32:Req_32_9> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:fdd32:Fdd32Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "coverage-gap" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:impact> "L" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "open" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-72a30666aad3586a> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "No cross-domain link exists between a worklist item (in any domain's own worklist aggregate) and the document(s) it references — 32.16.11 requires viewing worklist-attached documents directly from the worklist, but neither Documents' own DocumentAggregate nor any domain-specific worklist aggregate models this relationship. The underlying document-viewing mechanism itself is otherwise fully real (docs:Op_DownloadDocument, RBAC, access logs) — this is narrowly about the missing worklist<->document association, not a document-capability gap." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:fdd32:Req_32_16_11> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:fdd32:Fdd32Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "coverage-gap" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:impact> "L" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "open" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-72a719f41fac0be0> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Neither a pre-launch digital-standards review gate (32.2.1) nor mobile-responsive operability (32.2.2) is modeled by any node in mied-v3. Both are legitimate platform-wide NFRs with no current graph representation — grouped here since both trace to the same 'SOM Digital Standards' governing document and neither has domain-specific content to satisfy it." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:fdd32:Req_32_2_1> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:fdd32:Req_32_2_2> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:fdd32:Fdd32Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "coverage-gap" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:impact> "L" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "open" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-733693259943dc29> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Feature 22.4's own text defers entirely to FDD 21.5 (Employee Roster Data Input via API and File Upload) for its user stories — nothing to model here beyond the cross-reference. FDD 21 is out of this session's own scope (reviewed concurrently by another agent)." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:staffing:Req_22_4> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:staffing:Fdd22Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "out-of-scope" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "resolved" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-735a0cff374cbfdb> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "No MOECS/REP legacy-data-migration process (batch job, sequence, or even a named aggregate) exists anywhere in mied-v3, despite being referenced as a hard dependency by this Feature and independently flagged from two other domains' own Open Questions (credentialing's Open Question #35 on credential_number's likely-legacy-MOECS format; proflearning's Open Question #13 on a possible legacy-MOECS Sponsor ID) — three independent points of contact with the same undocumented gap, which raises confidence this is a real, unaddressed piece of scope rather than a one-off FDD phrasing. Separately, no historical-data long-term-retention platform (cold storage tier, 99-year retention schedule) is modeled outside Documents' own document-scoped retention policy." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:fdd32:Req_32_11_1> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:fdd32:Req_32_11_2> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:fdd32:Fdd32Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "coverage-gap" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:impact> "H" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "open" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-742f145547da9329> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "What is the actual State Retention Policy schedule referenced by Feature 16.4.1 — how long must historical educator records be retained, and does it vary by record type (certificates vs. conviction data vs. demographic info)? Not stated anywhere in this FDD." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_16_4_1> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#questioning> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd11_16Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:impact> "M" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "open" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-75985b57c7377263> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A queryable, versioned audit/history view for Positions and Assignments is referenced three separate times across this FDD (18.1.9 Assignment History, 18.3.5 historical org charts, 18.3.7 position audit/version details) but never modeled as a retrievable entity or endpoint anywhere in staffing-domain.ttl or staffing-api.ttl. Several sequences (staff:Seq_UpdatePositionStatus, staff:Seq_CertifyCollection) assert that changes are 'tracked in audit history,' but nothing surfaces that history back to a user via a modeled ApiOperation. The recurrence across three independent stories in the same FDD raises confidence this is a real, cross-cutting gap (a general Staffing audit/versioning read surface) rather than three unrelated small omissions." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:staffing:Req_18_1_9> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:staffing:Req_18_3_5> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:staffing:Req_18_3_7> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:staffing:Fdd18Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "coverage-gap" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:impact> "M" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "open" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-783255cf0598d9ab> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Citation check: credentialing-domain.ttl's cred:Rule_PublicEducatorCredentialSearch says FDD 31.3's Legacy Reports functionality is 'explicitly out of scope per the FDD; internal SOM users retrieve that historical data outside the system.' CONFIRMED ACCURATE by reading the actual FDD 31.3 docx in full (it has no embedded images and no review comments — a genuinely short, uncontested one-paragraph doc): the FDD states in its own words that this functionality 'will not be carried into MiEdWorkforce' and that SOM users will retrieve pre-2014 Special Education Approval data (L2K/SCR reports from MOECS) outside the system. A deliberate, documented non-requirement, not a coverage gap." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_31_3> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd31_3Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "rejected" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "resolved" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-7963fc9716637803> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Comment 28 (Dontje, 2026-03-18), on 14.1.1's own bullet list: 'As Public Professional Resources has it's own user story (14.1.2), the remainder of the list each needs a user story as well.' Never acted on: no Addendum number exists anywhere in this document for the SCECH Attendee reporting page or the Individual Level Professional Learning component specifically (the Sponsor/Program application form bullets are at least covered by FDD 26/28's own numbering, even if not by this FDD's). This is the FDD's own review process flagging an incomplete promotion from Business-Specification-prose to Addendum-numbered story — the same 'described, never promoted to a number' pattern FDD 28/29 found repeatedly in their own domains, but here surfaced as an explicit, still-open reviewer comment rather than something this review had to infer." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:proflearning:Req_14_1_1> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#questioning> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:proflearning:Fdd14Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:impact> "M" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "open" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-7b2123f7d6f40033> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Same deferral to Communications as Req_11_6, repeated verbatim for the 16.x feature set." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_16_3> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd11_16Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "out-of-scope" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "resolved" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-7ca683050dfc4e41> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Feature 32.3 (Auditing) was explicitly declared no longer necessary in the FDD's own Addendum, and the decision was independently re-confirmed in a 2026-01-02 comment-thread exchange between Punniyamoorthy and Caswell. Modeled as a deliberate rejection, not a coverage gap — but see this file's header and Question_AuditCapabilityAssumedButStubOnly for why the underlying capability need did not actually go away." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:fdd32:Req_32_3> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:fdd32:Fdd32Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "rejected" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "resolved" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-7fc95dd4e4364698> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Alert/notification generation and display (29.1.10) is owned by Business Specification #6 (Alerts and Communications) per this FDD's own Dependencies section, consistent with comm:CommunicationsContext already existing as a stub subscribing to Credentialing's own events." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_29_1_10> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd29Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "out-of-scope" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "resolved" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-80944e9cfeaa4ae8> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "File-queue administration (view/reset/delete queued files, upload-availability toggles) for EPP's bulk-upload pipeline was considered and explicitly declined as an admin-facing feature — 'technical management and maintenance tasks to be handled by developers,' per the FDD's own words. A real decision, not a gap." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:epp:Req_13_6> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:epp:Fdd13Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "rejected" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "resolved" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-83c64d2f85054263> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Mass email to selected/All Sponsors, with attachments (Wireframe 14, Wireframe 1's 'Email Sponsors' tab) is confirmed, real, wireframed functionality with no backing API operation anywhere: comm:Op_SendManualEmail (the closest existing mechanism, and the one that DOES satisfy the single-recipient plrn:Req_28_1_4) supports only one recipientEmail and no attachments. This independently confirms plrn:Question_MissingSponsorSequences (proflearning-domain.ttl, Open Question #10), which had already flagged the same missing 'Mass Email to Sponsors' sequence from the Sponsor aggregate's own 'Referenced In' list but, at the time of that conversion, without this FDD's concrete text/wireframe to confirm it — raising confidence this is real, needed functionality rather than stale documentation." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:proflearning:Req_28_BizSpec_MassEmailSponsors> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:proflearning:Fdd28Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "coverage-gap" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:impact> "M" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "open" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-84c9266f1dd315ab> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "No export/download ApiOperation exists anywhere for profp:ExternalBackgroundCheckAggregate (profp:Op_GetPprReportData is a differently-purposed, Power-BI-facing aggregated-metrics endpoint, not a row-level Excel case-management export). This one gap underlies all three of 30.5.1 (the download capability itself), 30.5.2 (the SID Review File's per-district row shape, additionally blocked on the employment-data gap in Feature 30.7), and 30.5.3 (the District Notification File's EEM-sourced lead-administrator data, additionally blocked on the missing profpractices-to-EEM Dependency)." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:profpractices:Req_30_5_1> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:profpractices:Req_30_5_2> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:profpractices:Req_30_5_3> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:profpractices:Fdd30Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "coverage-gap" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:impact> "M" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "open" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-862497a21f355786> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "No node in mied-v3 represents the platform's core persistence-architecture decision (CEDS IDS/SQL Server vs. CEDS JSON-LD/Cosmos DB) — each domain documents its own storage choices independently, and none of them is actually the CEDS IDS/JSON-LD 'primary database for educator information' this Feature describes. A future pass converting a genuine platform-architecture source document (if one exists beyond this FDD) should mint this centrally, likely at the sd:Solution level per its own sd:nonFunctionalRequirement/NonFunctionalRequirement guidance." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:fdd32:Req_32_4> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:fdd32:Fdd32Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "coverage-gap" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:impact> "M" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "open" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-877ac0eeb84c5ab2> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Email/communication behavior is explicitly owned by Business Specification #6 (Communications), not Credentialing. Consistent with comm:CommunicationsContext already being a real conversion that subscribes to Credentialing's own events." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_11_6> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd11_16Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "out-of-scope" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "resolved" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-8a18bdd9549ebd5d> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Staffing-Admin dashboard content is explicitly deferred, by this FDD's own text, to Feature 10.6 (Data Collection & Compliance - Staffing – Dashboard), owned by staff: (a real, already-converted domain). FDD 10 has not yet been reviewed in this session — accounting responsibility belongs to that future pass." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:dashboards:Req_03_7> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:dashboards:Fdd03Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "out-of-scope" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "open" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-8a837f4dead4c1b9> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "'Program Descriptions' (Add/View/Edit/Active-Inactive, admin-maintained, on the same Wireframe-1 tab as Program Categories) is a reusable-library concept distinct from Program's own free-text description field, and has no aggregate/entity/API anywhere in proflearning-domain.ttl. Not previously flagged by any earlier proflearning conversion pass — a new finding from this FDD, not a re-confirmation of an existing one." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:proflearning:Req_28_BizSpec_ProgramDescriptionsAdmin> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:proflearning:Fdd28Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "coverage-gap" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:impact> "L" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "open" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-8cd31db253ccdef6> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "No Reset-filters affordance is modeled anywhere for Endorsement search, consistent with how the FDD 11/16 pilot treated equivalent Reset-button stories elsewhere in the graph — a pure client-side UX convenience with no domain-model or API counterpart expected. Recorded as a formal (low-impact) gap only so this Requirement isn't left unaccounted per fdd-review/CONVENTIONS.md's validation rule, not because it's a substantive finding." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_05_2_5> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd05Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "coverage-gap" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:impact> "L" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "open" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-8d3b4c5045605b14> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Three requirements (31.4.1's landing-page hyperlink placement, 31.4.9/31.4.10's 'No results found' validation-message behavior) are pure client-side UI chrome with no backend data or operation behind them, same treatment as the equivalent credentialing (cred:Req_31_1_1/31.1.6) and proflearning (plrn:Req_31_5_1/31.5.5/31.5.6) stories in this same FDD-review pass. The landing-page hyperlink is shared MiEdWorkforce public-portal chrome (pub:PublicPortalContext stub), not an epp capability." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:epp:Req_31_4_10> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:epp:Req_31_4_1> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:epp:Req_31_4_9> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:publicportal:PublicPortalContext> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:epp:Fdd31_4Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "out-of-scope" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:impact> "L" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "resolved" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-929b7a7d8bd4ba59> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "This FDD's own Dependencies section names ten other Business Specifications it relies on (User Authorization (1), role-based dashboard admin (3), Business Rule Management (4) for college-credit/DPPD validation, Alerts and Communications (6), CEPAS (7) for fees, Credential Admin (11) for per-certificate-type configuration, Manage EPP (13) for enrollment data, Educator Certificate - Application Processing (17), Data Collection & Compliance - Employee Assignment Details (22), Candidate Tracking and Recommendation (25), Professional Learning - Processing (28)). Of these, this review confirms real mied-v3 conversions exist for: iam (User Authorization), payments (CEPAS/fees), communications (Alerts), epp (Manage EPP), proflearning (Professional Learning Processing). No mied-v3 conversion exists (11 real domains only) for: role-based-dashboard admin (3, dash: stub only), Business Rule Management (4), Credential Admin (11) as a distinct configuration surface beyond what credentialing-domain.ttl's own CredentialDefinition/EndorsementDefinition/AssessmentDefinition aggregates already model, 'Educator Certificate - Application Processing' (17) as a distinct FDD from this one, Employee Assignment Details (22), Candidate Tracking and Recommendation (25, though epp:Seq_BulkUploadCandidateTrackingData exists as a related but not identical concept). Not modeled as Requirements here per CONVENTIONS.md's 'no possible satisfiedBy/rejection target' rule for whole subject areas outside the 11 converted domains — logged to GAPS.md instead." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#questioning> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd29Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:impact> "L" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "open" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-935922e6bfc3a6d2> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Comment 18 (Groom, 2026-02-02, on the evaluation-review passage that became 28.4.6): 'Admin ability to manage/maintain the evaluations should be included in 14, this may belong with that admin functionality. Need to discuss.' This is an explicit, still-open scope question from the FDD's own reviewers about whether evaluation review/management belongs in FDD 28 (Processing, this document) or FDD 14 (Professional Learning Admin) — never resolved anywhere in this document's comment thread. Recorded as its own Annotation because it's a genuine open cross-FDD ownership question, not a coverage gap this review can resolve on its own (FDD 14 was not reviewed as part of this pass)." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:proflearning:Req_28_4_6> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#questioning> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:proflearning:Fdd28Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:impact> "L" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "open" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-93c16756a8a1344a> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A Notes/Internal-Comments concept on the Rapback record (profp:ExternalBackgroundCheckAggregate) — with edit history — does not exist anywhere in profpractice-domain.ttl. The closest domain-model precedent (Disclosure's InternalRemarks/ExternalRemarks) is add-only and lives on a different aggregate entirely. The FDD's own review-comment trail leaves the editability/versioning question open (comment 1467423164), so this is not simply an unmodeled-but-settled feature — the requirement itself is still evolving in its source document." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:profpractices:Req_30_4_2> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:profpractices:Req_30_4_3> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:profpractices:Fdd30Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "coverage-gap" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:impact> "M" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "open" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-95138e1c8e8322a0> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Independently corroborates plrn:Question_SponsorAddressAndHumanReadableId (Open Question #13) with a full field-by-field confirmation: this FDD's Advanced Search story (31.5.7) requires City/Zip/County/Sponsor-ID filters, and its Sponsor Detail story (31.5.13, see below) requires displaying Sponsor ID and mailing address on the detail page — neither exists in plrn:ProfessionalLearningSponsorAggregate (whose only address-adjacent data is plrn:SponsorContact's name/phone/email) or plrn:Op_SearchCatalog's filter set today. No new open question needed; this is the same gap the existing question already anticipated, now confirmed from the primary FDD source directly rather than secondhand." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:proflearning:Req_31_5_13> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:proflearning:Req_31_5_7> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:proflearning:Fdd31_5Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "coverage-gap" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:impact> "M" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:references> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:proflearning:Question_SponsorAddressAndHumanReadableId> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "open" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-951f73bcb8ab0b90> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Comment 67 (Groom, 2026-03-27), anchored directly on 4.2.5's own title/opening sentence: 'Is this story needed? The Interface Integrations should define the connections to these external sources, and the BRE should utilize those integrations to perform the validations.' Reply 68 (Doherty, relaying 'Yashi', 2026-04-01): 'This has been removed as it was not necessarily needed.' 4.2.5 is, in fact, STILL FULLY PRESENT in the document — title, statement, and all 4 acceptance criteria (confirmed against document.xml directly) — exactly the same 'reviewer's stated resolution contradicts the visible document' pattern the FDD 29 pass's Question_CoverLetterStoryContradiction found for its own cover-letter story, and structurally identical to it: a reviewer proposes cutting a story on the grounds that a DIFFERENT FDD/capability (here, Interfaces and Integrations Setup (8) — already an independently-confirmed unconverted dependency per GAPS.md's own FDD 02 entry) should own the underlying connection, the author agrees and reports it removed, and the removal never actually happened in the document. This directly affects how bre:BusinessRuleEngineContext's own future scope should be read: per this unresolved thread, the EEM/Data-Warehouse CONNECTION itself may belong to FDD 8's Interfaces/Integrations capability rather than to Business Rule Engine, with BRE only consuming an already-established integration — but since FDD 8 itself has no mied-v3 conversion either, this can't be confirmed or reassigned here, only flagged." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:businessruleengine:Req_04_2_5> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:businessruleengine:Fdd04Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "discrepancy" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:impact> "H" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "open" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-95a3290bd9e2734f> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "25.2.4 describes 'Add Program' as a bulk action applicable to one or multiple selected Verified Candidates in a single operation, parallel to the already-bulk Status Update action (epp:Op_BulkUpdateCandidateStatus). No bulk-add-program operation exists in epp-api.ttl — epp:Op_AddCandidateProgram/Op_UpdateCandidateProgram/Op_DeleteCandidateProgram (used by epp:Seq_ManageCandidatePrograms) all operate on one enrollmentId at a time. A narrower, lower-impact analogue of the same 'bulk vs. single' asymmetry the ontology already tolerates elsewhere (e.g. Reject Enrollment has no per-candidate remarks requirement unlike single-application denial) — worth a small addition (a bulk variant of Op_AddCandidateProgram) rather than a redesign." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:epp:Req_25_2_4> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:epp:Fdd25CandidateTrackingDoc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "coverage-gap" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:impact> "L" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "open" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-98018ec2c89a717e> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Feature 19.2's admin-configuration surface (19.2.1, 19.2.2, 19.2.3, 19.2.5, 19.2.6 — define/version/schedule/extract arbitrary DQ checks) is not modeled anywhere and has no obvious home even conceptually: it is not clearly Data Quality's own territory versus Business Rule Management's (FDD 4, also unconverted per mied-v3/CONVENTIONS.md). Two independent pieces of evidence surfaced by this pass point the same direction: (1) review comment 30 on this exact document explicitly ties the underlying validation-execution functionality to Staffing FDD 10.3, while separately flagging that the generic 'BR Validation functionality (reviewing the results of BRs to ensure system is enforcing rules appropriately)' still needs a home, possibly 'a report on the admin dashboard'; (2) Wireframe19_3, the image actually embedded at 19.2.1's own acceptance criteria, depicts a Credentialing > Business Rules admin table rather than any Data Quality screen. Together these suggest Feature 19.2's admin console may have been conceived as the SAME underlying capability as Business Rule Management (FDD 4) — a generic, versioned, per-domain rule/check authoring surface — rather than a Data-Quality-specific build. Recommend cross-referencing against FDD 4 when it is eventually ingested, rather than treating 19.2 and FDD 4 as two independent gaps in GAPS.md." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:dataquality:Req_19_2_1> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:dataquality:Req_19_2_2> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:dataquality:Req_19_2_3> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:dataquality:Req_19_2_5> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:dataquality:Req_19_2_6> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:dataquality:Fdd19Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "coverage-gap" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:impact> "H" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "open" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-99721c3f398fafb3> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Three Business-Specifications-only capabilities — an upcoming-reports-with-due-dates dashboard summary, System-Admin-authored preset/template dashboards, and a role-gated Personnel Search tile (which also surfaces an apparent gap in iam's own Person/ID Search 15.4, not yet FDD-reviewed) — are each described in enough narrative and structural detail to be real, intended features, but were never promoted into the Addendum's own 3.0.x/3.x numbering and have no domain-model counterpart anywhere in the graph." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:dashboards:Req_03_BizSpec_PersonnelSearchTile> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:dashboards:Req_03_BizSpec_PresetAdminDesign> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:dashboards:Req_03_BizSpec_ReportsSummary> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:dashboards:Fdd03Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "coverage-gap" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:impact> "M" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "open" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-9990b51c222f1a18> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Bulk/file-upload processing for the Employee Roster (staff:Perm_EmployeeRosterBulkUpload) has no backing sd:ApiOperation anywhere in staffing-api.ttl — a pre-existing gap from the Phase 1 staffing conversion, now independently reinforced by this FDD's own 24.4.1 acceptance criteria and by wireframes 11-12 (an Upload Employee Roster modal and its per-row 'No UID'/'Duplicate UID' rejection result), which describe the exact validation behavior with no implementing endpoint to attach it to. Separately, this FDD's own prose under 'Feature 24.4' raises two more open questions with NO resolution anywhere in the graph: (1) whether users can bulk-update an EXISTING Unique ID's associated data via file upload (distinct from 24.4.1's reject-on-missing-ID rule for NEW records) — the FDD's own text says 'Need to determine if users are able to perform updates to the Unique ID in bulk/file upload... File types, schema and processing are to be defined,' and a reviewer comment thread (Caswell asking for clarification, Groom replying 'Confirmed' without adding the missing detail) confirms this is still genuinely open, not settled off-page; and (2) whether/how external local-HR-system API connections might interact with Mi-Key directly rather than through MiEdWorkforce — the FDD's own text: 'This may include interactions directly with Mi-Key, which will need to interface with MiEdWorkforce. The specifications and service implementation plans are to be defined.' Also note wireframe 11's own file-type list (.doc/.docx/.pdf) is itself inconsistent with 'validate against the schema' implying a structured/tabular format — an internal FDD inconsistency, not resolved here." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:staffing:Req_24_4_1> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:staffing:Fdd24Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "coverage-gap" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:impact> "H" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "open" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-9b4b3a5b600db8d7> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The Business Specifications' own registration-detail-storage / potential-attendee-reporting language (High Level Scenarios use case 5) was explicitly superseded during review: comment 8 (Ross) says this is 'no longer the case' and that bookmarking is the real mechanism; comment 9 (Dontje) agrees. No action needed against proflearning-domain.ttl — no PotentialAttendee/RegistrationDetail concept should be modeled; the already-modeled Bookmark mechanism (plrn:Req_27_1_4/27_1_5) is the confirmed, current replacement." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:proflearning:Req_27_BizSpec_ProgramRegistrationDetailsStorage> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:proflearning:Fdd27Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "rejected" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "resolved" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-9c7197ef2334a20b> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "plrn:Rule_OnlyActiveProgramsInCatalog only states a Program-status filter ('only returns programs with status Active'). This FDD (31.5.2) requires the same Active-only filtering to apply to SCECH Sponsors as well ('SCECH Sponsors and Programs that have an Active status') — plrn:ProfessionalLearningSponsorAggregate does model an Active/Inactive sponsor state that could support this, but neither the rule's statement nor plrn:Op_SearchCatalog's documentation currently describes a Sponsor-side status filter. Likely just an under-documented rule (the sponsor-status check may already be intended/implemented) rather than a missing capability, but worth confirming and updating the rule's statement to name-check Sponsor status explicitly." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:proflearning:Req_31_5_2> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:proflearning:Rule_OnlyActiveProgramsInCatalog> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:proflearning:Fdd31_5Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "discrepancy" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:impact> "L" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "open" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-9e0db02201e5b736> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Features 3.1 (School District) and 3.2 (Educational Staff) are the only two of the seven per-role dashboard features with no cross-reference to another FDD's own feature number at all — the FDD's OWN text calls the widget catalog 'to be determined' with no pointer anywhere. This is a gap in both the source specification's own maturity and the graph, not just the graph; grouped as one Annotation since both are the identical 'TBD, no pointer' situation." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:dashboards:Req_03_1> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:dashboards:Req_03_2> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:dashboards:Fdd03Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "coverage-gap" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:impact> "L" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "open" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-a0f65ca3f5fc4c37> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Feature 11.9 (Identity Management Integration) has no user stories yet — blocked on FDD 15 (User Management - Identity Management Integration) being finished first. Not a Credentialing-side gap; revisit once FDD 15 exists." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_11_9> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#questioning> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd11_16Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "open" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-a1ee10b4ecd717c8> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Three requirements (31.1.1's landing-page hyperlink placement, 31.2.8's 'Back' button, 31.2.9's external 'Learn about Credential Types' link) are pure client-side navigation/UI chrome with no backend data or operation behind them — the kind of thing this graph models at the API/domain level, not the page-routing level. The landing-page hyperlink itself is shared MiEdWorkforce public-portal chrome (pub:PublicPortalContext, a stub with no real domain model of its own in this project) rather than a credentialing capability — see cred:WireframeLandingPageThreeSearches, which shows this same landing page also serving epp:Req_31_4_1 and plrn:Req_31_5_1's identical stories." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_31_1_1> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_31_2_8> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_31_2_9> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:publicportal:PublicPortalContext> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd31_1_2Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "out-of-scope" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:impact> "L" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "resolved" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-a4a6af1f83372733> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A Program/ProgramApplication-level Audit Log (Date/time, User, Action, Description) is described three separate times in this FDD alone (28.4.3 'store audit details on edit', 28.4.3b 'review the Audit Log', and 28.5.7, word-for-word the same Audit Log capability again under the Worklist feature) plus once more in the Business Specifications prose (Wireframe 6, using the stale term 'Activity log' — see comment 9). No audit/change-history concept exists on plrn:ProfessionalLearningProgramAggregate or plrn:ProgramApplication anywhere in proflearning-domain.ttl; the only AuditTrail ValueObject modeled in this domain belongs to the unrelated plrn:SCECHCorrectionRequestAggregate. High confidence this is a real, load-bearing gap (independently repeated four times within one FDD) rather than a one-off phrasing quirk." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:proflearning:Req_28_4_3> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:proflearning:Req_28_4_3b> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:proflearning:Req_28_5_7> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:proflearning:Fdd28Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "coverage-gap" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:impact> "M" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "open" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-a5944141c5a4470d> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "plrn:ProfessionalLearningProgramAggregate has no field for Program Description, Prerequisites/Restrictions, Technical Specifications, Program Website, or Participant Fee, and models only a single generic Contact (name/phone/email) rather than a distinct, possibly-multiple Program Facilitator concept with a hyperlinked email. plrn:Wireframe31_5_4 (viewed directly) confirms all of these are real, designed public-detail-page fields, not a speculative wish-list. Distinct from plrn:Question_SponsorAddressAndHumanReadableId (which is about Sponsor-side address/ID fields) — this is a Program-side field-richness gap." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:proflearning:Req_31_5_12> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:proflearning:Fdd31_5Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "coverage-gap" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:impact> "M" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "open" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-a5b98ce05fe7f614> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Corroborates epp:Question_ProPrepPublicCatalogFieldGaps's City/Website finding with two further, independent confirmations: this FDD's results-table story (31.4.4, City/Website as required display columns) AND its filter story (31.4.7, City as a required dynamic filter) both need a field that exists in neither this domain's data model nor Organizations today. Also newly surfaces that epp:Op_SearchProPrepProviders has no sd:parameters property at all, so even the filters this domain COULD support (Provider Name, Program Type, Pathway, EPP Type) aren't promoted onto the operation, purely a documentation gap distinct from the City/Website data gap." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:epp:Req_31_4_4> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:epp:Req_31_4_7> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:epp:Fdd31_4Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "coverage-gap" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:impact> "M" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:references> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:epp:Question_ProPrepPublicCatalogFieldGaps> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "open" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-a5ef65a047669564> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "credentialing-domain.ttl's Rule_ManualReviewTriggering lists missing/failing required assessment results as a condition that flags an application for MANUAL REVIEW after submission. This FDD's own review comments (#120 Punniyamoorthy / #121 Dontje, 'Agree') establish instead that the system should hard-block SUBMISSION itself when a required MTTC score is missing or failing — manual review should never be reached for this specific cause. Two source documents disagree on where in the pipeline this check belongs; not resolved here." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_11_8_2> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Rule_ManualReviewTriggering> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd11_16Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "contradiction" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:impact> "H" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "open" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-a671a22d66d10771> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "PL Coordinator dashboard content is explicitly deferred, by this FDD's own text, to Feature 14.5 (Professional Learning – Dashboard), owned by plrn: (a real, already-converted domain). FDD 14 has not yet been reviewed in this session — accounting responsibility belongs to that future pass." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:dashboards:Req_03_5> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:dashboards:Fdd03Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "out-of-scope" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "open" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-a9a81e173a46d5e3> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "This FDD is internally inconsistent about where the expand-to-detail hyperlink lives: 31.2.2's acceptance criteria say 'The hyperlink is to be applied to educator's Name,' while 31.2.4's acceptance criteria say 'The Educator Credential Search results must include hyperlinks for the Credential Numbers.' Both cannot be the primary hyperlink target in the initial-results table at once. Not resolved by any review comment in this doc (unlike the 11/16 FDD's PPR-timing contradiction, which a comment thread explicitly settled) — flagged here as an open discrepancy for product-owner clarification, not silently picked one way." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_31_2_2> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_31_2_4> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd31_1_2Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "discrepancy" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:impact> "L" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "open" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-acd09c290eed1bcd> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "No worklist concept — not even a filtered-view working assumption, unlike EPP/ProfLearning/ProfPractice — exists anywhere in staffing-domain.ttl for the Staffing-data-collection worklist this story describes. The only worklist-adjacent staffing content is a disclaimer that staffing does NOT own the (separate) Identity Administrator worklist." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:fdd32:Req_32_15_7> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:fdd32:Fdd32Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "coverage-gap" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:impact> "M" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "open" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-ad59c3e4cd42ee10> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Persistent per-user dashboard/widget-arrangement state (29.1.8) belongs to the Dashboards capability (dash:DashboardsContext), consistent with how the FDD 11/16 pass's Req_11_7 treated the same kind of cross-cutting dashboard concern for Credentialing's own landing-page content. Not a Credentialing-side build item." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_29_1_8> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd29Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "out-of-scope" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "resolved" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-b10b93e86a2b436c> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Dashboard layout/section/widget customization (add, remove, edit, drag-and-drop, protected 'mandatory' tiles) has no corresponding domain model anywhere in the graph. One coherent capability described across four stories; grouped into a single Annotation rather than four near-identical ones, consistent with CONVENTIONS.md's dedupe guidance for closely-related repeated findings." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:dashboards:Req_03_0_2> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:dashboards:Req_03_0_3> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:dashboards:Req_03_0_4> ;
