	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "coverage-gap" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:impact> "M" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "open" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-b24c15cc2c437470> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "No Alias/AKA concept exists anywhere in this project's graph (verified: no hits for 'Alias' anywhere under abox/mied-v3 outside this FDD's own review file). Feature 30.8 (add/maintain/audit alias names for manual identity-verification fallback) is entirely new — there is no partial match, near-miss, or related concept to point to, unlike most of this FDD's other gaps." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:profpractices:Req_30_8_1> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:profpractices:Req_30_8_2> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:profpractices:Req_30_8_3> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:profpractices:Fdd30Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "coverage-gap" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:impact> "M" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "open" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-b2d82c527608a4b6> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The FDD's own visible text hedges the CEDS IDS vs. CEDS JSON-LD/Cosmos DB decision ('the state retains the right to determine whether the final data model will be a CEDS IDS or CEDS JSON-LD schema'), but a 2025-12-29 reviewer comment (Handley, CEPI, comment id 10) states: 'I think this decision to use JSON-LD, SHACL & Cosmos is far enough along to update the doc to reflect that and eliminate ambiguity & the need for changing later.' Two related, still-open sibling comments from the same reviewer on the same section: comment 6 ('Not sure this section is complete?') and comments 7/8 (a new CEDS version releases ~Feb/Mar 2026; the doc should specify which version it targets and flag the 14.x figure may need updating). None of these were resolved in the visible document text as of this pass — genuine, unresolved tension between the document's own hedged framing and a specific reviewer's read that the decision is effectively already made." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:fdd32:Req_32_4> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:fdd32:Fdd32Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "discrepancy" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:impact> "M" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "open" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-b3f3c6efb261f9e3> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Duplicate-role-assignment prevention and retained-data-on-error form behavior (10.1.5) isn't a distinct IAM capability with its own node — it's an implementation-quality expectation on whatever screen implements Req_10_1_2's iam:Op_ManualGrantAuthorization mechanism, not something staffing-domain.ttl or iam-domain.ttl models (or needs to model) as a separate concept. Recorded as a low-impact gap only so this Requirement isn't left unaccounted for, not because a real capability is believed missing." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:staffing:Req_10_1_5> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:staffing:Fdd10Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "coverage-gap" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:impact> "L" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "open" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-b46e6fadaa083181> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Feature 10.16's own user story content was deliberately removed during review (Doherty/Sinha comment, 2026-04-10) as redundant with Epic 32 (Technology, Standards, and Auditing) and with historical-data-viewing ACs already present in other Features of this same FDD. FDD 32 remains unconverted in mied-v3 as of this pass (same status FDD 02's own review already flagged it as an unconfirmed dependency) — noted for GAPS.md, not modeled as a Staffing-side Requirement gap since the FDD itself says the content belongs elsewhere, not that it's missing entirely." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:staffing:Req_10_16> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:staffing:Fdd10Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "rejected" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "resolved" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-b66483a1e6e3c7bd> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "ISD/Auditor dashboard content is explicitly deferred, by this FDD's own text, to Feature 19.3 (Data Quality Review & Processing – Dashboard). FDD 19 has not been reviewed in this session and dq:DataQualityContext is itself a stub-only bounded context per mied-v3/CONVENTIONS.md's registry — so the deferral target is currently just as empty as Dashboards' own stub, but the accounting responsibility for this Requirement belongs to whichever future pass reviews FDD 19, not to this one." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:dashboards:Req_03_3> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:dashboards:Fdd03Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "out-of-scope" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "open" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-b67cf8867256838a> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Email-template authoring/management (the unnumbered Feature 9.2 intro story) belongs to the Communications capability (comm:CommunicationsContext), which profpractice's own conversion already models as the consumer of profpractice's domain events and the owner of all outbound notification content. Not a Professional Practices build item." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:profpractices:Req_09_2_0> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:profpractices:Fdd09Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "out-of-scope" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "resolved" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-b6b40a8dbdac66c1> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "No ApiOperation or Sequence exposes an 'MTTC Information' review view anywhere in the graph, despite Wireframe7 showing exactly this screen (Test Name/Test Code/Status/Date Passed/Exam Date columns) as a real, designed feature." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_11_8_3> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd11_16Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "coverage-gap" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:impact> "L" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "open" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-b6eeb93979b34255> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Feature 30.7 (employment and credential cross-checks against a Rapback-matched Unique ID) requires profpractices to query staffing's employee roster and credentialing's issued credentials — the reverse of every cross-domain relationship currently modeled between these bounded contexts (today, Staffing/Credentialing query/subscribe to PPR's own assessments, not the other way around). staff:EmployeeRosterAggregate/staff:EmploymentStatus and cred:Op_GetEducatorCredentials/cred:IssuedCredentialAggregate are plausible real satisfiers once this new dependency direction is designed, but nothing today models it. Two sub-questions remain genuinely unresolved even within the FDD's own review trail: where the per-district employment record is stored (comment 1108281494) and whether EPP Candidate Tracking data should also be in scope (comment 2071511738)." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:profpractices:Req_30_7_1> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:profpractices:Req_30_7_2> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:profpractices:Req_30_7_3> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:profpractices:Fdd30Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "coverage-gap" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:impact> "H" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "open" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-b79264c7629e12cb> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Five requirements (31.5.1's landing-page hyperlink placement, 31.5.5/31.5.6's 'No results found' validation-message behavior, 31.5.8's Reset-button form state, 31.5.9's hover-tooltip chrome) are pure client-side UI behavior with no backend data or operation behind them — same treatment as the equivalent credentialing and epp stories in this same FDD-review pass. The landing-page hyperlink is shared MiEdWorkforce public-portal chrome (pub:PublicPortalContext stub), not a proflearning capability." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:proflearning:Req_31_5_1> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:proflearning:Req_31_5_5> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:proflearning:Req_31_5_6> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:proflearning:Req_31_5_8> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:proflearning:Req_31_5_9> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:publicportal:PublicPortalContext> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:proflearning:Fdd31_5Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "out-of-scope" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:impact> "L" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "resolved" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-b7d4232b06ddd5b7> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "pay:Req_07_1_2's acceptance criteria state the CEPAS-returned webpage displays a Success or Error message and that comment 8 (Punniyamoorthy, the FDD's own author, 2025-11-24) states the opposite: 'MiEd will not display any message related to payment, but will change the status of application based on the CEPAS response.' Comment 9 (Caswell, 2026-01-06) explicitly flags this tension ('The wording here seems to imply that messaging related to payment... is displayed in MEWF. We've modified the wording to fit your explanation. Please review and modify or confirm the change.') with no reply confirming resolution anywhere in the thread. Independently, wireframes 04/10/11/15/16 (all viewed directly, not assumed) show explicit MiEdWorkforce-rendered 'Payment successful'/'Payment Error' panels with confirmation numbers, amounts, dates, and item descriptions — real, specific UI content, not a bare status-only page. The weight of evidence (four separate wireframes plus the story's own AC text) favors 'yes, MiEdWorkforce displays a real success/error page' over comment 8's claim, but the FDD's own author is on record saying otherwise and the thread never closes the loop. Not resolved here." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:payments:Req_07_1_2> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:payments:Fdd07Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "discrepancy" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:impact> "M" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "open" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-bb18eb55961fe8b1> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "No cross-cutting Batch Job Administration capability exists anywhere in mied-v3 — no bounded context, aggregate, or API operation lets an administrator view run history/prior configuration versions, view/create/modify/remove schedules with per-job read-only-vs-full access control, or manually trigger/cancel a run, across the 7 domains that already use sd:BatchJob for their own individual scheduled processes. Each domain's BatchJob instances describe WHAT the job does (content/errorScenarios/initiatedBy), never a management surface for WHEN/whether it runs or who administers it. This is a single, well-defined missing capability spanning six numbered stories (32.14.1-32.14.6), not six separate small gaps." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:fdd32:Req_32_14_1> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:fdd32:Req_32_14_2> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:fdd32:Req_32_14_3> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:fdd32:Req_32_14_4> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:fdd32:Req_32_14_5> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:fdd32:Req_32_14_6> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:fdd32:Fdd32Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "coverage-gap" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:impact> "M" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "open" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-bb1c9a7c59e5b738> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "staffing-domain.md's own methods list for updating the org chart explicitly promises three input paths — 'Online / Bulk file / API' — and this FDD's own Feature 18.5 and 18.2.6 describe bulk-file-upload, batch/multi-record API ingestion, and multi-select bulk status updates in detail (18.1.1/18.5.1-18.5.4/18.5.8/18.5.9, plus 18.2.6's bulk status-update variant). Only the 'Online' (single-record, per-operation) path is modeled anywhere in staffing-api.ttl/staffing-sequences.ttl. There is no bulk-file-upload endpoint, no batch/multi-record API payload shape, and no multi-select bulk-write sequence for Positions anywhere in the converted Staffing surface — a substantial, confirmed gap (not a documentation oversight, since the domain doc itself promises this capability), spanning nearly all of Feature 18.5 plus 18.2.6. staff:Op_CreatePosition/Op_UpdatePosition/Op_UpdatePositionStatus are already external-client-accessible per staffing-api.ttl's own file header, so the SINGLE-record half of API-based ingestion (18.5.5/18.5.6) is real and satisfied — see those Requirements' own sd:notes; only the BULK/batch half of the picture (file upload entirely, and multi-record API payloads) is missing." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:staffing:Req_18_2_6> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:staffing:Req_18_5_1> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:staffing:Req_18_5_2> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:staffing:Req_18_5_3> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:staffing:Req_18_5_4> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:staffing:Req_18_5_8> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:staffing:Req_18_5_9> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:staffing:Fdd18Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "coverage-gap" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:impact> "H" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "open" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-bc690b9030e9fafc> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Business Specifications and both 6.2.1/6.2.2 explicitly call out admin-configurable MERGE ORDER for name/entity fields (Prefix, First Name, Last Name, Suffix; District Code, District Name) as its own capability, distinct from which variables exist. Nothing in communications-capability.ttl/communications-api.ttl models a field-order concept — comm:TemplateVariable captures name+mandatory-flag only, and comm:Op_GetAvailableVariables' EventTypeVariables response has no ordering field either. A real, if narrow, gap called out twice in the same FDD." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:Req_06_2_1> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:Req_06_2_2> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:Fdd06Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "coverage-gap" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:impact> "L" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "open" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-bcc43eb15d2d4c7d> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Citation check: credentialing-domain.ttl's cred:Rule_PublicEducatorCredentialSearch cites 'FDD 31.1/31.2' as its source, and credentialing-api.ttl's cred:Op_SearchPublicEducatorCredentials/cred:Op_GetPublicEducatorCredentialHistory carry a header comment 'per FDD 31.1/31.2'. Both citations are CONFIRMED ACCURATE after reading the full FDD 31.1/31.2 docx (Business Specifications, Addendum stories 31.1.1-31.2.9, comments, and wireframes): the rule's stated search/matching/grouping/sorting behavior matches this FDD closely, with the specific gaps and discrepancies noted above (Advanced Search parameters not modeled; 2-way vs 3-way Active/Inactive grouping; Name-vs-Credential-Number hyperlink inconsistency) being genuinely new findings from this FDD-review pass, not contradictions of the original citation." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Rule_PublicEducatorCredentialSearch> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#commenting> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd31_1_2Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "resolved" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-bcdf5244c6787000> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "cred:Rule_AutoApprovalCriteria's own sd:notes cite 'FDD 29, Feature 29.3' as confirming that endorsement-addition applications are exempt from the ProfessionalPracticeStatus=Clear auto-approval criterion, based on Feature 29.3 'consistently omitting PPR/Needs-Responses routing language present in every other application type's feature description.' Verified: true for 29.3.1-29.3.10. But 29.3.11 (Route Endorsement Application) explicitly adds 'Routing considers applicable PPR workflows where required (if in future scope)' — the FDD's own authors flag PPR routing for endorsements as a plausible FUTURE addition, not a settled permanent exemption. Rule_AutoApprovalCriteria's exception should probably be understood as 'true today, per this FDD, but explicitly flagged by the same FDD as subject to change' rather than an unconditional, permanent carve-out. Recommend a small addition to Rule_AutoApprovalCriteria's own sd:notes reflecting this nuance next time that file is touched — not changed here, since this review's job is to surface it, not silently edit an existing BusinessRule's settled statement." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_29_3_11> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Rule_AutoApprovalCriteria> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd29Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "unconfirmed-assumption" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:impact> "M" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "open" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-be4da9e3b8b4cff7> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "An educator/citizen-facing 'my past attended programs' search-and-history view (High Level Scenarios use case 3, wireframed as a 'Completed Programs' tab in Wireframe 3) has no backing API operation anywhere in proflearning-api.ttl — every existing list/search operation is either admin/coordinator-scoped (plrn:Op_ListProgramApplications, plrn:Op_GetSessionRoster) or the public, unauthenticated catalog (plrn:Op_SearchCatalog). Not previously flagged by proflearning-domain.ttl's own conversion or by FDD 28's admin-side review; a new finding specific to this, the citizen-facing FDD." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:proflearning:Req_27_BizSpec_PastAttendedProgramsSearch> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:proflearning:Fdd27Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "coverage-gap" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:impact> "M" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "open" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-be8f4ddd2efe14c1> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Comment thread 566123317 (Punniyamoorthy: 'Missing user story and wireframe for confirm enrollment as a Citizen/Educator') -> 1837999721 (Doherty relaying Yashi/Sinha: 'Noted. I have added a high-level user story for the Confirm Enrollment flow. I will update the story with more granular details once the wireframe is finalized and attached.') -> 514914922 (Doherty relaying Yashi/Sinha, asking what columns/data points the reviewer wants in the enrollment list) explains the origin of Feature 29.4's duplicate/colliding numbering: a 'high-level' Confirm Enrollment story (Req_29_4_3) was inserted late, reusing the 29.4.3 heading number that the pre-existing 'View Enrollment Information' content already used, without renumbering what followed (which is why a second, unrelated story also ends up numbered 29.4.4, see Req_29_4_4 below). The reviewer's own words ('high-level... will update... once the wireframe is finalized') mean 29.4.3 as written should be read as a placeholder-grade story, not a fully detailed one, even though a matching wireframe (Wireframe4) already existed elsewhere in the document from before this thread." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_29_4_3> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd29Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "discrepancy" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:impact> "M" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "open" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-bf8ca19306c3f3f7> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Question_AuditCapabilityAssumedButStubOnly — the single highest-impact finding of this review pass. adt:AuditContext (the `audit` stub per CONVENTIONS.md's registry) is declared identically in credentialing-domain.ttl and iam-domain.ttl as `a sd:BoundedContext ; sd:status \"stub\"` with NO aggregates, NO permissions, and NO API operations of its own anywhere in mied-v3 — its only content is sd:subscribesTo edges from five domains (credentialing, communications, documents, iam) recording that it listens to their events, which is not the same thing as a working, queryable 'view recent actions and data changes' capability. Yet 'audit log'/'audit controls' is casually assumed to exist as a real, working platform capability by at least six stories across this FDD alone: 32.14.1 (batch job history for 'audit controls'), 32.14.7 (failure-related audit logging), 32.15.3 and 32.15.9 (worklist configuration 'captured under audit log' / 'logged for audit'), 32.16.2 and 32.16.5 (document administration/override-request auditability) — plus Feature 32.3 (Auditing) itself, which was explicitly REJECTED as no longer necessary (see Req_32_3). The only real, working audit-log capability anywhere in mied-v3 is Documents' own domain-scoped docs:Op_GetAuditLogs/docs:Op_ExportAuditLogs (backed by docs:DocumentAccessLog) — which covers document access/lifecycle events only, not the general cross-domain 'who changed what, when' trail these other stories assume. iam:Perm_AuditView additionally exists as a bare permission with no backing operation anywhere, the same 'permission with nothing behind it' pattern the FDD 29 review already found for cred:Perm_GuidanceView. Recommend logging this in GAPS.md as a genuinely whole-solution-level gap (not domain-specific): mied-v3 has no real, queryable, cross-domain audit trail, despite the project's own 'audit' stub existing specifically to be that thing eventually." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:fdd32:Req_32_14_1> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:fdd32:Req_32_15_3> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:fdd32:Req_32_15_9> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:fdd32:Req_32_3> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:fdd32:Fdd32Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "coverage-gap" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:impact> "H" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "open" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-bfa95a57fc80c4c3> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Feature 15.13 explicitly builds on the Communications domain's own alert/email-template framework (Business Specification #6) and the Business Rule Management capability (Business Specification #4) rather than describing IAM-owned build items — not modeled as IAM Requirements here, same pattern as FDD 01's Feature 1.7 deferral to Reporting. Business Rule Management (04) has no corresponding bounded context anywhere in the 11 converted mied-v3 domains per GAPS.md's existing FDD 29/28 findings — this FDD independently confirms the same gap a third time (an Identity-Management-specific admin screen for managing WHAT gets sent and its trigger events has no home either), worth folding into that existing GAPS.md entry rather than opening a new one. Communications itself (the `comm` domain) has not been reviewed as part of THIS iam-scoped pass, so whether its own existing email-template model already covers 'per-module template configuration with role-based recipients and trigger-event binding' is unconfirmed here." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:iam:Req_15_13> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:iam:Fdd15Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "out-of-scope" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "resolved" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-bfe67d21ef1cbe65> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Coverage Gap re: Feature 14.3 (this FDD-14 review's own label, cross-referenced by proflearning-domain.ttl's plrn:Question_ConfigurableWorklistStatuses, which named this review and this exact label in advance). That Annotation asked whether 14.3's 'define new statuses and modify displayed columns' language describes genuine admin-configurable status/column definitions beyond the current ApplicationReviewStatus/RequestStatus enums, or is just imprecise phrasing for filtering. Reviewed directly against this FDD's own text and comments.xml: 14.3.2's AC is unambiguous about PER-VIEW COLUMN customization (add/remove predefined data fields/columns, applied on Save) and RESOLVED/UNRESOLVED CATEGORIZATION with visual progress indicators — genuinely more than filtering an existing status enum, but comment 6/22 (Ross, 2026-01-14, duplicate) — 'Reviewed on 12/10/25 that worklists will be limited to worklist management in the UI' — is new evidence narrowing the scope: this is UI-level view/column customization over already-modeled status data (ApplicationReviewStatus/RequestStatus), not a request for admins to author entirely new backend status VALUES. No worklist-view-definition or column-configuration mechanism exists anywhere in proflearning-domain.ttl/proflearning-api.ttl regardless of that narrower reading — the gap stands, just scoped down from 'new status taxonomy' to 'admin-configurable view/column definitions', which is itself still unmodeled." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:proflearning:Req_14_3_1> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:proflearning:Req_14_3_2> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:proflearning:Fdd14Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "coverage-gap" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:impact> "M" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "open" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-c01b518526386b89> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "No business rule or invariant anywhere in credentialing-domain.ttl models an MCL-waiver override path for Full Year Basic Substitute Permit applications: when one of the four named MCL waiver provisions (380.1531f Tribal MOU, 380.1281(3) Foreign MOA/Residency/SPI waiver, 380.1233c Detroit Public Schools Community District, 380.505 University Faculty Public School Academy) applies, this FDD says the system skips standard test-score/subject-area validation entirely and force-sets the application to Pending Evaluation status regardless of ordinary eligibility outcome. This is a distinct branch from the ordinary 60-semester-hour/GPA eligibility gate (Req_17_FYB_3, which IS covered by cred:Rule_AutoApprovalCriteria) and from the auto-approval/manual-review criteria generally — a real, previously-uncaptured override path." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_17_FYB_2> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd17FullYearBasicDoc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "coverage-gap" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:impact> "M" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "open" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-c0ff1023d10a58af> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Three real, wireframed, field-level-specified capabilities from this FDD's main Business Specifications section (Add College Credits/Wireframe5, Add DPPD + PD-hours-summary/Wireframe6, Complete SCECH Evaluations) were never assigned their own Feature/story number in the Addendum at all — the Addendum only elaborates the landing page (29.1), the generic application flow (29.2), additional endorsements (29.3), and view/print+enrollment (29.4). None of the three has any corresponding DomainEntity, ApiOperation, or Sequence anywhere in credentialing's mied-v3 files either. The SCECH one specifically corroborates an ALREADY-DOCUMENTED gap (credentialing-domain.ttl's own header note on proflearning's missing SCECH endpoint); College Credits and DPPD data-capture are, as far as this review can tell, newly surfaced gaps with no prior corroboration in credentialing-domain.md." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_29_BizSpec_AddCollegeCredits> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_29_BizSpec_AddDPPD> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_29_BizSpec_CompleteSCECHEvaluations> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_29_BizSpec_ViewProfessionalLearningHoursSummary> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd29Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "coverage-gap" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:impact> "M" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "open" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-c143b85a7a18e056> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Two different bulk-payment wireframes in this same FDD look like they belong to two different designs: wireframe-05 ('Bulk payment and refund', Screenshot 6) is scoped to one named district ('Holt public school district') with Temporary credential/Select type/Status filter dropdowns matching the Business Specifications' AUDIT-table filter description almost verbatim, while wireframe-12 through -16 (the Addendum's own 'Unpaid Application Fees' screens) show a differently-shaped table (Application #/Type/Amount/Status/Submitted, no district-scoping chrome visible, reached via a left-nav Credential Management menu item) for what 7.3.2's own acceptance criteria describe. Both plausibly satisfy 7.3.1/7.3.2's text, but whether they represent the same screen at two design iterations, or two genuinely different screens (e.g. a district-admin bulk view vs. an individual Business User's own unpaid-fees view) is not stated anywhere in the source document. Not resolved here." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:payments:Req_07_3_2> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#questioning> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:payments:Fdd07Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "unconfirmed-assumption" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:impact> "L" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "open" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-c273d7e4bad48690> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Dashboard tile/report configuration (Feature 10.6) is explicitly deferred by the FDD itself to Business Specification #3 (Dashboards), which is a stub-only bounded context (dash:DashboardsContext) with no real mied-v3 conversion — same gap the FDD 29 pass already logged for Credentialing's own dashboard deferral. Recorded here as out-of-scope (the FDD's own scoping decision) rather than a Staffing-side coverage gap; the underlying absence of a real Dashboards conversion belongs in GAPS.md, not as a Staffing build item." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:staffing:Req_10_6> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:staffing:Fdd10Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "out-of-scope" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "resolved" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-c2994b8c400189c8> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Discrepancy #1 also covers plrn:Question_IdpAggregateGap (proflearning-domain.ttl, Open Question #7), which likewise named this review in advance ('the only source describing IDP at all is FDD 17... See 14-professional-learning-admin review, Discrepancy #1'). Checked directly against this FDD's full text (Business Specifications, HLS table, Addendum, and comments.xml): FDD 14 does NOT mention an Individual Development Plan / IDP anywhere, under any name. This is a negative result worth recording explicitly rather than silently — it confirms Question_IdpAggregateGap's own premise (no FDD in this Professional Learning folder describes IDP) rather than surfacing the missing content the forward reference may have anticipated finding here. The IDP aggregate-vs-document-category question remains exactly as open as proflearning-domain.ttl already stated." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:proflearning:Req_14_2_1> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:proflearning:Fdd14Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "coverage-gap" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:impact> "L" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "open" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-c54f8342cd68172e> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Independent of the open FDD-14-vs-28 ownership question above, reviewing submitted evaluation responses has no backing capability anywhere regardless of which FDD ends up owning it: plrn:Perm_EvaluationView's own notes already state 'proflearning-api.yml has no endpoint for listing/viewing submitted EvaluationSubmission records at all', and the matching submission-side plrn:Perm_EvaluationSubmit is separately flagged as a 'SIGNIFICANT GAP... a real, load-bearing gap, not a minor one.' This FDD's 28.4.6 is the review-side, third independent confirmation of the same missing end-to-end capability." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:proflearning:Req_28_4_6> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:proflearning:Fdd28Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "coverage-gap" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:impact> "M" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "open" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-c595f517fac865a3> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Comment thread 19/20/21 in the Worklist document (Punniyamoorthy: 'Where does \"Certifications & Endorsements\" and \"Provider Details & Contacts\" user stories will be?' / Dontje: 'Missing user stories' / Sinha: 'Working on getting wireframes for this so that the user stories can be revised') confirms the two rightmost navigation cards on the shared 'Education Prep' landing page (Wireframe25_AddendumEducationPrepLanding1/2, confirmed by viewing) were never written up as numbered stories in EITHER FDD 25 document — an acknowledged gap in the FDD's own paper trail, not something missed by this review. These two areas (EPP certificate-category/endorsement approvals, and EPP provider/contact details) are exactly epp:EducatorPreparationProviderAggregate's own territory and are already covered by FDD 13 ('EPP - Admin'), which epp-domain.ttl's own Open Question #11 note already cites and which is being reviewed concurrently by a separate pass in this same session — out-of-scope for FDD 25 specifically, not a gap in the EPP domain model as a whole (epp:Seq_ManageCertificateCategoryApprovals / epp:Seq_ManageApprovedEndorsements / epp:Seq_UpdateEPPConfiguration already cover this territory)." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:epp:EducatorPreparationProviderAggregate> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:epp:Fdd25WorklistDoc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "out-of-scope" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:impact> "L" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "resolved" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-c5ae9a551fb19519> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The notification format/content/channel for a batch-job-failure alert to admins and business owners was raised during drafting (comment 36, Punniyamoorthy: 'Need to add the notification format and the content') and the reply (comment 1682393414, Caswell, 2026-01-02) confirms it was never actually decided ('I'm not sure we officially determined what type of notification a user should receive. Can we confirm that?') — genuinely open, not resolved in the visible document text. comm:CommunicationsContext (Alerts & Communications) is the natural eventual home for this, consistent with how every other domain defers notification content to that same capability, but no batch-job-failure-specific alert type is defined there today." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:fdd32:Req_32_14_7> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:fdd32:Fdd32Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "unconfirmed-assumption" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:impact> "M" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "open" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-c5b133986aa44834> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "4.1.9 ('Preview the Question Set before activation') has a heading and a user-story statement but a completely empty Acceptance Criteria section in the source document. The comment-32/33 thread on 4.1.8 (Groom asking whether 4.1.8 'should capture the ability to submit the update after preview'; Caswell confirming yes and saying the story was rewritten) is the likely cause: 4.1.9's own intended content (preview-then-submit, orphan-protection guarantees, audit capture) appears to have been absorbed into 4.1.8's rewrite, leaving 4.1.9 an orphaned stub itself — an ironic parallel to the orphaned-workflow risk the thread was discussing. Not resolved here; flagged for whoever owns this FDD next to either backfill 4.1.9's AC or formally merge/retire it." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:businessruleengine:Req_04_1_8> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:businessruleengine:Req_04_1_9> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:businessruleengine:Fdd04Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "discrepancy" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:impact> "L" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "open" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-c5b9e7d5a692c579> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A second, wholly distinct outbound (and inbound) email channel — Microsoft Graph API sendMail from dedicated Outlook mailboxes, for two-way correspondence — is described in this FDD folder's own 'Interface Design document - Microsoft 365 (Outlook).docx' but has no counterpart anywhere in communications-capability.ttl/communications-api.ttl/communications-sequences.ttl (ext:Microsoft365GraphSystem is minted fresh in this ingestion pass, with no existing model to link it into). This also sits in apparent tension with the primary FDD's own Business Specifications text: 'The system will provide the ability to view actual email messages within the application, using an embedded viewer, WITHOUT requiring a direct or two-way integration with a Microsoft Outlook client' — language that reads as explicitly declining exactly the two-way Graph integration the Interface Design document then goes on to specify in full technical detail (auth flow, endpoint, sample code). Not resolved here which document should govern; flagged as a genuine, unaddressed contradiction between two source documents in the same FDD folder, worth surfacing prominently since it also represents unmodeled infrastructure (impact H)." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:CommunicationsContext> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:Req_06_Interface_Outlook> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:Fdd06InterfaceOutlookDoc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "coverage-gap" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:impact> "H" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "open" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-c5bc4195a8988b19> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Feature 14.4's own text explicitly defers the underlying email/alert send-track-display mechanics to Business Specification #6 (Communications, a real converted domain) and the send-trigger timing/audience logic to Business Specification #4 (Business Rule Management, which has no converted counterpart at all per this file's own reporting). Correctly out-of-scope for FDD 14 itself; the PL-specific configuration surface this paragraph claims IS in scope is separately modeled via the BizSpec-only Requirements below rather than left unaccounted for." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:proflearning:Req_14_4> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:proflearning:Fdd14Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "out-of-scope" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "resolved" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-c6ff16a289b87f9e> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Feature 5.6 explicitly defers all reporting/report-administration behavior to Feature 2.1 (Reporting), not modeled by Credentialing. The narrative section's own reports-management content (retiring report availability, role-based report access, ad-hoc/custom report creation, export options, report-resource text management) is the same deferred content — not modeled as its own Requirement per this file's header note on unformalized narrative content." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_05_6> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd05Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "out-of-scope" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "resolved" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-c83c455850c6db74> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Discrepancy #1 (this FDD-14 review's own numbering, cross-referenced by proflearning-domain.ttl's plrn:Question_ScechBalanceQueryVsEvents, which named this review in advance): 14.2.3 confirms credential-renewal-accuracy verification of historical SCECH data is a real, admin-facing need ('structured to support credential renewal calculations, e.g., counting toward 150 hours'), but does not itself state whether that structure is a live query or an event-maintained running balance — it neither corroborates nor resolves the disagreement already on record between credentialing-sequences.md's assumed GET /scech-hours live query and proflearning-domain.md's own Downstream table, which says Credentialing maintains its own balance via event subscription. Recorded here to close the forward reference plrn:Question_ScechBalanceQueryVsEvents made to this review by name; the underlying question remains open." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:proflearning:Req_14_2_3> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:proflearning:Fdd14Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "discrepancy" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:impact> "M" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "open" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-c935ed7f4f5bb2b3> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Comment id13 (Groom, anchored at the very start of 21.1.3's own paragraph, no reply/resolution found anywhere in comments.xml or commentsExtended.xml): 'This is not a not a valid use case, the user will need to establish the Unique ID for all employees per 15.2 Business User Request for ID Requirements.' This directly contradicts 21.1.3's own stated premise — the story's whole point is adding 'individuals who have not been assigned a Unique ID' by running the Mi-Key matching algorithm from within THIS flow — while the reviewer's comment says a Unique ID must always already exist, established through a separate, earlier FDD 15.2 process, before an employee can be added here at all. This FDD's own Dependencies section is ambiguous on which reading is correct: it says both 'Once an employee has been added to the roster, the user must report the Employee Assignment Details' (implying roster addition happens first) AND cites FDD 24.2/24.3 ('The initial reporting of an individual requires use of the Identity Management Integration with Mi-Key... ID Matching and Assignment (24.2) and ID Resolution (24.3)') as a prerequisite dependency, without saying whether that ID-establishment step happens strictly before or as part of this feature's own 'Add Individual Employee' flow. staff:Seq_AddNewEmployee's own 'No match - create new record' branch (used as this story's satisfiedBy target above) currently models the from-scratch path as happening WITHIN Staffing's Add Employee flow, i.e. the same shape 21.1.3 describes and comment id13 calls invalid — so this isn't just an FDD-text ambiguity, it's a live, unresolved question about whether staffing-domain.ttl's own already-converted sequence models the right shape. Comment id 1690889436 (elsewhere in the same document, on the Add Individual Employee search step) raises the same overlap from a different angle: 'This is also defined in 15.2 Business User Request for ID requirements. Need to ensure the requirements are aligned and effort is not duplicative.' Not resolved here; flagged rather than silently picking a reading." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:staffing:Req_21_1_3> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:staffing:Fdd21Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "discrepancy" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:impact> "H" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "open" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-c98e91397f95716d> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Feature 7.1's own title is 'CEPAS Interface (Payments and Refunds)', and the Business Specifications section describes refund processing (by the Credential Administrator) in the same depth and structure as payment processing (its own inbound/outbound data-element tables), with HLS Use Cases 9-11 devoted to it. But the Addendum — the document's own more-detailed, formally-numbered story breakdown that 7.1.1-7.1.5/7.2.1-7.2.3/7.3.1-7.3.2 all come from — never assigns refund processing a number anywhere. This is the same pattern FDD 29's own pilot review found for that FDD's Add-College-Credits/Add-DPPD/SCECH-Evaluation features (real, wireframed capabilities described in prose but never promoted into the Addendum's numbering). Modeled here as pay:Req_07_BizSpec_Refund with a synthetic ID so it isn't silently dropped or folded into 7.1's own numbering." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:payments:Req_07_BizSpec_Refund> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:payments:Fdd07Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "discrepancy" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:impact> "L" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "open" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-ca05d1123c39fed6> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Two features are visually confirmed in this FDD's own wireframes but appear NOWHERE in its Business Specifications prose, HIGH LEVEL SCENARIOS table, or Addendum stories: (1) Wireframe3's report-row context menu offers 'Delete Report' as a sibling option to 'Deactivate' — a hard-delete of a catalog entry, distinct from (and more destructive than) the well-documented Active/Inactive toggle (2.1.3); reporting-api.yml has no DELETE /admin/reports/{id} operation, and rpt:ReportDefinitionAggregate's invariants say nothing about deletion being permitted or forbidden. (2) Wireframe5's category-level report list has an 'All Reports'/'Favorite Reports' tab pair with a per-report star icon — a per-user favoriting capability with no mention anywhere in the text, no corresponding field on any Reporting aggregate, and no plausible ownership elsewhere (unlike the dashboard-preference-persistence gap FDD 11/16 and FDD 29 both found and attributed to the Dashboards capability stub, favoriting a REPORT specifically is squarely Reporting's own catalog concern, not a generic dashboard-widget-arrangement concept). Both are genuine gaps introduced by evidence the FDD itself carries (its own wireframes), not modeling assumptions." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:reporting:ReportDefinitionAggregate> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:reporting:Fdd02Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "coverage-gap" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:impact> "M" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "open" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-ccce2e36052bc36a> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The Business Specifications section devotes substantial text to a full CRUD-with-versioning admin lifecycle for ALERT DEFINITIONS (create/search/modify/remove, Group/Title/Message/Description/Coded-Inserts/Start-End-Date fields, on-demand vs. scheduled generation) — paraphrased again in HLS rows 8-11 — but this was never given its own Addendum feature number (unlike Templates, which got the equivalent treatment as Feature 6.3), and communications-api.ttl's Alert operations only cover instance-level create/list/resolve, not definition-level search/update/delete/versioning. This is a comparable gap in shape to the admin-facing Alert Template management side of comm:AlertAggregate that Templates (comm:EmailTemplateAggregate) already has full API coverage for." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:Req_06_BizSpec_AlertAdmin> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:Fdd06Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "coverage-gap" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:impact> "M" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "open" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-d05edd0537f43c99> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Two related employment-date chronological-ordering validations this FDD describes in detail (21.1.6: a re-added record's new Date of Hire must postdate both the original Date of Hire and the original termination date, and reject exact-match resubmissions of a prior termination; 21.2.4: Employment End Date must postdate Employment Start Date on the same record) have no counterpart anywhere in staffing-domain.ttl's BusinessRule set, StateDefinitions, or Aggregate invariants. staff:EmployeeRosterAggregate models the co-requirement between End Date and Separation Reason (Rule_EmploymentEndDateSeparationReasonCorequirement) but nothing about date ORDERING or duplicate-termination-record rejection. This looks like plain field-level validation logic that simply wasn't promoted to a BusinessRule node during the v1/v3 staffing conversion, rather than a deliberately unbuilt feature — a real, if narrow, gap." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:staffing:Req_21_1_6> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:staffing:Req_21_2_4> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:staffing:Fdd21Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "coverage-gap" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:impact> "M" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "open" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-d2afb960e7a47024> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Dashboard rendering is owned by Business Specification #3 (Dashboards) — dash:DashboardsContext (declared centrally in mied-v3/solution.ttl, still sd:status \"stub\": no FDD in mied-v3's 11-domain scope covers it yet). Comments #67-69 confirm at least one requirement was actively moved out of this FDD into the Dashboards spec during review ('This requirement should be moved to #3 dashboards')." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_11_7> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd11_16Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "out-of-scope" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "resolved" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-d354c201da17bee5> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "27.2.2 (educator/citizen-initiated SCECH hours correction/dispute request) independently confirms plrn:Question_EducatorInitiatedCorrectionPathway (proflearning-domain.ttl, Open Question #11) with concrete FDD text and a wireframed 'Appeal Hours' entry point (Wireframe 4) for the first time — previously that question existed only as an inference from the aggregate's own sponsor-only shape. High confidence this is real, needed functionality (a second correction-request entry point, parallel to but distinct from the existing coordinator-initiated plrn:Op_SubmitCorrectionRequest) rather than a documentation artifact." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:proflearning:Req_27_2_2> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:proflearning:SCECHCorrectionRequestAggregate> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:proflearning:Fdd27Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "coverage-gap" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:impact> "M" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "open" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-d3a3eb4aeea321ee> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Feature 18.6 (email notifications and dashboard alerts for deadlines, data-quality issues, and required actions) is owned by Business Specification #6 (Alerts, Emails and Communications), per this FDD's own Dependencies section naming it explicitly ('The functionality will be supported... by the specifications defined in Alerts, Emails and Communications (6.0)'). comm:CommunicationsContext already subscribes to several of Staffing's own events (staff:CollectionCertifiedEvent, staff:CollectionOpenedEvent, staff:CollectionExceptionApprovedEvent/DeniedEvent, etc.) — corroborating, not contradicting, this scoping. Dashboard-alert display specifically also implicates dash:DashboardsContext (a stub-only bounded context per CONVENTIONS.md's registry), consistent with the FDD 11/16 and FDD 29 passes' prior treatment of the same landing-page/dashboard split." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:staffing:Req_18_6_1> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:staffing:Req_18_6_2> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:staffing:Req_18_6_3> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:staffing:Req_18_6_4> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:staffing:Req_18_6_5> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:staffing:Fdd18Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "out-of-scope" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "resolved" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-d487df9ed692c62a> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "No notification/task-routing behavior exists off cred:EndorsementDefinitionUpdatedEvent (the closest existing event for 'a new endorsement code was added') to alert the MiEdWorkforce System Admin to define assignment mappings. The 'allowable assignment mappings for Appropriate Placement' being defined is itself a Staffing-domain concept per this FDD's own Dependencies section (Managing Credential use of Assignment Codes, Feature 12.1) — a business specification not yet converted anywhere in mied-v3. Cross-domain gap: the notification trigger belongs to Credentialing, the mapping being defined belongs to a domain this project hasn't reached yet." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_05_2_7> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd05Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "coverage-gap" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:impact> "M" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "open" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-d4b67adaf9e1fb5e> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "No tile/widget auto-refresh mechanism (scheduled or navigation-triggered) exists anywhere in the graph." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:dashboards:Req_03_0_7> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:dashboards:Fdd03Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "coverage-gap" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:impact> "L" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "open" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-d4e4860b9549252f> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Email/alert/notification configuration for EPP is explicitly deferred to Business Specification #6 (Alerts, Emails & Communications — comm:CommunicationsContext, a real converted domain, already comm:CommunicationsContext sd:subscribesTo several of epp's own DomainEvents) and Business Specification #4 (Business Rule Management — no bounded context exists for this anywhere per GAPS.md's existing FDD 29 entry). Not an EPP-side build item." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:epp:Req_13_4> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:epp:Fdd13Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "out-of-scope" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "resolved" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-d720a579a5fe7865> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "No per-user dashboard-preference/customization persistence entity or endpoint exists anywhere in the graph (the same gap two OTHER FDDs' own out-of-scope Annotations already assumed would be filled here: cred:Req_29_1_8, cred:Req_11_7). Independently re-confirmed by a third, direct source — raises confidence this is a real, permanent, whole-capability gap rather than a one-off omission." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:dashboards:Req_03_0_6> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:dashboards:Fdd03Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "coverage-gap" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:impact> "H" ;
