<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-d7f884974665403b> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Sponsor/Vendor Applications worklist search (Wireframe 1) has real filter fields, real result columns, and a real wireframe, but — like the rest of Feature 28.1 — has no SponsorApplication entity anywhere in proflearning-domain.ttl to search over. Same root cause and same Annotation family as this file's Feature-28.1 coverage-gap Annotation; called out separately here because it was never given an Addendum number at all (unlike 28.1.1-28.1.5) and could otherwise be missed by a query that only looks at numbered Addendum stories." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:proflearning:Req_28_BizSpec_SponsorWorklistSearch> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:proflearning:Fdd28Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "coverage-gap" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:impact> "H" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "open" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-d8e92dfec9f49ca2> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Dashboard rendering-on-login (identify role, route to dashboard, populate role-specific tiles/summaries) has no corresponding Aggregate, ApiOperation, or Sequence anywhere in the mied-v3 graph. This is the same landing-page/dashboard concern that BOTH cred:Req_11_7 (FDD 11/16) and cred:Req_29_1_8 (FDD 29) already deferred here as out-of-scope for Credentialing — this pass is the first to actually check the target those deferrals point at, and confirms it is empty. Genuine, foundational, whole-capability gap." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:dashboards:Req_03_0_1> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:dashboards:Fdd03Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "coverage-gap" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:impact> "H" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "open" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-dc559af9875e234d> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Feature 1.7 explicitly defers all User Authorization reporting to Feature 2.1 (Reporting Framework Implementation, a different FDD/domain), per the FDD's own text — not modeled as IAM build items here. Worth flagging a nuance for whoever ingests FDD 2/the Reporting domain: iam-api.ttl already implements three IAM-owned report endpoints directly (Op_GetNewUsersReport, Op_GetDeniedRequestsReport, Op_GetInactivityReport, all backed by iam:BatchJob_GenerateReports) that closely match this FDD's own example bullet list ('Count of new user accounts by MiLogin Type since X date', 'Count of authorized user requests denied by Lead Administrator', 'Users with inactivity for X timeframe') — i.e. IAM already has its own dedicated reporting surface, not solely a consumer of a generic cross-domain Reporting Framework. This FDD's 'fully addressed by Feature 2.1' framing may understate what IAM already owns directly; not resolved here, just noted for the Reporting-domain ingestion to reconcile." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:iam:Req_01_7> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:iam:Fdd01Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "out-of-scope" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "resolved" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-e01f7f5f4c807893> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Data Quality Review & Processing admin configuration (staff:Req_10_BizSpec_DataQualityAdmin) is explicitly owned by FDD 19/20 per this FDD's own Dependencies section; reviewed separately in that concurrent pass, not duplicated here." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:staffing:Req_10_BizSpec_DataQualityAdmin> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:staffing:Fdd10Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "out-of-scope" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "resolved" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-e10c5c8e590c6272> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Four of this FDD's own embedded wireframes (wireframe-06, -08, -09, -10 — the 'ID Management Requests' list and all three Near-Match resolution action screens) carry a '< Back to Rapbacks' breadcrumb and title their content 'ID Collection Request #NNNNNN'. Neither this FDD's own text nor iam-domain.ttl/iam-sequences.ttl (which model this exact Identity-Administrator-review workflow as iam:IdentityResolutionRequestAggregate / iam:Seq_IdentityAdministratorResolveRequest, using only 'identity resolution'/'Near Match' terminology) ever use the word 'Rapback' anywhere. FDD 30 (Rapbacks) is itself still unreviewed as of this pass (fdd-review/STATUS.md's 'not yet done' list). Left open rather than assumed: it's plausible the product literally nests this whole worklist under a broader 'Rapbacks' section of the Identity Administrator's UI, but that can't be confirmed or ruled out until FDD 30 itself is reviewed." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:staffing:Wireframe24_10> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:staffing:Wireframe24_6> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:staffing:Wireframe24_8> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:staffing:Wireframe24_9> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:staffing:Fdd24Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "discrepancy" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:impact> "L" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "open" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-e3f73c4d79837079> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Still-open reviewer thread, not resolved anywhere in the document's own comment history: comment id6 (Groom, anchored at the Business Specifications section's 'The system will store all audit data for all changes applied to the Employee Roster' sentence) says 'Need to address in user story/design' — i.e. the audit-storage CLAIM exists in prose but was never itself promoted into a numbered Addendum story. Comment id27 (Groom, at the very end of the document, referencing a Professional Learning FDD's own audit-log story as a model: '28.5.7 As a Professional Learning Administrator, I want to review the Audit Log...Do we need to add a similar user story (like this one from 28) to address the audit requirements?') with reply id330543191 (Sinha: 'Yes this can be added. Can we get details on specifically what actions should trigger this? Eg: Roster status change.') confirms both reviewers agree an explicit audit-log user story SHOULD be added to this FDD, but as of this document's latest revision it had not been — meaning this FDD, as written, never actually specifies WHAT audit data is captured, on WHAT actions, or how it's surfaced to a user (contrast with FDD 28's own 28.5.7, which does specify an Audit Log review UI). Not modeled as its own numbered Requirement (there is no 21.x number for it to attach to), but flagged here since staffing-domain.ttl also has no distinct audit-trail Aggregate/Entity for Employee Roster changes specifically (audit modeling that DOES exist in staffing, staff:AuditWorkItemAggregate, is the ISD-auditor district-submission-review workflow — a different concept from a per-change audit log of roster edits)." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#commenting> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:staffing:Fdd21Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "unconfirmed-assumption" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:impact> "M" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "open" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-e4081b54c7b9f098> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "27.3.1, 27.3.3, and 27.3.4 all depend on the SAME missing capability: a configurable, RECURRING reminder interval/threshold for an unresolved condition (a pending evaluation, or — per plrn:Question_AttestationVsEvaluationSubmissionUnresolved — a pending attestation). communications-capability.ttl/-sequences.ttl model real, generic event-driven email/alert delivery (comm:EmailTemplateAggregate, comm:Seq_MassEmailWithConsolidation) but the only configurable-timing concept anywhere in Communications is a one-time, per-event-type consolidation-buffer window (15 minutes default) — a fundamentally different mechanism from 'keep reminding on interval N until the condition clears.' One coverage-gap Annotation covering all three stories rather than three near-duplicate ones, since the fix, if made, is a single new mechanism (a configurable recurring-reminder scheduler/BatchJob keyed off an unresolved-condition flag) that would satisfy all three at once, not three separate fixes." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:proflearning:Req_27_3_1> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:proflearning:Req_27_3_3> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:proflearning:Req_27_3_4> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:proflearning:Fdd27Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "coverage-gap" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:impact> "M" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "open" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-e40b2bc470512148> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Comment 24 (Dontje, 2026-03-18) on the Worklist wireframe: 'Is this wireframe representative of the general functionality, and if so will it be customized for PL admin?' Comment 681365075 (Doherty, 2026-04-06, quoting Sinha): 'This wireframe was originally meant for PL Admin. Can we get more insights on the changes that are needed here?' Comment 1996490306 (Doherty, 2026-04-06, quoting Sinha) responds: 'Noted as an action item. We are having internal discussions to gather the wireframes for these user stories. I'll be updating these user stories once the wireframes are complete.' Confirmed by directly viewing the referenced wireframe (plrn:Wireframe14_2Doc): it is a 'Worklist Management' screen whose own breadcrumb and row content ('Credentialing Data', 'Desktop/Dashboard Credentialing Worklist') are Credentialing's, not Professional Learning's — genuinely reused and, as of the document's latest comment thread, NOT yet customized. An open, FDD-self-acknowledged wireframe gap, not something this review is inferring." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:proflearning:Req_14_3_1> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:proflearning:Req_14_3_2> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#questioning> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:proflearning:Fdd14Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:impact> "L" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "open" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-e7e53a07799ad45b> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Wireframe2 (the 'New Report' admin form, confirmed by viewing both highlight variants) shows a single free-text 'Power BI Link' URL field and a 'Workspace' dropdown, not the two Power BI Service GUIDs (workspaceId, reportId) rpt:PowerBIReportReference/reporting-api.yml's ReportCreate schema actually model — nothing in either document describes how a pasted link would be parsed into those two identifiers, or whether the Workspace dropdown is really a second, separate field the wireframe redundantly also shows. Separately, the wireframe's Availability panel offers Role / Category / Sub-Category dropdowns, richer than the single flat rpt:DomainAssociationVO enum (iam/credentialing/profpractice/staffing/proflearning/epp/reporting) and single rpt:PermissionKeyVO string the domain model actually captures — Category/Sub-Category also matches the two-level functional-area/subcategory navigation Wireframe4/Wireframe5 show on the end-user side (2.1.5), suggesting the real taxonomy is deeper than DomainAssociation's flat enum. A UI-vs-model shape mismatch, not merely underspecified — this is evidence the domain model may need a genuine two-tier category taxonomy and a Role-based (not raw string PermissionKey) availability mechanism, not just documentation polish." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:reporting:DomainAssociationVO> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:reporting:PermissionKeyVO> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:reporting:ReportDefinitionAggregate> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:reporting:Req_02_1_2> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:reporting:Fdd02Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "discrepancy" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:impact> "M" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "open" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-e84e357c2c15c360> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Email/communication behavior is explicitly owned by Business Specification #6 (Communications), matching the identical deferral already modeled for Req_11_6/Req_16_3 in credentialing-fdd-11-16.ttl." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_17_2> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd17DailySubDoc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "out-of-scope" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "resolved" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-ed6038cfb06ec0c3> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Features 15.7 (Historical Records), 15.14 (ID Migration & Conversion), and 15.15 (Citizen File Upload) are each explicitly withdrawn by the FDD's own Business Specifications text — considered during scoping and deliberately dropped once Mi-Key/Data Warehouse ownership and process definition made them unnecessary. Genuine decisions, not gaps: nothing in iam-domain.ttl/iam-sequences.ttl models any of the three, which is the CORRECT outcome given the withdrawal, not a coverage miss." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:iam:Req_15_14> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:iam:Req_15_15> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:iam:Req_15_7> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:iam:Fdd15Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "rejected" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "resolved" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-f079adde0db728ea> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Every one of Feature 26.1's six stories (26.1.1-26.1.6) depends on a SponsorApplication-shaped entity with its own status lifecycle (locked-on-submit / Pending Local Approval / Pending Review), a Lead Administrator (Superintendent) e-signature approval actor and gate, and Coordinator/Assistant-Coordinator capture at intake — none of which exists anywhere in proflearning-domain.ttl, proflearning-permissions.ttl, or proflearning-api.ttl. This IS the original source material for plrn:Question_SponsorApprovalWorkflowContradiction (Open Question #9, raised during proflearning-domain.ttl's own v3 conversion from this FDD's description) and is independently corroborated by 28-professional-learning-processing.ttl's own Feature-28.1 coverage-gap Annotation (the admin/review side of the exact same missing entity). Three independent sources — this FDD's submission side, FDD 28's admin/review side, and proflearning-permissions.ttl's own pre-existing proflearning.sponsor.approve/proflearning.sponsor.delete permissions — now confirm the same missing SponsorApplication aggregate (parallel in shape to the already-modeled plrn:ProgramApplication). High-impact, cross-cutting, and now triple-confirmed rather than merely asserted once." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:proflearning:Req_26_1_1> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:proflearning:Req_26_1_2> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:proflearning:Req_26_1_4> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:proflearning:Req_26_1_5> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:proflearning:Req_26_1_6> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:proflearning:Fdd26Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "coverage-gap" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:impact> "H" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "open" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-f5d4104bde6d4d37> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "No modeled operation or sequence lets an admin select a criteria-filtered recipient group (e.g. 'all lead admins with alternative ed programs', sourced from EEM) and send a single mass-email blast to it, restricted to State/System Administrators. comm:Seq_MassEmailWithConsolidation is architecturally different (many individual triggering events consolidated per-recipient, not an admin-initiated group broadcast), and comm:Op_SendManualEmail/comm:Op_CreateAlert both target explicit individuals/ID-lists, not a criteria filter. The FDD's own review comments show even the 'large volume' threshold itself was still undefined ('This needs to be defined') as of the latest comment (2025-12-23)." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:Req_06_1_4> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:Fdd06Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "coverage-gap" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:impact> "M" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "open" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-f7935631098499ad> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "No modeled concept anywhere lets an audit/action-history entry resolve to the specific email or PPR-worklist item it produced (30.6.2), nor therefore express the negative case of that link being absent (30.6.3). Comment 1157398303 confirms the intended design (a normal PPRWorklist item with a Rapback-provenance indicator) but no such indicator field exists on profp:PPRWorklistAggregate/profp:DisclosureRoutedToWorklistEvent today." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:profpractices:Req_30_6_2> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:profpractices:Req_30_6_3> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:profpractices:Fdd30Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "coverage-gap" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:impact> "L" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "open" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-fad0e5587e9906e4> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "9.2.2 (configurable per-status/per-flag visibility for PPR Reviewers) is explicitly marked outdated and slated for removal by the vendor team (comment 131, 2025-12-08), and the identical note recurs unaddressed in a second review pass (comment 1774396353, 2026-03-11). Treated as a deliberate rejection, not a coverage gap — do not build reviewer-visibility configuration on this story's account." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:profpractices:Req_09_2_2> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:profpractices:Fdd09Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "rejected" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "resolved" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-fb5eb5f962086775> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "No graph node anywhere in mied-v3 models a standards-conformance/deviation-approval process (a place to record 'this feature deviates from SOM standard X, approved by business owner Y, documented for ATO'). This is a genuine, if process-shaped rather than feature-shaped, gap — none of the 11 converted domains' own BusinessRule/Annotation machinery is used for cross-cutting platform standards governance, only for domain-specific rules. Not necessarily something the SOLUTION needs to build (it may be a pure project-management/documentation process outside the application itself), but flagged since the FDD frames it as a system requirement ('the system must maintain...')." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:fdd32:Req_32_1> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:fdd32:Fdd32Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "coverage-gap" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:impact> "L" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "open" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:annotation-fea3aaf2743457c6> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Wireframe 1 (plrn:Wireframe1Doc, confirmed by viewing) shows a persistent Professional-Learning-Admin tab bar including a 'Coupons and Payments' tab, alongside tabs that DO match modeled/described capabilities (Sponsor Worklist, Program Worklist, Sponsor List, Program List, Category/Program description, Email Sponsors). Nothing anywhere in this FDD's Business Specifications, Addendum, or comments.xml describes what 'Coupons and Payments' does, and no coupon/discount concept exists anywhere in proflearning-domain.ttl or payments-domain.ttl (Professional Learning's own program-fee field, plrn:UT_ProgramFee, is explicitly display-only — 'actual payment collection happens on the sponsor's external registration website, not within MiEdWorkforce', which makes an in-app Coupons/Payments admin screen doubly unexplained). Wireframe-only feature with zero narrative backing — flagged rather than silently ignored or force-fit to an existing story." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:proflearning:ProfessionalLearningContext> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:proflearning:Fdd28Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "coverage-gap" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:impact> "M" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "open" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:dependency-0040828c4dc57320> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Dependency> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:fromContext> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:epp:EppContext> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:mechanism> "rest-api" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Retrieve previously uploaded candidate/EPP documents." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:toContext> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:DocumentsContext> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:viaOperation> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:Op_DownloadDocument> .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:_generated:dependency-0c249fd540c338e1> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Dependency> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:fromContext> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:payments:PaymentsContext> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:mechanism> "rest-api" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Used to calculate payment amount at initiation (fee amounts per credential type). Best-effort mapping: credentialing-api.yml has no endpoint dedicated purely to fee lookup — fee data lives in CredentialDefinitionFeeSchedule, presumably returned as part of this list response body, but response-body detail isn't captured at the sd:ApiOperation granularity in credentialing's own conversion. Ambiguous, not fabricated." ;
