<urn:solutiondesign:instance:businessruleengine:BreRequirementsDoc> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:SourceDocument> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:businessruleengine:Fdd04Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:docType> "fdd" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Companion prose draft (CEPI/MDE example business rules plus a coarser 'Add/Manage Business Rule/Validation Requirements' bullet list) — corroborating background for Feature 4.2, not independently re-derived into Requirements of its own since it restates the same content the Addendum states more precisely and with real story numbering. No sign-off table or author metadata of its own." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:section> "functional-design-docs/04 - Business Rule Management/Business Rule Engine/Business Rule Engine Requirements.docx" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:businessruleengine:BusinessRuleEngineContext> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:BoundedContext> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:displayName> "Business Rule Engine" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:identifier> "businessruleengine" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:kind> "PlatformCapability" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "MINTED BY THIS PASS, not previously in CONVENTIONS.md's stub-only registry. Justification: 'Business Rule Engine' (as the mermaid participant alias 'BRM') already appears, unresolved, as a named collaborator in multiple sequence diagrams in BOTH credentialing-sequences.ttl and epp-sequences.ttl — both files' own header comments explicitly say calls to it aren't modeled as SequenceReferences because 'there's nothing for them to resolve to'. GAPS.md's own FDD 29 entry independently flagged the same gap from the credentialing side ('Business Specification #4 — Business Rule Management... no bounded context... exists anywhere'). This FDD is the first real source document for that long-referenced capability, so it gets a real (if minimal) stub IRI now, the same way proflearning-domain.ttl minted qset:QuestionSetContext for a cross-cutting capability it referenced but didn't own. Deliberately NOT populated with any Aggregate/ApiOperation/Sequence beyond this bare BoundedContext declaration — this FDD's own Addendum describes only the desired admin UI/behavior, not any concrete API or domain-model shape, and inventing one here would be exactly the kind of fabricated satisfiedBy target this project's conventions warn against. Flagged in this pass's final report as a candidate addition to CONVENTIONS.md's stub-only registry table." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:purpose> "The cross-domain admin-facing authoring/configuration surface this FDD (4.0 Business Rules Management) describes: assigning validations to a functional area/collection/category/data element, toggling them on/off (on-demand or by effective-date range), setting severity (Error/Warning) and justification requirements, connecting to external data sources (EEM, Data Warehouse) for cross-system validation, applying validations uniformly across online/bulk/API entry points, versioning rule changes with an audit trail, managing the workflow error-message catalog, and producing business-rule/file-schema extracts for external publication. Feature 4.2 (Business Logic/Rules) of this FDD is the primary source for this stub; Feature 4.1 (Question Sets) is a related but conceptually distinct cross-cutting capability that already has its own stub — see qset:QuestionSetContext — not modeled as part of this context." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "stub" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:businessruleengine:Fdd04Doc> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:SourceDocument> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:docType> "fdd" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Covers Features 4.1-4.2 (document subtitle: '4.0 Business Rules Management (4.1 - 4.2)'). Author Vidhya Punniyamoorthy (DTMB); approved by Beth Dontje (MDE) and Caitlin Groom (CEPI), both 08/01/2025 per the signoff table — but comments.xml contains dated entries through 2026-04-01, well after that signoff date, same 'approved-but-still-actively-revised' pattern the FDD 29 pass already found for that document. Not resolved here; noted so the signoff table isn't read as 'nothing changed after this.'" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:section> "functional-design-docs/04 - Business Rule Management/4 - Business Rule Management.docx" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:businessruleengine:Req_04_1_1> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:UserStory> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "Search interface within the Business Rule Management area; input a Question Set Code or Text (Name, Description) to retrieve records; results display Code, Name, Version, and Status; results limited to Question Sets corresponding to workflows associated with the admin's functional-area permissions." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:businessruleengine:Fdd04Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Functional-area-scoped search results imply a Permission/PermissionScope concept scoped by functional area — no such scoping concept exists on any Permission anywhere in the 11 converted domains beyond the existing generic PermissionScope vocabulary (System-wide/Entity/District/etc.), none of which is 'functional area.' Wireframe1 (confirmed by viewing) directly corroborates the search+picker UI." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "4.1.1" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a MiEdWorkforce System Admin, I want to search for existing Question Sets based on the assigned code or defining text so that I can locate the specific application form or validation logic to maintain." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Search existing Question Sets" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:businessruleengine:Req_04_1_2> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:UserStory> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "'Edit' function modifies text parameters (Question Text, Error Messages, Option Text) of an existing Question Set; 'Copy'/'Version' function duplicates an existing set's structure/text into a new draft; net-new Question Set creation (new workflows/structures from scratch) is restricted to developer/database updates — Admin UI only maintains existing defined sets; Admin can modify Question Options (e.g. add a dropdown value) within a version; actions restricted to Admins with permission for the specific Functional Area." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:businessruleengine:Fdd04Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Deliberately narrow authoring scope (text/options only, no new workflow structures) is a significant, load-bearing design decision for this whole capability — an admin CANNOT define a brand-new application flow through this UI, only retexture an existing developer-built one. This bounds every other 4.1/4.2 story's 'no developer intervention needed' framing to cosmetic/parametric changes only, not new business logic. Wireframe1 corroborates the Edit/Copy actions." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "4.1.2" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a MiEdWorkforce System Admin, I want to maintain Question Sets by editing text or creating new versions of existing sets so that I can update language and options without developer intervention." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Maintain Question Sets via edit/copy, not net-new creation" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:businessruleengine:Req_04_1_3> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:UserStory> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "Entry form requires a 'Group' selection/entry; user enters 'Question' text shown to the end-user; user selects a 'Question Type' (e.g. text, numeric, date, boolean/yes-no); user enters a 'Description' for internal context; mandatory fields (Group, Question, Type) validated before saving." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:businessruleengine:Fdd04Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Wireframe3 (confirmed by viewing) shows a 'Select from Data Source' Question Type bound to a named external data source ('Michigan Higher Education Institutions') that this story's own example list (text/numeric/date/boolean) doesn't mention — the mockup is richer than the acceptance criteria text here. The prose Business Specifications section (not the Addendum) separately lists example workflows this framework applies to (Permit Application, Teaching Certification Application, Teaching Cert Renewal, 'Etc.') — comment thread 20 (Caswell: 'Please confirm the scope of Etc.') -> 21 (Groom: notes a decision-tree/dependency-matrix discussion is needed to determine which workflows apply) -> 22 (Caswell: 'Revised this specification per your comment... please resolve') shows this was reworked during review; the resolution isn't visible in the extracted text (the revision replaced rather than annotated the passage), so the current 'Etc.' framing should be read as still slightly provisional rather than a closed list." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "4.1.3" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a MiEdWorkforce System Admin, I want to define Question Set Details including Group, Question, Type, and Description so that the set is properly categorized and displayed." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Define Question Set Details (Group, Question, Type, Description)" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:businessruleengine:Req_04_1_4> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:UserStory> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "Unique Question Set Code auto-generated/assigned on initial save; 'Created by' captures the creating admin's username/ID; 'Creation date' captures the creation timestamp; Question Set Code, Created by, and Creation date are all read-only after creation." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:businessruleengine:Fdd04Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Comment 24 (Caswell: 'Can detail be added here about the assignment of the question set code?') -> 25 (Groom: 'intended to assign an ID to the question set for easy reference and storage') -> 26 (Caswell: 'Revised to include that note') is a resolved clarification thread, folded in here rather than given its own Annotation — it just confirms the Code is a simple reference identifier, not a load-bearing business key with its own format rules." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "4.1.4" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a MiEdWorkforce System Admin, I want the system to assign a Question Set Code and automatically display the Created by and Creation date so that provenance is tracked." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Auto-assign Question Set Code and provenance fields" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:businessruleengine:Req_04_1_5> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:UserStory> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "Effective Date (start) selectable; optional End Date selectable, including future dates; manual Active/Inactive toggle; system prevents the Question Set from firing in workflows outside its Effective/End Date range." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:businessruleengine:Fdd04Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "4.1.5" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a MiEdWorkforce System Admin, I want to set an Effective Date and an optional End Date for a Question Set so that its period of validity is controlled." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Set Effective/End Date and Active/Inactive status for a Question Set" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:businessruleengine:Req_04_1_6> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:UserStory> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "Modify the Question text shown to the applicant; add/edit/remove Error Message text shown on validation failure; changes reflected in the application workflow immediately upon the Question Set's effective date/activation; error message fields support alphanumeric characters for specific citations (e.g. credit-hour counts)." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:businessruleengine:Fdd04Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "4.1.6" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a MiEdWorkforce System Admin, I want to edit the text of questions and associated error messages so that I can update application requirements without requiring developer changes." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Edit question text and error messages without developer changes" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:businessruleengine:Req_04_1_7> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:UserStory> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "System assigns a version number; activating a new version auto-sets the previous version to Inactive/Archived; system prevents two versions of the same Question Set (same Group/Code) from being Active simultaneously; historical versions and notes remain viewable for audit but are not applied to live data entry." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:businessruleengine:Fdd04Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "4.1.7" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a MiEdWorkforce System Admin, I want to set the version of the Question Set and ensure the system enforces that only one version is active at a time, allowing older versions to be archived, so that it is utilizing the most recent and up to date version." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Version Question Sets with single-active-version enforcement" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:businessruleengine:Req_04_1_8> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:UserStory> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "Application workflow dynamically displays questions using text/error messages from the 'Active' version; branching logic (e.g. 'If Yes, jump to Question 3') enforced per the hard-coded/developer-defined workflow structure; a stop-condition answer (e.g. 'No' to a required eligibility question) displays the Admin-configured Error Message for that rule; user input validated against the defined Question Type before proceeding." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:businessruleengine:Fdd04Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Comment 32 (Groom: 'Should this capture the ability to submit the update after preview? Is there validation here to ensure workflows that require a question set are not left orphaned? Audit details stored upon save?') -> 33 (Caswell: 'Yes, we absolutely need...submit/save after previewing... developers structurally tie workflows and question sets together in code so an admin can't accidentally orphan a workflow... admins restricted from deleting core question sets, only modifying text/options within them... standard audit details will be captured... rewritten the story to better align...please accept the changes and resolve') is a substantive, resolved thread — its answers (orphan-protection is a structural/code-level guarantee, not a UI feature; audit capture confirmed) are folded in here as the best available account of the intended design, since the visible acceptance-criteria text for THIS story doesn't literally restate them. See Question_PreviewStoryAcOrphaned below for why this thread's rewrite likely explains 4.1.9's now-empty Acceptance Criteria section. Wireframe2's own broken 'Jump to Question 4 — Question no longer exists' branch is a concrete illustration of the exact orphaning risk this thread discusses." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "4.1.8" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a User, I want the system to present questions based on the developer-defined workflow logic and the active Question Set text so that I am guided through the correct application path based on my responses." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Present questions per developer-defined workflow logic and active Question Set text" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:businessruleengine:Req_04_1_9> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:UserStory> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:businessruleengine:Fdd04Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "NO Acceptance Criteria text exists under this story's heading in the source document — confirmed by inspecting document.xml directly (the heading 'Acceptance Criteria' is immediately followed by the 'Feature 4.2' section heading, with nothing in between). See Question_PreviewStoryAcOrphaned below: the comment-33 rewrite of 4.1.8 explicitly added submit-after-preview language to THAT story, which is circumstantial evidence the preview-and-submit content originally meant for 4.1.9 was folded into 4.1.8 during revision and 4.1.9's own AC was never backfilled — left here as an open documentation gap rather than guessed at." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "4.1.9" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a MiEdWorkforce System Admin, I want to be able to preview the Question Set before activation so that I can validate the intended user experience and logic flow." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Preview Question Set before activation" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:businessruleengine:Req_04_2_10> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:UserStory> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "Admin selects specific pending/draft business rules to execute against current system data; the test run identifies potential data violations WITHOUT permanently rejecting or altering live records; results report lists which records would fail the new validation logic, for impact assessment; interface confirms the validation logic enforces the defined conditions correctly against known data scenarios." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:businessruleengine:Fdd04Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "This dry-run/simulation capability is genuinely distinct from anything in the domain model of any of the 11 converted domains — none of them models a non-destructive 'test this rule against live data without applying it' concept anywhere, credentialing's Rule_ManualReviewTriggering and staffing's staff:TP_ValidationRuleEngine included." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "4.2.10" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a MiEdWorkforce System Admin, I want to be able to run specified validations against current system data before publishing them to production so that I can validate enforcement." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Dry-run validations against current data before publishing" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:businessruleengine:Req_04_2_11> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:UserStory> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "Interface configures extract parameters (Data Collection, Type, or specific Data Elements for inclusion); generates a Business Rule Validations extract with validation rule text and error codes for replication in local systems; generates a File Schemas extract with file-upload structural requirements; the File Schema extract automatically includes Sample Files populated with test data for external vendors." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:businessruleengine:Fdd04Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "The main Business Specifications prose section (not the Addendum) cites CEPI's own public MSDS collection-component-matrix and sample-XML-file pages as the real-world precedent this extract capability is meant to replicate for MiEdWorkforce — concrete, checkable examples of the target output format, not just abstract 'produce documentation' language." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "4.2.11" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a MiEdWorkforce System Admin, I want to produce extracts of validation rules and file schemas with specific criteria for inclusion so that I can publish documentation for use by external partners and data hubs." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Produce validation rule and file schema extracts for external publication" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:businessruleengine:Req_04_2_1> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:UserStory> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "Display developer-defined business rules available for the selected hierarchy level; Admin activates/deactivates specific rules for a Collection or Data Element (not creating new logic from scratch); Admin sets rule parameters where applicable (e.g. a credential cost or credit-hour threshold); configuration saved so the rule executes per the Admin's settings in that context." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:businessruleengine:Fdd04Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Same 'configure existing developer-built logic, don't author new logic' scoping as 4.1.2 — this is consistently how the whole FDD frames 'no developer intervention required.' Wireframe4 (confirmed by viewing) shows this modeled as a large-scale catalog (paginated '6115 items'), which is useful context for why search/filter (this story's own hierarchy-level selection) matters at this scale." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "4.2.1" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a MiEdWorkforce System Admin, I want to configure available business rules for Functional areas, Collections, Categories, and Data elements so that I can enforce specific validation logic defined for my area of responsibility." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Configure available business rules by Functional Area/Collection/Category/Data Element" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:businessruleengine:Req_04_2_2> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:UserStory> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "Manual toggle immediately sets a rule's status Active/Inactive; Admin enters a Start Date (Effective Date) and optional End Date; future-dated rules configurable to auto-activate on their Effective Date; validation engine checks current system date against the rule's date range and does not fire outside it; system prevents a rule remaining active past its End Date." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:businessruleengine:Fdd04Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Wireframe5 (confirmed by viewing) shows the single-rule Status/Effective Date fields this story describes, plus a read-only Actions list (send email, send notification, add to worklist) that ISN'T described anywhere in this story's own acceptance criteria — a rule apparently does more than gate a validation outcome, it can also directly trigger Communications-style side effects and worklist routing, per the mockup. See the two Annotations below (Question_BackdatingAndSystemLiveDateUnresolved, Question_DateRangeGapValidationClaimedNotVisible) for two distinct, still-open threads on this exact story." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "4.2.2" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a MiEdWorkforce System Admin, I want to be able to turn business rules on or off on-demand or set them using effective date ranges so that I can control when rules are enforced." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Turn business rules on/off on-demand or by effective date range" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:businessruleengine:Req_04_2_3> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:UserStory> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "Rule configuration interface includes an Error/Warning severity selector; Error blocks saving/submission until resolved; Warning alerts the user but allows the process/submission to proceed; UI indicator reflects severity (e.g. red for Error, yellow for Warning)." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:businessruleengine:Fdd04Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Comment 83 (Groom, 2026-03-27) reads simply 'Success, Error and Warnings' — anchored near this story's severity-selector text, likely proposing a third state ('Success') be represented in the UI indicator scheme alongside Error/Warning; no reply or resolution recorded, and the visible AC still only names Error/Warning. Minor, not raised as its own Annotation given how little content the comment itself carries." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "4.2.3" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a MiEdWorkforce System Admin, I want to set the validation severity status to Error or Warning so that the system enforces whether a user must correct the issue or may potentially bypass it." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Set validation severity: Error or Warning" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:businessruleengine:Req_04_2_4> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:UserStory> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "Justification configuration setting available specifically when Severity Status is Warning; Admin selects Required (forces a text explanation before bypass) or Optional (allows bypass without comment); justification text stored alongside the submitted data record for audit purposes." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:businessruleengine:Fdd04Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "4.2.4" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a MiEdWorkforce System Admin, I want to define whether justification options for warnings are Required or Optional so that exceptions can be appropriately documented." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Justification requirement (Required/Optional) for Warning-severity bypass" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:businessruleengine:Req_04_2_5> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:UserStory> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "Business rule engine connects to the Educational Entity Master (EEM) to validate entity data (e.g. verifying a building code is open/active); connects to the Data Warehouse to validate against historical data records; business rules can reference values from these external sources as criteria (e.g. 'If Building Status in EEM = Closed, trigger Error'); validation fails/triggers the configured error if submitted data doesn't match the external-source criteria." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:businessruleengine:Fdd04Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "SEE Question_ExternalDataSourceStoryContradiction below — the single most important finding of this pass. The full 4-criterion story text above is what's actually in the document today, but a review comment thread on this exact story says it was removed as unneeded." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "4.2.5" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a MiEdWorkforce System, I want to connect to external data sources to validate data submissions against required external criteria." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Connect to external data sources (EEM, Data Warehouse) for validation" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:businessruleengine:Req_04_2_6> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:UserStory> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "Active business rules execute on manual online-form entry/save; the same rule set executes record-by-record during bulk file upload; the same rule set executes on API-received data; consistent error/warning messages returned to the user or API response log regardless of submission method." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:businessruleengine:Fdd04Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "4.2.6" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a MiEdWorkforce System, I want to apply business rule validations to all data submissions regardless of whether the data comes from an online form, a bulk file upload, or an API entry point." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Apply business rule validations uniformly across online, bulk, and API submission" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:businessruleengine:Req_04_2_7> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:UserStory> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "Admin enters/saves custom 'Validation Message' text; Admin associates a validation code with the message for local-system reference; Admin edits existing message text without a code deployment; Admin removes/unlinks a message from a rule; updates reflected immediately upon saving (or upon the rule's effective date)." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:businessruleengine:Fdd04Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "4.2.7" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a MiEdWorkforce System Admin, I want to manage messages (Add, Edit, Remove) so that I can update the specific text and codes presented to users when validation fails." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Manage validation messages (Add, Edit, Remove)" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:businessruleengine:Req_04_2_8> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:UserStory> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "New version number auto-assigned whenever a rule is modified or a new effective-date range is created; User ID/Account Name of the modifying admin captured and stored; admin enters Submission Notes explaining the change before saving a modification; viewable history of previous rule versions including Created By, timestamps, and notes; audit data is read-only once committed." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:businessruleengine:Fdd04Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "The visible acceptance-criteria text for the Submission-Notes bullet is grammatically broken in the source document — 'The  enter \"Submission Notes\" explaining the change before saving a modification' (missing subject/verb, e.g. 'The Admin can/must enter') — consistent with a mid-edit artifact from comment 91 (Groom: 'Need to confirm if the submission notes are required or optional across functional areas') -> 92 (Doherty, relaying 'Yashi': 'This has been changed') never being fully re-typeset. Modeled above with the evident intended meaning ('admin enters Submission Notes...') rather than the broken literal text; flagged here rather than silently corrected." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "4.2.8" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a MiEdWorkforce System Admin, I want the system to version all rule creation and modifications and store comprehensive audit data (including user account information and submission notes) so that all changes are traceable." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Version rule changes and capture full audit trail with submission notes" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:businessruleengine:Req_04_2_9> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:UserStory> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "Dashboard/report view listing active validation rules and trigger-frequency counts; detailed metrics distinguishing Online Form / Bulk File Upload / API-entry triggers; Admin can filter frequency data by functional area, collection, or timeframe; associated trigger details displayed to help assess whether a rule is functioning as intended or causing excessive errors; frequency metrics available as a predefined widget addable to the System Admin Dashboard." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:businessruleengine:Fdd04Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "The 'predefined widget... on the System Admin Dashboard' clause is the same kind of cross-cutting Dashboards-capability dependency the FDD 29 pass's Req_29_1_8 already found for Credentialing's own landing page — dash:DashboardsContext (a stub-only context) is this story's natural second home for that one clause, though the bulk of the story (the frequency-review capability itself) is squarely Business Rule Engine's own, not Dashboards'." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "4.2.9" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a MiEdWorkforce System Admin, I want to review the frequency and details of specific validations being triggered so I can monitor system usage and rule necessity." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Review validation frequency and trigger details" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:businessruleengine:Wireframe1> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:SourceDocument> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:businessruleengine:Fdd04Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:docType> "wireframe" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Confirmed by viewing: 'Manage question sets' screen — optional Group filter, '+ Add question set' action, an 'Include historical versions' checkbox, and a 'Select a set of questions to edit or copy' picker with a Copy action. Directly corroborates 4.1.1 (search) and 4.1.2 (edit/copy existing sets)." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:section> "abox/mied-v3/fdd-review/04-business-rule-management/wireframes/wireframe-01-manage-question-sets.png" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:businessruleengine:Wireframe2> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:SourceDocument> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:businessruleengine:Fdd04Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:docType> "wireframe" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Confirmed by viewing: 'Standard Teaching Certificate' > 'Preliminary Teaching Certificate Questions' builder, showing 5 sequential Question cards with per-question Question Text/Question Type, conditional 'If Yes'/'If No' branching (Show Next Question / Show Error Message with custom text / Jump to Question N), a Select-type question with an inline option-list editor (Add Option), and — notably — a broken branch in the mockup itself: Question 2's 'If No' branch reads 'Jump to Question 4' with a visible validation error 'Question no longer exists.' This is the mockup's own author demonstrating what the branching-integrity validation from 4.1.2/4.2's story text should prevent, not a defect in this ingestion — but it's also a real, mockup-level illustration of exactly the kind of dangling-reference risk 4.1.2's comment thread (Question_PreviewStoryAcOrphaned below) was probing when it asked whether workflows could be left orphaned." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:section> "abox/mied-v3/fdd-review/04-business-rule-management/wireframes/wireframe-02-question-set-builder-teaching-cert.png" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:businessruleengine:Wireframe3> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:SourceDocument> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:businessruleengine:Fdd04Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:docType> "wireframe" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Confirmed by viewing: single-question 'Question Detail' sub-screen ('Completed Approved Teacher or Prep Program') with Question Name, Question Text, a 'Select from Data Source' Question Type bound to a named Data Source ('Michigan Higher Education Institutions'), plus Status/Effective Date fields. The 'Select from Data Source' question type is new information not spelled out in 4.1.3's own acceptance criteria (which only lists text/numeric/date/boolean as example types) — a real, if minor, type the Addendum text doesn't enumerate." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:section> "abox/mied-v3/fdd-review/04-business-rule-management/wireframes/wireframe-03-question-detail-data-source.png" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:businessruleengine:Wireframe4> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:SourceDocument> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:businessruleengine:Fdd04Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:docType> "wireframe" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Confirmed by viewing: paginated 'Business Rules' list (breadcrumb: Dashboard > Credentialing > Credential Data & Management > Business Rules) explicitly showing '1-10 of 6115 items' — i.e. the mockup's own author modeled this as a large-scale catalog (thousands of rules), not a handful of hand-managed toggles, which matters for reading 4.2.1/4.2.9's search/filter/frequency-review requirements as necessary rather than nice-to-have at this scale. Each row has a status toggle; a filter icon and an export/download icon sit above the table." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:section> "abox/mied-v3/fdd-review/04-business-rule-management/wireframes/wireframe-04-business-rules-list.png" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:businessruleengine:Wireframe5> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:SourceDocument> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:businessruleengine:Fdd04Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:docType> "wireframe" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Confirmed by viewing: single Business Rule's 'Details' tab (Rule Name, Description, Status, Effective Date) plus a read-only 'Actions' panel listing what firing the rule does (Send Email to Application Submitter, Send Notification to Application Submitter, Add application to a named worklist) — i.e. the mockup ties a business rule directly to Communications-style side effects and worklist routing, a concrete detail neither Feature 4.2's Addendum text nor this stub context currently spells out. Also has its own 'History' tab (not screenshotted), consistent with 4.2.8's versioning/audit requirement." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:section> "abox/mied-v3/fdd-review/04-business-rule-management/wireframes/wireframe-05-business-rule-detail.png" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:AlertAggregate> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Aggregate> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:CapabilityDoc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:description> "Manages system alerts with display context (dashboard vs on-screen), resolution tracking, and automatic expiration." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:emits> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:DashboardAlertCreatedEvent> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:emits> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:DashboardAlertResolvedEvent> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:hasEntity> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:AlertResolution> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:hasEntity> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:AlertRoleTarget> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:hasEntity> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:AlertVersion> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:hasState> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:AlertState_Active> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:hasState> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:AlertState_Draft> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:hasState> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:AlertState_Expired> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:hasState> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:AlertState_Pending> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:hasState> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:AlertState_Resolved> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:invariants> "Alerts must have an effective start date; expiration date is optional. Alerts automatically transition to Expired status when past their expiration date. Dashboard alerts persist until explicitly resolved or expired." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:rootEntity> "Alert" .

