<urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:PredefinedComment> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:DomainEntity> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:description> "A template comment available per functional area, for quick reuse." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:name> "PredefinedComment" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:Question_DuplicateSendMvpMitigation> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Idempotency for the email-send path is keyed on the triggering event's globally unique event_id (checked against existing EmailInstance rows before sending). The one edge case this doesn't cover: if the EmailInstance write fails AFTER the SendGrid send already succeeded, Service Bus will retry the message and can produce a duplicate send, since the idempotency check itself depends on that same EmailInstance write having succeeded. communications-technical-design.md's own stated mitigation is \"Accept rare duplicates for MVP (simpler), revisit if frequent\" — a deliberately deferred decision, not a designed solution (e.g. a two-phase/outbox pattern, or writing the EmailInstance row before calling SendGrid instead of after). Left open rather than assuming a resolution." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:EmailInstanceAggregate> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:TP_VariableResolution> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#questioning> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:TechnicalDesignDoc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:impact> "M" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "open" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:Question_PostRetentionArchivalOwnership> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "What happens to emails beyond the 7-year audit retention period — export to Data Lake, permanent deletion, or something else? Who owns archival after year 7? (communications-capability.md Open Question #19.) communications-technical-design.md's own Blob Lifecycle Policy states \"7+ years: Delete (after Data Lake export)\" as the mechanism, but doesn't name an owner for that export/deletion process or confirm it against Michigan's state records retention schedule (communications-capability.md's Compliance section states email audit metadata is retained \"for 7 years per Michigan state records retention schedule\" without addressing what the schedule requires afterward)." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:BatchJob_EmailContentArchival> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#questioning> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:TechnicalDesignDoc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:impact> "M" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:owner> "Records/Compliance + Engineering" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "open" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:Question_TemplateDuplicateDefinition> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "What constitutes a template \"duplicate\" — exact name match, content similarity, or subject match? (Open Question #5)" ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:EmailTemplateAggregate> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#questioning> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:CapabilityDoc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:impact> "L" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "open" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:Question_TemplateVariableFailureHandling> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Three related, still-open questions about mandatory-variable resolution failure handling, collapsed into one annotation since they all bear on the same rule: (1) should the system allow a \"send anyway\" option that replaces unresolved mandatory variables with a \"[DATA UNAVAILABLE]\" placeholder — this would avoid notification delays but might confuse recipients; (2) should repeated resolution failures (more than 10 in 24 hours) automatically deactivate the template to prevent ongoing issues (Open Question #17); (3) what is the appropriate DLQ retention period before permanent failure — 7 days, 30 days, or indefinite (Open Question #18)?" ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:Rule_TemplateVariableMandatoryResolution> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#questioning> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:CapabilityDoc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:impact> "M" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "open" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:Question_TemplateVariablesInSubjectLine> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Can the email subject line contain template variables? (Open Question #4)" ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:TemplateVersion> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#questioning> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:CapabilityDoc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:impact> "L" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "open" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:Question_TemplateVersionRestoration> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Can old template versions be restored and reactivated, or are they viewable for history only? (Open Question #7)" ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:Rule_SingleActiveTemplateVersion> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#questioning> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:CapabilityDoc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:impact> "M" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "open" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:Req_06_1_1> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:UserStory> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "Configure \"To:\" recipients dynamically based on User Roles (e.g. Staffing Admin, Credentialing Admin) or specific contact types; support \"CC:\" recipients for automated notifications where secondary stakeholders require visibility; allow a System Admin to manually add a \"CC:\" recipient when resending a historical email; utilize existing database fields to populate recipient information." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:Fdd06Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Direct, strong match: automated-trigger path via Seq_EventTriggeredEmailSend, manual path via Seq_ManualEmailSendWithCustomization, and the manual-CC-on-resend detail specifically via Op_ResendEmail's own recipientEmail+ccEmails request shape (comm:EmailResend). Role-based To: targeting matches comm:TemplateRecipient's own description ('Role-based recipient targeting configuration for a template') closely." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "6.1.1" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:EmailRecipient> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:Op_ResendEmail> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:Seq_EventTriggeredEmailSend> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:Seq_ManualEmailSendWithCustomization> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:TemplateRecipient> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As the MiEdWorkforce System, I must support sending emails to \"To:\" and \"CC:\" recipients based on system triggers or manual admin action so that the communication framework can support both automated and manual messaging needs." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Send to To:/CC: recipients on system trigger or manual action" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:Req_06_1_2> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:UserStory> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "Successfully transmit to internal (@michigan.gov) and external (non-state domain) recipients; allow System Admins to authorize emails to both audiences without differentiation in the sending process; record both kinds of transmission in historical communication logs." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:Fdd06Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "comm:EmailRecipient's recipient_type (User|External) is a plausible but not exact match: it distinguishes an internal system-user reference from an external contact, not specifically an @michigan.gov vs. non-state EMAIL DOMAIN — the story's 'no differentiation in the sending process' criterion is satisfied either way (the send path genuinely doesn't branch on domain), but the domain-based classification itself isn't a separately modeled field. Minor terminology-level gap, not raised as its own Annotation." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "6.1.2" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:EmailInstanceAggregate> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:EmailRecipient> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:Seq_EventTriggeredEmailSend> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:Seq_ManualEmailSendWithCustomization> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As the MiEdWorkforce System, I must support sending emails both internally (@michigan.gov) and externally, so that communication can be done effectively with all MiEdWorkforce users." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Send both internally (@michigan.gov) and externally" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:Req_06_1_3> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:UserStory> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "Integrate directly with the SendGrid API for dispatch of all system-generated emails; authenticate successfully with SendGrid; create batches for transmission if the number of emails exceeds SendGrid-defined thresholds." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:Fdd06Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Strong match, including the batching-on-threshold criterion specifically: communications-technical-design.ttl's comm:TP_SendGridWebhookProcessing documents the confirmed 10,000 req/sec SendGrid account tier and an in-memory queue processing at 9,500 req/sec (5% safety margin) with Service Bus backpressure — this IS the threshold-driven batching this story describes, not merely a related detail. Interface Design document - SendGrid.docx corroborates the same rate limit and Bearer-token auth independently." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "6.1.3" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:TP_SendGridCircuitBreaker> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:TP_SendGridWebhookProcessing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:external:SendGridSystem> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As the MiEdWorkforce System, I must interface with the SendGrid API, so that the email notification service can be reliably executed." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Interface with SendGrid API" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:Req_06_1_4> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:UserStory> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "Allow the System Admin to select recipient groups for mass emails based on specific criteria or user types (e.g. data from the EEM); support processing/sending \"large volume\" blasts per defined performance standards; restrict mass/bulk-email initiation to State System Administrators, excluding District-level staff; provide a confirmation mechanism before sending; successfully send to group examples such as \"all lead admins that have alternative ed programs.\"" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:Fdd06Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "No satisfiedBy: no operation or sequence anywhere in communications-api.ttl/communications-sequences.ttl lets an admin select an EEM-sourced recipient GROUP BY CRITERIA and send one message to it. The two closest existing mechanisms are both a different shape: comm:Op_SendManualEmail sends to one explicit recipient (or comm:Op_CreateAlert's targetUserIds, an explicit ID list, not a criteria filter), and comm:Seq_MassEmailWithConsolidation batches many already-individual PER-RECIPIENT events into one email per recipient (consolidation), not one email fanned out to a criteria-selected group. comm:Perm_EmailSendAdhoc ('System Admin only... bypasses the template framework') is the closest PERMISSION match for the State-Admin-only restriction, but nothing gates a criteria-based-mass-send operation specifically since no such operation exists. Comment 921997058 ('This needs to be defined') sits directly on this FDD's own '\"Large volume\" will be defined' placeholder text, confirming even the FDD's own authors left the volume threshold undefined at review time. Genuine coverage gap — see the Annotation below." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "6.1.4" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As the MiEdWorkforce System, I must support sending a large volume of emails, so that communication can be sent to a wide group of users based on defined criteria." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Send large-volume/mass emails by criteria, restricted to State Admins" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:Req_06_2_1> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:UserStory> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "Dynamically filter the available Coded Inserts list by the Email Template Group/Type; support tags including but not limited to <<applicationNumber>>, <<denialReason>>, <<holdReason>>, <<fee>>, <<paymentLink>>, <<firstName>>, <<lastName>>, <<accountLogin>>; parse tags at generation time and replace with actual record data; let the admin define the merge order of name fields; allow saving template-structure changes." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:Fdd06Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Strong match for insertion/parsing/replacement/save (Op_GetAvailableVariables' per-event-type variable-family list is exactly the dynamically-filtered-by-Group/Type mechanism this story describes; TP_VariableResolution's resolver-registry design is the parse-and-replace mechanism). The 'admin defines merge order' criterion is NOT separately modeled — see the coverage-gap Annotation shared with Req_06_2_2 below, which describes the identical gap more specifically." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "6.2.1" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:Op_CreateTemplateVersion> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:Op_GetAvailableVariables> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:Rule_EventPayloadStructureAndVariableResolution> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:TP_VariableResolution> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:TemplateVariable> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a MiEdWorkforce System Admin, I want to insert coded data fields (e.g. <<applicationNumber>>, <<denialReason>>) into email templates so that the generated emails contain specific, relevant details for the recipient." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Insert coded data-field variables into templates" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:Req_06_2_2> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:UserStory> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "Utilize existing database records to populate recipient information; let the Admin define merge order for name fields (Prefix, First Name, Last Name, Suffix); ensure merged data corresponds accurately to the specific recipient entity (e.g. District Code, District Name); support merging data across functional areas (Staffing, Credentialing) where required." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:Fdd06Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Cross-functional-area merging is well matched (TP_VariableResolution's resolver-registry pattern is explicitly per-event-type, and event types span every functional area). The field-ORDER configuration itself (an admin-settable sequence, not just which fields exist) has no modeled counterpart — comm:TemplateVariable 'only captures a placeholder's name/mandatory flag' per communications-api.ttl's own file-header note, not an order. See the shared coverage-gap Annotation below." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "6.2.2" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:TP_VariableResolution> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a MiEdWorkforce System Admin, I want to define the order of database fields merged into email templates so that recipient names and details are formatted correctly." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Define database-field merge order for template variables" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:Req_06_2_3> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:UserStory> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "Identify specific action items associated with the user's current status/application; merge action-item details (e.g. missing documents, required verifications) directly into the email template; ensure the action-item details included match what's displayed to the user in the system interface." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:Fdd06Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Plausible but not confirmed exact match: TP_VariableResolution's worked example variable families (Applicant, Certificate, Application, Approver) don't explicitly name an 'action item' family the way this story implies; the consistency criterion ('matches what's displayed to the user') is architecturally supported by Rule_EventPayloadStructureAndVariableResolution's single-resolver-per-event-type design (one source of truth for formatting) but not independently confirmed against any specific action-item data source. Not raised as its own Annotation — a plausible extension of the existing resolver pattern, not a demonstrated absence." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "6.2.3" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:Rule_TemplateVariableMandatoryResolution> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:TP_VariableResolution> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As the MiEdWorkforce System, I need to include details of action items when merging database fields into an email template." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Merge action-item details into templates" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:Req_06_3_1> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:UserStory> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "Provide a search interface to filter templates by Template Name, Group, or Status; allow editing Template Title, Description, Version, Effective Date, Urgency, and Frequency; restrict modification/deletion to System Administrators assigned to the specific Functional Area (e.g. a Staffing Admin cannot edit Credentialing templates)." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:Fdd06Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Functional-area isolation is a strong, direct match (comm:EmailTemplateAggregate's own invariants plus the functional-area-scoped Permission alternatives on every Template operation in communications-api.ttl). The specific Title/Group/Status search-FILTER parameters aren't independently asserted on comm:Op_ListTemplates (sd:parameters is unset there) — a minor documentation gap, not raised separately. 'Urgency'/'Frequency' as editable template fields also have no direct counterpart on comm:TemplateVersion/comm:EmailTemplateAggregate beyond the general template-metadata shape — folded into this same minor-gap note rather than a separate Annotation." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "6.3.1" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:EmailTemplateAggregate> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:Op_DeleteTemplate> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:Op_ListTemplates> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:Op_UpdateTemplate> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a MiEdWorkforce System Admin, I want to search for and modify email templates within my functional area so that I can maintain the standard communication content used by the system." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Search and modify templates within functional area" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:Req_06_3_2> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:UserStory> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "Provide a rich text editor for the Message Body supporting Bold, Italics, Lists, Cut, Copy, Paste; support HTML input for advanced formatting; allow insertion of Images (e.g. MDE/CEPI letterheads); restrict font selection to a pre-defined set of ADA-compliant system fonts." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:Fdd06Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "ARCHITECTURE CONTRADICTION, not a simple partial match: communications-technical-design.ttl's comm:TP_TemplateStorageAndEditing explicitly documents that template content authoring uses MARKDOWN with a narrow server-controlled extension allowlist (:::alert{}, :::button{}) and explicitly states raw HTML input and a WYSIWYG editor were BOTH considered and REJECTED ('for XSS complexity and noisy version diffs'), with 'raw HTML blocks, custom CSS/JS... all disallowed.' This story's own acceptance criteria ask for exactly what was rejected: an HTML-capable rich text editor, image insertion (for letterheads), and font-selection UI — none of which the Markdown-plus-allowlist design supports. See Question_TemplateEditorArchitectureContradiction below; this is a live, unresolved discrepancy between this FDD and the technical design, not folded silently into either." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "6.3.2" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:TP_TemplateStorageAndEditing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a MiEdWorkforce System Admin, I want a rich text editor for the email body that supports standard formatting and images while enforcing ADA-compliant font standards so that I can create professional, accessible communications." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Rich text/HTML editor with image insertion and ADA font restriction" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:Req_06_3_3> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:UserStory> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "On saving a new or modified template, check for existing templates with the same Title or Subject within the same Group; if a duplicate is detected, prevent the save and display an error message." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:Fdd06Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Business-Specifications-level duplicate-validation intent is present ('Validating for duplicate email templates'), but the PRECISE definition of 'duplicate' this story specifies (same Title OR Subject within the same Group) is exactly what communications-capability.ttl's own comm:Question_TemplateDuplicateDefinition (Open Question #5, already on record) flags as unresolved — reused here rather than re-raised as a new Annotation, since this story doesn't resolve that open question, it just restates one candidate definition among the ones still under discussion." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "6.3.3" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:EmailTemplateAggregate> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:Op_CreateTemplate> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:Op_CreateTemplateVersion> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a MiEdWorkforce System Admin, I want the system to validate email templates for duplication upon saving so that redundant templates are not created." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Validate templates for duplication on save" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:Req_06_3_4> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:UserStory> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "Capture and display Modified Date and Modified By for each template version; store Version Begin Date and Version End Date for each version; make these details viewable in a Template History/Audit log." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:Fdd06Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Strong match: the exact field set requested (Modified Date/By, Version Begin/End) is the field set communications-capability.ttl's own Business Rules/Aggregate design already documents for this purpose, and adt:AuditContext subscribes to both EmailTemplateCreatedEvent and EmailTemplateActivatedEvent (not EmailTemplateVersionCreatedEvent, which communications-capability.ttl's own file header already notes has no documented consumers anywhere — a pre-existing, not newly found, gap)." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "6.3.4" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:EmailTemplateActivatedEvent> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:EmailTemplateCreatedEvent> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:EmailTemplateVersionCreatedEvent> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:TemplateVersion> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a MiEdWorkforce System Admin, I want to view audit details for email templates so that I can trace who modified a template and when it was active." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "View template audit details" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:Req_06_4_1> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:UserStory> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "Provide text-entry capability for comments within defined user workflows; allow saving narrative text to flag items requiring attention; associate the entered comment with the specific record/transaction being processed." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:Fdd06Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Good general match. The story's own example, 'Rapbacks', is FDD 30 (Data Collection & Compliance area) — not yet converted anywhere in mied-v3 (see STATUS.md's 'not yet done' list) — so comm:CommentAggregate's invariant enumerating valid process-item types (CredentialApplication, StaffingRecord, EPPEnrollment) doesn't yet include a Rapback-shaped process item; not itself a Communications-side gap (the generic Comment mechanism is domain-item-agnostic), just downstream of Rapbacks itself not existing yet. Not raised as a separate Annotation here since it's really an FDD-30-side gap, not a Communications one." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "6.4.1" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:CommentAggregate> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:Op_CreateComment> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a MiEdWorkforce Admin/Business User, I want to enter comments within various workflows (e.g. Rapbacks) so that I can flag items or provide specific context for the record." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Enter comments within workflows" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:Req_06_4_2> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:UserStory> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "Provide an input field specifically labeled for \"Internal Remarks\"; restrict display of \"Internal\" comments to authorized internal users only." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:Fdd06Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Direct match, corroborated by comm:Wireframe1/Wireframe2's own explicit, separately-labeled 'Internal Remarks' field." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "6.4.2" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:CommentAggregate> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:Op_CreateComment> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:Perm_CommentsCreateInternal> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:Perm_CommentsViewInternal> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a MiEdWorkforce Admin/Business User, I want to mark comments as \"Internal\" so that the remarks are visible only to authenticated internal users and hidden from the applicant." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Mark comments as Internal" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:Req_06_4_3> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:UserStory> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "Allow the user to enter \"External Remarks\" (comments intended for the applicant); provide an option (e.g. \"Send Email\" button/checkbox) to include these remarks in a notification to the user; allow sending external remarks independent of a status change if configured for that workflow." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:Fdd06Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Excellent match — this story is essentially a restatement of comm:Rule_ExternalCommentInclusionRequiresSelection's own worked example almost verbatim (explicit selection required, never automatic inclusion). Directly corroborated by comm:Wireframe1's 'Send Email?' checkbox next to the Application Remarks (external) field, and by Emails and Remarks.docx's own narrative of the Hold-action flow (template selected for application remarks, optionally also sent as an email, with a separate mandatory internal remark on the same screen)." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "6.4.3" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:Op_CreateComment> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:Op_SendManualEmail> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:Perm_CommentsCreateExternal> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:Rule_ExternalCommentInclusionRequiresSelection> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a MiEdWorkforce Admin/Business User, I want to enter remarks and email, so that I can provide specific instructions or feedback to the applicant." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Enter external remarks and email them to the applicant" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:Req_06_4_4> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:UserStory> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "Display a \"Remarks History\"/\"Action History\" table with columns: Action, Status, Email Sent (Yes/No), Modified By, Modified On; preserve the text of remarks entered at the time of the action in the history log." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:Fdd06Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Exact wireframe match: comm:Wireframe1 (and its MOECS/Comment-Logs/Emails-and-Remarks source screenshots, 4 of which were independently viewed) all show precisely this Action/Status/Email Sent/Modified By/Modified On column set. comm:CommentEmailHistory's own description ('tracking of which sent emails included a given comment') is the exact backing entity for the 'Email Sent (Yes/No)' column specifically." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "6.4.4" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:CommentEmailHistory> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:Op_ListComments> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a MiEdWorkforce Admin, I want to view a history of remarks and actions on a record so that I can track who modified the record and if an email was sent to the user." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "View remarks/action history" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:Req_06_5_1> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:UserStory> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "Integrate historical communication data directly with the reporting platform; make historical communication logs available for trend analysis; ensure integrated data includes key details such as date and type of communication." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:Fdd06Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Partial satisfaction — see the coverage-gap Annotation shared with 6.5.2/6.5.3 below: communications-capability.ttl asserts rpt:ReportingContext sd:subscribesTo only ONE event (comm:EmailTemplateCreatedEvent), not any of the actual send/delivery events (EmailSent, EmailDelivered, EmailBounced, etc.) that would carry 'communication trends and volumes' data. The domain-model data this story needs to see in Reporting (comm:EmailInstanceAggregate's own history) exists; the asserted event-subscription pipeline into Reporting does not cover it." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "6.5.1" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:EmailInstanceAggregate> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:Perm_ReportsView> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As the MiEdWorkforce System, I want historical communication data to be integrated with the reporting platform, so that communication trends and volumes can be analyzed." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Integrate historical communication data with the reporting platform" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:Req_06_5_2> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:UserStory> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "Display the aggregate number of emails sent; identify the specific users who received reminder notifications; present this data to satisfy audit/business review requirements; allow the Admin to view details on 'who needed reminders' as part of the report data." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:Fdd06Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Comment 814829069 on the primary FDD ('This view would display the appropriate information necessary to observe how many emails were sent and who received reminders') is a near-verbatim restatement of this story's own acceptance criteria, confirming reviewer intent lines up with the written text — not a new finding, just corroboration. Same underlying gap as 6.5.1/6.5.3: the reporting-platform-facing data pipeline (event subscriptions into rpt:ReportingContext) doesn't yet carry EmailSent-level data, only template-creation events. comm:Perm_ReportsView's own description ('Send counts, frequency, trigger analysis') is aspirationally the right permission but has no backing operation/sequence exposing that aggregation." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "6.5.2" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:EmailInstanceAggregate> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:Perm_ReportsView> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a System Admin, I want the reporting platform to display data on how many emails were sent and who received reminders, so that I can satisfy audit and business review requirements." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Reporting platform shows email-sent counts and reminder recipients" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:Req_06_5_3> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:UserStory> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "Integrate historical alerts and notifications, in addition to emails, with the reporting framework; ensure the integration supports audit and business needs; include relevant audit details (Modified By, Modified On) within the integrated data." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:Fdd06Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Weakest of the three Reports stories: communications-capability.ttl asserts NO rpt:ReportingContext subscription to ANY Alert-related event (comm:DashboardAlertCreatedEvent/comm:DashboardAlertResolvedEvent are both subscribed only by adt:AuditContext) — Alerts have literally zero modeled path into Reporting, compared to Emails' one narrow (template-creation-only) path. See the shared coverage-gap Annotation below." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "6.5.3" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:AlertAggregate> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As the MiEdWorkforce System, I need to integrate historical alerts and notifications with the reporting framework, so that I can support comprehensive business analysis." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Integrate historical alerts and notifications with the reporting framework" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:Req_06_BizSpec_AlertAdmin> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Requirement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "Per HLS rows 8-11 (Ref 3): System Admin can search for existing defined alerts by functional area; create defined alerts with versioning control by functional area; modify defined alerts with versioning control; remove defined alerts with versioning control — each independently available on-demand or scheduled." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:Fdd06Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Partial satisfaction only, and this is the real point of modeling this synthetic requirement: the EVENT-TRIGGERED alert-instance path (an alert created automatically and shown to a targeted user, then resolved) is well modeled (comm:Seq_DashboardAlertCreationAndDisplay, comm:Seq_UserResolvesDashboardAlert), but the ADMIN-FACING alert-DEFINITION lifecycle this requirement actually describes — search existing alert definitions, modify a definition, remove a definition, versioning control over definitions, on-demand-vs-scheduled GENERATION of alerts (as opposed to instance targeting) — has no API counterpart: communications-api.ttl's only Alert operations are comm:Op_ListAlerts (lists a CALLING USER's own alert INSTANCES, not searchable alert DEFINITIONS), comm:Op_CreateAlert (creates one instance targeted at explicit user IDs, no versioning, no Group/Title/Description/Coded-Inserts authoring fields), and comm:Op_ResolveAlert. No Op_UpdateAlert, Op_DeleteAlert, Op_SearchAlertDefinitions, or Op_ListAlertDefinitions exists anywhere. See the coverage-gap Annotation below." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "6.BizSpec.Alerts" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:AlertAggregate> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:Op_CreateAlert> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:Op_ListAlerts> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "(No user-story stem given — this is Business Specifications prose, never promoted to its own Addendum feature number, unlike every other capability area in this FDD.) MiEdWorkforce System Administrators, by functional area, will be able to create, modify, and remove defined alerts with versioning control. Alerts may be informational or configured as Action Items requiring user resolution. Create new alert templates (Group: Staffing/Credentialing/EPP/Professional Learning; Alert Title; Alert Message; Alert Description; Coded Inserts; Start/End Dates; on-demand or scheduled). Search for existing alerts. Modify existing alerts (on-demand or scheduled). Remove existing alerts (on-demand or scheduled)." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Full alert-definition admin lifecycle (create/search/modify/remove, versioning, on-demand vs. scheduled)" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:Req_06_Interface_Outlook> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Requirement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "Per the Interface Design document: application-registration-plus-RBAC authentication to Microsoft Graph; HTTPS POST to the Graph sendMail endpoint; supports To/CC/BCC recipients, attachments, and a message body; PROD and UAT (Testing) environments; internal data classification (no PII, since email is not considered a private communication channel)." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:Fdd06InterfaceOutlookDoc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "No satisfiedBy: this is a wholly separate integration from ext:SendGridSystem (the only outbound email channel modeled anywhere in communications-capability.ttl/communications-api.ttl), used for genuinely two-way correspondence from dedicated mailboxes rather than one-way system-generated notifications. Nothing in comm:'s domain model, API, or sequences references Microsoft 365/Graph/Outlook at all. See Question_OutlookTwoWayChannelUnmodeled below for the additional contradiction this raises against the primary FDD's own Business Specifications text." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "6.Interface.Outlook" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "(Drawn from 'Interface Design document - Microsoft 365 (Outlook).docx', a supplementary interface-design document in this FDD's own folder, not a numbered Addendum story.) MiEdWorkforce can send emails from dedicated email addresses intended for two-way communication, as opposed to alerts or notifications — using the Microsoft Graph API (POST https://graph.microsoft.com/v1.0/me/sendMail) rather than direct SMTP." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Two-way email via Microsoft 365 / Outlook Graph API" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:Rule_EmailResendAvailabilityWindow> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:BusinessRule> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:appliesTo> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:EmailInstanceAggregate> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:CapabilityDoc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:enforcedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:EmailInstanceAggregate> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:enforcedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:Op_ResendEmail> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:example> "Email sent January 1, 2026; content retention policy 90 days; user can resend through March 31, 2026; after April 1, 2026 content is purged and the resend button is disabled, though audit metadata (sent date, recipient, status) remains visible." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:rationale> "Prevents brittle and error-prone reconstruction of historical email content after variable data sources may have changed or been deleted." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "Email resend functionality is only available while the email content exists in hot storage (typically 90 days). After content archival, resend is disabled." .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:Rule_EventPayloadStructureAndVariableResolution> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:BusinessRule> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:appliesTo> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:EmailTemplateAggregate> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:CapabilityDoc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:enforcedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:Seq_EventTriggeredEmailSend> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:example> "CredentialApplicationApproved event payload carries only {event_type, application_id, approved_by_user_id, approved_at}. Template uses <<ApplicantName>>, <<CertificateType>>, <<ApprovalDate>>. The event-type-specific resolver fetches the applicant record via application_id, formats the name as \"FirstName LastName\", the certificate type as \"Elementary Education\" (not \"elem_ed\"), and the date as \"January 15, 2026\" (not the ISO timestamp)." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Source names the enforcing components as \"Event schema definitions + Variable Resolver registry\" — sd:enforcedBy points at comm:Seq_EventTriggeredEmailSend since sd:TechnicalProcess is outside enforcedBy's range; see comm:TP_VariableResolution (sd:references) in communications-technical-design.ttl for the resolver registry's own design." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:rationale> "Keeps events lightweight and focused on core information; prevents event payload bloat with denormalized data; centralizes formatting logic in resolvers rather than event publishers; ensures consistent user-facing formatting across all templates." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:references> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:TP_VariableResolution> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "Domain events that trigger emails must carry minimal, intrinsic payload data (primarily IDs and essential context). Variable resolution is handled by event-type-specific resolvers that fetch and format additional data as needed. All resolved values are user-facing formatted strings — dates as \"January 15, 2026\", names as \"First Last\", credential/certificate types as human-readable display names, never raw codes/ISO timestamps." .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:Rule_ExternalCommentInclusionRequiresSelection> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:BusinessRule> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:appliesTo> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:CommentAggregate> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:CapabilityDoc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:enforcedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:CommentAggregate> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:enforcedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:Op_SendManualEmail> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:example> "Credential application has 3 external comments. Processor composes a denial email; the UI presents a checklist of external comments; the processor selects 2 of 3; only the selected 2 comments appear in the email body." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Source names the enforcing components as \"Comment Service + Email Send Orchestrator\" — modeled via comm:CommentAggregate plus comm:Op_SendManualEmail/comm:Seq_ManualEmailSendWithCustomization (the actual send-time integration point named by the Include Comments in Outbound Email sequence referenced in communications-capability.md, which is otherwise not separately promoted to its own sd:Sequence instance in communications-sequences.ttl since communications-sequences.md itself doesn't include a matching diagram for it)." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:rationale> "Prevents accidental disclosure of sensitive information or draft comments not intended for external recipients." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "External comments are eligible for inclusion in outbound emails but are NOT automatically included. The user must explicitly select which external comments to include." .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:Rule_RecipientEmailUpdateDetection> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:BusinessRule> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:appliesTo> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:EmailInstanceAggregate> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:CapabilityDoc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:enforcedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:Op_ResendEmail> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:enforcedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:Seq_EmailResendWithRecipientOverride> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:example> "Original email sent to user_123 at old@example.com on January 1; the email bounces (invalid address); the user updates their email in the identity system to new@example.com on January 5; an admin initiates a resend on January 10; the UI pre-fills old@example.com (the original) but shows a hint: \"Replace with user's current address: new@example.com\"; the admin can accept the suggestion or manually override." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Source names the enforcing components as \"Resend Service + Identity API integration\" — modeled via comm:Op_ResendEmail/comm:Seq_EmailResendWithRecipientOverride, the concrete operation and sequence where this detection happens (calling iam:Op_GetUser, a cross-domain stub declared below)." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:rationale> "Improves user experience by nudging administrators to use current contact information, especially useful for bounced emails or help desk escalations." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "When resending an email, the system should detect if the recipient user's email address has been updated in the identity system since the original send, and surface this as a suggested recipient override." .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:Rule_RenderedContentStorageOnly> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:BusinessRule> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:appliesTo> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:EmailInstanceAggregate> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:CapabilityDoc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:enforcedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:EmailInstanceAggregate> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:enforcedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:Seq_EventTriggeredEmailSend> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:example> "Template content: \"Dear <<ApplicantName>>, your application for <<CertificateType>> has been approved.\" Event provides application_id: 12345. Resolver produces ApplicantName = \"Jane Doe\", CertificateType = \"Elementary Education\". Stored in EmailInstance: \"Dear Jane Doe, your application for Elementary Education has been approved.\" NOT stored: the original template text, the event payload, or the variable mappings. Implication: resending replays the exact rendered content from the original send; it cannot \"re-render\" with updated data — a new email must be sent for that." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Source names the enforcing components as \"EmailInstance aggregate + Email Send Orchestrator\" — the orchestrator isn't separately modeled as its own sd:TechnicalProcess/ApiOperation node, so sd:enforcedBy points at the sequence where the store-rendered-content-only step actually occurs." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:rationale> "Audit requirements focus on \"what was sent\" not \"how it was constructed\"; simplifies resend (just retransmit the stored content); reduces storage footprint (no need to persist event payloads); prevents confusion about what version of data was used at send time." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "EmailInstance records store ONLY the fully rendered email content (subject and body with all variables replaced). The original event payload, template structure, and variable placeholders are NOT stored." .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:Rule_SingleActiveTemplateVersion> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:BusinessRule> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:appliesTo> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:EmailTemplateAggregate> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:CapabilityDoc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:enforcedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:EmailTemplateAggregate> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:enforcedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:Op_ActivateTemplateVersion> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:enforcedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:Seq_TemplateVersionUpdateAndActivation> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:example> "Template \"Credential Approved\" has v1.0 (active) and v1.1 (draft). Admin activates v1.1. The system automatically sets v1.0 to inactive, v1.1 to active. Future sends use v1.1; historical sends still reference v1.0." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "See Question_TemplateVersionRestoration below — whether a deactivated version can later be restored/reactivated is unconfirmed." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:rationale> "Prevents ambiguity about which template content to use when an event triggers a notification." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "Only one version of a template can be marked as \"current/active\" at any given time. Activating a new version automatically deactivates the previous current version." .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:Rule_TemplateVariableMandatoryResolution> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:BusinessRule> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:appliesTo> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:EmailTemplateAggregate> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:CapabilityDoc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:enforcedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:EmailTemplateAggregate> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:enforcedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:Seq_EventTriggeredEmailSend> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:example> "Template contains <<ApplicantName>> (mandatory). Event CredentialApplicationApproved includes application_id: 12345. The variable resolver for this event type queries the Applications table but the applicant record is missing. Send is blocked; the event moves to DLQ; the admin is alerted; the template remains active but flagged." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Source names the enforcing components as \"Event-type-specific Variable Resolver component + Event Processing Service\" — modeled here via the EmailTemplateAggregate invariant plus comm:Seq_EventTriggeredEmailSend (the sequence where the mandatory-variable check actually happens), since sd:enforcedBy's range excludes sd:TechnicalProcess; see communications-technical-design.ttl's comm:TP_VariableResolution (sd:references) for the resolver's own implementation detail. See Question_TemplateVariableFailureHandling below for this rule's own open questions." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:rationale> "Prevents sending incomplete or misleading communications (e.g. \"Your application for <<CertificateType>>\" where CertificateType is null) while giving administrators tools to diagnose and resolve the issue." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:references> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:TP_VariableResolution> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "If a template variable is marked as mandatory and cannot be resolved from available data sources, the notification send must be blocked and the event must be moved to a processing queue for manual intervention. Failed-resolution handling: (1) send blocked, error logged with full context (template_id, version_id, event_id, missing variable names); (2) event moved to Dead Letter Queue with retry metadata; (3) dashboard alert created for the template owner; (4) manual recovery options — fix the template, trigger a manual retry, export events to CSV, or after 7 days in DLQ the event is archived and marked permanently failed. Prevention: template validation on save (variables must exist in the event type's available-variables list), an activation gate that test-resolves against sample event data, and UI warnings showing which variables are mandatory." .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:Seq_DashboardAlertCreationAndDisplay> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Sequence> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:belongsToContext> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:CommunicationsContext> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:content> "sequenceDiagram\n    participant Domain as Domain Service\n    participant EventBus\n    participant Comms as Communications Service\n    participant AlertRepo as Alert Repository\n    participant Dashboard as Dashboard UI\n    participant User\n\n    Domain--)EventBus: Publish event (e.g., DataQualityIssueDetected)\n    EventBus->>Comms: Event received\n\n    Comms->>Comms: Check alert template for event type\n    Comms->>Comms: Evaluate alert targeting rules\n    Note over Comms: Target: Users with role<br/>\"District Data Steward\"<br/>at District XYZ\n\n    Comms->>Comms: Resolve alert content variables\n    Note over Comms: Alert: \"You have 5 data quality<br/>issues requiring attention\"\n\n    Comms->>AlertRepo: Create Alert instances\n    Note over AlertRepo: One alert per targeted user<br/>Status: Active<br/>Expires: 30 days from now\n    AlertRepo-->>Comms: alert_ids[]\n\n    Comms--)EventBus: DashboardAlertCreated {alert_id, user_id}\n\n    Note over User,Dashboard: User logs in\n\n    User->>Dashboard: Access dashboard\n    Dashboard->>Comms: GET /api/communications/alerts?user_id={id}&status=Active\n\n    Comms->>Comms: Validate user permissions\n    Comms->>AlertRepo: Query active alerts for user\n    Note over AlertRepo: SELECT * FROM alerts<br/>WHERE user_id = {id}<br/>AND status = 'Active'<br/>AND (expiration_date IS NULL<br/>  OR expiration_date > NOW())\n    AlertRepo-->>Comms: List of alerts\n\n    Comms-->>Dashboard: Alerts with action links\n    Dashboard-->>User: Display alert banner/widget\n    Note over User: Alert: \"5 data quality issues<br/>require your attention\"<br/>[View Issues]\n\n    User->>Dashboard: Click alert action link\n    Dashboard->>User: Navigate to target page (e.g., data quality dashboard)\n" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:SequencesDoc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:errorScenarios> "No users match targeting rules > alert template misconfigured, log warning. User lacks access to action link > display alert but disable link." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:eventsPublished> "DashboardAlertCreated - Per user who received the alert." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:initiatedBy> "internal-system" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:keyDecisions> "Role-based targeting: alerts sent to users with specific roles at specific scopes. Automatic expiration: alerts expire after a configured period (default 30 days). Action links: each alert includes a deep link to the relevant page. One alert per user: system creates individual alert instances (not shared)." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "confirmed" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Dashboard Alert Creation and Display" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:whatWhenWho> "What: System creates dashboard alert for user. When: Important action required (e.g., pending authorization, data quality issue). Who: System (automated)." .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:Seq_EmailHistorySearchAndDetailsView> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Sequence> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:belongsToContext> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:CommunicationsContext> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:content> "sequenceDiagram\n    actor User\n    participant UI\n    participant Comms as Communications Service\n    participant InstanceRepo as EmailInstance Repository\n    participant Identity\n\n    User->>UI: Navigate to Email History\n    UI->>Comms: GET /api/communications/email-history?functional_area=Credentialing&page=1\n\n    Comms->>Comms: Validate permissions (functional area scoped)\n    Note over Comms: Checks: communications.credentials-emails.view-history\n\n    Comms->>InstanceRepo: Query EmailInstances\n    Note over InstanceRepo: SELECT * FROM email_instances<br/>WHERE functional_area='Credentialing'<br/>ORDER BY sent_at DESC<br/>LIMIT 50\n    InstanceRepo-->>Comms: List of instances (metadata only)\n\n    Comms-->>UI: Email list (sent_at, recipient, subject, status)\n    UI-->>User: Display searchable table\n\n    Note over User,UI: User applies filters\n\n    User->>UI: Filter by recipient, date range, status\n    UI->>Comms: GET /api/communications/email-history?recipient=jane@example.com&status=Bounced\n    Comms->>InstanceRepo: Query with filters\n    InstanceRepo-->>Comms: Filtered results\n    Comms-->>UI: Updated list\n\n    User->>UI: Click email to view details\n    UI->>Comms: GET /api/communications/email-history/{instance_id}\n\n    Comms->>Comms: Validate permissions\n    Comms->>InstanceRepo: Get EmailInstance with full content\n    InstanceRepo-->>Comms: Complete instance\n    Note over InstanceRepo: Includes:<br/>- Rendered subject/body<br/>- Delivery events timeline<br/>- Template version used<br/>- Sent by user (if manual)\n\n    alt Email content archived\n        Comms-->>UI: Instance metadata only (content unavailable)\n        Note over UI: Display: \"Email content archived<br/>(retention period expired)\"\n    else Content available\n        Comms-->>UI: Full instance details\n        UI-->>User: Display email preview, metadata, delivery timeline\n    end\n" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:SequencesDoc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:errorScenarios> "Insufficient permissions > 403 Forbidden. Instance not found > 404 Not Found. Content archived but audit metadata available > display limited info." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:eventsPublished> "None." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:initiatedBy> "user" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:keyDecisions> "Functional area scoping: user only sees emails for their permitted functional areas. Pagination: default 50 results per page. Metadata vs content: list view shows metadata, detail view fetches full content. Content availability: UI indicates if content has been archived." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "confirmed" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Email History Search and Details View" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:whatWhenWho> "What: User searches sent emails and views full details. When: Help desk troubleshooting, user inquiry, audit review. Who: Credentialing Administrator, Help Desk Staff, System Administrator." .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:Seq_EmailResendWithRecipientOverride> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Sequence> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:belongsToContext> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:CommunicationsContext> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:content> "sequenceDiagram\n    actor User\n    participant UI\n    participant Comms as Communications Service\n    participant InstanceRepo as EmailInstance Repository\n    participant Identity\n    participant SendGrid\n    participant EventBus\n\n    User->>UI: View email details (from history)\n    UI->>Comms: GET /api/communications/email-history/{instance_id}\n    Comms->>InstanceRepo: Get EmailInstance\n    InstanceRepo-->>Comms: Instance details\n\n    alt Email content archived\n        Comms-->>UI: Content unavailable (archived)\n        Note over UI: Resend button disabled<br/>\"Content retention period expired\"\n    else Content available\n        Comms-->>UI: Full instance with content\n        UI-->>User: Display email with \"Resend\" button enabled\n\n        User->>UI: Click \"Resend\"\n        UI->>Comms: GET /api/communications/email-history/{instance_id}/resend-context\n\n        Comms->>Comms: Validate resend permissions\n        Comms->>InstanceRepo: Get original recipient user reference\n        InstanceRepo-->>Comms: Original recipient (user_id, email)\n\n        alt Recipient has user_id reference\n            Comms->>Identity: GET /api/identity/users/{user_id}\n            Identity-->>Comms: Current user email\n\n            alt Email updated since original send\n                Comms-->>UI: Resend form with hint\n                Note over UI: Pre-filled: old@example.com<br/>Hint: \"Replace with current:<br/>new@example.com\"\n            else Email unchanged\n                Comms-->>UI: Resend form (original email)\n            end\n        else No user reference (external recipient)\n            Comms-->>UI: Resend form (original email only)\n        end\n\n        User->>UI: Modify recipient email (or accept default)\n        User->>UI: Click \"Send\"\n\n        UI->>Comms: POST /api/communications/email-history/{instance_id}/resend\n        Note over UI: Request: {recipient_email, cc_emails[]}\n\n        Comms->>Comms: Validate permissions\n        Comms->>InstanceRepo: Get original email content\n        InstanceRepo-->>Comms: Rendered subject/body\n\n        Comms->>SendGrid: POST /v3/mail/send\n        Note over SendGrid: Uses original rendered content<br/>(no re-resolution)\n        SendGrid-->>Comms: 202 Accepted (new message_id)\n\n        Comms->>InstanceRepo: Create new EmailInstance\n        Note over InstanceRepo: Links to original instance:<br/>resent_from_instance_id\n        InstanceRepo-->>Comms: new_instance_id\n\n        Comms--)EventBus: EmailResent {original_instance_id, new_instance_id}\n        Comms-->>UI: Success\n        UI-->>User: \"Email resent\" confirmation\n    end\n" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:SequencesDoc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:errorScenarios> "Content archived > 400 Bad Request \"Content no longer available\". Insufficient permissions > 403 Forbidden. SendGrid error > display error, allow retry." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:eventsPublished> "EmailResent - Links original and new instances." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:initiatedBy> "user" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:keyDecisions> "Content availability: resend only available during the retention period. Email update detection: system detects if the user's email changed in the identity system since original send. No re-resolution: resend uses the original rendered content (not re-rendered). New instance created: resend creates a new EmailInstance linked to the original." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "confirmed" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Email Resend with Recipient Override" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:whatWhenWho> "What: User resends a previously sent email to a new/corrected recipient. When: Email bounced, user provided an updated email, or help desk escalation. Who: Credentialing Administrator, Help Desk Staff." .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:Seq_EventTriggeredEmailSend> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Sequence> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:belongsToContext> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:CommunicationsContext> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:content> "sequenceDiagram\n    participant Domain as Domain Service\n    participant EventBus\n    participant Comms as Communications Service\n    participant TemplateRepo as Template Repository\n    participant Resolver as Variable Resolver\n    participant Identity\n    participant SendGrid\n    participant InstanceRepo as EmailInstance Repository\n\n    Domain--)EventBus: Publish event (e.g., CredentialApplicationApproved)\n    Note over EventBus: Event payload:<br/>{event_type, application_id, approved_at}\n\n    EventBus->>Comms: Event received\n    Comms->>Comms: Identify event type\n    Comms->>TemplateRepo: Get active template for event type\n    TemplateRepo-->>Comms: Template (with placeholders)\n\n    alt No active template for event type\n        Comms->>Comms: Log warning (no template configured)\n        Note over Comms: Silent failure - no email sent<br/>Alert admin if critical event\n    else Template found\n        Comms->>Resolver: Resolve variables for event type\n        Note over Resolver: Event-type-specific resolver:<br/>CredentialApplicationApprovedResolver\n\n        Resolver->>Domain: GET /api/credentials/applications/{id}\n        Domain-->>Resolver: Application data\n        Resolver->>Identity: GET /api/identity/users/{id}\n        Identity-->>Resolver: User data\n\n        Resolver->>Resolver: Format values to user-facing strings<br/>e.g., \"Jane Doe\", \"Elementary Education\"\n        Resolver-->>Comms: Resolved variables\n\n        alt Mandatory variable missing/null\n            Comms->>Comms: Block send, log error\n            Comms--)EventBus: EmailSendFailed\n            Note over Comms: Error: Mandatory variable unresolvable\n        else All variables resolved\n            Comms->>Comms: Render email (replace placeholders)\n            Note over Comms: Rendered content:<br/>\"Dear Jane Doe, your application<br/>for Elementary Education...\"\n\n            Comms->>Identity: Resolve recipient(s) from template config\n            Identity-->>Comms: Recipient email(s)\n\n            Comms->>SendGrid: POST /v3/mail/send\n            Note over SendGrid: Email queued for delivery\n            SendGrid-->>Comms: 202 Accepted (message_id)\n\n            Comms->>InstanceRepo: Store EmailInstance\n            Note over InstanceRepo: Stores ONLY rendered content<br/>NOT event payload or template structure\n            InstanceRepo-->>Comms: instance_id\n\n            Comms--)EventBus: EmailSent {instance_id, recipients, sent_at}\n        end\n    end\n" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:SequencesDoc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:errorScenarios> "No active template for event type > silent failure, log warning (alert admin if critical event). Mandatory variable null/missing > block send, publish EmailSendFailed. SendGrid API error > retry with exponential backoff (max 3 attempts)." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:eventsPublished> "EmailSent - Email successfully queued to SendGrid. EmailSendFailed - Variable resolution failed or SendGrid rejected." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:initiatedBy> "internal-system" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:keyDecisions> "Event payload: lightweight (IDs only), resolver fetches display data. Variable resolution: event-type-specific resolver handles formatting. Silent failure: no active template for the event type means no email is sent (prevents spam on misconfigured events) rather than an error. Rendered content only: EmailInstance stores the final output, not intermediate data." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "confirmed" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Event-Triggered Email Send" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:whatWhenWho> "What: Domain event triggers automatic email send using pre-configured template. When: Business event occurs (e.g., credential application approved, payment due). Who: System (automated)." .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:Seq_ManualEmailSendWithCustomization> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Sequence> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:belongsToContext> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:CommunicationsContext> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:content> "sequenceDiagram\n    actor User\n    participant UI\n    participant Comms as Communications Service\n    participant TemplateRepo as Template Repository\n    participant Resolver as Variable Resolver\n    participant Identity\n    participant SendGrid\n    participant InstanceRepo as EmailInstance Repository\n    participant EventBus\n\n    User->>UI: Navigate to \"Send Email\"\n    UI->>Comms: GET /api/communications/templates?functional_area=Credentialing\n    Comms->>TemplateRepo: Query active templates\n    TemplateRepo-->>Comms: List of templates\n    Comms-->>UI: Templates with event types\n\n    User->>UI: Select template (e.g., \"Application Approved\")\n    UI->>Comms: GET /api/communications/event-types/{event_type}/available-variables\n    Comms-->>UI: Available variables for event type\n    Note over UI: Displays variable picker:<br/><<ApplicantName>>, <<CertificateType>>, etc.\n\n    User->>UI: Enter context data (e.g., application_id)\n    UI->>Comms: POST /api/communications/preview\n    Note over UI: Request: {template_id, context: {application_id}}\n\n    Comms->>Resolver: Resolve variables using context\n    Resolver->>Identity: Fetch user data\n    Identity-->>Resolver: User details\n    Resolver-->>Comms: Resolved variables\n\n    Comms->>Comms: Render preview\n    Comms-->>UI: Preview HTML\n\n    User->>UI: Customize subject/body (optional)\n    User->>UI: Enter recipient email, click Send\n\n    UI->>Comms: POST /api/communications/send-manual\n    Note over UI: Request: {template_id, context,<br/>custom_subject, custom_body, recipient}\n\n    Comms->>Comms: Validate permissions\n    Comms->>Comms: Render final email (with customizations)\n\n    Comms->>SendGrid: POST /v3/mail/send\n    SendGrid-->>Comms: 202 Accepted (message_id)\n\n    Comms->>InstanceRepo: Store EmailInstance\n    Note over InstanceRepo: Stores rendered content<br/>with user customizations applied\n    InstanceRepo-->>Comms: instance_id\n\n    Comms--)EventBus: EmailSent {instance_id, sent_by_user_id}\n    Comms-->>UI: Success (instance_id)\n    UI-->>User: Email sent confirmation\n" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:SequencesDoc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:errorScenarios> "Insufficient permissions > 403 Forbidden. Invalid context data (e.g., application_id not found) > 400 Bad Request. SendGrid error > display error, allow retry." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:eventsPublished> "EmailSent - Includes sent_by_user_id for manual sends." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:initiatedBy> "user" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:keyDecisions> "Preview before send: user sees resolved content before sending. Customization scope: user can modify subject/body but NOT template variables. Permissions: requires communications.email.send-manual (and communications.email.customize when overriding subject/body). Audit trail: EmailInstance captures who sent it (sent_by_user_id)." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "confirmed" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Manual Email Send with Template Customization" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:whatWhenWho> "What: User composes and sends one-time email using a template as a starting point. When: User needs to send a custom communication (e.g., follow-up, clarification). Who: Credentialing Administrator, Help Desk Staff." .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:Seq_MassEmailWithConsolidation> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Sequence> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:belongsToContext> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:CommunicationsContext> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:content> "sequenceDiagram\n    participant DataQuality as Data Quality Service\n    participant EventBus\n    participant Comms as Communications Service\n    participant Consolidator as Event Consolidator\n    participant TemplateRepo as Template Repository\n    participant Resolver as Variable Resolver\n    participant SendGrid\n    participant InstanceRepo as EmailInstance Repository\n\n    loop Multiple events over time\n        DataQuality--)EventBus: DataQualityIssueDetected (issue_id: 101)\n        DataQuality--)EventBus: DataQualityIssueDetected (issue_id: 102)\n        DataQuality--)EventBus: DataQualityIssueDetected (issue_id: 103)\n    end\n\n    EventBus->>Comms: Events received\n    Comms->>Consolidator: Buffer events\n    Note over Consolidator: Consolidation window: 15 minutes<br/>Group by: recipient_user_id\n\n    Consolidator->>Consolidator: Wait for window to close\n    Note over Consolidator: Timer started on first event\n\n    Note over Consolidator: 15 minutes elapsed\n\n    Consolidator->>Consolidator: Group events by recipient\n    Note over Consolidator: User_123: [101, 102, 103]<br/>User_456: [104, 105]\n\n    loop For each recipient group\n        Consolidator->>TemplateRepo: Get consolidation template\n        Note over TemplateRepo: Template: \"Data Quality Issues Summary\"\n        TemplateRepo-->>Consolidator: Template\n\n        Consolidator->>Resolver: Resolve variables\n        Note over Resolver: <<IssueCount>>: \"3\"<br/><<IssueList>>: formatted list of issues\n\n        Resolver->>DataQuality: GET /api/data-quality/issues?ids=101,102,103\n        DataQuality-->>Resolver: Issue details\n\n        Resolver->>Resolver: Format as user-facing list\n        Note over Resolver: \"1. Missing certification date<br/>2. Invalid endorsement code<br/>3. Duplicate employee record\"\n\n        Resolver-->>Consolidator: Resolved variables\n\n        Consolidator->>Consolidator: Render email\n        Note over Consolidator: \"You have 3 data quality issues<br/>requiring your attention:<br/><br/>1. Missing certification date...\"\n\n        Consolidator->>SendGrid: POST /v3/mail/send\n        SendGrid-->>Consolidator: 202 Accepted\n\n        Consolidator->>InstanceRepo: Store EmailInstance\n        Note over InstanceRepo: Links to all source events:<br/>consolidated_event_ids: [101,102,103]\n        InstanceRepo-->>Consolidator: instance_id\n\n        Consolidator--)EventBus: EmailSent (consolidated: true)\n    end\n" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:SequencesDoc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:errorScenarios> "Consolidation window timeout > process buffered events even if incomplete. Template not found > fall back to individual emails per event." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:eventsPublished> "EmailSent with consolidated: true flag." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:initiatedBy> "internal-system" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:keyDecisions> "Consolidation window: 15 minutes default (configurable per event type). Grouping key: typically the recipient user, but can be customized. Special templates: consolidation templates support list variables. Event tracking: EmailInstance links to all consolidated event IDs." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "confirmed" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Mass Email with Consolidation" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:whatWhenWho> "What: System consolidates multiple related events into a single email. When: Multiple data quality issues detected for the same user within the consolidation window. Who: System (automated)." .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:Seq_SendGridWebhookStatusUpdate> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Sequence> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:belongsToContext> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:CommunicationsContext> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:content> "sequenceDiagram\n    participant SendGrid\n    participant Webhook as Webhook Endpoint\n    participant Validator as Signature Validator\n    participant Comms as Communications Service\n    participant InstanceRepo as EmailInstance Repository\n    participant EventBus\n\n    SendGrid->>Webhook: POST /api/webhooks/sendgrid\n    Note over SendGrid: Event: delivered, bounced, etc.<br/>Includes: message_id, timestamp, status\n\n    Webhook->>Validator: Validate HMAC signature\n    Note over Validator: Prevents spoofed events<br/>Uses shared secret from Key Vault\n\n    alt Invalid signature\n        Validator-->>Webhook: Signature mismatch\n        Webhook-->>SendGrid: 401 Unauthorized\n    else Valid signature\n        Validator-->>Webhook: Signature valid\n\n        Webhook->>Comms: Process delivery event\n        Comms->>Comms: Extract message_id, status, substatus\n        Comms->>InstanceRepo: Find EmailInstance by message_id\n\n        alt Instance not found\n            Comms->>Comms: Log warning (orphaned webhook)\n            Note over Comms: Possible race condition:<br/>webhook arrived before instance saved\n            Comms-->>Webhook: 200 OK (idempotent)\n        else Instance found\n            Comms->>InstanceRepo: Check for duplicate event\n            Note over InstanceRepo: Idempotency check:<br/>event_id already processed?\n\n            alt Duplicate event\n                Comms->>Comms: Log duplicate, skip processing\n                Comms-->>Webhook: 200 OK (already processed)\n            else New event\n                Comms->>InstanceRepo: Add EmailDeliveryEvent\n                Note over InstanceRepo: Event: {status, substatus,<br/>timestamp, raw_payload}\n\n                Comms->>InstanceRepo: Update instance delivery_status\n                InstanceRepo-->>Comms: Success\n\n                Comms--)EventBus: Publish appropriate event\n                Note over EventBus: EmailDelivered, EmailBounced,<br/>EmailDeferred, or EmailDropped\n\n                Comms-->>Webhook: 200 OK\n                Webhook-->>SendGrid: 200 OK\n            end\n        end\n    end\n" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:SequencesDoc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:errorScenarios> "Invalid signature > 401 Unauthorized (prevents processing). Instance not found > log warning, return 200 (idempotent). Duplicate event > return 200 (already processed)." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:eventsPublished> "EmailDelivered - Successful delivery. EmailBounced - Permanent failure (includes substatus). EmailDeferred - Temporary failure (will retry). EmailDropped - SendGrid rejected before sending." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:initiatedBy> "external-system" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:keyDecisions> "Signature validation: HMAC SHA256 prevents spoofed webhooks. Idempotency: duplicate events ignored (SendGrid may retry). Race condition handling: orphaned webhooks logged but accepted (200 OK, idempotent). Status mapping: SendGrid statuses mapped to domain events." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "confirmed" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "SendGrid Webhook - Delivery Status Update" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:whatWhenWho> "What: Process incoming delivery events from SendGrid. When: Email delivered, bounced, deferred, or dropped. Who: SendGrid (external system)." .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:Seq_TemplateVariableResolutionInternal> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Sequence> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:belongsToContext> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:CommunicationsContext> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:content> "sequenceDiagram\n    participant Comms as Communications Service\n    participant Resolver as CredentialApplicationApprovedResolver\n    participant CredAPI as Credentials API\n    participant IdentityAPI as Identity API\n    participant Cache\n\n    Comms->>Resolver: Resolve variables for event\n    Note over Comms: Event: CredentialApplicationApproved<br/>Context: {application_id: 12345}\n\n    Resolver->>Resolver: Parse template variables\n    Note over Resolver: Found: <<ApplicantName>>,<br/><<CertificateType>>, <<ApprovalDate>>\n\n    Resolver->>CredAPI: GET /api/credentials/applications/12345\n    CredAPI-->>Resolver: Application data\n    Note over Resolver: {applicant_id, certificate_type_code,<br/>approved_at, approved_by_id}\n\n    Resolver->>Cache: Check cache for applicant\n    Cache-->>Resolver: Cache miss\n\n    Resolver->>IdentityAPI: GET /api/identity/users/{applicant_id}\n    IdentityAPI-->>Resolver: User data\n    Note over Resolver: {first_name: \"Jane\", last_name: \"Doe\",<br/>email: \"jane.doe@example.com\"}\n\n    Resolver->>Cache: Store user data (TTL: 1 hour)\n\n    Resolver->>Resolver: Format values to user-facing strings\n    Note over Resolver: ApplicantName: \"Jane Doe\"<br/>(NOT \"janeDoe\" or \"JANE DOE\")<br/><br/>CertificateType: \"Elementary Education\"<br/>(NOT \"elem_ed\" or \"ELEM_ED\")<br/><br/>ApprovalDate: \"January 15, 2026\"<br/>(NOT \"2026-01-15T10:30:00Z\")\n\n    Resolver-->>Comms: Resolved variables map\n    Note over Comms: {<br/>  \"ApplicantName\": \"Jane Doe\",<br/>  \"CertificateType\": \"Elementary Education\",<br/>  \"ApprovalDate\": \"January 15, 2026\"<br/>}\n\n    Comms->>Comms: Replace placeholders in template\n    Note over Comms: Original:<br/>\"Dear <<ApplicantName>>, your<br/>application for <<CertificateType>>...\"<br/><br/>Rendered:<br/>\"Dear Jane Doe, your application<br/>for Elementary Education...\"\n" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:SequencesDoc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:errorScenarios> "API unavailable > retry with exponential backoff. Mandatory variable null > throw exception, block send. Invalid data format > log error, use fallback value if available." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:eventsPublished> "None (internal process)." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:initiatedBy> "internal-system" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:keyDecisions> "Event-type-specific resolvers: each event type has a dedicated resolver class. Lightweight events: event carries only IDs, resolver fetches display data. User-facing formatting: all values formatted for human readability. Caching: frequently accessed data (user profiles) cached for 1 hour. Batch API calls: resolver batches requests when resolving multiple variables from the same source." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "confirmed" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Template Variable Resolution (Internal)" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:whatWhenWho> "What: Event-type-specific resolver fetches and formats data for template variables. When: Email send triggered (event-driven or manual). Who: Variable Resolver (internal component)." .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:Seq_TemplateVersionUpdateAndActivation> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Sequence> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:belongsToContext> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:CommunicationsContext> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:content> "sequenceDiagram\n    actor Admin\n    participant UI\n    participant Comms as Communications Service\n    participant TemplateRepo as Template Repository\n    participant EventBus\n\n    Admin->>UI: Navigate to Template Management\n    UI->>Comms: GET /api/communications/templates/{template_id}\n    Comms->>TemplateRepo: Get template with all versions\n    TemplateRepo-->>Comms: Template + versions\n    Comms-->>UI: Template details\n\n    Admin->>UI: Click \"Create New Version\"\n    UI->>Comms: GET /api/communications/event-types/{event_type}/available-variables\n    Comms-->>UI: Available variables for this template's event type\n    Note over UI: Variable picker shows only<br/>context-appropriate variables\n\n    Admin->>UI: Edit subject/body, insert variables\n    Admin->>UI: Save as Draft\n\n    UI->>Comms: POST /api/communications/templates/{template_id}/versions\n    Note over UI: Request: {subject, body, status: Draft}\n\n    Comms->>Comms: Validate permissions\n    Comms->>Comms: Validate variable placeholders match event type\n\n    Comms->>TemplateRepo: Create new TemplateVersion\n    TemplateRepo-->>Comms: version_id\n\n    Comms--)EventBus: EmailTemplateVersionCreated\n    Comms-->>UI: Success (version_id)\n\n    Note over Admin,UI: Admin reviews draft, tests with preview\n\n    Admin->>UI: Click \"Activate Version\"\n    UI->>Comms: POST /api/communications/templates/{template_id}/versions/{version_id}/activate\n\n    Comms->>Comms: Validate permissions\n    Comms->>TemplateRepo: Begin transaction\n    TemplateRepo->>TemplateRepo: Deactivate current active version\n    TemplateRepo->>TemplateRepo: Set new version as active\n    TemplateRepo->>TemplateRepo: Commit transaction\n    TemplateRepo-->>Comms: Success\n\n    Note over TemplateRepo: Template now has:<br/>v1.0 (inactive), v2.0 (active)\n\n    Comms--)EventBus: EmailTemplateActivated {template_id, version_id}\n    Comms-->>UI: Success\n    UI-->>Admin: \"Template activated\" confirmation\n" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:SequencesDoc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:errorScenarios> "Invalid variable placeholder (not in event type) > 400 Bad Request. Insufficient permissions > 403 Forbidden. Concurrent activation conflict > 409 Conflict, retry." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:eventsPublished> "EmailTemplateVersionCreated - New draft created. EmailTemplateActivated - Version set as active." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:initiatedBy> "user" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:keyDecisions> "Single active version: activating v2.0 automatically deactivates v1.0. Draft-then-activate workflow: prevents accidental activation of untested content. Variable validation: system validates placeholders match the event type's available variables. Audit trail: all versions preserved (never deleted)." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "confirmed" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Template Version Update and Activation" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:whatWhenWho> "What: Admin creates a new template version and activates it. When: Template content needs updating (e.g., policy change, branding update). Who: Credentialing Administrator, System Administrator." .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:Seq_UserResolvesDashboardAlert> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Sequence> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:belongsToContext> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:CommunicationsContext> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:content> "sequenceDiagram\n    actor User\n    participant Dashboard\n    participant Comms as Communications Service\n    participant AlertRepo as Alert Repository\n    participant EventBus\n\n    User->>Dashboard: Complete alert action (e.g., fix data quality issue)\n    Dashboard->>Comms: POST /api/communications/alerts/{alert_id}/resolve\n    Note over Dashboard: Request: {resolution_type: \"Completed\"}\n\n    Comms->>Comms: Validate user owns alert\n    Comms->>AlertRepo: Get alert\n    AlertRepo-->>Comms: Alert details\n\n    alt User does not own alert\n        Comms-->>Dashboard: 403 Forbidden\n    else User owns alert\n        Comms->>AlertRepo: Update alert status\n        Note over AlertRepo: status: Active > Resolved<br/>resolved_at: timestamp<br/>resolved_by: user_id\n        AlertRepo-->>Comms: Success\n\n        Comms--)EventBus: DashboardAlertResolved {alert_id, user_id}\n        Comms-->>Dashboard: Success\n\n        Dashboard->>Dashboard: Remove alert from UI\n        Dashboard-->>User: Alert dismissed\n    end\n" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:SequencesDoc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:errorScenarios> "User does not own alert > 403 Forbidden. Alert already resolved > 409 Conflict (idempotent response). Alert expired > 400 Bad Request \"Alert expired\"." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:eventsPublished> "DashboardAlertResolved - Alert completed by user." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:initiatedBy> "user" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:keyDecisions> "User ownership validation: only the alert owner can resolve it. Resolution types: Completed, Dismissed, No Action Needed. Automatic resolution: some alerts auto-resolve when the underlying condition clears. Audit trail: resolution timestamp and user ID captured." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "confirmed" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "User Resolves Dashboard Alert" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:whatWhenWho> "What: User completes action and dismisses alert. When: User clicks the alert action link and completes the required task. Who: District Data Steward, Authorization Approver, etc." .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:SequencesDoc> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:SourceDocument> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:docType> "sequences" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:section> "abox-tests/mied/communications/communications-sequences.md" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:TP_EmailStorageArchitecture> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:TechnicalProcess> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:TechnicalDesignDoc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:implementationNotes> "Dual-retention model: Cosmos DB (hot) holds full rendered content (body_html, body_text, rendered subject) for content_retention_days (default 90), targeting <100ms p95 read latency to support 500 concurrent users browsing email history and burst traffic (e.g. 1000 emails sent in 5 minutes, all queried immediately) — chosen over SQL Server for hot storage because large TEXT columns hurt query performance, read replicas scale worse, and row-level locking contends on delivery-status updates. SQL Server (warm) holds metadata only (recipient, subject text, status, template_version_id) for audit_retention_years (default 7), with covering indexes on (functional_area, sent_at DESC), (recipient_email, sent_at DESC), (event_type, sent_at DESC), and monthly partitions for lifecycle management. Cosmos DB partition key is /functional_area — chosen because most queries filter by functional area, volume is roughly even across areas, and it aligns with RBAC (users typically query one area at a time); explicitly NOT partitioned by recipient_email, since a small number of users would create a hot partition and 'all emails sent today' queries would need to cross partitions anyway. Cosmos DB excludes body_html/body_text from its automatic indexing (large, never queried directly, hurts write performance)." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Trade-offs accepted: higher cost per GB than SQL, eventual consistency (acceptable for email history), no JOIN support. See comm:EmailInstanceAggregate in communications-capability.ttl, which sd:references this process, and comm:BatchJob_EmailContentArchival below for what happens after the 90-day hot-storage window." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Email Storage Architecture (Dual-Retention)" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:TP_SendGridCircuitBreaker> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:TechnicalProcess> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:TechnicalDesignDoc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:implementationNotes> "In-memory circuit breaker per pod (eventual, not immediately consistent, detection across the fleet) guarding the SendGrid API call." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:steps> "Closed (normal): all requests attempted, consecutive failures tracked. After 10 consecutive failures -> Open: fail immediately without calling SendGrid, messages remain queued in Service Bus, CRITICAL alert emitted. After a 5-minute cooldown -> Half-Open: one test request allowed to probe recovery; success returns to Closed, failure returns to Open." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "SendGrid Circuit Breaker" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:TP_SendGridWebhookProcessing> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:TechnicalProcess> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:TechnicalDesignDoc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:implementationNotes> "Dedicated webhook-receiver deployment (separate from the main service) so webhook traffic during a mass send can't block normal processing, and to respond to SendGrid within its 10-second expectation. Flow: SendGrid -> Webhook Receiver Pod (validates HMAC, queues to Service Bus, responds 200 OK) -> Service Bus Queue -> Main Service Pod (dequeues, looks up EmailInstance by message_id, updates delivery_status, publishes the matching domain event) -> Cosmos DB." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "SendGrid rate limiting (related, same integration): confirmed account tier is 10,000 requests/second (communications-capability.md Open Question #1, resolved 2026-08-27) — an in-memory queue processes at 9,500 req/sec (5% safety margin), pausing Service Bus consumption above 1000 queued and releasing backpressure below 500. The in-memory queue only smooths spikes; Service Bus itself is the durable queue, so a pod restart just returns queued messages to Service Bus." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:steps> "1. Validate HMAC SHA256 signature; reject with 401 if invalid. 2. Idempotency check on sg_event_id; skip if already processed. 3. Look up EmailInstance by message_id; if not found, log as an orphaned webhook (expected <0.1% of emails, caused by Cosmos DB eventual consistency racing SendGrid's own processing speed) and retry the lookup after 30 seconds via a scheduled Service Bus message, alerting admins after 3 failed retries. 4. Record EmailDeliveryEvent, update instance delivery_status, publish EmailDelivered/EmailBounced/EmailDeferred/EmailDropped." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "SendGrid Webhook Processing" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:TP_TemplateStorageAndEditing> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:TechnicalProcess> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:TechnicalDesignDoc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:implementationNotes> "Templates stored in SQL Server (not Cosmos DB): relational structure (template -> versions -> variables), strong consistency required for the single-active-version invariant (UNIQUE constraint on (template_id, status) where status='active'; activating a new version is a transaction that both deactivates the old and activates the new), complex queries (search by functional area, filter by status), and a version-history audit trail. Content authoring format is Markdown with a server-side-controlled extension allowlist — :::alert{type=info|warning|error|success} and :::button{url=...}{text=...} plus standard Markdown — rather than raw HTML or a WYSIWYG editor (a WYSIWYG-with-sanitization alternative was considered and rejected for XSS complexity and noisy version diffs). Markdown -> HTML conversion happens at send time; variable substitution happens AFTER HTML conversion, and variables are HTML-escaped, so there is no user-provided-HTML XSS surface at all — raw HTML blocks, custom CSS/JS, and <iframe>/<object>/<embed> are all disallowed." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "The event_type field on EmailTemplate is the binding between domain events and templates (one template -> one event type, 1:1). See comm:EmailTemplateAggregate in communications-capability.ttl, which sd:references this process." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:steps> "Template validation flow, run on save, on activation, and on manual send (all blocking): 1. Extract placeholders from template content via regex <<(\\w+)>>. 2. Look up available variables for the template's event type. 3. Check each placeholder against the available-variables list. 4. Block save if unknown variables are found. 5. Warn (non-blocking, user can override) if mandatory variables are missing." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Template Storage and Editing" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:TP_VariableResolution> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:TechnicalProcess> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:TechnicalDesignDoc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:implementationNotes> "Event-type-specific resolver classes (e.g. CredentialApplicationApprovedResolver), registered in a factory/registry pattern mapping event_type -> resolver. Each event type exposes 'variable families' (e.g. Applicant, Certificate, Application, Approver) — a single event-payload ID unlocks an entire family of related, formatted, user-facing variables. Resolvers batch API calls when resolving multiple variables from the same source and cache results (user profiles 1hr, application details 5min, reference data 24hr, whole resolved-variable-map 5min keyed on event_type+payload hash). Resolvers subclass a common VariableResolverBase<TEvent> pattern (FetchData + FormatVariables abstract methods)." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Error handling: mandatory variable null -> throw VariableResolutionException -> block send, emit EmailSendFailed. Optional variable null -> empty string, continue. API timeout >5s -> retry once, then block if mandatory. API 404 -> throw if mandatory, empty string if optional. Formatting error -> log warning, fall back to raw value, continue send. Performance target: <2 seconds for manual sends (BRD 6.2), cache hit <100ms p95, cache miss (single API call) <2s p95, target cache hit rate >80%. Caching is Redis (3-node cluster, 16GB RAM/node, allkeys-lru eviction). Validation happens on template save, template activation, and manual email send — all blocking. See comm:Rule_TemplateVariableMandatoryResolution and comm:Rule_EventPayloadStructureAndVariableResolution in communications-capability.ttl, which sd:references this process." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:steps> "1. Event arrives with minimal payload (IDs only). 2. Resolver identifies available variable families for the event type. 3. Resolver fetches data from source domain REST APIs (with caching). 4. Resolver formats every variable in every family into a display-ready string (dates as \"January 15, 2026\", names as \"First Last\", credential/certificate types as human-readable display names, never raw codes/ISO timestamps/booleans). 5. Template substitution occurs after formatting; all values are HTML-escaped." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Variable Resolution" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:TechnicalDesignDoc> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:SourceDocument> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:docType> "technical-design" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:section> "abox-tests/mied/communications/communications-technical-design.md" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:TemplateRecipient> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:DomainEntity> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:description> "Role-based recipient targeting configuration for a template." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:name> "TemplateRecipient" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:TemplateReference> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:ValueObject> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:description> "Immutable reference to the template version used (template_id, version_id, functional_area, event_type). NULL template_id for a manual/ad-hoc send." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:name> "TemplateReference" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:TemplateState_Active> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:StateDefinition> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:isTerminal> false ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:name> "Active" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:TemplateState_Archived> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:StateDefinition> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:isTerminal> true ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:name> "Archived" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:TemplateState_Draft> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:StateDefinition> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:isTerminal> false ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:name> "Draft" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:TemplateState_Pending> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:StateDefinition> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:isTerminal> false ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:name> "Pending" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:TemplateVariable> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:DomainEntity> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:description> "Variable placeholder name and metadata (NOT resolution logic — that lives in event-type-specific Variable Resolvers)." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:name> "TemplateVariable" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:TemplateVersion> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:DomainEntity> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:description> "Versioned snapshot of template content (subject, body, variable placeholders)." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:name> "TemplateVersion" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:UT_Alert> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:UbiquitousTerm> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A user-facing notification displayed in dashboards or on-screen that requires attention or action, with lifecycle states (Active, Resolved, Expired)." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Alert" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:describesConcept> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:AlertAggregate> .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:UT_Comment> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:UbiquitousTerm> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A text annotation on a process item (credential application, staffing record) with visibility control (internal-only or external-visible) and optional inclusion in outbound emails." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Comment" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:describesConcept> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:CommentAggregate> .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:UT_Consolidation> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:UbiquitousTerm> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Batching multiple related events into a single notification to reduce communication volume (e.g. 10 data quality issues -> 1 email listing all)." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Consolidation" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:describesConcept> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:EmailInstanceAggregate> .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:UT_DeliveryStatus> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:UbiquitousTerm> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "SendGrid-provided status indicating email lifecycle: Processed, Delivered, Bounced, Deferred, Dropped (with substatus details)." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Delivery Status" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:describesConcept> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:EmailInstanceAggregate> .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:UT_EmailInstance> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:UbiquitousTerm> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "An immutable historical record of a sent email containing the fully rendered email content (after all variable resolution), recipients, delivery metadata, and audit trail. Does NOT store the original event or template structure." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Email Instance" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:describesConcept> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:EmailInstanceAggregate> .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:UT_Resend> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:UbiquitousTerm> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Capability to retransmit a previously sent email, optionally to different recipient(s), available only during the content retention period." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Resend" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:describesConcept> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:EmailInstanceAggregate> .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:UT_Template> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:UbiquitousTerm> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A reusable email or alert content structure containing static text and variable placeholders, versioned over time and scoped to a functional area (e.g. Credentialing, Professional Learning)." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Template" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:describesConcept> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:EmailTemplateAggregate> .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:UT_TemplateVariable> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:UbiquitousTerm> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A dynamic placeholder (e.g. <<ApplicantName>>) in template content that resolves to user-facing formatted data at send time. Variables are contextual to the event type that triggers the email." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Template Variable" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:describesConcept> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:EmailTemplateAggregate> .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:UT_TriggerEvent> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:UbiquitousTerm> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A standardized domain event (e.g. CredentialApplicationApproved) that initiates notification evaluation. Events carry minimal payload (typically IDs and core intrinsic data) rather than verbose denormalized data." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Trigger Event" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:describesConcept> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:EmailTemplateAggregate> .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:Wireframe1> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:SourceDocument> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:Fdd06Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:docType> "wireframe" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Confirmed by viewing: 'Remarks History' table (Action/Status/Email Sent/Modified By/Modified On columns, hyperlinked Action values) above a 'Hold' action form — Action dropdown, 'Hold Reasons' checklist (predefined-comment-library style options), 'Send Email?' checkbox, separate 'Application Remarks' (external, sent to applicant) and 'Internal Remarks' text areas (5000-char max each), with a note warning applicants cannot reply to the system-sent email. Direct, field-for-field match to Req_06_4_1/6_4_2/6_4_3/6_4_4. Per comment 2098536325, this is a screenshot reused from the legacy MOECS reference doc, not a purpose-built new-system mockup — corroborates the SHAPE of the feature, not a confirmed new-UI design." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:section> "abox/mied-v3/fdd-review/06-alerts-emails-communications/wireframes/wireframe-01-remarks-history-and-hold-action.png" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:Wireframe2> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:SourceDocument> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:Fdd06Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:docType> "wireframe" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Confirmed by viewing: 'Approval Worklist' popup showing read-only Application Remarks (external, applicant-facing) and Internal Remarks for one specific remarks-history row — i.e. the detail view reached by clicking an Action hyperlink in Wireframe1's table. Same MOECS-reuse provenance note as Wireframe1." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:section> "abox/mied-v3/fdd-review/06-alerts-emails-communications/wireframes/wireframe-02-approval-worklist-popup.png" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Annotation_UnformalizedAdminNarrativeContent> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The Business Specifications narrative section describes several further Credential-Admin capabilities that were never split into their own Addendum user stories at all, unlike Features 5.1-5.4: Alternative Test Scores management ('detailed requirements will be provided' — a stub even in the narrative), Online Credentialing Viewing management for out-of-state EPPs, Public Credential Search page administration (-> Business Specs 31.1/31.2, corroborated by Wireframe05_28_Redesign's public-facing counterpart), Credential-related system pages administration, Alerts/Notifications management for Credentialing (explicitly 'using the framework of alerts and notifications, Epic 6.0' -> Communications), Email template management for Credentials (same Epic 6.0 framework -> Communications), document-upload availability toggling and file-queue/API-data-ingestion administration (-> Documents capability), and Question Sets/decision-tree management for credential processes (-> the qset:QuestionSetContext stub already declared in solution.ttl) and Internal Comments group/visibility management (-> cred:ApplicationProcessingNotes, already corroborated once by the FDD 11/16 pilot's Req_16_2_2/Question_InternalCommentVisibility). None of these are modeled as sd:Requirement nodes here: most explicitly name their owning Business Specification already (Communications/Documents/Reporting), making them out-of-scope-by-the-FDD's-own-words rather than Credentialing gaps, and the FDD's own numbering caps at 5.6 with no sub-numbers ever assigned to this content — inventing Requirement IDs the source never gave would overstate this ingestion's precision. Flagged collectively here so this content doesn't silently vanish from the coverage picture; worth revisiting once Communications/Documents/Reporting/Question-Sets get their own FDD-review passes, to confirm each item is actually captured somewhere and not lost between FDDs." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd05Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "out-of-scope" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:impact> "M" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "open" .

