	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:name> "QualifyingAssessments" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Question_ApplicationNumberFormatResolved> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Reading 'Decision Sheet for Creating A Code in the Application Numbers.docx' in full for this ingestion pass RESOLVES a related-but-distinct open question the domain doc's Open Question #35 doesn't directly ask: how is CredentialApplication.application_number (distinct from IssuedCredential.credential_number) generated? Decision made 08/01/2024 (Option 3, preferred): two alpha-prefixed identifiers, TXXXXXX (Temporary) and CXXXXXX (Certifications), each with its own incrementing-integer generator starting at 1, unpadded, capped at 6 digits, extending/resetting the scheme to be determined if the threshold is reached. This directly informs cred:CredentialApplicationAggregate's application_number field/generation rule, which nothing in credentialing-domain.ttl currently documents. IMPORTANT: this decision does NOT resolve Question_CredentialNumberFormat (credentialing-domain.ttl, Open Question #35) — that question is specifically about IssuedCredential.credential_number, whose own documented examples ('PV0000000772064', 'CC-K46940078990') don't match the TXXXXXX/CXXXXXX scheme this decision describes at all (different length, different prefix conventions, no relation to the T/C temporary-vs-certificate split). See Question_CredentialNumberFormat's updated resolutionNotes (credentialing-domain.ttl) for how this sharpens rather than closes that question." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:CredentialApplicationAggregate> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:DecisionSheetAppNumbersDoc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd11_16Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "unconfirmed-assumption" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:impact> "M" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:resolutionNotes> "application_number generation is now documented: TXXXXXX/CXXXXXX prefix + unpadded incrementing integer per type, per the 08/01/2024 Decision Sheet. credential_number (a different field on a different aggregate) remains unresolved — see Question_CredentialNumberFormat." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "resolved" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Question_ApplicationStatusVocabularyMismatch> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "All eight FDD 17 documents gate their confirmation messaging and worklist routing on a (application status x Needs Responses flag) combination, using a status vocabulary — Pending PPR, Conviction Review, Pending Evaluation (routed to the OEE worklist), Pending Payment, Approved — that does not map cleanly 1:1 onto cred:CredentialApplicationAggregate's AppState_* enumeration (Draft/Submitted/PendingPayment/PendingDocuments/ProfessionalPracticeHold/RequiresManualReview/Approved/Denied/Cancelled/Blocked). 'Pending Evaluation' most plausibly corresponds to RequiresManualReview and 'Conviction Review' to ProfessionalPracticeHold, but neither mapping is stated anywhere, and the 'Needs Responses' boolean flag itself — which gates FIVE explicitly-named invalid status combinations in every one of the eight FDDs — is not a modeled field on cred:CredentialApplicationAggregate or any ValueObject at all. This is the same underlying gap credentialing-fdd-11-16.ttl's Req_11_4_1 already flagged from a different FDD (11.4.1's PPR-flag/Needs-Responses eligibility filter) — FDD 17 corroborates it as load-bearing, cross-permit-type logic rather than a one-off, strengthening rather than duplicating that earlier finding." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:CredentialApplicationAggregate> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_17_1_0> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_17_FYB_5> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_17_SA_7> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd17DailySubDoc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "coverage-gap" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:impact> "H" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "open" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Question_AssignmentEndorsementMappingNotModeled> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Features 12.1.1-12.1.4 and 12.1.7 ask for an admin-maintained, reusable mapping catalog (SCED code, Grade/Educational-Setting, CTE CIP code -> one or more allowable endorsements) used to bulk-identify existing Staffing assignments that are out of alignment with Credentialing endorsement requirements, plus an audit trail over changes to that catalog. Nothing in credentialing-domain.ttl or staffing-domain.ttl models this as a distinct entity: the closest real mechanism, staff:Rule_EndorsementAlignmentForTeaching (enforced by staff:AssignmentAggregate), is a real-time, per-assignment BLOCKING validation at assignment-creation time — structurally different from an admin-configurable mapping table plus a batch audit process over already-existing records. cred:EndorsementDefinitionAggregate models what an endorsement itself allows (grade band, required assessments) but has no notion of 'which SCED/CIP codes may use this endorsement,' the inverse relationship this FDD's mapping catalog needs. wireframe-01 (cred:WireframeAddEndorsementMapping, viewed) reinforces this: the screen embedded at 12.1.1 is credentialing's existing single-Endorsement Requirements editor, not a purpose-built mapping-catalog UI, meaning this capability was never concretely designed on the wireframe side either. Distinct from any User-Group/impersonation concern — this is a Credentialing/Staffing cross-domain modeling gap with no relationship to FDD 01's IAM findings." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_12_1_1> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_12_1_2> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_12_1_3> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_12_1_4> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_12_1_7> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd12Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "coverage-gap" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:impact> "M" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:references> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:EndorsementDefinitionAggregate> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:references> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:staffing:Rule_EndorsementAlignmentForTeaching> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "open" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Question_BatchJobAdminVisibility> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Open Technical Question #3 (plus #4's nightly-run-time logistics folded in): should Definition Version Activation and Credential/Permit Expiration Processing be admin-visible, schedulable jobs through FDD 05's 'Run & View Batch Jobs' console (Feature 5.4), or purely internal scheduled logic with no admin-facing run history? The generic multi-job admin console itself (arbitrary job search/trigger/schedule) may be broader platform tooling rather than a credentialing-owned capability — this section only covers the two jobs credentialing's own business rules already imply. Exact nightly run time for both jobs is also TBD; coordinate with other domains' nightly jobs (e.g. Organizations' CEPI sync) to avoid contention." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:BatchJob_CredentialExpirationProcessing> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:BatchJob_DefinitionVersionActivation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_05_4_1> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_05_4_2> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_05_4_3> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_05_4_4> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#questioning> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:TechnicalDesignDoc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:impact> "M" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:owner> "Product" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:resolutionNotes> "FDD 05 Feature 5.4 (this file's primary source for this question) resolves the FIRST half affirmatively: yes, batch jobs are meant to be admin-visible and searchable/executable through a generic 'Run & View Batch Jobs' console, not purely internal scheduled logic — Wireframe05_9 (confirmed by viewing) shows this console already exists as real/legacy functionality, populated with 8+ real job names, run history, and free-text status descriptions. None of those job names literally match cred:BatchJob_DefinitionVersionActivation or cred:BatchJob_CredentialExpirationProcessing (closest conceptual overlaps: 'Process Credential data (Daily)' and 'Delete Certificate Applications (Daily)' x3), so whether OUR two specific batch jobs are meant to surface through this exact console, or are distinct nightly processes alongside it, remains unconfirmed. The SECOND half (exact nightly run time, generic-console-as-credentialing-owned-vs-platform-tooling) stays open, and a NEW open point surfaces: comment #127 (Dontje, anchored to the Feature 5.4 heading) shows the client was still actively discussing, as of the last comment on that thread, whether jobs should support 1) a 'health report' and/or 2) re-run-on-demand with what authorization implications — i.e. even the source FDD's own review process hadn't settled the manual re-run/authorization question by ingestion time. Impact downgraded from the admin-visibility question (now largely answered) to this narrower re-run/authorization sub-question." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "open" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Question_ConfigurabilityModel> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Open Technical Question #1/#2: which configurability model does the client actually want for admin-editable parameters (FDD 05's 'Global Parameters'/'Credentialing Controls', Feature 5.3)? Three competing shapes: (a) fully independent per credential type (extends the existing per-type FeeSchedule pattern but gives no 'change once, applies everywhere' lever); (b) a shared default with per-type override (most flexible, matches how CredentialProperties.CanApply/CanRenew already hint at per-type-with-fallback, but needs a clear override-precedence rule); (c) fully centralized with no per-type variation (simplest, but doesn't accommodate the FDD's own permit-side evidence that per-type variation already exists in practice, e.g. Rule_PermitDurationAndRenewalLimits). This determines the shape of any GlobalParameter/CredentialingControl aggregate — not drafted in this pass since it isn't decided. Also unresolved: whether 'Global Parameters' is credentialing-owned at all, or a shared cross-domain configuration capability other domains would also consume (see patterns-and-principles/configuration.md)." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:CredentialDefinitionAggregate> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_05_3_1> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_05_3_2> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_05_3_3> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_05_3_4> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_05_3_5> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#questioning> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:TechnicalDesignDoc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:impact> "H" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:owner> "Product" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:resolutionNotes> "FDD 05 Feature 5.3 (this file's primary source for this question) does NOT resolve which of the three competing configurability shapes was chosen — it neither confirms nor rules out per-credential-type variation in so many words. But it supplies concrete new evidence leaning toward shape (c), 'fully centralized, no per-type variation': Wireframe05_7 (confirmed by viewing) shows a single FLAT 'Credentialing Controls' results table with genuinely heterogeneous, unrelated example rows (a numeric fee-like value, a free-text 'Governor'/'Charter' pair, a datetime-format string) and no credential-type-scoping column anywhere in the search filters (only 'Parameter Description') or results columns (Description/Value/Format/Modified By/Modified On). This reads as a generic system-wide key-value settings store, not a per-credential-type override mechanism — more centralized than even shape (c) originally envisioned (which still assumed some per-type structure), closer to a flat global settings table that happens to include credentialing-relevant entries among unrelated ones (e.g. 'Governor'/'Charter' looks unrelated to credentialing at all). This actually strengthens the OTHER half of the open question — whether 'Global Parameters' is even credentialing-owned rather than a shared cross-domain configuration capability — since the sample data shown isn't credentialing-specific. Still open; not resolved by this FDD." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "open" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Question_CredentialNumberFormat> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "credentialing-domain.md Open Question #35: what is the actual format/generation rule for credential_number (e.g. the 'PV' vs 'CC-K' prefixes seen in FDD 31.1/31.2 examples)? Is it generated by MiEdWorkforce at issuance, or migrated/preserved from legacy MOECS numbering per credential type? The field is on ISSUED_CREDENTIALS (see the domain doc's ERD) since it's clearly required — the source explicitly calls it a CEDS-aligned 'Credential Number' element, keyed by both the public search and internal credential views — but the generation/migration rule itself is undefined in any FDD reviewed so far. Per CONVENTIONS.md's cedsAlignment guidance, this CEDS alignment is scoped to the credential_number FIELD, not IssuedCredential's whole shape, so sd:cedsAlignment is deliberately NOT asserted on cred:IssuedCredentialAggregate — this annotation is where that partial-field alignment is captured instead." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:IssuedCredentialAggregate> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:DomainDoc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "unconfirmed-assumption" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:impact> "M" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:resolutionNotes> "SHARPENED, not resolved, by FDD-review Phase 2 (fdd-review/11-16-educator-credentialing/11-16-educator-credentialing.ttl): 'Decision Sheet for Creating A Code in the Application Numbers.docx' (08/01/2024) resolves a related-but-distinct field's generation rule — CredentialApplication.application_number, not IssuedCredential.credential_number — as two alpha-prefixed identifiers (TXXXXXX temporary, CXXXXXX certification) each with its own incrementing integer generator. That scheme does NOT match this field's own documented examples ('PV0000000772064', 'CC-K46940078990'), confirming credential_number is a genuinely separate identifier (likely legacy-MOECS-derived) whose own format/generation rule is still undocumented anywhere reviewed so far. See fdd-review's Question_ApplicationNumberFormatResolved for the full finding." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "open" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Question_ESignatureLegalSufficiency> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Open Technical Question #6: is typed-name electronic signature capture legally sufficient for state credentialing attestations, or is a stronger mechanism (drawn signature capture, a third-party e-sign vendor such as DocuSign/Adobe Sign, or a click-to-attest pattern with additional identity verification) required?" ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:TP_ElectronicSignatureAttestationCapture> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#questioning> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:TechnicalDesignDoc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:impact> "H" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:owner> "Legal / Compliance" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "open" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Question_EducatorPerformanceRatingSourceMissing> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "cred:Rule_PermitDurationAndRenewalLimits's own statement requires 'effective/highly effective ratings' for Full Year Shortage Substitute Permit renewals (confirmed verbatim against the Renewals FDD and the Full Year Shortage Substitute Permit FDD). No domain converted into mied-v3 so far (credentialing, staffing, or otherwise) models educator performance/effectiveness ratings as data anywhere — not as a ValueObject, not as an external-system dependency, not even as an open question elsewhere. This is a genuine, narrow but real gap: the rating data this specific renewal rule depends on has no known source in the solution design at all yet." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_17_FYS> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Rule_PermitDurationAndRenewalLimits> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd17FullYearShortageDoc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "coverage-gap" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:impact> "M" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "open" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Question_FullYearExpertPermitTypeMissing> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "An eighth permit type, 'Full Year Expert' (a.k.a. 'Expert Substitute Permit'), is named in the eligible-permit list of ALL EIGHT FDD 17 documents (Daily Substitute Permit's own 17.1.3/17.1.7/17.1.9, and identically in Extended Daily, Emergency Extended Daily, Full Year Basic, Full Year Shortage, School Administrator, School Social Worker, and Renewals) alongside the seven permit types cred:Rule_PermitDurationAndRenewalLimits already models. The Renewals FDD gives it real, specific renewal criteria: unlimited renewals subject to (1) an approved IDP, (2) mandatory district-assigned-and-maintained mentor teacher, and (3) for non-core-discipline assignments qualified only under a specific subrule, verification of a valid business/industry license or a bachelor's degree or higher at renewal time. None of this appears anywhere in cred:CredentialCategory's enumerated list, cred:Rule_PermitDurationAndRenewalLimits's statement, or any other rule/aggregate in credentialing-domain.ttl. This is the single largest gap found in this review pass — a whole permit type with its own eligibility and renewal rules, entirely unmodeled, not merely under-specified." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_17_1_3> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_17_1_9> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_17_REN> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Rule_PermitDurationAndRenewalLimits> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd17RenewalsDoc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "coverage-gap" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:impact> "H" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "open" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Question_MttcApiIntegrationNotYetBuilt> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "No API-based Pearson MTTC integration exists anywhere in credentialing-domain.ttl/credentialing-sequences.ttl today — only the manual CSV/XLSX import path (cred:Seq_ImportAssessmentResults) is built. This is not a newly-discovered gap: asp:AssessmentProviderSystem's own integrationNotes already say the same thing ('may transition to API integration in the future'), and this story independently confirms it from the FDD side. Logged as its own coverage-gap Annotation (rather than folded into a satisfiedBy note) since this Requirement has no partial satisfaction at all to note against — it is a pure future item." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_11_8_2i> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd11_8MttcDoc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "coverage-gap" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:impact> "L" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "open" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Question_MttcIdentityMatchingNotBuilt> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "11.8.3i's demographic (SSN/Name/DOB) fuzzy-matching-with-manual-resolution-queue behavior for unmatched MTTC records has no counterpart in cred:Seq_ImportAssessmentResults, which only checks whether an educator ID already exists and skips-and-logs on failure -- no matching algorithm, no confidence threshold, no queue for an MTTC Specialist to work. Given the FDD's own text frames long-term transition toward Unique-ID-based matching (implying SSN/Name/DOB fuzzy-matching is understood as an interim need, not a permanent one), this may be intentionally deferred rather than overlooked -- but nothing in credentialing-domain.ttl/technical-design.ttl says so explicitly, so it is logged as an open gap rather than assumed resolved." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_11_8_3i> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd11_8MttcDoc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "coverage-gap" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:impact> "M" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "open" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Question_MttcPearsonIntegrationRealityCheck> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "RESOLVED by reading 'Interface Design document - MTTC EdReports (Pearson).docx' in full for this ingestion pass, per the task brief's instruction. Prior state: FDD Feature 11.8.1 describes 'the MTTC Data Store (populated via Pearson integration)' as an already-established, per-applicant-queryable data source, while credentialing-domain.md's AssessmentResult aggregate describes the current state as manual entry from uploaded score reports, with Pearson API integration listed only as a 'Data Source (Future State)' possibility. The interface document settles which is accurate: it specifies a monthly (Frequency: Monthly, Data Volume: 4MB/month), one-way-receive (Data Direction: 'One way receive'), HTTPS GET file download from a Pearson-hosted website — explicitly still 'Incoming File (Prod & Test): N/A (manual process today)' as of the document's own text. There is no live, synchronous, per-applicant Pearson API — 'the MTTC Data Store' is exactly cred:AssessmentResultAggregate as populated by the existing cred:Op_ImportAssessmentResults/cred:Seq_ImportAssessmentResults manual-bulk-import flow (an admin downloads Pearson's monthly file and uploads it via credentialing.assessment-result.import), consistent with — not contradicting — credentialing-domain.md's 'Current State' description. asp:AssessmentProviderSystem's existing sd:hasApi false is therefore CONFIRMED correct, not stale. FDD 11.8.1's phrasing ('populated via Pearson integration') is real but describes this batch-file pipeline, not a live query; worth flagging to the FDD's own authors that 'integration' reads as more automated than the interface spec they themselves wrote actually describes." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:AssessmentResultAggregate> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_11_8_1> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd11_16Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:MttcPearsonInterfaceDoc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "discrepancy" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:impact> "M" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:resolutionNotes> "Confirmed via Interface Design document - MTTC EdReports (Pearson).docx (abox-tests/mied-fdds/functional-design-docs/11 - Educator Credentialing/): monthly manual file download, not a live API; existing cred:Op_ImportAssessmentResults/Seq_ImportAssessmentResults modeling is accurate and needs no change." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "resolved" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Question_PPRCheckTiming> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "credentialing-domain.md Open Question #33: what is the timing of the initial Professional Practice Review check — synchronous on submission, or purely event-driven? What latency is acceptable? Rule_ProfessionalPracticeClearance's own 'Integration Pattern' note calls this UNRESOLVED, with two live options: (A) purely event-driven (eventual consistency), or (B) synchronous check on submission plus event subscription for status changes. Both options appear in the sequence diagrams as written (credentialing-sequences.md shows a synchronous PPR check in every submission sequence), but which is the deliberate target design vs. an interim sketch isn't confirmed." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Rule_ProfessionalPracticeClearance> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#questioning> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:DomainDoc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:impact> "H" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "open" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Question_PaymentStatusCheckEndpoint> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Open Technical Question #7: how should Credentialing check current payment status for an application? payments-api.yml has no internal-service status-check endpoint — GET /payments/search is a scoped, permission-gated, org-context-requiring admin/UI endpoint, not built for service-to-service polling. Options: (a) rely purely on the PaymentCompleted event subscription with no synchronous check at all, or (b) request a new internal-service endpoint from the payments team, mirroring the pattern already used for GET /educators/{id}/ppr-clearance. Also confirm credentialing-domain.md's Rule_PaymentRequirement (one fee per school year) has no counterpart on the payments side — per the FDD 07 review, PaymentTransaction has no academic-year concept, so this stays a credentialing-side dedup check before ever calling payments, not something payments needs to model." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Rule_AutoApprovalCriteria> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Rule_PaymentRequirement> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Seq_ApplicationAutoApproval> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:TechnicalDesignDoc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "discrepancy" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:impact> "H" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:owner> "Engineering (credentialing + payments)" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "open" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Question_PermitRenewalActorMismatch> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "cred:Seq_RenewCredential (credentialing-sequences.ttl) models renewal as educator self-service ('Who: Authenticated educator with renewable credential', actor 'Educator') and its gating cred:Op_SubmitRenewal is permissioned via cred:Perm_ApplicationSubmit, scoped scope:SelfOnly ('All authenticated educators'). Every FDD 17 document that discusses permit renewals (Daily Substitute Permit 17.1.7, and the Renewals FDD's own framing throughout) instead describes permit renewals as submitted by a School district/ISD/Staffing Agency user on the educator's behalf — the same org-submitted actor as the original permit application (cred:Op_AdminIssuePermit, gated by district/ISD-scoped cred:Perm_PermitIssue), consistent with both FDDs' shared assumption that 'Temporary Credentials are applied for by a district or ISD on behalf of an individual.' No org-submitted 'renew a permit' ApiOperation exists anywhere in credentialing-api.ttl. Seq_RenewCredential most plausibly describes CERTIFICATE renewal (matching FDD 11/16's scope) rather than PERMIT renewal — but nothing currently distinguishes the two paths in the graph, and permit renewal as these FDDs describe it may be entirely unimplemented." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Op_SubmitRenewal> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_17_1_7> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Seq_RenewCredential> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd17DailySubDoc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "discrepancy" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:impact> "M" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "open" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Question_StaffingMentorVerificationEndpoint> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Open Technical Question #8: two Credentialing-to-Staffing integration points have no confirmed shape, surfaced during the FDD 10 (Staffing Admin) review. (a) Rule_MentorAssignmentRequirementForPermits calls GET /educators/{uniqueId} on the Staffing API expecting 'verify educator exists and holds valid, relevant credential' — staffing-api.yml has no such endpoint, and the closest one (GET /educators/search) only returns a free-text activeCredentialSummary string, while staffing-domain.md's own Dependencies table has Staffing calling Credentialing for credential validation, the reverse of what this rule assumes. (b) Seq_SubmitPermitApplication calls 'Staffing: Verify employment assignment (if required)' with no corresponding endpoint anywhere in staffing-api.yml (closest is the org-scoped, permission-gated GET /employee-roster/search, not built as a single-lookup verification call). Options for (a): have Credentialing check its own domain data directly (credential validity is credentialing-owned) and let staffing's free-text activeCredentialSummary stay a UI-only convenience field, or add a purpose-built endpoint. Options for (b): confirm whether 'employment assignment' verification is even a real requirement (no FDD source describes it) or add a purpose-built internal-service endpoint to staffing-api.yml if it is." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Rule_MentorAssignmentRequirementForPermits> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Seq_SubmitPermitApplication> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:TechnicalDesignDoc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "discrepancy" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:impact> "H" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:owner> "Engineering (credentialing + staffing)" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "open" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Question_WorklistAssignmentScope> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "credentialing-domain.md Open Question #34 (flagged in the source itself as exceeding the working assumption for what a permission scope can express): credentialing-permissions.md's credentialing.application.approve/.deny/.place-hold permissions carry an 'Assigned-only' scope (see scope:AssignedOnly in permission-scopes.ttl) narrower than the domain's own System-wide/Entity/District/ISD scope model — implying a specific application gets assigned to a specific individual processor, not just to 'anyone holding the approve permission for this scope.' This is routing/queue-assignment behavior, not a filtered list, and isn't expressible via the application's own fields (ManualReviewReason, status, org scope) today. Corroborated by the FDD-05 review (fdd-sdd-review/reviews/05-system-admin-credentialing.md, Coverage Gap #4), which describes an admin capability to assign specific worklists/reports to an individual user, not just at the role level. Needs its own design (an assignment/queue concept) rather than being resolved as an ordinary permission scope. Not resolved here." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:CredentialApplicationAggregate> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_05_5_1> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_05_5_2> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:iam:RoleDefinitionAggregate> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:DomainDoc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "coverage-gap" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:impact> "M" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:resolutionNotes> "UPDATE from the actual FDD 05 review (the prior cross-reference to 'fdd-sdd-review/reviews/05-system-admin-credentialing.md, Coverage Gap #4' predates this ingestion and reflects only the FDD's stale narrative text/wireframes, not its final resolution). This FDD's own review comments reverse the individual-assignment premise: comment #128 (Dontje, MDE) states 'We don't want to have users assigned specific/custom access; it needs to remain role-based while still allowing the admin to update those attributes for the role', and the FDD's final comment on the matching user story (203926376, Doherty relaying Yashi, 2026-04-21) confirms 'Since worklist and report management is strictly role-based and not assigned at the individual user level, I have completely revised this user story... search for User Roles (filtered by User Type) and manage the worklist and report assignments globally for that role.' So the premise this Annotation was originally raised against (individual-level worklist assignment as real product behavior) is the OPPOSITE of the client's final decision — worklist/report access assignment is role-based, via iam:RoleDefinitionAggregate, not a per-individual queue-assignment concept. This doesn't fully close the question, though: iam:RoleDefinitionAggregate has no exposed manage/update API today (iam-api.ttl's only Role operations are read-only Op_ListRoles/Op_GetRole), and neither 'worklist' nor 'report' exists anywhere as a first-class, nameable, assignable unit distinct from an ordinary Permission — so the SETTLED (role-based) version of this capability is arguably a bigger, still-unmodeled gap than the individual-assignment version this Annotation originally described." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "open" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_05_1_1> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Requirement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "Page accessible from the Credentialing Data area. Searchable, tabular list of certificate types (Name, Status). Search field filters by name. 'Add Certificate' action initiates creation of a new certificate type. Filter and download actions refine/export the list. Only certificate types configured in the system are displayed." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd05Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Good match for the list/search/create core; cred:Op_CreateCredentialDefinition covers 'Add Certificate'. Filter/download-as-export actions shown in Wireframe05_14_Redesign have no corresponding sd:parameters/export-format detail on cred:Op_ListCredentialDefinitions — same minor, low-impact UI-export gap the FDD 11/16 pilot flagged for worklist search (Question_MissingWorklistSearchAndExportUX), not re-raised as its own Annotation here." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "5.1.1" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Op_ListCredentialDefinitions> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a Credential Admin, I want to view a list of types, so that I can review and manage core credential definitions within the system." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "View a searchable list of certificate/permit types" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_05_1_2> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Requirement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "Results table populated per selected category with Type/Modified By/Modified On columns; user selects a row to open the detailed record." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd05Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Per comment 2044568528 ('It has been updated to Credential Type'), the 'Type' column itself was renamed to 'Credential Type' late in review — the acceptance criteria text above is the pre-rename wording. Modified By/Modified On are not explicit fields on cred:CredentialDefinitionVersion in credentialing-domain.ttl today (that entity's own description is generic 'audit trail' prose) — minor gap, folded into Req_05_1_4's note rather than duplicated." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "5.1.2" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Op_ListCredentialDefinitions> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a Credential Admin, I want to view details including Type, Modified By, and Modified On in the search results table, so that I can see audit information at a glance." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "View Type/Modified By/Modified On in search results" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_05_1_3> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Requirement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "Selecting a Certificate Type opens a detailed, editable view: Category Name, Type, Print Name, Is Permanent?, Is Advanced?, Is Active?, Validity (years), Fee, Effective From date. Effective From captures when the changes become active." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd05Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Strong direct match — CredentialProperties already carries IsPermanent/IsAdvanced/IsActive/CanApply/CanRenew, and FeeSchedule/ValidityPeriod/EffectiveDateRange cover the rest. Comment #9/#10 (Caswell -> Dontje, 'Yes it should be editable') confirms future-dated Effective From edits are intentional, not an oversight — this is the admin-facing origin of cred:BatchJob_DefinitionVersionActivation (the nightly 'Cleanup of Future-Dated Changes' job in credentialing-technical-design.ttl), which activates exactly these future-dated changes. See Req_05_1_5 for the versioning-on-save behavior this feeds." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "5.1.3" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:CredentialDefinitionEffectiveDateRange> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:CredentialDefinitionFeeSchedule> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:CredentialDefinitionValidityPeriod> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:CredentialProperties> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Op_UpdateCredentialDefinition> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a Credential Admin, I want to edit a Type and update fields like Validity, Fee, and Effective From date, so that I can maintain current credential requirements." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Edit a Type's Validity, Fee, and Effective From fields" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_05_1_4> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Requirement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "System captures the identity of the user making changes (Modified By) and the timestamp (Modified On) upon save; both visible in the search results table for the modified record." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd05Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "No satisfiedBy: cred:CredentialDefinitionVersion (credentialing-domain.ttl) is described only as generically carrying 'change audit trail' with no explicit Modified By/Modified On fields listed in sd:fields anywhere on CredentialDefinitionAggregate's entities/value objects. Comment #78 (Dontje, 'Further discussion about audit details/history is needed') shows this was still an open point on the client side too, not just a modeling gap on our end. Genuine coverage gap." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "5.1.4" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a Credential Admin, I want the system to capture Modified By and Modified On details upon saving changes, so that I have an audit trail of modifications." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Capture Modified By/Modified On audit details on save" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_05_1_5> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Requirement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "On save, system versions the certificate record based on Effective From; current date is the default Effective From; changes affect only new applications generated after the effective date, existing/pending applications unaffected." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd05Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Direct, well-corroborated match — this is precisely what Rule_CredentialDefinitionVersioning plus BatchJob_DefinitionVersionActivation (the nightly job that actually flips a future-dated version to Active once its Effective From date arrives) already model. This FDD story is the missing admin-UI-side confirmation that the batch job's premise (admins schedule changes in advance) is real product behavior, not a speculative technical-design assumption." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "5.1.5" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:BatchJob_DefinitionVersionActivation> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:CredentialDefinitionEffectiveDateRange> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Rule_CredentialDefinitionVersioning> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a Credential Admin, I want the system to version the record based on the Effective From date upon save, so that changes are applied correctly to new applications." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Version the record based on Effective From date upon save" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_05_1_6> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Requirement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "Selecting a Permit type opens a detailed view with editable Category Name, Type, Print Name, Is Permanent?, Is Advanced?, Is Active?, Can Apply?, Can Renew?, Fee, Effective From, plus a 'Message' field with Rich Text Editor formatting." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd05Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "CanApply/CanRenew are already modeled on CredentialProperties. Genuine small gap: no rich-text 'Message' field exists anywhere on CredentialDefinitionAggregate's value objects. Comment #32/#33 (Caswell: 'Can a permit be permanent?' / Dontje: 'There are legacy permits that are permanent') doesn't conflict with the existing invariant ('If IsPermanent=true then CanRenew must=false') since that invariant is already generic across credential types, not certificate-only — no change needed, just confirmation permits use the same flag. Per comment 1332550677 ('Thank you. We can remove this user story'), a draft bullet proposing admins could 'optionally add internal comments about the update' on this screen was agreed to be removed during review — not carried into the acceptance criteria above, and not counted as a separate gap." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "5.1.6" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:CredentialProperties> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Op_UpdateCredentialDefinition> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a Credential Admin, I want to edit permit-specific fields, so that I can maintain the distinct configuration permits require beyond what certificates need." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Edit Permit-specific fields (Can Apply/Can Renew/rich-text Message)" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_05_1_7> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Requirement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "The 'Type' field (functioning as the record's name) is editable within the record details screen; admins can rename an existing type; the change is saved and versioned per the standard save logic." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd05Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "This is the FDD's own unnumbered addendum story (rendered '5.1.' in the source with no digit — an evident drafting gap, assigned 5.1.7 here for a stable IRI). Straightforward extension of the same update+versioning path as 5.1.3/5.1.5." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "5.1.7" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Op_UpdateCredentialDefinition> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Rule_CredentialDefinitionVersioning> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a Credential Admin, I want the ability to change the 'Type' (name) field of an existing record, so that I can update the credential name to reflect current administrative naming conventions." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Rename the 'Type' (name) field of an existing record" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_05_2_1> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Requirement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "List of existing classifications (Code/Name/Certificate Type/Subject Area/Modified By/Modified Date/Is Active). 'Create Endorsement' requires Endorsement Name, Certificate Type, Subject Area, Status, with Core/Grade-band-not-applicable checkboxes under Subject Area. 'Edit' updates Endorsement Name/Certificate Type/Subject Area/Status. Within an endorsement, admins manage Grade Levels/Codes (Grade Band/Code/Out-of-State/Start/End Date) and Test Codes (Grade Band/Code/All Tests Required/Test Start/End Date), and select applicable Certificates/Temporary Credentials." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd05Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Good match. The FDD's own terminology is loose here — the narrative section separately describes a 'Manage Endorsement Classification' page (Class Name/Class Description/Is Active) distinct from full endorsement management, but this Addendum story conflates 'Endorsement Classification' with creating/editing a full Endorsement — treated as one requirement against EndorsementDefinitionAggregate, consistent with how the underlying domain model doesn't separately break out a 'classification' sub-concept either." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "5.2.1" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:EndorsementDefinitionAggregate> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Op_CreateEndorsementDefinition> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Op_UpdateEndorsementDefinition> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a Credential Admin, I want to manage Endorsement Classifications so that I can maintain the organization of credential categories." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Manage Endorsement Classifications (create/edit endorsements)" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_05_2_2> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Requirement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "Search filters: CIP Code, Name, Cert Type, Subject Area, Modified By, Modified Date, Status, Include Inactive Endorsements, Begin/End Date, Progress to Professional, Out-of-State applicants, Initial endorsement eligible?" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd05Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Operation exists as a generic list; the specific filter fields (CIP Code, Progress to Professional, Out-of-State, Initial-endorsement-eligible) are not individually modeled as sd:parameters on cred:Op_ListEndorsementDefinitions — consistent with the ontology's guidance that filter parameters stay opaque prose rather than a promoted class; not counted as a separate gap." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "5.2.2" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Op_ListEndorsementDefinitions> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a Credential Admin, I want to search for existing endorsements, so that I can quickly locate records for management." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Search existing endorsements" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_05_2_3> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Requirement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "The 'Cert Type' dropdown filter on the Endorsement search page contains only 'Teacher' and 'School Administrator'; other credential types do not appear." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd05Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Pure UI filter-option restriction; no corresponding invariant exists on CredentialCategory/EndorsementDefinitionAggregate limiting which categories can carry endorsements, though it's consistent with the domain model's own description ('subject area specializations added to teaching certificates'). Low-impact, not raised as a separate Annotation." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "5.2.3" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Op_ListEndorsementDefinitions> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a Credential Admin, I want the Cert Type filter to only display Teacher and School Administrator options, since endorsements are only available for those types." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Restrict the Cert Type filter to Teacher and School Administrator" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_05_2_4> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Requirement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "Results table with Code/Name/Certificate Type/Subject Area/Modified By/Modified Date columns; clicking a record opens it for editing." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd05Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Same Modified By/Modified Date audit-field gap noted on Req_05_1_4 applies here too — EndorsementDefinitionVersion has no explicit audit fields listed either." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "5.2.4" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Op_ListEndorsementDefinitions> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a Credential Admin, I want to view search results including Code, Name, Certificate Type, Subject Area, Modified By, and Modified Date, so that I can track recent changes." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "View Code/Name/Certificate Type/Subject Area/Modified By/Modified Date in search results" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_05_2_5> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Requirement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "A Reset action clears all entered search criteria and reverts dropdowns/checkboxes to defaults." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd05Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "No satisfiedBy: pure client-side UX affordance with no domain-model or API counterpart expected — consistent with how the FDD 11/16 pilot treated equivalent Reset-button stories as not worth a coverage-gap Annotation on their own (too low-impact to be the 'point' of the exercise). Not modeled as a gap." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "5.2.5" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a Credential Admin, I want a Reset option on the endorsement search page, so that I can quickly clear entered criteria and restore defaults." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Reset endorsement search filters" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_05_2_6> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Requirement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "Endorsement Code table supports Add/Edit(Begin/End Date, etc.)/Delete." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd05Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Per comment 156325117 (Doherty relaying Yashi, 2026-04-21): 'Delete' was refined late in review to apply ONLY to endorsement codes that have never been active/utilized — a code that has been active cannot be deleted, only 'retired' by setting an End Date. This is a real, specific business rule (a delete-guard tied to activation history) not currently expressed anywhere in credentialing-domain.ttl's invariants for EndorsementDefinitionAggregate; folded into this Requirement's notes rather than minted as its own sd:BusinessRule given its narrow scope, but worth carrying forward if EndorsementCode/GradeBandRange ever gets its own dedicated lifecycle." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "5.2.6" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:GradeBandRange> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Op_UpdateEndorsementDefinition> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a Credential Admin, I want to manage endorsement codes in a table format, allowing me to Add, Edit (dates/fields), and Delete rows, so that I can define specific validity parameters." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Manage endorsement codes (Add/Edit/Delete) in a table" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_05_2_7> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Requirement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "Saving a new Endorsement Code automatically triggers a notification/task routed to the MiEdWorkforce System Admin, alerting them to define the allowable assignment mappings for appropriate placement of the new endorsement." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd05Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "No satisfiedBy: cred:EndorsementDefinitionUpdatedEvent is the closest existing event (adding a code is an update to the EndorsementDefinition) but no notification/task-routing behavior is modeled off it, and 'allowable assignment mappings for Appropriate Placement' is itself a Staffing-domain concept per this FDD's own Dependencies section ('credential data... available for mapping to assignments — Managing Credential use of Assignment Codes 12.1'), a business specification not yet converted anywhere in mied-v3. Genuine, cross-domain coverage gap — the notification mechanism belongs to Credentialing (on EndorsementDefinitionUpdatedEvent) but the mapping being defined belongs to a domain this project hasn't reached yet." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "5.2.7" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As the MiEdWorkforce system, when a new endorsement code is added, I want to generate a notification/task for the MiEdWorkforce System Admin, so that allowable assignment mappings are defined." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Notify System Admin to define assignment mappings when a new endorsement code is added" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_05_2_8> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Requirement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "Test Codes table: Grade Band, Code, Test Codes (comma-separated), All Tests Required, Test Start/End Dates, Certificates, Temporary Credentials (comma-separated)." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd05Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Good conceptual match — RequiredAssessments already models AssessmentIdentifier/CombinationLogic/MinimumScore per endorsement. The FDD's comma-separated-text input shape is a UI/data-entry detail, not a structural gap." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "5.2.8" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:RequiredAssessments> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a Credential Admin, I want to define MTTC requirements in the Test Code table using comma-separated test codes, so that multiple required tests can be mapped to an endorsement." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Define MTTC test-code requirements via comma-separated codes" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_05_2_9> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Requirement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "'All Tests Required' column: Yes requires every listed test code to pass; No requires only one of the listed test codes to pass." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd05Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Direct match — this is exactly RequiredAssessments.CombinationLogic (AND/OR), also confirmed as the 'All Tests Required' flag by cred:Rule_SubjectAreaAssessmentValidation's own existing notes (per the FDD 11/16 pilot's Req_11_8_1)." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "5.2.9" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:RequiredAssessments> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a Credential Admin, I want the option to designate whether All Test Codes Required must be passed, or if passing just one is sufficient for the endorsement." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Toggle All-Tests-Required vs. any-single-test-passes logic" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_05_3_1> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Requirement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "A 'Manage Credentialing Controls' page with a 'Parameter Description' search field and a Search button." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd05Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "No satisfiedBy — see Annotation_ConfigurabilityModelEvidence below (updates cred:Question_ConfigurabilityModel)." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "5.3.1" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a Credential Admin, I want to search for Credentialing Controls by Parameter Description, so that I can quickly find the parameter I need to update." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Search Credentialing Controls by Parameter Description" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_05_3_2> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Requirement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "Results table: Description, Value, Format, Modified By, Modified On." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd05Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "No satisfiedBy — see Annotation_ConfigurabilityModelEvidence." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "5.3.2" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a Credential Admin, I want to view the Description, Value, Format, and audit details (Modified By, Modified On) in the search results table, so that I understand the control's configuration and history." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "View Description/Value/Format/audit details in Credentialing Controls results" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_05_3_3> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Requirement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "Description field is editable within the record details view and savable." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd05Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "No satisfiedBy — see Annotation_ConfigurabilityModelEvidence." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "5.3.3" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a Credential Admin, I want to update the Description of a Credentialing Control, so that I can clarify its purpose within the system." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Update a Credentialing Control's Description" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_05_3_4> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Requirement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "Value field accepts text or configuration values for credentialing-specific messaging or parameters; editable and savable." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd05Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "No satisfiedBy — see Annotation_ConfigurabilityModelEvidence. Note the FDD's own example pairs a free-text landing-page-message use case with a numeric fee-amount use case in the SAME flat Value field — direct textual evidence for option (c) ('fully centralized, no per-type variation') in Question_ConfigurabilityModel's three competing shapes, though it doesn't settle the cross-domain-ownership half of that question." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "5.3.4" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a Credential Admin, I want to update the Value of a Credentialing Control, so that I can change associated system text or configurations (e.g. credentialing landing page text or specific fee amounts)." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Update a Credentialing Control's Value" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_05_3_5> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Requirement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "On Save, system captures user identity (Modified By) and timestamp (Modified On), immediately reflected in the results table." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd05Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "No satisfiedBy — see Annotation_ConfigurabilityModelEvidence." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "5.3.5" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a Credential Admin, I want the system to capture Modified By and Modified On audit details when saving changes to the control, so that I can maintain an audit trail of modifications to credentialing configurations." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Capture Modified By/Modified On on Credentialing Control save" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_05_4_1> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Requirement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "Page for managing/viewing batch jobs; filters for Run Date and Batch Job (dropdown of available job names); Search button." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd05Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "No satisfiedBy — see Annotation_BatchJobAdminVisibilityEvidence below (updates cred:Question_BatchJobAdminVisibility)." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "5.4.1" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a Credential Admin, I want to search for batch job status using filters like Run Date and Batch Job name, so that I can monitor specific job history." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Search batch job status by Run Date and Batch Job name" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_05_4_2> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Requirement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "Results table: Batch Job, Run Status, Run Start Date (date+time), Run End Date (date+time), auto-generated Run Status Description." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd05Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "No satisfiedBy — see Annotation_BatchJobAdminVisibilityEvidence. Wireframe05_9 (confirmed by viewing) shows exactly this table, already populated with real run history and free-text status descriptions (e.g. 'File(s) Processed: MDEEducatorLicense_250417.txt (Total 6): processed (0))', 'No records to update')." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "5.4.2" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a Credential Admin, I want to view the Batch job table including Run Status, Run Start/End Dates, and an auto-generated Run Status Description, so that I can easily assess the outcome and duration of past job executions." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "View batch job run history table" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_05_4_3> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Requirement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "Admin selects a batch job from a predefined, fixed list and triggers immediate manual execution; the admin cannot add new batch job types to the list." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd05Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Partial: satisfiedBy points at the two batch jobs this manual-execution capability WOULD apply to if the admin console existed, per credentialing-technical-design.ttl — but no ApiOperation/Sequence models the manual-trigger console itself anywhere in the graph. See Annotation_BatchJobAdminVisibilityEvidence: comment #127 (Dontje, on the Feature 5.4 heading itself) shows the client was still actively discussing whether re-run-on-demand should even be allowed and what authorization it needs, as of the last comment on that thread — i.e. even the source FDD hadn't settled this by the time of ingestion." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "5.4.3" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:BatchJob_CredentialExpirationProcessing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:BatchJob_DefinitionVersionActivation> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a Credential Admin, I want to manually execute a predefined batch job from a list, so that I can run required jobs on demand." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Manually execute a predefined batch job" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_05_4_4> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Requirement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "On manual execution, system records the initiating user's identity and the timestamp of the manual run." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd05Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "No satisfiedBy — see Annotation_BatchJobAdminVisibilityEvidence. Comment #128 (Dontje, anchored to this same acceptance-criteria text) is actually about Feature 5.5's role-vs-individual question, not this story — an apparent comment-anchor drift in the source docx; not treated as bearing on this Requirement." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "5.4.4" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a Credential Admin, I want the system to capture audit details when I manually execute a batch job, so that there is a record of the manual intervention." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Capture audit details for manual batch job execution" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_05_5_1> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Requirement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "The Addendum's own text for this story is a stub ('5.5. / Acceptance Criteria / T') — reconstructed here from the narrative Business Specifications section instead: admin searches by User Type (EPP/School District/Applicant, each with type-specific extra filters), selects a user from results, and manages that user's Worklist assignment (list of worklists) and Report access assignment (list of reports), with audit capture (Modified By/On) on updates." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd05Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "PARTIAL and CONTRADICTED match — see Annotation_WorklistAssignmentRoleVsIndividual below. The narrative text and Wireframes 11-13 (all confirmed by viewing) describe and show INDIVIDUAL-level assignment (searching for and editing a specific named person's worklist/report access), directly matching what credentialing-domain.ttl's own Question_WorklistAssignmentScope already anticipated from the FDD 11/16 pass. But the FINAL review comment on this FDD (203926376, Doherty relaying Yashi, 2026-04-21) reverses this: 'Since worklist and report management is strictly role-based and not assigned at the individual user level, I have completely revised this user story... search for User Roles (filtered by User Type) and manage the worklist and report assignments globally for that role' — directly responding to comment #128 (Dontje: 'We don't want to have users assigned specific/custom access; it needs to remain role-based'). iam:RoleDefinitionAggregate is the correct home for the FINAL (role-based) shape, but it currently has no exposed manage/update API (iam-api.ttl only has read-only Op_ListRoles/Op_GetRole) and no first-class 'worklist' or 'report' concept as an assignable unit distinct from an ordinary Permission — so even the settled version of this requirement is not actually modeled end-to-end anywhere yet." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "5.5.1" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:iam:RoleDefinitionAggregate> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a Credential Admin, I want to assign worklist and/or report access, so that the right staff can see the applications and reports relevant to their job." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Assign worklist and/or report access to a user or role" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_05_5_2> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Requirement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "Also an Addendum stub (title text present, Acceptance Criteria section left empty). Reconstructed from Wireframe05_13 (confirmed by viewing): a 'Manage Report assignment' screen listing reports currently assigned." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd05Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Same contradiction and gap as Req_05_5_1 — see Annotation_WorklistAssignmentRoleVsIndividual. cred:Perm_ReportsView (Cat_Reporting) is the closest existing permission concept but models scope-based report visibility, not an assignable per-user/per-role list of specific named reports." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "5.5.2" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a Credential Admin, I want to view a user's assigned Report access, so that I can verify which reports they are authorized to run." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "View a user's/role's assigned report access" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_05_6> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Requirement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd05Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "5.6" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "The reporting capabilities described for this feature align with the broader reporting functionality defined under Feature 2.1. As outlined in those user stories, administrators (scoped by functional area) are expected to have access to the same reporting capabilities." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Reports (feature-level pointer)" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_11_10_1> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Requirement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "List of uploaded documents with metadata (File Name, File Type/Size, Upload Date, Uploaded By). View/Download in PDF, PNG, or JPEG." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd11_16Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Real improvement over the miedw-v2 pilot pass, which could only cite a placeholder-named docs:DocumentRetrievalOperation stub (documents wasn't a real conversion yet). Documents' now-real API models exactly this shape: docs:Op_SearchDocuments (list by attachment), docs:Op_GetDocumentMetadata (file name/size/upload metadata — docs:DocumentAggregate's own invariants explicitly preserve original filename in metadata), docs:Op_DownloadDocument (SAS-token download). Remaining gap: docs:DocumentAggregate's own metadata doesn't appear to carry an explicit 'Uploaded By' user-identity field in its stored value objects (docs:MalwareScanResultVO/BlobReference/RetentionPolicyVO/LegalHoldVO) — worth confirming whether that's tracked via docs:DocumentAccessLog instead; and no dedicated 'export' (as opposed to plain download) operation or PNG/JPEG-specific handling is called out. Minor, folded into this note rather than a separate Annotation." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "11.10.1" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:Op_DownloadDocument> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:Op_GetDocumentMetadata> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:Op_SearchDocuments> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a user with the Credential Applications role, I want to view, download, and export supporting documents uploaded to a credential application, so that I can verify the applicant's eligibility and ensure all requirements are met before approving or denying the request." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "View, download, and export supporting documents on a credential application" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_11_1_1> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Requirement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "Login and navigate to Home > Credential Management > Permits. Landing page has Open Applications and Closed Applications tabs (each showing counts). Search field supports partial match across Unique ID, Name, and Email with the standard hover text. Results table: Name, Email Address, UID, etc. User can filter on all columns and download results as Doc/Excel/Pdf. 'No results found' message shown/cleared per the standard eligibility-exclusion pattern." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd11_16Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Partial match only: cred:Op_ListApplications (generic GET /applications) has no Open/Closed tab concept, no Unique-ID/Name/Email combined search, and no Doc/Excel/Pdf export. Per comments #45-48, the Open/Applications-needing-Attention tab concept was itself revised mid-review ('the wireframe has been updated to remove the concept... new wireframe has been attached'), so this acceptance criteria may already be stale relative to the current (unattached) wireframe. See Question_MissingWorklistSearchAndExportUX (shared with 11.5.1/16.1.4) for the recurring search/export gap." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "11.1.1" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Op_ListApplications> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a Business User with a Temporary Credential role, I want to view the Permits landing page so that I can search, renew, and manage permit applications." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Permits landing page: search, renew, and manage permit applications" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_11_1_2> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Requirement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "Application Number column displayed as a clickable hyperlink; clicking opens the detailed credential view page; Cancel returns to the Permits page." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd11_16Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Direct match: GET /applications/{applicationId} is exactly this. Comments #56-58 clarify this links via Application Number, not Credential Number, after an earlier draft confusion ('I'm confused... if the search here is referring to the screen above, then the column will have Application number as hyperlink and not the Credential number') — the acceptance criteria above already reflects the corrected version." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "11.1.2" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Op_GetApplication> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a Business User with a Temporary Credential role, I want the table on the Permits Page to display the Application number as a hyperlink, so that I can open a detailed view of the credential when necessary." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Application number as hyperlink to detailed credential view" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_11_1_3> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Requirement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "Dropdown on Permits landing page includes 'Renew Daily Substitutes' among several new-application options. Renewal landing page: eligibility text, partial-match search (Unique ID/Name/Email), results filtered to exclude actionable-PPR-flag records, checkbox multi-select, final price shown after selection, records with expired PPR shown but blocked from renewal (with notify-and-continue option), Review page with advisory + 3 attestation checkboxes, Submit, then a confirmation page offering 'Continue to Payment' or 'Pay Later' (moves applications to an 'Unpaid Application Fees' queue)." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd11_16Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Core bulk-submission flow matches Op_InitiateBulkRenewals/Seq_BulkRenewalInitiation well. Two confirmed gaps, both re-checked against the now-real cross-domain graphs: (1) the 3-checkbox attestation flow is richer than credentialing-technical-design.ttl's TP_ElectronicSignatureAttestationCapture (a single typed-name field) — see Question_ESignatureLegalSufficiency (already modeled in credentialing-technical-design.ttl), now also linked from here; (2) the 'Pay Later'/'Unpaid Application Fees' queue has no backing endpoint anywhere — payments-sequences.ttl's OWN SequenceReference on `GET /applications/pending-payment?districtId=...` already says 'No such path in payments-api.yml', independently corroborating this exact gap from the Payments side, not just Credentialing's. Per comments #62/63, this story was agreed to need splitting from a 'new permit application' story that got tangled into the same acceptance criteria — the acceptance criteria above already isolates the renewal-specific parts." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "11.1.3" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Op_InitiateBulkRenewals> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Seq_BulkRenewalInitiation> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a MiEdWorkforce Business User with the Credential Application role, I want to select multiple eligible educators and submit their renewal applications at once, so that I can efficiently manage large volumes of permit renewals." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Bulk-select eligible educators and submit renewal applications at once" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_11_2_1> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Requirement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "Dashboard shows a 'Temporary Credential Guidance' tile, restricted to the Business User/Temporary Credential role, listing all guidance docs defined by the Credentialing Admin; each is viewable/previewable and downloadable as PDF; 'No guidance documents available' message when empty." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd11_16Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "cred:Perm_GuidanceView exists but has no backing ApiOperation or Sequence in credentialing-api.ttl/credentialing-sequences.ttl. Documents' now-real category-scoped document model (docs:DocumentCategoryAggregate, docs:Op_SearchDocuments/Op_DownloadDocument, both internal-service — meant to be called by another domain's own backend, exactly this shape) is a genuinely plausible underlying mechanism, an improvement on the pilot's finding of nothing at all behind this permission — but no credentialing-owned endpoint composes them into a role-gated 'guidance tile' list, and no 'guidance' DocumentCategory instance is declared anywhere. Per comment #70 (Punniyamoorthy: 'the download, view/open is outside the scope of MiEd' since the guidance documents live in Documents capability) this split is intentional, similar to the existing PDF-generation split with TP_CertificatePdfGeneration. Not fully resolved here — see Question_GuidanceDocumentTileGap below." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "11.2.1" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Perm_GuidanceView> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:Op_DownloadDocument> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:Op_SearchDocuments> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a MiEdWorkforce user with the Business user/Temporary Credential role, I want Temporary Credential guidance documents to be available on the dashboard, so that I can easily access relevant information." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Temporary Credential guidance documents on dashboard" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_11_2_2> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Requirement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "Dashboard shows a 'Certificate Guidance' tile, Citizen-only, listing all Certificate guidance docs; each viewable/openable and downloadable; must work on desktop and mobile; empty-state message." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd11_16Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Same gap as 11.2.1 — Wireframe5 (the Citizen 'I Want to' home page) shows a 'Certification Guidance Documents' button matching this story, but no backing endpoint composes the role-gated tile. Comments #72/73 debated whether the empty-state message is even a real requirement ('I don't think there will be a scenario where there will be no guidance documents' / 'There could be a lapse... upon implementation or when being reviewed') — resolved in favor of keeping it." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "11.2.2" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Perm_GuidanceView> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:Op_DownloadDocument> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:Op_SearchDocuments> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a MiEdWorkforce Citizen user, I want Certificate guidance documents to be available on the dashboard, so that I can easily access relevant information." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Certificate guidance documents on dashboard (Citizen)" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_11_3> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Requirement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd11_16Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Self-referential pointer within the same FDD, not a standalone requirement — content lives in 11.5's 'view applicant's current and historical data' story and 16.4's Historical Records feature. Cross-referenced for completeness, not double-counted as its own gap." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "11.3" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Seq_ViewDefinitionHistory> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "All user stories regarding the Business and Admin users' ability to view the citizen user's historical data can be found within the user stories associated with other features in this FDD." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Historical Data (feature-level pointer)" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_11_4_1> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Requirement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "System checks PPR flag and Needs Responses flag per permit during a renewal search. Includes: Needs Responses = N AND (no PPR flag OR non-actionable PPR flag). Excludes: actionable PPR flag AND Needs Responses = Y." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd11_16Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Genuine coverage gap, re-confirmed against the now-real profpractice-domain.ttl (grepped for 'Needs Responses'/'NeedsResponse': zero hits): 'Needs Responses' is a distinct flag from ProfessionalPracticeStatus (Clear/ConditionalClearance/Hold/Blocked) and exists in neither credentialing-domain.ttl's CredentialApplication/IssuedCredential model NOR profpractice's own real DisclosureAggregate/EducatorPPRStatusAggregate model — this FDD's PPR-flag-plus-Needs-Responses-flag combination is more granular than what either domain's real conversion has modeled, on both sides of the boundary." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "11.4.1" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Rule_ProfessionalPracticeClearance> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a Business User, I want the Renewal and Bulk Renewal search to display only Daily Substitute Permit records that meet the eligibility criteria based on the PPR and Needs Responses flags, so that I can identify and renew only those permits that are eligible for processing." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Renewal search filtered by PPR and Needs-Responses flags" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_11_5_1> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Requirement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "Evaluate every submission against eligibility rules (PPR flags, Needs Responses, MTTC scores, expiration status, renewal count, academic year, in/out-of-state, payment, other Business Rule Management rules). If met: auto-approve, auto-issue, no worklist task, confirmation email. If not: route to the correct worklist (Permits/Career Authorization, Special Education, Educator Standard/Professional, School Nurse, School Administrator, Additional Endorsements, Renewal License, Candidate Tracking) by credential type/status/PPR/Needs-Responses; create a worklist task for the Citizen to fill out PPR when applicable. Each worklist has its own defined search filters and result columns." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd11_16Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "The routing/auto-approve LOGIC matches Rule_AutoApprovalCriteria/Rule_ManualReviewTriggering/Seq_ApplicationAutoApproval closely, and the PPR-flag check is now corroborated by a real cross-domain operation: profp:Op_GetEducatorPprStatus IS the same GET /educators/{id}/ppr-clearance credentialing's own Rule_ProfessionalPracticeClearance already stubbed as profp:PPRClearanceOperation (profpractice-api.ttl reuses that exact IRI verbatim) — a genuine corroboration the pilot pass couldn't make with profpractices still a stub. The discrete NAMED worklists with per-type search filters/result columns remain a separate, unmodeled UX layer — see Question_MissingWorklistSearchAndExportUX. Wireframe6/Wireframe7 are the visual evidence for this gap: real filter fields (Has conviction?, Use alternative pass, SSN) and an MTTC Information sub-panel with no corresponding ApiOperation anywhere. This also directly corroborates Question_WorklistAssignmentScope (credentialing-domain.ttl, Open Question #34) — the FDD independently describes real, named, filterable worklists, not just 'anyone holding the approve permission for this scope.'" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "11.5.1" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Rule_AutoApprovalCriteria> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Rule_ManualReviewTriggering> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Seq_ApplicationAutoApproval> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:profpractices:Op_GetEducatorPprStatus> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As the MiEdWorkforce system, I want to automatically approve credential applications or route them to the appropriate worklist based on business rules, so that applications are processed efficiently and consistently without manual intervention." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Auto-approve or route credential applications to the correct worklist" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_11_5_2> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Requirement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "Credential Administrator role only. Works on Valid and Expired. Admin enters a reason (predefined or free text) and may notify educator/employing districts. Status updates immediately across worklists/dashboards/profile. Audit entry: Username/ID, Date/time, Previous Status, New Status. Suspended/Revoked items unusable for any credentialing function. Confirmation message shown." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd11_16Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Strong direct match on the core action. 'Suspend/revoke EXPIRED credentials' is new detail — cred:IssuedCredentialAggregate's invariants only explicitly discuss Valid credentials being suspended/revoked; extending to Expired is consistent with the existing state model (Expired is not terminal) but wasn't explicitly called out before. Reason-capture and notify-district are not modeled as distinct fields anywhere; minor gap, folded into this note rather than a separate Annotation." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "11.5.2" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Op_RevokeCredential> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Op_SuspendCredential> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Rule_CredentialStatusTransitions> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Seq_SuspendOrRevokeCredential> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a MiEdWorkforce Credential Administrator, I want to suspend or revoke a certificate, credential (whether valid or expired), so that I can enforce compliance, address violations, and manage educator credential statuses appropriately." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Suspend or revoke a certificate/credential (valid or expired)" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_11_5_3> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Requirement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "Credential Administrator role only. Applies to endorsements, not certificates directly. Nullified endorsements cannot be reactivated (re-application required). System should warn or prevent nullification that would leave a certificate with zero endorsements (unless the certificate type allows it). Status updates immediately; audit entry as above; educator and district notified." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd11_16Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Good direct match on the core action. Genuine gap: the 'warn or prevent zero-endorsement certificates' rule is a new invariant not present on cred:IssuedEndorsementAggregate or cred:IssuedCredentialAggregate today." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "11.5.3" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Op_NullifyEndorsement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Seq_NullifyEndorsement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a MiEdWorkforce Credential Administrator, I want to nullify an endorsement (whether valid or expired), so that I can permanently invalidate endorsements that were issued in error or violate requirements." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Nullify an endorsement (valid or expired)" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_11_5_4> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Requirement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "Admin selects a citizen user, clicks Add Certificate, application still runs the full business-rule validation (eligibility, endorsement matching, academic year, coursework, validity period, MTTC) — cannot save if rules fail, with clear error messages. Admin can add/edit/save internal remarks (predefined templates or free text), not visible to Citizen/Business users. Action recorded in audit history including timestamp, certificate type, rule validations applied, and remarks." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd11_16Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Strong, previously-missing corroboration re-confirmed in mied-v3: cred:Perm_ApplicationManualSubmit's own notes already say 'for bulk data entry, historical corrections, or single-application submission on behalf of an educator who cannot access the system (application still passes through standard validations — not a bypass)' — almost verbatim what this story describes — but no single-application ApiOperation or Sequence exists anywhere in credentialing-api.ttl/credentialing-sequences.ttl (only cred:Op_InitiateBulkRenewals for the bulk path; no 'Op_InitiateApplication'-style single-admin-submit endpoint was added between the pilot pass and this one). Real, still-undetected-in-code coverage gap." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "11.5.4" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Perm_ApplicationManualSubmit> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a MiEdWorkforce Credential Administrator, I want to submit a credential application on behalf of a Citizen User, so that I can process necessary credentials for educators who cannot access the system or rectify administrative errors while ensuring the application passes through standard system validations." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Admin submits a credential application on behalf of a Citizen User" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_11_6> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Requirement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd11_16Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "11.6" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "All underlying logic for sending, tracking, and displaying emails, alerts and notifications are derived from Business Specification #6 (Alerts, Emails & Communications). This feature is strictly limited to the configuration of these tools specifically for the Educator Credentialing module." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Email/Communication (feature-level pointer)" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_11_7> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Requirement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd11_16Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "11.7" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "All underlying logic for the display, organization, and rendering of the dashboard is derived from Business Specification #3 (Dashboards). This feature is strictly limited to the configuration of these elements specifically for the Educator Credentialing workflow." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Dashboard (feature-level pointer)" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_11_8_1> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Requirement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "Retrieve Test Code(s) from Business Rule Management's Endorsement-to-Test-Code mapping. Search the MTTC Data Store (populated via Pearson integration) by Unique ID (or SSN) + Test Code. Link the most recent passing score. If multiple tests map to one endorsement and 'All Tests Required' is active, verify status for all required codes." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd11_16Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "The AND/OR combination logic on EndorsementDefinition.RequiredAssessments matches the 'All Tests Required' flag concept well. The Pearson-integration reality-check is now RESOLVED by reading the Interface Design document (see Question_MttcPearsonIntegrationRealityCheck below): 'the MTTC Data Store (populated via Pearson integration)' this story describes is, concretely, cred:AssessmentResultAggregate records populated by cred:Op_ImportAssessmentResults/cred:Seq_ImportAssessmentResults — an admin manually downloads a monthly fixed-width file from a Pearson website (per the interface doc, 'Incoming File (Prod & Test): N/A (manual process today)') and bulk-imports it. There is no live per-applicant query against Pearson itself; 'populated via Pearson integration' describes this monthly manual-import pipeline, matching credentialing-domain.md's own 'Data Source (Current State): manual entry from uploaded score reports' almost exactly." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "11.8.1" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:AssessmentResultAggregate> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Op_ImportAssessmentResults> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Rule_SubjectAreaAssessmentValidation> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a System, I must automatically reference an educator's stored MTTC score(s) when they select an endorsement during a credential application, so that the correct test results are associated with the requested subject area without manual data entry." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Automatically reference an educator's stored MTTC score(s) on endorsement selection" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_11_8_1i> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:UserStory> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "Provides a secure file-upload interface for the MTTC EdReports file; parses the standard Pearson fixed-width file layout (Last Name, First Name, Middle Initial, SSN, Test Code, Test Date, Pass/Fail status, Numeric Score); provides upload status (success/failure) and logs the date/time of the batch upload." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd11_8MttcDoc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Strong, direct match: cred:Op_ImportAssessmentResults/cred:Seq_ImportAssessmentResults is exactly this workflow (admin selects provider, uploads CSV/XLSX, system parses provider-specific schema, keeps highest score on retake, publishes AssessmentResultImported per row) — asp:AssessmentProviderSystem's own integrationNotes independently confirm this current-state manual-upload framing ('Pearson-MTTC, ETS-Praxis... do not integrate via API today. Educators/admins manually upload score reports... credentialing.assessment-result.import lets an admin bulk-import a provider's CSV/XLSX export'). The FDD's incoming layout is fixed-width, not CSV/XLSX as asp:AssessmentProviderSystem's note assumes — a minor format-detail mismatch, not a functional gap (the existing Op/Seq's own escape-hatch request-body modeling doesn't care about field-delimiter specifics)." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "11.8.1i" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:assessmentprovider:AssessmentProviderSystem> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Op_ImportAssessmentResults> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Seq_ImportAssessmentResults> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As an OEE Administrator (MTTC Specialist), I want to manually upload the monthly MTTC EdReports bulk data file into MiEdWorkforce, so that educators' test scores are updated in the system while we wait for Pearson's API to become fully available." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Manual bulk file upload of MTTC scores" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_11_8_2> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Requirement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "If a passing MTTC score is required and none is on file, block submission with an error (not: flag after submission). If the endorsement requires no test (e.g. certain World Languages), bypass score validation. If no passing score for a Temporary Credential, dynamically present alternative eligibility questions per the Business Rule Management decision tree. If all criteria including MTTC pass, mark eligible for Auto-Approval." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd11_16Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Real contradiction, not just a gap: credentialing-domain.ttl's Rule_ManualReviewTriggering lists 'required assessment results missing or failing' as a condition that flags an application for MANUAL REVIEW after submission. This FDD's own comment thread (#120 Punniyamoorthy: 'There is no need to flag the application for missing/fail MTTC score as the system will not allow the applicant to proceed to submit the application without the passing test score' / #121 Dontje: 'Agree') establishes the opposite: missing/failing MTTC should HARD-BLOCK submission, never reach manual review at all. See Question_ManualReviewVsHardBlockForMttc below — a genuine disagreement between two source documents, not resolved here." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "11.8.2" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Rule_AutoApprovalCriteria> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Rule_SubjectAreaAssessmentValidation> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a System, I must use the referenced MTTC score status to validate eligibility against Business Rules, so that I can automatically prevent the issuance of credentials to unqualified candidates or flag them for review." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Use MTTC score status to validate eligibility and gate submission" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_11_8_2i> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:UserStory> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "Establishes an interface to connect with Pearson's system via API to receive MTTC scores; maps incoming Pearson data to CEDS data elements; processes the integration on a scheduled interval (e.g. daily or monthly)." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd11_8MttcDoc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Explicitly a FUTURE capability per this story's own text ('...in the future'), and asp:AssessmentProviderSystem's own integrationNotes in credentialing-domain.ttl already say the same thing independently ('May transition to API integration in the future'). Not a new finding — this pass corroborates an already-documented, already-deferred future item rather than surfacing it for the first time." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "11.8.2i" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As the MiEdWorkforce System, I need to automatically retrieve MTTC test scores from Pearson via an API connection, so that educator records can be updated in near real-time without relying on manual monthly file uploads in the future." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Automated MTTC EdReports API integration" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_11_8_3> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Requirement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "'MTTC Information' section: Test Name, Test Code, Status (Passed/Failed), Date Passed, Exam Date. Highlight endorsements whose required test code has no 'Passed' status. Viewable even for tests taken prior to the current application." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd11_16Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "No satisfiedBy: no ApiOperation or Sequence exposes this view anywhere in credentialing-api.ttl/credentialing-sequences.ttl. Wireframe7 shows exactly this 'MTTC Information' table with the same columns the acceptance criteria lists — strong visual confirmation the requirement is real and specific, not speculative. Genuine coverage gap." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "11.8.3" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a Credential Administrator or Credential Processor, I want to view the detailed MTTC test history for an applicant within the application review screen, so that I can verify they have passed the specific tests required for the requested endorsements." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "View detailed MTTC test history within the application review screen" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_11_8_3i> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:UserStory> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "Attempts to match incoming scores to an existing educator profile using demographic data (SSN, Name, DOB, with a long-term transition toward Unique ID); on a confident match, automatically applies Test Code, Date, and Pass/Fail status; on an unconfident/failed match (e.g. name mismatch or missing profile), flags the record and routes it to a manual resolution queue for the MTTC Specialist." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd11_8MttcDoc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Parsing itself matches cred:Seq_ImportAssessmentResults well. The MATCHING logic does not: the existing sequence validates that an educator ID ALREADY exists and simply skips-and-logs the row if not ('Invalid educator ID > Skip row, log error') — it has no fuzzy demographic matching (SSN/Name/DOB) and no manual-resolution-queue concept at all. This story asks for meaningfully more sophisticated identity-resolution behavior than what's built. See Question_MttcIdentityMatchingNotBuilt below." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "11.8.3i" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Seq_ImportAssessmentResults> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As the MiEdWorkforce System, I must parse the ingested MTTC EdReports data (whether via bulk upload or API) and match the test scores to the appropriate educator profiles, so that credential processors can accurately verify endorsement eligibility." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "MTTC data parsing and educator identity matching" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_11_9> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Requirement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd11_16Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Not a gap in Credentialing's own modeling — the FDD itself says this can't be written yet because an upstream spec (FDD 15) isn't finished. Tracked here so it doesn't silently disappear from the coverage picture; revisit once FDD 15 exists. Note: iam-domain.ttl is now a real conversion, but it documents IAM's OWN identity-matching/authorization model (Mi-Key, near-match resolution, etc.), not the specific FDD-15 user stories this pointer awaits — so this remains genuinely pending, not incidentally resolved by IAM's real conversion existing." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "11.9" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "User stories for this feature are currently pending and will be developed upon completion of the related business specification, User Management - Identity Management Integration (15)." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "pending" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Identity Management Integration (feature-level pointer, pending)" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_12_1_1> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:UserStory> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "The system allows the System Administrator to access the 'Add Endorsement' administrative screen. The system allows the System Administrator to select SCED as the mapping type. The system allows the System Administrator to enter or select a valid SCED code as assignment criteria. The system allows the System Administrator to select one or more allowable endorsements associated with the SCED code. The system includes all active credential types, including temporary credentials, in the list of allowable endorsements. The system validates that required mapping inputs are provided before allowing the mapping to be saved. Upon save, the system stores the mapping and makes it available for audit and validation processes. Audit details are stored including Time/Date stamp and User ID." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd12Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "No satisfiedBy asserted — see Question_AssignmentEndorsementMappingNotModeled below. wireframe-01 (cred:WireframeAddEndorsementMapping, viewed) shows the screen actually embedded here is credentialing's existing per-Endorsement Requirements editor (grade bands, test codes, certificate/permit checkboxes) — a real, useful screen, but for editing ONE cred:EndorsementDefinitionAggregate's own requirements, not for authoring a reusable, admin-maintained SCED-code -> endorsement-set mapping catalog distinct from any single endorsement's definition. Confirms (rather than resolves) the gap." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "12.1.1" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a MiEdWorkforce System Administrator, I want to define mappings between SCED codes and allowable endorsements, so that the system can identify educator assignments that are out of alignment with credential requirements." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Define SCED-to-endorsement mapping" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_12_1_2> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:UserStory> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "The system allows the System Administrator to select Grades/Educational Setting as the mapping type. The system allows the System Administrator to define grade level and educational setting criteria. The system allows the System Administrator to associate one or more allowable endorsements to the defined criteria. The system includes all active credential types, including temporary credentials, when defining allowable endorsements. The system prevents saving if required criteria or endorsements are not defined. The system saves valid mappings and applies them to placement audit logic. Audit details of the mapping are stored including Time/Date stamp and User ID." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd12Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "No satisfiedBy asserted — same mapping-catalog gap as 12.1.1, see Question_AssignmentEndorsementMappingNotModeled below." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "12.1.2" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a MiEdWorkforce System Administrator, I want to define mappings between grade levels and educational settings to allowable endorsements, so that educator placement can be evaluated across different instructional environments." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Define Grade/Educational-Setting-to-endorsement mapping" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_12_1_3> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:UserStory> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "The system allows the System Administrator to select CTE CIP as the mapping type. The system allows the System Administrator to define a CIP code as assignment criteria. The system allows the System Administrator to associate allowable endorsements with the CIP code. The system includes all active credential types, including temporary credentials, in the endorsement selection. The system validates that both assignment criteria and endorsements are present before saving. Saved mappings are applied to identify CTE placement records that are out of alignment. Audit details of the mapping are stored including Time/Date stamp and User ID." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd12Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "No satisfiedBy asserted — same mapping-catalog gap as 12.1.1, see Question_AssignmentEndorsementMappingNotModeled below." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "12.1.3" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a MiEdWorkforce System Administrator, I want to define mappings between CTE CIP codes and allowable endorsements, so that career and technical education assignments can be audited for appropriate placement." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Define CTE-CIP-to-endorsement mapping" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_12_1_4> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:UserStory> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "The system applies defined mappings during employee and credential audit processes. The system identifies individual records that do not meet the defined placement criteria. The system makes out-of-alignment records available for review through audit reports or worklists. The system does not modify educator assignment data as part of this identification process." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd12Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "No satisfiedBy asserted. staff:Rule_EndorsementAlignmentForTeaching ('A Teacher position assignment with reported course details (SCED code and grade span) requires the employee to hold endorsements covering that content area and grade level') is a real, closely-related mechanism enforced by staff:AssignmentAggregate — but it is a real-time, single-assignment BLOCKING check at assignment-creation time, not a batch/audit-report identification of already-existing out-of-alignment records against an admin-maintained mapping catalog, and it isn't driven by anything resembling the SCED/Grade-Setting/CIP mapping tables 12.1.1-12.1.3 ask for (the rule presumably checks endorsement coverage directly, with no separate mapping-table indirection). Grouped with 12.1.1-12.1.3 under Question_AssignmentEndorsementMappingNotModeled below since the audit-report capability this story asks for depends on the same missing mapping catalog." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "12.1.4" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a MiEdWorkforce System Administrator, I want the system to use defined assignment-to-endorsement mappings to identify records that are out of alignment, so that audit and corrective actions can occur." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Apply mappings to identify out-of-alignment placement records" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_12_1_5> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:UserStory> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "When a Credential Admin or Staffing Admin adds a new credential, endorsement, or assignment type, the system generates a Dashboard Notification/Alert that requires action for the System Administrator. The notification includes identifying information about the newly added item. The notification requires acknowledgment and resolution by the System Administrator. The notification remains active until the required placement mappings are defined or the item is otherwise resolved." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd12Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Good match on mechanism: comm:AlertAggregate's own role/scope-targeted, event-triggered dashboard-alert model (comm:Seq_DashboardAlertCreationAndDisplay: an arbitrary domain event on the EventBus triggers alert creation, targeted by role, with an action link, persisting until resolved) is exactly this story's shape. One real, narrower gap: no SequenceReference or subscribesTo edge currently wires a specific credentialing/staffing event (e.g. cred:EndorsementDefinitionCreatedEvent, which adt:AuditContext and refd:ReferenceDataContext already subscribe to) into this alert-creation path — the generic mechanism exists, but this specific trigger isn't concretely connected to it. Not raised as a separate Annotation given how much of the story the generic mechanism otherwise covers." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "12.1.5" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:AlertAggregate> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:Op_CreateAlert> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:Seq_DashboardAlertCreationAndDisplay> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a MiEdWorkforce System Administrator, I want to receive an action item when a new credential, endorsement, or assignment type is added by another administrator, so that required placement mappings can be defined." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Receive action item when a new credential/endorsement/assignment type is added" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_12_1_6> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:UserStory> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "The system allows the System Administrator to access alerts/notifications regarding missing mappings from their dashboard or notification area. The system allows the System Administrator to review the details of the item (credential, endorsement, or assignment) requiring mapping. The system allows the System Administrator to define the appropriate mappings using the existing mapping interface. The system automatically clears/resolves the alert once the required mappings are saved (or provides a mechanism to dismiss if the mapping is not applicable). The system records the resolution/modification in the audit." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd12Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Good match for the alert-resolution half (comm:Seq_UserResolvesDashboardAlert's own ownership-validated, audit-timestamped resolve flow). The 'define the appropriate mappings using the existing mapping interface' half depends on the same missing mapping catalog as 12.1.1-12.1.4 (Question_AssignmentEndorsementMappingNotModeled) — not re-targeted by that Annotation since the dominant, alert-specific half of this story is solidly covered. Review comment id 35/36 (Groom/Doherty, 2026-04-15): Groom asks to discuss 'action items, and the status throughout the resolution process' — Doherty's reply is only 'Noted,' leaving open exactly what intermediate status states (e.g. In Progress, Escalated) an action item can hold beyond comm:AlertState_Active/Resolved/Expired. A real, still-open design question, not resolved by this pass." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "12.1.6" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:Op_ResolveAlert> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:Seq_UserResolvesDashboardAlert> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a MiEdWorkforce System Administrator, I want to resolve action items by defining required assignment-to-endorsement mappings, so that the system remains aligned with current credential and assignment definitions." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Resolve action items by defining required mappings" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_12_1_7> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:UserStory> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "The system records changes made to assignment-to-endorsement mappings. The system retains historical information about when mappings were created or updated. The system records the specific Username/User ID of the administrator who made the change. Audit history is available for review as part of compliance and reporting needs." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd12Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "No satisfiedBy asserted: an audit trail over mapping changes presupposes the mapping entity itself, which doesn't exist — see Question_AssignmentEndorsementMappingNotModeled below." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "12.1.7" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a MiEdWorkforce System Administrator, I want the system to retain audit details for changes made to assignment-to-endorsement mappings, so that traceability and compliance requirements are met." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Retain audit details for mapping changes" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_16_1_1> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Requirement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "Assign to the sub-worklist matching Credential Type (Certificates/Permits/Career Authorizations/Special Education Approvals). If PPR Admin Flag = On, place in 'PPR Hold' status regardless of other criteria. Assign to exactly one active worklist; update the assignment automatically on status change; display the assigned worklist on the application details screen." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd11_16Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "'Assign to exactly one ACTIVE worklist' and 'display the assigned worklist on the application' is the clearest FDD-level statement yet that discrete, named worklist assignment is real product behavior — directly reinforcing Question_WorklistAssignmentScope (credentialing-domain.ttl, Open Question #34) and Question_MissingWorklistSearchAndExportUX below. Strong corroboration of an existing finding, not a new one." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "16.1.1" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Rule_ManualReviewTriggering> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Rule_ProfessionalPracticeClearance> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a Credential Processor I want applications to be routed to the correct worklist so that they can be reviewed by the appropriate team." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Route applications to the correct worklist" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_16_1_2> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Requirement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "Evaluate Business Rule Management eligibility on submission; auto-approve and auto-issue if met; no worklist task created; record approval in the audit log." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd11_16Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Direct match, no gaps identified." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "16.1.2" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Rule_AutoApprovalCriteria> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Seq_ApplicationAutoApproval> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a Credential Processor I want eligible applications to be auto approved so that certificates can be issued without manual intervention." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Auto-approve eligible applications" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_16_1_3> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Requirement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "Block auto-approval when any eligibility rule fails; assign to a review worklist; display ineligibility reasons to authorized users; do not issue until explicit approval." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd11_16Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Direct match. Per comment #127 (Punniyamoorthy: 'ineligible applications - doesn't sound right, applications that do not meet auto-approval are sent to worklist for review. If they are not eligible then system should have stopped them from submission' / Dontje: 'Agree') the FDD's own wording was corrected during review — 'require manual review' means 'didn't qualify for the fast path,' not 'is ineligible to exist as an application' — consistent with how Rule_ManualReviewTriggering is already modeled, no change needed here." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "16.1.3" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Rule_ManualReviewTriggering> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Seq_ApplicationManualReviewAndApproval> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a Credential Processor I want applications to require manual review so that incorrect certificates are not issued." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Require manual review when eligibility rules fail" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_16_1_4> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Requirement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "Search filters specific to each worklist type (Permit/Career Authorization/Special Education Approvals; Certificate), filterable per column, sortable, hyperlinked application numbers, 'No results found' empty state, downloadable as Word/Excel/Pdf." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd11_16Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "No satisfiedBy: same structural gap as 11.1.1/11.5.1 — see Question_MissingWorklistSearchAndExportUX." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "16.1.4" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a Credential Processor I want to search and view credential worklists so that I can locate applications efficiently." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Search and view credential worklists" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_16_2_1> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Requirement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "Allow status updates to predefined values (Submitted, Approved, Denied, On Hold, and others per credentialing-domain.md's fuller state list). Restrict by role. Log all changes (timestamp, User ID, previous/current status) under a History tab. Display current status on the application summary page." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd11_16Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Approve/Deny are covered; 'On Hold' is not — this is the exact same gap credentialing-permissions.ttl's own notes already flagged on cred:Perm_ApplicationPlaceHold ('no API operation exists for this permission yet') and credentialing-sequences.ttl's own SequenceReference on the same `POST /applications/{id}/on-hold` call (resolutionStatus \"no-such-endpoint\"), both still true in mied-v3. This FDD story is independent, later confirmation of the same known gap, not a new one." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "16.2.1" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Op_ApproveApplication> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Op_DenyApplication> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a Credential Processor I want to update the status of an application so that it reflects its current position in the workflow." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Update application status through the workflow" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_16_2_2> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Requirement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "Free-form editing; visibility restricted to authorized users; deletable by admins; audit history (Modified By, Modified On)." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd11_16Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Matches cred:ApplicationProcessingNotes (DomainEntity: 'Internal comments from credential processors, attached to an application'). This FDD's generic 'restricted to authorized users' is consistent with, not more specific than, credentialing's existing access-gating notes on that entity." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "16.2.2" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:ApplicationProcessingNotes> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a Credential Administrator I want to enter internal comments so that internal staff can collaborate." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Enter internal comments for staff collaboration" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_16_3> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Requirement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd11_16Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "16.3" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "All underlying logic for sending, tracking, and displaying emails, alerts and notifications are derived from Business Specification #6 (Alerts, Emails & Communications). This feature is strictly limited to the configuration of these tools specifically for the Educator Credentialing module." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Email/Communication (feature-level pointer)" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_16_4_1> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Requirement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "Clicking a Username hyperlink displays current and historical certificates, permits and endorsements, uploaded documents, enrollment and conviction data, and Demographic/Employment/Education information. Access restricted by role. Data retained per the State Retention Policy." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd11_16Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "No single consolidated 'educator history' view/endpoint exists anywhere across the graph — that core finding from the miedw-v2 pilot pass still stands, but it is now visible as a NAMED cross-domain aggregation gap rather than a wholesale absence, now that epp/profpractices/documents are real conversions: epp:Op_SearchCandidateEnrollments (enrollment info), profp:Op_ListDisclosures (conviction/disclosure info), docs:Op_SearchDocuments (uploaded documents) are each real, individually-callable operations that WOULD need to be composed by a single 'view educator history' screen — no such composing operation/sequence exists in credentialing, epp, profpractices, or documents today. Demographic/Employment/Education information isn't clearly owned by any of these four domains either (iam holds identity-matching data, not employment/education history) — see Question_HistoricalRecordsCompositionGap below. The 'State Retention Policy' reference is new and doesn't correspond to anything in the graph — captured as a Solution-level NFR below rather than invented as a credentialing-specific rule, per this project's convention of attaching NFRs at the sd:Solution root." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "16.4.1" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:Op_SearchDocuments> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:epp:Op_SearchCandidateEnrollments> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:profpractices:Op_ListDisclosures> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a Credential Processor I want to view historical records so that I can make informed decisions." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "View historical records" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_17_1_0> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Requirement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "See body text — condensed into Req_17_1_1 through Req_17_1_5's individual acceptance criteria below; this Requirement exists so the narrative section (as opposed to the Addendum's discrete user stories) is itself accounted for once, not left implicitly uncovered." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd17DailySubDoc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Strong direct match: cred:Seq_SubmitPermitApplication's own whatWhenWho already says 'district/ISD/staffing-agency user submits... educators never self-submit a permit application' and its actor is explicitly 'District/ISD/Staffing Agency User' — this FDD is exactly that flow. See Question_ApplicationStatusVocabularyMismatch below for the one real gap found in this flow (the FDD's Pending PPR/Conviction Review/Pending Evaluation/Pending Payment/Approved status-and-Needs-Responses-flag vocabulary does not map cleanly onto cred:CredentialApplicationAggregate's AppState_* enumeration, and 'Needs Responses' itself is not a modeled field anywhere)." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "17.0" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Op_AdminIssuePermit> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Rule_AutoApprovalCriteria> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Rule_ProfessionalPracticeClearance> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Seq_SubmitPermitApplication> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "The FDD's main 'Business Specifications' narrative (distinct from the numbered Addendum below) describes the full org-submitted permit application flow: Unique-ID search with PPR-flag gating, permit-type selection, academic-year confirmation, the valid-teaching-certificate and 60-semester-hour/2.0-GPA eligibility questions, attestation/digital signature, and a confirmation message that varies by (application status x Needs Responses flag) combination." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Submit Daily Substitute Permit application (end-to-end narrative flow)" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_17_1_1> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Requirement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "Requires appropriate profile permissions. Navigate Dashboard > Roster of Employees. Clicking the Name hyperlink opens the educator's profile. Navigate to the Credentials tab; see options to apply for Permit/Career Authorization/Special Education Approval. System displays Apply or Cancel." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd17DailySubDoc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Wireframes 2-6 (all confirmed by viewing) are direct visual confirmation of this exact navigation path (nav menu > Employment Management > Roster of Employees > educator profile > Credentials/Permits tab > Apply for Permit). Comment (Sinha, 2026-03-18, unresolved/no reply on record): 'A district can also use the Person/ID search to initiate a temporary credential' — a second entry point (direct Person/ID search rather than Roster of Employees) not otherwise described in the FDD body text; not modeled as a separate Requirement since it's an alternate path to the same Op_AdminIssuePermit call, but worth surfacing since it implies at least one other search UI (Personnel Search, per wireframe-2's own nav) feeds the same flow." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "17.1.1" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Op_AdminIssuePermit> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Perm_PermitIssue> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a School district/ISD user, I want to Search for an educator by Unique ID, so that I can easily initiate a temporary credential application for the correct individual." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Search for an educator by Unique ID to initiate a temporary credential application" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_17_1_2> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Requirement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "If the Unique ID has a PPR flag indicating an actionable offense, display: 'Adverse actions have been taken on a credential for this individual...' when the user clicks Apply for Permit/Career Authorization/Special Education Approval. If the PPR flag is allowable/eligible (e.g. non-actionable misdemeanor), allow the user to proceed." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd17DailySubDoc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Direct match on the Blocked/Clear-or-ConditionalClearance branching already modeled in Rule_ProfessionalPracticeClearance and dramatized identically in cred:Seq_SubmitPermitApplication's own sequence diagram (PPR status = Blocked > error; Clear/ConditionalClearance/Hold > proceed). No gap." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "17.1.2" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Rule_ProfessionalPracticeClearance> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a School district/ISD user, I want to be prevented from applying for an individual with an adverse PPR status, so that I am prevented from initiating an application for an individual who is currently ineligible due to adverse actions." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Block application initiation for an individual with an adverse PPR status" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_17_1_3> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Requirement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "System references the individual's existing temporary credentials and the user's district/ISD to display only available/eligible permit types from the full list: Daily Substitute, Full Year Expert, Full Year Basic Substitute, Full-Year Shortage Substitute, Extended Daily or Emergency Extended Daily Substitute, School Administrator, School Social Worker." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd17DailySubDoc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "'Full Year Expert' appears in this eligible-permit list — same as in all seven other FDD 17 documents — and is the permit type this file's headline finding concerns (see cred:Question_FullYearExpertPermitTypeMissing below): no GET /permit-types-style filtering logic anywhere in credentialing-api.ttl/credentialing-domain.ttl accounts for it specifically, since the aggregate that would define it (CredentialDefinitionAggregate/CredentialCategory) never lists it at all." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "17.1.3" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Op_AdminIssuePermit> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a School district/ISD user, I want to see the full list of eligible permits for an individual upon selecting 'Apply for Permit', so that I can choose the correct temporary credential type quickly." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Show the full list of eligible permits for an individual" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_17_1_4> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Requirement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "Confirmation page prior to final submission, displaying an Advisory statement of legal considerations/district responsibilities; explicit checkboxes to agree to the Advisory and the permit's requirements; a dedicated free-form-text digital-signature area (the user's own name); submission blocked until both checkboxes and the signature are complete." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd17DailySubDoc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Partial match: cred:Rule_CertificateDocumentGeneration models certificate PDF generation, not the attestation-capture step itself. Same gap already identified in credentialing-fdd-11-16.ttl's Req_11_1_3 for the general (non-permit-specific) attestation flow — this FDD's version is simpler (checkboxes + free-text name, no separate typed-name field distinct from the checkboxes) but is the same underlying, still-unresolved attestation-modeling gap, not a new one. Wireframe-11 (School Administrator Permit's Submit Application screen, confirmed by viewing) shows the identical pattern." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "17.1.4" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Rule_CertificateDocumentGeneration> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a School district/ISD user, I want to be required to digitally sign the application, so that I can legally attest to the requirements and validity of the information provided." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Require digital signature attestation before submission" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_17_1_5> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Requirement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "If the same endorsement/grade combination already exists (active), block submission and display an error message." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd17DailySubDoc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "No satisfiedBy: no invariant on cred:CredentialApplicationAggregate or cred:IssuedCredentialAggregate enforces uniqueness of (endorsement, grade level) per individual/district/academic year for permits specifically — Extended/Emergency Extended Daily's own FDD describes the identical rule in much more detail ('The system will prevent a user from applying... for the same Endorsement and Grade Level combination, when there is an existing active Extended Daily Substitute Permit...'). Genuine coverage gap, corroborated across two of the eight FDDs." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "17.1.5" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "I want the system to block duplicate endorsement/grade so that policy limits are enforced." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Block duplicate endorsement/grade combination submissions" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_17_1_6> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Requirement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "Extended Daily is offered only if an existing Daily Substitute Permit exists for the same individual/district/academic year; Emergency Extended is offered only if an existing Extended Daily Substitute Permit exists likewise. System reminds the user the combined Daily + Extended + Emergency Extended coverage 'could total 270 consecutive calendar days.'" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd17DailySubDoc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Direct, exact numeric match — see this file's header for the full cross-check. No discrepancy." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "17.1.6" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Rule_PermitDurationAndRenewalLimits> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a School District/ISD/Staffing Agency User, I want to select the Extended Daily or Emergency Extended Daily Substitute permit type, so that I can apply for coverage for a teaching assignment lasting more than 90 consecutive calendar days." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Select Extended Daily/Emergency Extended Daily and see the 270-day total-coverage reminder" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_17_1_7> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Requirement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "Clear renewal pathway for each of the four listed permit types; attestation + digital signature required prior to submission; messaging/confirmation throughout the renewal process." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd17DailySubDoc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Genuine discrepancy worth flagging: cred:Seq_RenewCredential's own actor is 'Educator' (self-service, 'Who: Authenticated educator with renewable credential') and cred:Op_SubmitRenewal's gating permission cred:Perm_ApplicationSubmit is scoped scope:SelfOnly ('All authenticated educators'). But this FDD, and every other FDD-17 document, consistently describes PERMIT renewals (as opposed to certificate renewals) as org-submitted by a School district/ISD/Staffing Agency user on the educator's behalf — the same actor as the original permit application (cred:Op_AdminIssuePermit, gated by district/ISD-scoped cred:Perm_PermitIssue), not the educator. No org-submitted 'renew a permit on behalf of an educator' ApiOperation exists anywhere in credentialing-api.ttl — Op_SubmitRenewal is the only renewal endpoint, and its actor/scope doesn't match what these FDDs describe. This corroborates the same Question_WorklistAssignmentScope-adjacent actor confusion already flagged in credentialing-domain.ttl, but specifically for renewals, which hadn't been checked before. See cred:Question_PermitRenewalActorMismatch below." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "17.1.7" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Op_SubmitRenewal> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Seq_RenewCredential> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a School district/ISD/Staffing Agency user, I want to be able to renew Full Year Basic Substitute, Full Year Expert, Full Year Shortage Substitute, and School Social Worker permits." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Provide a renewal pathway for renewable permit types" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_17_1_8> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Requirement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "The option to apply for renewal is explicitly not available for these four permit types." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd17DailySubDoc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Direct match for the School Administrator (not-renewable) case; Daily/Extended/Emergency Extended are implicitly non-renewable in the rule's statement (no renewal count given, only duration caps) but the rule's text never says 'not renewable' for those three the way it explicitly does for School Administrator — a minor textual-completeness gap in the rule statement itself (not a numeric error), worth a light note rather than a full Annotation." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "17.1.8" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Rule_PermitDurationAndRenewalLimits> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a School district/ISD/Staffing Agency user, I want the system to prevent renewal applications for Daily Substitute, Extended Daily Substitute, Emergency Extended Daily Substitute, and School Administrator permits, so that I avoid submitting applications for non-renewable credentials." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Prevent renewal applications for non-renewable permit types" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_17_1_9> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Requirement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "Full Year Basic Substitute: max 3 renewals (4 years total). Full Year Shortage Substitute: max 3 renewals. School Social Worker: max 1 renewal. Full Year Expert: unlimited renewals, provided specific criteria are met." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd17DailySubDoc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "The Full Year Basic / Full Year Shortage / School Social Worker numbers are an exact match — see this file's header cross-check. 'Full Year Expert Substitute Permits have unlimited renewals available, provided specific criteria are met' is the clearest single-sentence confirmation, across all eight FDDs, that Full Year Expert is a real, distinct, currently-unmodeled permit type — see cred:Question_FullYearExpertPermitTypeMissing below." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "17.1.9" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Rule_PermitDurationAndRenewalLimits> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a School district/ISD/Staffing Agency user, I want to be able to have a max number of renewals for Full Year Basic Substitute, Full Year Expert, Full Year Shortage Substitute, and School Social Worker permits, so that renewals aren't over utilized." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Enforce maximum renewal counts per renewable permit type" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_17_2> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Requirement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd17DailySubDoc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Covers 17.2.1-17.2.7 (confirmation message content, Application Reference Number display, Conviction Review / Pending Payment messaging, and the two educator-facing PPR-completion and payment-link emails) — all seven stories are specific instances of the same (application status x Needs Responses flag) confirmation-message pattern already covered narratively by Req_17_1_0/Req_17_SA_7 below, with the actual send/track mechanism explicitly deferred to Communications by the FDD's own text, same pattern as credentialing-fdd-11-16.ttl's Req_11_6/Req_16_3." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "17.2" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "All underlying logic for sending, tracking, and displaying emails, alerts and notifications are derived from Business Specification #6 (Alerts, Emails & Communications). This feature is strictly limited to the configuration of these tools (defining what is sent) specifically for the Educator Credentialing module. Additionally, Business Specification #4 (Business Rules Management) will specify when and to whom it is sent." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Temporary Credentials User Feedback (feature-level pointer)" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_17_ED> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Requirement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd17ExtendedDailyDoc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Numbers match exactly (+90 days; see this file's header). Mentor requirement matches cred:Rule_MentorAssignmentRequirementForPermits (EDSP is already in its listed scope). The 'observed with satisfactory feedback' hard stop is NOT captured by that rule or anywhere else in credentialing-domain.ttl — a genuine coverage gap distinct from the mentor-capture requirement itself (mentor assignment and a documented satisfactory observation are two separate hard stops in this FDD, only the first is modeled)." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "17.ED.1" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Rule_MentorAssignmentRequirementForPermits> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Rule_PermitDurationAndRenewalLimits> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "Extended Daily Substitute Permit is offered only when the individual already holds a Daily Substitute Permit for the same district/ISD/academic year, provides an additional 90 consecutive calendar days of coverage, and requires (in order): a >90-day-need confirmation, the same 60-semester-hour/GPA gate as other permit types, a mentor-assignment question (with dynamic-search-or-free-form mentor name capture), and an observed-with-satisfactory-feedback question — all four hard stops." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Extended Daily Substitute Permit: eligibility, mentor + observation gate, and duration" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_17_EED> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Requirement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd17EmergencyExtendedDailyDoc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "270-day cap and mentor/observation hard stops (shared with Extended Daily, same gate) match cred:Rule_PermitDurationAndRenewalLimits/Rule_MentorAssignmentRequirementForPermits (EEDSP is already in the latter's listed scope). The permit-type AUTO-DETERMINATION logic (differing/added grade+endorsement -> new Extended Daily; same grade+endorsement -> Emergency Extended) is business-rule detail not represented anywhere in credentialing-domain.ttl — a real, previously-uncaptured piece of eligibility logic, though narrower in scope than the Extended Daily gap already flagged in Req_17_ED (that 'observed with satisfactory feedback' gap applies identically here, not repeated as a second Annotation)." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "17.EED.1" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Rule_MentorAssignmentRequirementForPermits> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Rule_PermitDurationAndRenewalLimits> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "Emergency Extended Daily Substitute Permit provides a further 90 consecutive calendar days after Extended Daily (270-day total cap across Daily + Extended + Emergency Extended), granted at the discretion of the Superintendent of Public Instruction, not guaranteed, with processing up to 4 weeks. The system automatically determines whether a new application is 'Extended' or 'Emergency Extended' based on whether the endorsement/grade-level combination differs from or duplicates an existing Extended Daily Substitute Permit for the same district/individual/academic year." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Emergency Extended Daily Substitute Permit: 270-day cap and Extended-vs-Emergency-Extended auto-determination" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_17_FYB_1> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Requirement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "Eligibility text displayed; Back/Continue options; academic-year/expiration-date confirmation follows, same pattern as every other permit type." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd17FullYearBasicDoc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "The core-subject major-or-MTTC logic matches Rule_SubjectAreaAssessmentValidation's existing EndorsementDefinition.RequiredAssessments AND/OR model well. The four named MCL waiver provisions (380.1531f Tribal MOU, 380.1281(3) Foreign MOA/Residency/SPI waiver, 380.1233c Detroit Public Schools Community District, 380.505 University Faculty Public School Academy) are not captured as data anywhere — same 'eligibility criteria is configuration' pattern noted elsewhere in this file, not a separate Annotation." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "17.FYB.1" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Rule_SubjectAreaAssessmentValidation> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "After permit-type selection, the system displays Full Year Basic Substitute Permit eligibility text: a non-certified/endorsed individual may instruct students when a properly certified/endorsed teacher is unavailable; core-subject assignments require a matching transcript major or passing content-area MTTC scores; several MCL waiver provisions can waive one or more requirements." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Display Full Year Basic Substitute Permit eligibility information" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_17_FYB_2> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Requirement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "MCL waiver selected -> skip standard eligibility checks, application status forced to Pending Evaluation, user still required to enter at least one endorsement and grade level." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd17FullYearBasicDoc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "No satisfiedBy: no invariant or business rule anywhere models an MCL-waiver override path that skips standard validation and forces a specific application status — this is a real, previously-invisible branch in the eligibility logic (distinct from the ordinary 60-semester-hour/GPA path modeled in Req_17_FYB_3) that Rule_AutoApprovalCriteria/Rule_ManualReviewTriggering don't account for. Genuine coverage gap." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "17.FYB.2" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "If the application is authorized under one of the four named MCL waiver provisions, the system shows a dropdown of waiver selections; each existing waiver selection skips test-score and subject-area confirmation entirely, and all such applications are set to Pending Evaluation status." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "MCL-waiver branch bypasses test-score/subject-area checks and forces Pending Evaluation" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_17_FYB_3> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Requirement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "No -> error: 'The Full Year permit application cannot be submitted because the individual does not meet the credit requirements for the permit.' Yes -> proceed to endorsement/grade-level selection." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd17FullYearBasicDoc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Same eligibility-gate shape already used by Daily Substitute Permit's equivalent 60-hour/GPA question (Req_17_1_0) and Extended Daily's version — consistent pattern across permit types, no new gap." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "17.FYB.3" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Rule_AutoApprovalCriteria> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "If no MCL waiver applies, the system asks whether the individual has completed at least 60 semester hours of credit (grade C or better) or an associate degree from a CHEA/USED-recognized institution; No hard-stops the application." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "60-semester-hour/associate-degree eligibility gate (non-waiver path)" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_17_FYB_4> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Requirement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "Non-core endorsement -> straight to application review. Core endorsement with verified score -> application review. Core endorsement, no verified score, 20-hour minor confirmed -> application review, status set to Pending Evaluation. Core endorsement, no verified score, no minor -> error: 'Educator is not eligible for this endorsement because there is no verification of test scores or a major for one or more of the subject areas.'" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd17FullYearBasicDoc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "The core/non-core branch and MTTC score check match Rule_SubjectAreaAssessmentValidation well. The specific '20 semester credit hour minor' fallback quantity is new, previously-uncaptured detail — not modeled as a separate Annotation since it is additive precision on an already-modeled rule rather than a structural gap, but worth folding into that rule's own statement in a future domain-file pass." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "17.FYB.4" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Rule_SubjectAreaAssessmentValidation> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "The system requires at least one endorsement/grade-level selection; for core-subject endorsements without a verified passing MTTC score, it asks whether the educator holds at least a minor (20 semester credit hours) in the content area as a fallback path to Pending Evaluation status." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Endorsement selection with core/non-core branching and 20-semester-hour minor fallback" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_17_FYB_5> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Requirement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd17FullYearBasicDoc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Same pattern already covered by Req_17_1_0/Req_17_SA_7 — see cred:Question_ApplicationStatusVocabularyMismatch below; not re-modeled as a separate Annotation, just cross-referenced." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "17.FYB.5" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Rule_AutoApprovalCriteria> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Rule_ManualReviewTriggering> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "Same (application status x Needs Responses flag) confirmation-message pattern as every other permit type: Pending PPR, Conviction Review, Pending Evaluation, Pending Payment, Approved, with the same five invalid combinations rejected." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Submit Full Year Basic Substitute Permit application and display status-specific confirmation" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_17_FYB_6> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Requirement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd17FullYearBasicDoc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Exact match on both the renewal count/duration (Rule_PermitDurationAndRenewalLimits) and the per-renewal-tier IDP detail (Rule_IdpForPermitRenewals — whose own statement already spells out the identical 1st/2nd/3rd-renewal tiers this FDD describes, sourced from the Renewals FDD). Strong corroboration, no discrepancy — this is the single cleanest confirmation in the whole FDD-17 set that a previously-modeled rule's fine detail is accurate against its actual source document." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "17.FYB.6" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Rule_IdpForPermitRenewals> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Rule_PermitDurationAndRenewalLimits> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "Full Year Basic Substitute Permit renewals are capped at 3 (4 years of teaching total), each renewal requiring an Individual Development Plan (IDP) — 1st renewal: enrollment in a state-approved teacher-prep program; 2nd and 3rd renewals: minimum 6 semester hours completed since the previous renewal." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Full Year Basic Substitute Permit renewal: max 3 renewals / 4 years, per-renewal IDP requirements" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_17_FYS> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Requirement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd17FullYearShortageDoc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Max-3-renewals and effective/highly-effective-ratings requirement match cred:Rule_PermitDurationAndRenewalLimits exactly — see this file's header. The professional-certificate-tier eligibility gate and the <=.5 FTE numeric-field validation are not captured anywhere as structured data (same 'eligibility criteria as configuration' pattern noted elsewhere). More significant: nothing in credentialing-domain.ttl, staffing-domain.ttl, or any other converted mied-v3 domain models educator PERFORMANCE RATINGS (effective/highly effective) at all — see cred:Question_EducatorPerformanceRatingSourceMissing below, this FDD's own source for that half of the rule." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "17.FYS.1" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Rule_PermitDurationAndRenewalLimits> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "Full Year Shortage Substitute Permit requires the educator to hold a Professional/Advanced Professional/Permanent/Life/Continuing certificate (Provisional does not qualify) and the assignment to be <=.5 FTE; renewals (max 3) require effective or highly effective performance ratings in the assigned area." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Full Year Shortage Substitute Permit: professional certificate + <=.5 FTE gate, and effective/highly-effective-rated renewals" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_17_REN> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Requirement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd17RenewalsDoc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "This is the primary source document for cred:Rule_PermitDurationAndRenewalLimits and cred:Rule_IdpForPermitRenewals, and confirms both are accurate (see this file's header). It is also the single clearest source, across all eight FDDs, for the missing Full Year Expert permit type: 'Expert Substitute Permits will have unlimited renewals available when the following criteria is met: Development and implementation of an IDP; the district/school must assign and maintain a mentor teacher... If the assignment is in a non-core discipline area and the individual qualified for an initial full-year expert substitute permit under only subrule (1)(g)(i)... the applicant shall verify that the business or industry license or credential... is valid... or that the individual holds a bachelor's degree, or higher.' See cred:Question_FullYearExpertPermitTypeMissing below." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "17.REN.1" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Rule_IdpForPermitRenewals> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Rule_MentorAssignmentRequirementForPermits> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Rule_PermitDurationAndRenewalLimits> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "This document is the cross-permit reference for which temporary credentials can/cannot be renewed, their renewal caps, and the shared eligibility-factor list business rules draw on (non-MCL vs. MCL permit history, 4th-renewal same-endorsement/grade/district check, academic progress, mentor assignment, formal-observation ratings, remaining endorsement/grade-level coverage)." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Cross-permit renewal rules and eligibility factors" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_17_SA_1> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Requirement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "PPR flag on: error message displayed (text explicitly left TBD in this FDD, unlike Daily Substitute Permit's fully-specified equivalent message). PPR flag off: proceed to Apply for a permit (new/renewal)." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd17SchoolAdminDoc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Logic matches Req_17_1_2's Daily-Substitute equivalent exactly; the only difference is this FDD leaves its own error-message text as an explicit placeholder ('Error message will be defined') rather than a gap in the graph — noted here for traceability, not modeled as a separate Annotation since it is a documented, self-acknowledged TBD in the source, not a silent omission." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "17.SA.1" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Rule_ProfessionalPracticeClearance> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "Dependent upon profile permissions, the user searches for a Unique ID; a PPR flag on the individual blocks the application with an error message (this document's own text: 'Error message will be defined')." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Search for an educator and gate on PPR flag (School Administrator Permit)" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_17_SA_2> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Requirement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "Permit valid from date of payment through August 31 of the applied academic year (MCL 380.1246). Eligible-individual categories displayed: MI-certified admins needing renewal-credit time, out-of-state initial certification applicants, interim placements, MCL 380.1246(3)/(2) initial-certification seekers." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd17SchoolAdminDoc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "CredentialDefinitionAggregate's CredentialDefinitionRequirementRule DomainEntity is the right general shape for this ('Business rules defining eligibility criteria') but none of the MCL-380.1246-specific eligibility text is captured anywhere as actual data — same class of gap as most eligibility-criteria detail across this domain; not modeled as a separate Annotation since it is the same already-acknowledged general pattern (business rules are configuration data, not hand-authored graph content) rather than a School-Administrator-specific surprise." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "17.SA.2" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:CredentialDefinitionAggregate> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "After permit-type selection, the system displays detailed eligibility information for the School Administrator Permit, referencing MCL 380.1246 and its subrules, and lists the categories of individuals who may be eligible." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Display School Administrator Permit eligibility information (MCL 380.1246)" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_17_SA_3> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Requirement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "Academic year populated from system date (July 1 rollover rule, same as every other permit type). Hire date required via date picker before proceeding to attestations." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd17SchoolAdminDoc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "cred:ApplicantResponses ('Answers to business rule management questions') is the closest existing field but has no explicit hireDate concept called out — folded into the general ApplicantResponses shape rather than treated as a distinct gap, since that value object is deliberately opaque/schema-free by design." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "17.SA.3" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:CredentialApplicationAggregate> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "The system confirms the current academic year with the user, then prompts for the individual's hire date via a date picker." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Confirm academic year and capture hire date for School Administrator Permit" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_17_SA_4> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Requirement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "If the district does not attest to one or more required statements, display an error and block progress (per wireframe-8, confirmed by viewing: 'All questions must be answered to qualify for School Administrator Permit')." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd17SchoolAdminDoc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Wireframe-8 (confirmed by viewing) is direct visual confirmation this is a real, implemented hard stop. The specific attestation content (6-month/3.5-year MCL 380.1246(3) timeline, state-aid-deduction audit acknowledgment) is not itself captured as structured data anywhere — same general 'eligibility criteria are configuration, not hand-authored graph content' pattern as Req_17_SA_2, not modeled as a separate Annotation." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "17.SA.4" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:CredentialApplicationAggregate> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "The system requires the district to attest to several statements (certified-administrator unavailability, the assignment being under 6 months for most eligible-individual categories, MCL 380.1246(3) individuals' 6-month/3.5-year enrollment-and-completion timeline, and audit/state-aid-deduction acknowledgment) before the application can proceed." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Require multiple district attestations before proceeding (School Administrator Permit)" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_17_SA_5> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Requirement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "No -> error message, application cannot proceed (wireframe-9, confirmed by viewing: 'does not meet the Bachelor's Degree requirement for this permit'). Yes -> proceed to the mentor-assignment question." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd17SchoolAdminDoc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Same pattern as Req_17_SA_2/4 — the eligibility CHECK exists conceptually (CredentialDefinitionRequirementRule) but the specific degree-requirement criterion is not captured as structured data. No separate Annotation; consistent with how eligibility-criteria detail is handled domain-wide." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "17.SA.5" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:CredentialDefinitionAggregate> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "The system asks whether the individual holds a bachelor's or higher degree from a regionally/nationally accredited institution; answering No blocks the application." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Hard-stop on missing bachelor's degree (School Administrator Permit)" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_17_SA_6> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Requirement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "No -> error (wireframe-10, confirmed by viewing: 'does not meet the permit requirement to have an assigned mentor'). Yes -> dynamically-filtered search field for certified educators, required, with a free-form fallback if the search returns no results." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd17SchoolAdminDoc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Strong, direct corroboration — cred:Rule_MentorAssignmentRequirementForPermits already explicitly lists SAP (School Administrator Permit) among the four permit types requiring mentor capture (EDSP, EEDSP, SAP, SSWP), and already models both the Mentor-Unique-ID (Staffing-validated) path and the free-form/external-mentor manual-review path. Wireframe-10 (confirmed by viewing) is direct visual proof this hard stop is real, implemented behavior, not merely a documented intention. No gap — this is exactly the kind of independent-FDD corroboration this review exercise exists to produce." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "17.SA.6" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Rule_MentorAssignmentRequirementForPermits> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "For MCL 380.1246(3) individuals, the system asks whether the district did or will assign a mentor; answering No blocks the application. Answering Yes requires entering the mentor's name via a dynamically-filtered search (falling back to free text if no match)." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Hard-stop on missing mentor assignment (School Administrator Permit)" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_17_SA_7> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Requirement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "Five named invalid status/Needs-Responses combinations are explicitly rejected (Pending Evaluation+Y, Pending Payment+Y, Approved+Y, Pending PPR+N, Conviction Review+Y). Wireframe-11 (confirmed by viewing) shows the shared advisory/attestation/signature screen immediately preceding this step." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd17SchoolAdminDoc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "See cred:Question_ApplicationStatusVocabularyMismatch below (shared with Req_17_1_0) — this FDD's 'Pending Evaluation' status (routed to the OEE worklist) is the clearest of all eight documents that the FDDs' own status vocabulary is richer/differently-shaped than cred:CredentialApplicationAggregate's AppState_* enumeration (Draft/Submitted/PendingPayment/PendingDocuments/ProfessionalPracticeHold/RequiresManualReview/Approved/Denied/Cancelled/Blocked has no obvious 1:1 'Pending Evaluation' or 'Conviction Review' counterpart, and 'Needs Responses' is not a modeled field at all)." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "17.SA.7" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Rule_AutoApprovalCriteria> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Rule_ManualReviewTriggering> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "Upon Submit, the system displays a confirmation message that varies by (application status x Needs Responses flag), and routes the application: Pending PPR (hold, awaiting PPR responses), Conviction Review (hold, PPR worklist), Pending Evaluation (submitted, assigned to OEE worklist), Pending Payment (hold, awaiting payment), Approved (issued)." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Submit School Administrator Permit application and display status-specific confirmation" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_17_SA_8> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Requirement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd17SchoolAdminDoc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Triple-corroborated across three independent FDD documents (this one by omission, Daily Substitute Permit 17.1.8, and Renewals) — no discrepancy." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "17.SA.8" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Rule_PermitDurationAndRenewalLimits> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "This FDD does not describe any renewal pathway for the School Administrator Permit — consistent with both the Daily Substitute Permit FDD (17.1.8) and the Renewals FDD's own non-renewable list." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "School Administrator Permit is not renewable" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_17_SSW> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Requirement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd17SchoolSocialWorkerDoc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Max-1-renewal matches cred:Rule_PermitDurationAndRenewalLimits exactly. The supervising-School-Social-Worker capture matches cred:Rule_MentorAssignmentRequirementForPermits's existing scope (SSWP is already listed, and that rule's own worked example is specifically an SSW-Permit-with-an-external-mentor scenario) — strong corroboration, no gap on the mentor/supervision side. The LARA license number + expiration date fields themselves are not captured anywhere in cred:ApplicantResponses or any other ValueObject — a minor, narrow coverage gap (a specific external-license-reference shape, not previously seen in any other permit type's FDD) not modeled as a separate Annotation given its narrow scope, but noted here for completeness." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "17.SSW.1" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Rule_MentorAssignmentRequirementForPermits> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Rule_PermitDurationAndRenewalLimits> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "School Social Worker Permit requires a Master of Social Work degree (or equivalent), a valid LARA-issued LLMSW or LMSW license (number + expiration date captured), enrollment/acceptance in an approved SSW preparation program, and supervision by a fully credentialed Michigan School Social Worker (captured the same way as a mentor — dynamic search or free-form, required, with supporting documentation retained for audit). Exactly one renewal is available, requiring demonstrated progress toward program completion." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "School Social Worker Permit: LARA license eligibility, supervision requirement, and 1-renewal cap" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_29_1_10> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Requirement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "Display alerts for: expiring certificates, insufficient professional learning hours, missing MTTC scores, PPR/Needs Responses status blocking actions. Alerts link to the appropriate actions/pages." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd29Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "No satisfiedBy: no alert/notification model of any kind exists in credentialing-domain.ttl or credentialing-api.ttl — this is explicitly Alerts & Communications (Business Specification #6) territory per the Dependencies section's own 'email notification... will be defined in Alerts and Communications (6)' line, matching how the FDD 11/16 pass's Req_11_6/16_3 treated the same deferral. Out-of-scope, not a coverage gap." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "29.1.10" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a Citizen User, I want to see alerts related to my certifications, so that I am aware of required updates or incomplete prerequisites." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Display system alerts related to credentialing" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_29_1_1> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Requirement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "Landing page action set as defined in the main spec; certificate status shown per certificate; navigation to application flows gated by eligibility." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd29Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Status vocabulary (Valid/Expired/Nullified/Revoked/Suspended) is an exact match to cred:CredState_Valid/Expired/Nullified/Revoked/Suspended. Op_GetEducatorCredentials's own EducatorCredentialSummary projection (all credentials+endorsements grouped by educator) is the natural backing call. Comment thread 181233542/6381586 (Punniyamoorthy: 'this landing page is more like Dashboard... I do not see any other story for other functionality like dashboard' / Caswell, agreeing the global Citizen Dashboard is broader but this FDD is deliberately scoped to certificate-related aspects only) is the same landing-page-vs-Dashboard overlap the FDD 11/16 pass already surfaced for dash:DashboardsContext (Req_11_7 there) — resolved amicably in-thread, not a new gap, so not re-raised as its own Annotation here." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "29.1.1" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:IssuedCredentialAggregate> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Op_GetEducatorCredentials> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "(No user-story stem given in the FDD for this item — it is the feature's baseline acceptance criteria, not phrased as a story.) The system displays actions such as Apply/Renew, Add Endorsement, Print Certificate, and access to certification guidance documents; displays each certificate's status (Valid, Expired, Nullified, Revoked, Suspended); and allows navigation to application flows when available based on eligibility." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Certificate landing page: actions, status, and navigation eligibility" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_29_1_2> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Requirement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "Apply/Renew eligibility per certificate-type prerequisites; Apply/Renew disabled/hidden when Needs Responses = Y; Add Endorsement NOT disabled for lack of MTTC score alone (not all endorsements require a test); on attempting to add a specific endorsement, dynamically verify whether it requires MTTC or a Professional Knowledge and Skills (PKS) test, and require a passing score not older than 5 years; block adding that endorsement with an error if no valid passing score is on file; Print Certificate disabled if no valid certificate exists." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd29Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "5-year validity window is an exact match to Rule_AssessmentResultValidity. Per-endorsement dynamic test-requirement check (some require none) matches Rule_SubjectAreaAssessmentValidation's AND/OR-configurable requirement model. Genuine new detail: comment 2095209523/1225736752 (Dontje: 'some endorsements require a Professional Knowledge and Skills (PKS) test' / 'Added') introduced PKS as a SECOND named test type alongside MTTC mid-review — nothing in credentialing-domain.ttl's AssessmentDefinition/AssessmentResult model names PKS specifically (nor does it need to, if PKS is just another configured AssessmentDefinition instance — but that's an assumption, not confirmed anywhere). See Question_PksAssessmentTypeUnconfirmed below. 'Needs Responses = Y' gating is a distinct, still-unmodeled flag — see Question_NeedsResponsesFlagNotModeled (shared with several other stories below)." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "29.1.2" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Rule_AssessmentResultValidity> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Rule_SubjectAreaAssessmentValidation> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a Citizen User, I want the system to show only the certificate actions I am eligible for, so that I do not attempt actions that I cannot perform." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Display eligible certificate actions (MTTC/PKS-aware)" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_29_1_3> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Requirement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "Display all applications in Submitted or Pending statuses, using main-workflow-consistent status text (flow diagrams show routing to OPPS, EPP, or Alternate Route Providers depending on type); show a Delete option only while Submitted; prevent deletion once routing has begun (OPPS/EPP/ARP involvement)." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd29Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Good direct match on the Submitted-only delete gate (Op_DeleteApplication's own summary is literally 'Delete draft application', and cred:AppState_Submitted is a real, early, non-terminal state). 'OPPS' (undefined acronym here — likely 'Office of Professional Preparation Services' or similar) and 'Alternate Route Providers' as named routing destinations don't correspond to any modeled concept in credentialing-domain.ttl beyond the generic worklist/manual-review routing (Rule_ManualReviewTriggering) — minor terminology gap, not raised as its own Annotation given how minor it is." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "29.1.3" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:AppState_Submitted> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Op_DeleteApplication> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Op_ListApplications> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a Citizen User, I want to view my pending certificate applications, so that I can track the status of applications that have not yet been processed." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Display pending applications, with conditional delete" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_29_1_4> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Requirement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "Display eligible certificates to apply for/renew per eligibility flows (e.g. Interim -> Standard, Provisional -> Professional); show an error if ineligible; prevent starting when Needs Responses = Y or PPR indicates actionable restrictions." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd29Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "PPR-actionable gating matches Rule_ProfessionalPracticeClearance well (Blocked/Hold semantics). Interim->Standard / Provisional->Professional progression path terminology matches cred:ProgressToProfessional (an EndorsementDefinition field, per credentialing-domain.ttl line ~310) only loosely — that field is endorsement-scoped, not a certificate-level state-machine transition; a genuine, if minor, terminology/granularity gap. 'Needs Responses = Y' gating: see Question_NeedsResponsesFlagNotModeled." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "29.1.4" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Op_SubmitApplication> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Op_SubmitRenewal> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Rule_ProfessionalPracticeClearance> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Seq_RenewCredential> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Seq_SubmitNewCertificateApplication> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a Citizen User, I want to select Apply/Renew from my landing page, so that I can begin a new credential application or renewal." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Navigate to Apply/Renew" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_29_1_5> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Requirement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "Display available endorsements for the certificate type (flow diagrams show validation based on MTTC test scores, endorsement level, and grade band rules); display static text that MTTC scores must be verified for approval; show an error if prerequisites for endorsement addition aren't met." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd29Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Direct match; grade-band filtering matches cred:GradeBandRange on EndorsementDefinitionAggregate." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "29.1.5" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Op_ListEndorsementApplications> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Op_SubmitEndorsementAddition> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Rule_SubjectAreaAssessmentValidation> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a Citizen User, I want to select Add Endorsement from my landing page, so that I can add new endorsements to my existing certificates." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Navigate to Add Endorsement" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_29_1_6> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Requirement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "Display Print Certificate for any valid certificate; generate a PDF containing certificate type, endorsements, issue date and expiration date (or blank for revoked/nullified/suspended per main spec); allow download or printing." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd29Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "CITATION VERIFIED: this story is one of Rule_CertificateDocumentGeneration's two cited sources for the blank-date-on-Revoked/Nullified/Suspended rendering rule, and it does say almost exactly that ('Issue date and expiration date (or blank for revoked/nullified/suspended per main spec)') — accurate citation, no correction needed. Comment 1070770097 (Dontje: 'your attachment is a sample ITC but the citizen user will be able to print their certificate(s) regardless of type') confirms Print Certificate isn't type-restricted, consistent with Op_PrintCredential's own general shape." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "29.1.6" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Op_PrintCredential> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Rule_CertificateDocumentGeneration> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Seq_PrintCertificate> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a Citizen User, I want to print my certificate, so that I can produce an official version for my employer or personal records." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Navigate to Print Certificate" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_29_1_7> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Requirement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "Display a link/section for guidance documents; open in a new tab or viewer; ensure documents reflect current certificate/endorsement rules." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd29Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Same structural gap the FDD 11/16 pass already found for this same permission (Req_11_2_1/11_2_2 there): cred:Perm_GuidanceView exists but has no backing ApiOperation/Sequence anywhere in credentialing-api.ttl/credentialing-sequences.ttl in mied-v3 either — this is carried-forward, not newly introduced. Not re-raised as its own Annotation; folded into the existing known gap." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "29.1.7" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Perm_GuidanceView> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a Citizen User, I want to access certificate-related guidance documents from my landing page, so that I can understand requirements and processes." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Display certificate guidance documents" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_29_1_8> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Requirement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "Store dashboard preferences tied to the user profile; display the user's preferred section/widget arrangement on return; preferences persist across sessions and devices." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd29Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "No satisfiedBy: nothing in credentialing-domain.ttl models a per-user dashboard-preference concept, and per the comment-thread resolution on 29.1.1 (181233542/6381586) this kind of cross-cutting dashboard/widget behavior is explicitly the Dashboards capability's territory (dash:DashboardsContext — a stub-only context in this project, same as the FDD 11/16 pass found for its own Req_11_7). Genuine coverage gap from Credentialing's own graph, but out-of-scope in the same sense Req_11_7 was — see the coverage-gap Annotation below rather than treating it as a Credentialing-side build item." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "29.1.8" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a Citizen User, I want the system to remember my certificate landing page preferences, so my view is consistent each time I return." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Persistent certificate dashboard state" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_29_1_9> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Requirement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "Display certificate type, status, validity dates, and endorsements; visually distinguish revoked/suspended/nullified certificates (dates may be blank); display endorsements and their grade bands." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd29Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "CITATION VERIFIED: this is Rule_CertificateDocumentGeneration's second cited source for the blank-date rule ('The system visually distinguishes revoked, suspended, or nullified certificates (as their dates may be blank)') — accurate, consistent wording with 29.1.6. Grade-band display matches cred:GradeBandRange (via cred:AssociatedEndorsements on IssuedCredentialAggregate)." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "29.1.9" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:AssociatedEndorsements> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Op_GetCredential> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Op_GetEducatorCredentials> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Rule_CertificateDocumentGeneration> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a Citizen User, I want to view details for each certificate and its endorsements, so that I understand what I hold and what I can apply for." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Display certificate and endorsement details" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_29_2_10> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Requirement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "Block submission until all required fields/uploads/fees/validations succeed; create an application record with all inputs on submission; trigger Alerts & Communications alerts/emails; lock initial user-entered data from further editing; display confirmation and route as required." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd29Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Direct match. 'Locks initial user-entered data from further editing' isn't an explicit invariant on CredentialApplicationAggregate today but is consistent with its state model (post-Submitted states don't describe a citizen-editable path back to Draft) — not raised as a separate gap." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "29.2.10" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Op_SubmitApplication> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Seq_SubmitNewCertificateApplication> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a citizen user, I want to submit my application when all required information is complete, so that the credential review process can begin." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Submit application when complete" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_29_2_1> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Requirement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "Evaluate eligibility per Credentialing-Administrator-defined prerequisites; display only eligible certificate types (Teaching, ITC, School Counselor, School Administrator, School Psychologist, School Social Worker); hide ineligible types, including those ineligible due to Needs Responses = Y or PPR restrictions; navigate into the appropriate flow on selection." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd29Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Comment thread 2062160207 ('seems already covered in 29.1.4') -> 2092676098 ('you are correct, user story has been removed') indicates an earlier, more duplicative draft of this story was trimmed during review; the surviving 29.2.1 text is scoped distinctly enough from 29.1.4 (list-of-types vs. navigate-to-flow) that it's kept as its own Requirement here. 'Needs Responses = Y' gating: see Question_NeedsResponsesFlagNotModeled." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "29.2.1" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Op_SubmitApplication> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Rule_ProfessionalPracticeClearance> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a citizen user, I want to view a list of all certificate types for which I am eligible to Apply/Renew, so that I can easily initiate the correct application process." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "View eligible certificate types to Apply/Renew" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_29_2_2> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Requirement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "Load the certificate-type-specific flow; display type-specific question sets per Business Rule Management; adjust question sets across Teaching/ITC/Counselor/Administrator/Psychologist/Social Worker; block progress on unanswered required questions; move to upload/validation steps on completion." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd29Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Per-certificate-type dynamic question sets aren't modeled as a distinct configuration concept in credentialing-domain.ttl beyond CredentialDefinition's general eligibility-rule configurability — partial match, not a hard gap (this is squarely the kind of 'Business Rule Management' decision-tree content credentialing-technical-design.ttl's own Question_ConfigurabilityModel already flags as unresolved)." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "29.2.2" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:CredentialDefinitionAggregate> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Seq_SubmitNewCertificateApplication> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a citizen user, I want the system to begin the appropriate application flow when I select a certificate type, so that I can proceed through the required questions and validations." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Begin the appropriate application flow per certificate type" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_29_2_3> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Requirement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "Field-level validation on entry; application-level validation before submission; errors block submission until resolved; warnings allow submission but remain visible; all validation outcomes logged on the application record." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd29Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Direct match for the block-on-error/warn-but-allow shape; 'all validation outcomes logged' as a discrete audit concept isn't explicitly modeled beyond IssuanceHistory's general audit-trail scope on the issued-credential side (not the in-flight application side) — minor gap." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "29.2.3" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Rule_ManualReviewTriggering> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Seq_SubmitNewCertificateApplication> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a MiEdWorkforce system, I must perform field-level and application-level validations during the application flow for all certificate types, so that incomplete or erroneous submissions are prevented and errors/warnings are displayed." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Field-level and application-level validation for all certificate types" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_29_2_4> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Requirement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "Upload fields per certificate type; accept only allowed file types; validate required-upload presence; block progress on missing required uploads; store uploaded documents with the application record." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd29Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Unlike the FDD 11/16 pilot pass (which predated documents-api.ttl's real mied-v3 conversion and could only point at a placeholder docs:DocumentRetrievalOperation stub), mied-v3's documents-api.ttl now has a real docs:Op_RequestDocumentUpload — a genuinely good match, not a stub-only reference. Per-certificate-type upload-field configuration (which uploads are required for which certificate type) still isn't modeled as a distinct concept anywhere, consistent with Credential Admin (11)'s general configurability scope." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "29.2.4" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:Op_RequestDocumentUpload> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a citizen user, I want the ability to upload supporting documents for my application, so that I can provide necessary evidence for credentialing requirements." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Upload supporting documents for any certificate application" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_29_2_5> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Requirement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "Display fee amount for the selected certificate type; collect payment via the CEPAS payment service; prevent submission until payment succeeds; display an error on failed payment; log successful payment against the application record." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd29Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "WireframeAddendumC (confirmed by viewing) directly corroborates the CEPAS-named payment error state described here. Credentialing's own Dependency on pay:PaymentsContext (event-subscription on PaymentCompletedEvent) matches the 'log successful payment' half; the CEPAS-specific integration detail (vs. a generic Payments-capability abstraction) lives in payments' own domain, not credentialing's, consistent with existing scope." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "29.2.5" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Rule_PaymentRequirement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:payments:PaymentsContext> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a MiEdWorkforce system, I need to collect and process required fees for all certificate applications, utilizing CEPAS services, so that application costs are secured." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Collect and process required fees via CEPAS" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_29_2_6> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Requirement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "Real-time check for a passing score tied to the endorsement's test code on selection; visual indicator next to the endorsement; block submission with an error if a Core-Subject endorsement requiring a test has no passing score; allow proceeding without a score if the endorsement requires none." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd29Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Direct match, including the exception-handling branch for no-test-required endorsements. This story's explicit 'shall display an error message preventing the user from proceeding' (hard block at selection time, not after submission) is the SAME resolution the FDD 11/16 pass's Question_ManualReviewVsHardBlockForMttc already flagged as contradicting credentialing-domain.md's Rule_ManualReviewTriggering (which lists missing/failing assessment results as a MANUAL REVIEW trigger, not a submission-time hard block) — this FDD independently reinforces the hard-block reading a second time, strengthening that existing open contradiction rather than raising a new one." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "29.2.6" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Rule_AssessmentResultValidity> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Rule_SubjectAreaAssessmentValidation> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a Citizen User, I want the system to validate my MTTC test completion when I select endorsements during an application, so that I know immediately if I am eligible to apply for that specific subject area." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Real-time MTTC validation on endorsement selection" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_29_2_7> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Requirement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "Check the Needs Responses flag on submission; prevent starting/renewing when Needs Responses = Y unless a rule explicitly allows continuation; continue normal processing when N; record the outcome in application metadata; display informational messaging." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd29Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "No satisfiedBy: 'Needs Responses' as a distinct flag from ProfessionalPracticeStatus (Clear/ConditionalClearance/Hold/Blocked) does not exist anywhere in credentialing-domain.ttl's CredentialApplication model, in mied-v3 exactly as in the FDD 11/16 pass's finding on this same gap (there, Req_11_4_1). See the consolidated Question_NeedsResponsesFlagNotModeled below (targets this Requirement plus 29.1.2/29.1.4/29.2.1/29.2.8/29.2.9, all of which independently reference the same still-unmodeled flag)." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "29.2.7" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a MiEdWorkforce system, I must determine the status of the application based on the Needs Responses flag, so that applications proceed according to Professional Practices Review requirements." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Determine application status from Needs Responses flag" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_29_2_8> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Requirement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "Check PPR flag for actionable status after submission; route to the required worklist if actionable; allow standard processing if not actionable; log routing decisions with timestamp and flag values; confirm submission and routing to the user." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd29Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Core routing logic matches well. The discrete NAMED worklists with per-type search/filters that the FDD 11/16 pass's Question_MissingWorklistSearchAndExportUX already flagged as unmodeled UX aren't re-described here (this FDD doesn't itself describe worklist search screens), so not re-raised as a separate Annotation — same known gap, no new evidence either way." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "29.2.8" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Rule_ManualReviewTriggering> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Rule_ProfessionalPracticeClearance> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a MiEdWorkforce system, I must route the application to the appropriate worklist(s) based on the Professional Practice Review (PPR) flag, so that staff review is initiated when necessary." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Route application to worklist based on PPR flag" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_29_2_9> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Requirement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "Determine In-state/Out-of-state from data captured in the application flow; apply certificate-type-specific validation/routing rules; follow a specialized evaluation path for Out-of-state; log the determination; let it influence routing, document requirements, and processing logic." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd29Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "No satisfiedBy: an applicant-level In-state/Out-of-state determination does not exist anywhere in credentialing-domain.ttl. The only similarly-named field found is cred:EndorsementDefinitionAggregate's own 'OutOfState' ValueObject flag, but that describes special handling for an ENDORSEMENT TYPE, not an applicant's residency/application-routing status — a different concept with a confusingly similar name. Genuine coverage gap; see the coverage-gap Annotation below (grouped with Needs Responses since both are applicant/application-level flags absent from the same aggregate)." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "29.2.9" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a MiEdWorkforce system, I must process or assign the application based on whether the applicant is In-state or Out-of-state, so that proper handling procedures are followed." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Process/assign application by in-state vs. out-of-state" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_29_3_10> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Requirement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "Block submission only for incomplete required fields/uploads/eligibility validations (MTTC/PKS); create an endorsement application record on submission; generate confirmation/payment-link alerts; make submitted data read-only for the educator; display confirmation with a payment-completion option/link." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd29Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Second mention of 'PKS' in this FDD (alongside 29.1.2) as a named test type distinct from MTTC — see Question_PksAssessmentTypeUnconfirmed." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "29.3.10" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Op_SubmitEndorsementAddition> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a citizen user, I want to submit my additional endorsement application, so that the application record is created and I can proceed to payment (if applicable)." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Submit additional endorsement application" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_29_3_11> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Requirement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "Route per endorsement type and Business Rule Management routing rules; 'Routing considers applicable PPR workflows where required (if in future scope)'; log routing decisions with timestamp and user ID; confirm routing; the routed application appears immediately in the appropriate staff worklist." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd29Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "THE HEDGE: this story's own acceptance criteria ('...where required (if in future scope)') is the one place in all of Feature 29.3 that mentions PPR at all — everywhere else (29.3.1-29.3.10) is silent on it, which is what Rule_AutoApprovalCriteria's existing 'Confirmed by FDD 29, Feature 29.3, which consistently omits PPR/Needs-Responses routing language' note relies on. The hedge doesn't contradict that note (PPR routing for endorsements is explicitly framed as NOT current scope, 'if future scope'), but it does mean the exemption Rule_AutoApprovalCriteria documents as settled is understood by the FDD's own authors as a current-state carve-out that may not hold going forward. See Question_EndorsementPprHedgeIn29311." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "29.3.11" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Rule_ManualReviewTriggering> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a MiEdWorkforce system, I must route the completed endorsement application to the appropriate staff worklist, so that the review process can begin." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Route endorsement application" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_29_3_1> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Requirement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "Verify the user holds an existing certificate eligible for endorsement addition; offer a certificate-type choice (Teacher or School Administrator) when more than one is eligible; disable/hide the action if none is eligible; navigate to the type-specific endorsement flow on confirmed eligibility; log initiation." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd29Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "29.3.1" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Op_ListEndorsementApplications> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Op_SubmitEndorsementAddition> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a citizen user, I want to initiate an additional endorsement request from my landing page, so that I can begin the process of adding an endorsement to my eligible certificate." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Initiate additional endorsement request" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_29_3_2> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Requirement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "Confirm a valid, active certificate exists for endorsement addition; check Credential-Admin-defined eligibility rules (prerequisites, certificate type, status); prevent continuation with an informational message if ineligible; results determine which endorsement options display; log all eligibility checks and outcomes." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd29Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "No PPR/Needs-Responses check appears anywhere in this story's acceptance criteria — see this file's header note on Rule_AutoApprovalCriteria's Feature-29.3 citation." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "29.3.2" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:CredState_Valid> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:CredentialDefinitionAggregate> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a MiEdWorkforce system, I must verify that the existing certificate is eligible before allowing a citizen user to apply for an additional endorsement, so that application errors are minimized." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Verify certificate eligibility before allowing additional endorsement" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_29_3_3> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Requirement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "Display available endorsements for a selected Teacher certificate; allow selecting an endorsement even before prerequisite verification (verification occurs on next step); log displayed options." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd29Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "29.3.3" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:EndorsementDefinitionAggregate> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a citizen user, I want to see a list of available additional endorsements for Teacher certificates, so that I can select the specific endorsement I wish to add." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Display eligible endorsements for Teacher certificates" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_29_3_4> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Requirement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "Display available endorsements for a selected School Administrator certificate; require an endorsement selection to proceed; log displayed endorsements." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd29Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "29.3.4" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:EndorsementDefinitionAggregate> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a MiEdWorkforce citizen user, I must display the list of available additional endorsements for School Administrator certificates, so that the user can select the specific endorsement they wish to add." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Display eligible endorsements for School Administrator certificates" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_29_3_5> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Requirement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "Display all required/optional questions per Business Rule Management for the selected endorsement; block progress on incomplete required inputs; mark optional inputs; save all inputs to the endorsement application record." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd29Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "29.3.5" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Op_SubmitEndorsementAddition> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a citizen user, I want to provide inputs required for the additional endorsement application, so that my submission meets the required criteria." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Capture application inputs for additional endorsement" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_29_3_6> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Requirement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "Upload fields per certificate type; block submission on missing/invalid required uploads; validate accepted file formats; store uploads with the application; display an error on missing/invalid documents." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd29Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Same real match as 29.2.4 (docs:Op_RequestDocumentUpload)." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "29.3.6" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:Op_RequestDocumentUpload> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a citizen user, I want to upload documents when applying for an additional endorsement, so that I can support my application." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Upload supporting documents for additional endorsement" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_29_3_7> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Requirement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "Field-level validation on entry; application-level validation before submission; failed validations block submission with errors; Teacher- and School-Administrator-specific validations applied; outcomes logged." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd29Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "29.3.7" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Op_SubmitEndorsementAddition> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a MiEdWorkforce system, I must perform field-level and application-level validations for additional endorsement applications, so that errors are identified before submission." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Field-level and application-level validation for additional endorsement" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_29_3_8> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Requirement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "Validate MTTC scores for Teacher endorsements requiring them; display an error/warning if requirements aren't met; block submission when unmet; save verification results in the application record; log verification checks." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd29Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "29.3.8" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:AssessmentResultAggregate> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Rule_SubjectAreaAssessmentValidation> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a MiEdWorkforce system, I must perform MTTC score verification for the specific endorsement(s) requested for Teacher certificates, so that eligibility requirements are met." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Verify MTTC scores for Teacher endorsements" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_29_3_9> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Requirement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "Display the required fee amount; provide a 'Pay Fee' link to CEPAS; set status to 'Pending Payment' if not paid immediately; on successful payment, update status to 'Submitted' (or next workflow step)." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd29Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "'Pending Payment' and 'Submitted' status names are an exact match to cred:AppState_PendingPayment/AppState_Submitted." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "29.3.9" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:AppState_PendingPayment> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:AppState_Submitted> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Rule_PaymentRequirement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a MiEdWorkforce system, I must facilitate the collection of required application fees for additional endorsement requests, so that the application can be processed." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Collect and process required endorsement fees" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_29_4_1> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Requirement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "Display the user's approved/issued certificates; allow single-certificate selection via a per-row download icon; generate the selected certificate(s) in a downloadable format (PDF) on Download; disable/inform if no approved certificates exist; log downloads with timestamp and user ID." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd29Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "'select ONE OR MORE... download icon within the row' (a per-row, single-select-looking icon in WireframeAddendumA) is slightly at odds with its own 'one or more' framing in the story stem vs. 'allows the selection of a SINGLE certificate' in its own acceptance criteria — an internal inconsistency in the FDD text itself, not a graph gap; Op_PrintCredential's own request shape (credentialId, includeEndorsements) is single-credential-oriented, consistent with the acceptance-criteria (singular) reading." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "29.4.1" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Op_PrintCredential> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Seq_PrintCertificate> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:TP_CertificatePdfGeneration> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a citizen user, I want to select and download one or more approved certificates, so that I can save digital copies for my records or print them using my device." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Select and download one or more approved certificates" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_29_4_2> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Requirement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "On 'Download Cover Letter', check for pending certificate applications; generate cover letters per certificate-type business rules if any exist; display a list of generated cover letters; allow downloading a selected one; display 'No Pending Applications' if none exist; log all cover letter generation and download actions." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd29Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "See Question_CoverLetterStoryContradiction below — this is the single most significant finding of this review pass. No satisfiedBy asserted: not because nothing exists (credentialing-technical-design.ttl's cred:TP_CertificatePdfGeneration already has a 'related, not yet modeled' note pointing at exactly this feature), but because drafting a TechnicalProcess now, from contradictory evidence about whether the feature is even wanted, risks encoding the wrong thing." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "29.4.2" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a MiEdWorkforce system, I must generate downloadable cover letters based on defined business rules relevant to the type of certificate applied for, so that the user can obtain accurate documentation." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Generate downloadable cover letters" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_29_4_3> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Requirement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "Display a 'Confirm Enrollment' action button on the landing page; on click, prompt for EPP Name (from a list of EPPs), Program Level (per EPP), Program Type (per Program Level), and Student ID; on successful submission, automatically send an email to the applicant." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd29Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "PARTIAL match only, and on the wrong side of the write/read line: epp:EnrollmentStatusOperation (per epp-api.ttl) is a READ operation (checking enrollment status), while this story describes a WRITE — the citizen submitting a new enrollment-confirmation record for EPP verification. No write operation for citizen-submitted enrollment confirmation exists in either credentialing-api.ttl or epp-api.ttl. This story itself was a LATE ADDITION to the Addendum's own numbering (see Question_ConfirmEnrollmentLateAddition) — it reuses the 29.4.3 number already claimed by the 'View Enrollment Information' heading immediately above it, which is why 29.4.3/29.4.4 collide throughout the rest of Feature 29.4 (see this file's header note). Wireframe4 (Confirm enrollment form, viewed independently) already existed in the main Business Specifications section and matches this story's fields exactly, despite the review thread implying the story itself was newly drafted — the UI design outpaced its own formal user-story writeup." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "29.4.3" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:epp:EnrollmentStatusOperation> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a MiEdWorkforce Citizen user, I want to confirm my enrollment with a Michigan Educator Preparation Provider (EPP) from my landing page, so that I can establish my enrollment record in the system for verification by my EPP." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Confirm enrollment with a Michigan EPP" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_29_4_3b> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Requirement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "On 'My Professional Learning' > 'View Enrollment Information', retrieve enrollment data from the Manage EPP source; display Student ID, Provider, Program Level, Program(s), Submitted Date, Status, Enrollment Date, Exit Date exactly as provided by the EPP source; include filter/sort options if designed; log each access." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd29Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "The FDD's own text numbers this story '29.4.4' but it sits directly under the '29.4.3 View Enrollment Information' heading and is conceptually that heading's story — kept here as Req_29_4_3b (not Req_29_4_4) to avoid colliding with the differently-themed View-Pending-Applications story that the FDD ALSO numbers 29.4.4 (Req_29_4_4 below); sd:requirementId preserves the FDD's own literal, colliding number verbatim per this file's header note. 'My Professional Learning' as a containing menu location corroborates the comment-96517507 thread (Punniyamoorthy: 'Professional learning is different from Enrollment Information. Need a separate story for view Professional Learning' -> 'Added'/'This has been changed') — Enrollment Information appears to have been nested under a broader Professional Learning area in response to that comment, consistent with plrn:ProfessionalLearningContext (a stub-only context for Credentialing) being the actual home for a standalone 'View Professional Learning' capability this FDD doesn't itself detail. Read operation exists (epp:EnrollmentStatusOperation); filter/sort ('if designed') is explicitly conditional in the FDD's own text, not asserted as required." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "29.4.4 (heading: View Enrollment Information)" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:epp:EnrollmentStatusOperation> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a MiEdWorkforce citizen user, I want to view the status and details of my enrollment information in a clear table format, so that I can review my EPP details." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "View enrollment status/details in table format" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_29_4_4> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Requirement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "On selecting View List of Pending Certificate Applications, check whether pending applications exist; if so, display Application #/Certificate Type/Submitted On/Status per MiEdWorkforce UI/UX table standards; display an informational message if none exist; log each access." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd29Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Direct match; near-duplicate of 29.1.3's pending-applications display (same table shape) but framed as its own dedicated list view rather than a landing-page section — consistent with WireframeAddendumE's separate 'My Credentials > Applications' tab. Same '29.4.4' collision as Req_29_4_3b — see this file's header note and Question_ConfirmEnrollmentLateAddition." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "29.4.4 (heading: View Pending Certificate Applications)" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Op_ListApplications> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a MiEdWorkforce citizen user, I want to view a list of all pending certificate applications with status and submission date details, so that I can track my application progress." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "View pending certificate applications list" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_29_4_5> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Requirement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "Select a pending application from the list; check its status; if Submitted, allow deletion via a 'More' (three-dot) menu's Delete option; require confirmation before permanent deletion; if no longer Submitted, prevent deletion with an informational message; log deletes with timestamp, user ID, and application ID; deleted applications cannot be recovered by the citizen." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd29Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Strong direct match, including the exact Submitted-only gate. WireframeAddendumE (viewed) directly confirms the 'More' three-dot menu -> Delete UX pattern described here." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "29.4.5" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:AppState_Submitted> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Op_DeleteApplication> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Seq_DeletePendingApplication> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a MiEdWorkforce citizen user, I want to delete a pending certificate application that is still in 'Submitted' status, so that I can remove erroneous applications before they are processed." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Delete a pending certificate application" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_29_BizSpec_AddCollegeCredits> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Requirement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd29Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "No satisfiedBy: no CollegeCredit-shaped DomainEntity/ValueObject nor any corresponding ApiOperation/Sequence exists anywhere in credentialing-domain.ttl/credentialing-api.ttl/credentialing-sequences.ttl. This is one of the three Business-Specifications-only features never given its own Addendum Feature number at all (see Question_AddendumOmitsThreeBizSpecFeatures) — genuine coverage gap, grouped with Add DPPD and Complete SCECH Evaluations below since all three share the same 'wireframed and described, never formalized into a numbered story, never modeled downstream' shape." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "29 (Business Specifications, unnumbered — 'Add College Credits')" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "The MiEdWorkforce Citizen user will be able to click on Add College Credits on the landing page and provide: Course number, Course Title, Semester Credit hours, Name of the College/University, Date Completed. The system will perform business rule validation when collecting the college credit information." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Add college credits toward certificate requirements" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_29_BizSpec_AddDPPD> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Requirement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd29Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "No satisfiedBy: no DPPD-shaped entity or operation exists anywhere in credentialing's files. Dependencies section's own 'College credit validation and DPPD validation will be defined in Business Rule Management (4)' line is consistent with the validation LOGIC being out of Credentialing's own scope, but the DATA CAPTURE (the form itself, the stored DPPD record) has no home either — that half isn't a Business-Rule-Management concern and does need a Credentialing (or Professional Learning) model somewhere. Grouped with the other two unpromoted Business-Specifications features below." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "29 (Business Specifications, unnumbered — 'Add DPPD')" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "The MiEdWorkforce Citizen user will be able to click on Add DPPD on the landing page to add: Professional Development Category, Activity Title, School District, Hours Engaged, Date — with Business Rule validation — and will have the ability to submit additional DPPD form(s) as part of the certificate renewal application." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Add District Provided Professional Development (DPPD) hours" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_29_BizSpec_CompleteSCECHEvaluations> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Requirement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd29Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "No satisfiedBy: credentialing-domain.ttl's own header comment already documents that 'proflearning's SCECH endpoint' doesn't exist as a real integration ('Left unresolved on purpose so the ambient SHACL check surfaces it as the real, documented gap it is') — this FDD independently describes a full citizen-facing UI (view-awaiting-evaluation list + submit-evaluation action) for exactly that already-known-missing SCECH surface. Corroborates, rather than newly discovers, the existing gap on credentialing's Dependency to plrn:ProfessionalLearningContext." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "29 (Business Specifications, unnumbered — 'Complete SCECH Evaluations')" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "The MiEdWorkforce Citizen user will be able to click on Complete SCECH Evaluations on the landing page to view programs attended that are awaiting evaluation (SCECH Sponsor, SCECH Coordinator, Program Name, Event Date, Evaluation), select a record, and submit the evaluation." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "View and complete SCECH evaluations for attended programs" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_29_BizSpec_ViewProfessionalLearningHoursSummary> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Requirement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd29Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "No satisfiedBy. This is exactly the capability comment thread 96517507 (Punniyamoorthy: 'Professional learning is different from Enrollment Information. Need a separate story for view Professional Learning') asked to have split out as its own story — the replies ('Added'/'This has been changed') suggest something was adjusted, but no distinct 'View Professional Learning [hours]' Feature/story number exists anywhere in the Addendum as written; only the enrollment-information view (Req_29_4_3b) got a 'My Professional Learning' menu placement. Whether a genuinely separate PD-hours-summary story was ever drafted elsewhere (a later revision, or FDD 28 - Professional Learning - Processing, named in this FDD's own Dependencies section) isn't confirmable from this document alone." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "29 (Business Specifications, unnumbered — 'view PD hours by source and total')" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "The MiEdWorkforce Citizen user will have the ability to view the Professional Development hours they earned by source and total hours: College credits, District uploaded PD and SCECHs, DPPD Earned prior to July 01, 2020, Totals." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "View Professional Development hours earned by source and total" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_31_1_1> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Requirement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "Landing page displays hyperlink 'Educator Credential Search' below the banner; no login required; clicking navigates to the Michigan Educator Credential Search Landing Page." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd31_1_2Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "The 'no authentication' half of this story is solidly confirmed by cred:Rule_PublicEducatorCredentialSearch ('no authentication and no permission check') and cred:Op_SearchPublicEducatorCredentials's sd:requiresAuth false. The landing-page-hyperlink PLACEMENT itself is public-portal chrome, not a credentialing capability — see the out-of-scope Annotation below (shared with epp:Req_31_4_1/plrn:Req_31_5_1, all three describing the same shared landing page per cred:WireframeLandingPageThreeSearches)." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "31.1.1" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Rule_PublicEducatorCredentialSearch> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a member of the public, I want an Educator Credential Search hyperlink available on the MiEdWorkforce landing page, found below the MiEdWorkforce banner, so that I can access the search without logging in." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Educator Credential Search hyperlink on MiEdWorkforce landing page, no login" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_31_1_2> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Requirement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "System ignores special characters entered in the search field; accepts letters/numbers/special characters as input; still returns matches for text including special characters (e.g. D'Angelo returning DAngelo)." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd31_1_2Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Direct match — the rule's statement explicitly says 'special characters ignored'." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "31.1.2" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Rule_PublicEducatorCredentialSearch> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a member of the public, I want the system to ignore special characters during a basic search so that minor differences in input do not prevent a match." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Ignore special characters during basic search" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_31_1_3> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Requirement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "Returns full and partial matches for text and numeric criteria; strips leading/trailing spaces; does not strip embedded spaces." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd31_1_2Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Direct match — the rule's statement explicitly says 'free-text, partial-match, whitespace-stripped'." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "31.1.3" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Rule_PublicEducatorCredentialSearch> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a member of the public, I want the search function to return full and partial matches and strip leading and trailing spaces but not embedded spaces so that I can find credentials even with incomplete or slightly inaccurate input." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Full/partial match, strip leading/trailing (not embedded) spaces" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_31_1_4> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Requirement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "Filters out educators with a NULL Code ID. Displays Certificate statuses Valid/Expired/Nullified/Revoked/Suspended. Displays Temporary Credential statuses Valid/PPR Withdrawn (current school year only)." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd31_1_2Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Direct match — the rule's statement explicitly says 'Only credentials with a non-null CredentialStatus are returned... results include Valid, Expired, Nullified, Revoked, and Suspended credentials, plus temporary permits Valid or PPR Withdrawn within the current academic school year.'" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "31.1.4" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Rule_PublicEducatorCredentialSearch> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a system user, I require the system to filter out educators whose Code ID has a NULL value from the returned search results." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Filter out NULL Code ID; include only defined Certificate/Temporary-Credential statuses" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_31_1_5> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Requirement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "Credential Type search field dynamically filters results; allows multiple selections; default value is 'All'; filters apply once 'Apply Filters' is selected." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd31_1_2Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "No satisfiedBy: cred:Op_SearchPublicEducatorCredentials has no sd:parameters property at all — neither this multi-select Credential Type filter nor the Advanced Search's free-text Credential Number field (also part of this FDD's Business Specifications, though not separately numbered in the Addendum) are modeled as queryable parameters anywhere in credentialing-api.ttl. Genuine coverage gap — see Annotation below." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "31.1.5" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a member of the public, I want the Credential Type filter to allow multiple selections or default to All so that I can search broadly or narrowly by specific credential types." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Credential Type filter: multiple selections or default All" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_31_1_6> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Requirement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "Displays 'No results found' on a no-match search; message disappears on Clear/Clear Search or on a corrected search that returns results." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd31_1_2Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "No satisfiedBy: this is purely a client-side validation-message behavior with no corresponding modeled element (no sd:errorResponses on cred:Op_SearchPublicEducatorCredentials either). Confirmed as a real, designed screen by cred:WireframeNoResultsHifi (viewed directly). Folded into the same coverage-gap Annotation as 31.1.5, since both are 'search-request-shape' details never promoted onto the ApiOperation." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "31.1.6" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a member of the public, I want to see an error message ('No results found') when my search criteria yields no results." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "'No results found' validation message" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_31_2_1> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Requirement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "Initial search results reflect real-time data." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd31_1_2Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "A synchronous GET endpoint over live data satisfies 'real-time' by construction; no separate caching/staleness concern documented anywhere else in credentialing." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "31.2.1" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Op_SearchPublicEducatorCredentials> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a member of the public, I want the search results to be real-time data so that I view the most current credential statuses." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Real-time search results" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_31_2_2> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Requirement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "Initial results table includes Name and Credential Type(s), hyperlinked on Name; clicking displays the Credential Information for that educator." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd31_1_2Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Good match on the two-step search-then-detail flow. Discrepancy worth flagging: this story (31.2.2) says the hyperlink is on the educator's Name, but 31.2.4 below says the hyperlink is on the Credential Number. The FDD's own Business Specifications section (non-addendum prose) also describes both patterns in different paragraphs. Not resolved here — see the discrepancy Annotation below (shared with 31.2.4)." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "31.2.2" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Op_GetPublicEducatorCredentialHistory> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Op_SearchPublicEducatorCredentials> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a member of the public, I want the initial results to be hyperlinked so that I can click to view the full Credential Information for an individual." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Hyperlinked initial results to full Credential Information" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_31_2_3> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Requirement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "Credentials compartmentalized into 'Active Credentials,' 'Active Temporary Credentials,' and 'Inactive Credentials.' Columns: Name, Credential Number, Subject/Grade Level, Issue Date, Expiration Date, Status. No Issue/Expiration Date shown for an individual endorsement." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd31_1_2Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Real discrepancy: cred:Rule_PublicEducatorCredentialSearch's own statement describes a two-way split ('a detail view groups that educator's credentials into Active (Valid) and Inactive... sections'), but this FDD's acceptance criteria (and cred:WireframeCredentialHistoryHifi, confirmed by direct viewing) describe a THREE-way split — Active Credentials / Active Temporary Credentials / Inactive Credentials — with Active Temporary Credentials carrying its own District column not modeled anywhere on cred:IssuedCredentialAggregate or any permit-related entity. The rule and cred:Op_GetPublicEducatorCredentialHistory's projection need to be extended to a 3-way grouping with a District field on temporary-credential rows, not just the 2-way split currently documented." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "31.2.3" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Op_GetPublicEducatorCredentialHistory> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Rule_PublicEducatorCredentialSearch> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a member of the public, I want the Credential History display to show Credential Number, Name, Subject/Grade Level, Issue Date, Expiration Date, and Status so that I have a comprehensive view of the educator's credentials." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Credential History display: Number, Name, Subject/Grade, Issue/Expiration, Status" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_31_2_4> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Requirement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "Results include hyperlinks on Credential Numbers; default view collapsed; Credential Numbers with more than one result display a hyperlink to expand ('x' icon to collapse); expanded view shows all certificates/endorsements with expiration dates/statuses at the certificate level." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd31_1_2Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Same hyperlink-placement discrepancy as 31.2.2 — see Annotation below." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "31.2.4" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Op_GetPublicEducatorCredentialHistory> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a member of the public, I want multiple credentials under the same credential, for an individual, to be collapsed by default and viewable via a hyperlink on the Credential Number, so the initial results are concise." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Multiple credentials collapsed by default, expand via Credential Number hyperlink" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_31_2_5> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Requirement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "Multiple credentials sorted descending by Issue Date; same-Credential-Type secondary sort ascending alphabetically by Status." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd31_1_2Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Direct match — the rule's statement explicitly says 'Sort: multiple credentials descending by Issue Date; within the same Credential Type, ascending alphabetically by Status.'" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "31.2.5" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Rule_PublicEducatorCredentialSearch> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a member of the public, I want the system to sort multiple credentials in descending order by Issue Date, and those of the same type alphabetically by Status (Valid, Expired, Nullified, Revoked, Suspended)." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Sort: descending Issue Date, then ascending Status" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_31_2_6> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Requirement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "Nullified/Revoked/Suspended certificates and PPR-Withdrawn temporary credentials (current school year) display blank Issue Date and Expiration Date." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd31_1_2Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Direct match — cred:Op_GetPublicEducatorCredentialHistory's projection explicitly says 'issuedAt/expiresAt blanked for Nullified/Revoked/Suspended/PPR-Withdrawn per Rule_PublicEducatorCredentialSearch.'" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "31.2.6" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Op_GetPublicEducatorCredentialHistory> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Rule_PublicEducatorCredentialSearch> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a member of the public, when a credential has an adverse action (Nullified, Revoked, Suspended, or PPR Withdrawn), I want the Issue Date and Expiration Date to be blank." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Blank Issue/Expiration Date for adverse-action statuses" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_31_2_7> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Requirement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "Exclamation icon next to PPR Withdrawn/Revoked/Suspended statuses; message below results: 'Adverse actions have been taken on a credential for this individual. For information regarding this credential, contact the Michigan Department of Education at MDE-Professional-Practice@michigan.gov.'" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd31_1_2Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Direct match — projection explicitly includes 'hasAdverseAction/adverseActionMessage.' cred:WireframeCredentialHistoryHifi (viewed directly) shows the exact red banner text described here." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "31.2.7" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Op_GetPublicEducatorCredentialHistory> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a member of the public, I want an exclamation icon and an adverse action message to display for revoked or suspended credentials, providing MDE contact information." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Adverse-action icon and MDE contact message" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_31_2_8> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Requirement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "Credential results page includes a 'Back to Educator Credentials' button; clicking navigates to the previous search page." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd31_1_2Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "No satisfiedBy: pure client-side page navigation, no backend operation involved. Folded into the out-of-scope UI-chrome Annotation below (shared with 31.2.9 and the landing-page hyperlinks) rather than treated as a credentialing coverage gap." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "31.2.8" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a member of the public, I want a 'Back to Educator Credentials' button to easily return to my previous search results page." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "'Back to Educator Credentials' navigation button" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_31_2_9> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Requirement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "Hyperlink titled 'Learn about Credential Types' opens a new window; URL provided by MDE." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd31_1_2Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "No satisfiedBy: a static MDE-provided external link, not modeled data. Folded into the out-of-scope UI-chrome Annotation below." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "31.2.9" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a member of the public, I want a 'Learn about Credential Types' hyperlink that opens a new window so that I can gain external context about credentials." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "'Learn about Credential Types' external link" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Req_31_3> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Requirement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd31_3Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "No satisfiedBy — deliberately rejected, not a gap. The FDD's own Addendum confirms: 'There are no user stories defined for implementation. If data regarding these historical special education approvals is needed, internal State of Michigan users will work internally to retrieve it, rather than having it available through the MiEdWorkforce public interface.' This exactly matches, and CONFIRMS AS ACCURATE, credentialing-domain.ttl's existing citation on cred:Rule_PublicEducatorCredentialSearch." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "31.3" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "This feature was created to account for the Special Education Approvals issued prior to 2014, L2K and SCR reports available within MOECS. This functionality will not be carried into MiEdWorkforce, and therefore this feature is not needed. Internal SOM users will have access to the Special Education Approvals issued prior to 2014 outside of MiEdWorkforce when necessary." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Legacy Reports (pre-2014 Special Education Approvals) — feature not carried into MiEdWorkforce" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:RequiredAssessments> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:ValueObject> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:description> "List of required competency assessments with combination logic (AND/OR)." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:fields> "AssessmentIdentifier (reference to assessment definition), CombinationLogic (AND/OR), MinimumScore (may override assessment definition default)" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:name> "RequiredAssessments" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Rule_AssessmentResultValidity> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:BusinessRule> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:appliesTo> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:AssessmentResultAggregate> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:DomainDoc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:enforcedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:AssessmentResultAggregate> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:enforcedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Seq_ValidateAssessmentResults> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:example> "An educator has a valid MTTC-022 score of 230 from 2018. In 2023 the state updates the AssessmentDefinition to require scores from the last 5 years. When the educator applies for a new endorsement in 2024, their 2018 score is expired and cannot be used; they must retake the assessment or apply for a waiver." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:rationale> "Ensures educators demonstrate current competency. Validity periods vary by assessment type and jurisdiction policy." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "Some assessments have validity periods (e.g., scores older than 5 years are not accepted). Assessment results with expiration dates cannot be used for endorsement applications after expiration, even if the score was previously valid." .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Rule_AutoApprovalCriteria> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:BusinessRule> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:appliesTo> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:CredentialApplicationAggregate> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:DomainDoc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:enforcedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Seq_ApplicationAutoApproval> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:example> "Educator submits teaching certificate application with valid assessment scores, complete documents, and payment. Professional Practices clears them within 2 hours. Application automatically transitions from Submitted -> Approved -> CredentialIssued without human intervention." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Exception — Endorsement Additions: criterion 1 (ProfessionalPracticeStatus = Clear) does not apply to endorsement-addition applications (ApplicationType = Endorsement) — these are gated only by assessment results, documents, and payment. Confirmed by FDD 29, Feature 29.3, which consistently omits PPR/Needs-Responses routing language present in every other application type's feature description; see credentialing-sequences.md's 'Add Endorsement to Certificate' sequence, which has no PPR check step. Exception Handling: if any criterion fails, application transitions to Awaiting Manual Review with ManualReviewReason set to indicate which criterion failed." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:rationale> "Reduces processing time for routine applications; reserves manual review for edge cases or policy exceptions." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "Applications are automatically approved (without manual review) when ALL of: (1) ProfessionalPracticeStatus = Clear; (2) all required assessment results meet passing criteria; (3) payment received (or waived); (4) all required documents uploaded and verified; (5) all eligibility rules satisfied per CredentialDefinition." .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Rule_CertificateDocumentGeneration> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:BusinessRule> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:appliesTo> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:IssuedCredentialAggregate> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:DomainDoc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:enforcedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Op_PrintCredential> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:enforcedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Seq_PrintCertificate> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:example> "Application approved -> CredentialIssued event published -> PDF generation service consumes event, retrieves credential details via Credentialing API, renders PDF using a Documents-capability template, stores PDF in Documents referenced by credential ID -> educator downloads from 'My Credentials'." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Revoked/Nullified/Suspended Certificates: per FDD 29 (Feature 29.1.6, 29.1.9), the citizen-facing certificate list/print action displays credentials in these three statuses with issuance and expiration dates BLANK rather than omitting them or showing the original dates — a new, previously-undocumented rendering rule for the PDF/list, not a new aggregate state. Technical implementation detail lives in credentialing-technical-design.ttl's cred:TP_CertificatePdfGeneration, not duplicated here." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:rationale> "Provides official documentation of credential for employment verification, compliance audits, and educator records." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "When a credential is issued, the system generates a printable PDF certificate containing official credential details (educator name, credential type/category, issuance date, expiration date, endorsements with grade bands, unique credential ID, state seal/branding). The PDF is stored in the Documents capability and accessible to the credential holder for download." .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Rule_CleanupOfFutureDatedChanges> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:BusinessRule> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:appliesTo> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:CredentialDefinitionAggregate> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:appliesTo> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:EndorsementDefinitionAggregate> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:DomainDoc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:enforcedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:CredentialDefinitionAggregate> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:enforcedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:EndorsementDefinitionAggregate> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:example> "An admin schedules a fee increase for July 1, 2025. In June they realize the amount is incorrect and update the scheduled change. The July 1 version reflects the corrected fee, and the original scheduled change is replaced in the audit history." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "The nightly batch process implied by this rule is modeled as cred:BatchJob_DefinitionVersionActivation in credentialing-technical-design.ttl." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:rationale> "Allows administrators to schedule changes in advance while retaining flexibility to adjust before they take effect." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "If an administrator sets a future Effective From date for a credential definition change and then modifies or cancels it before that date arrives, the pending change is replaced or removed without affecting the currently active version." .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Rule_CredentialDefinitionVersioning> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:BusinessRule> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:appliesTo> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:CredentialDefinitionAggregate> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:appliesTo> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:EndorsementDefinitionAggregate> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:DomainDoc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:enforcedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:CredentialDefinitionAggregate> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:enforcedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:EndorsementDefinitionAggregate> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:enforcedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Seq_ConfigureCredentialDefinition> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:enforcedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Seq_ConfigureEndorsementDefinition> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:example> "On January 1, 2025 the State changes the GPA requirement for Teaching Certificates from 2.5 to 3.0. An application submitted December 30, 2024 is evaluated against the 2.5 requirement; an application submitted January 2, 2025 is evaluated against the 3.0 requirement." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:rationale> "Ensures applicants are evaluated against the rules in effect when they applied, not rules that change mid-process. Maintains historical accuracy for compliance audits." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "Changes to credential or endorsement definitions must create a new version with an Effective From date. Historical versions remain queryable for audit and reporting purposes. Applications in progress use the definition version active at the time of submission." .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Rule_CredentialStatusTransitions> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:BusinessRule> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:appliesTo> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:IssuedCredentialAggregate> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:DomainDoc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:enforcedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:IssuedCredentialAggregate> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:enforcedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Seq_SuspendOrRevokeCredential> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:example> "An educator whose teaching certificate was revoked due to professional misconduct cannot submit a renewal. They must apply as a new applicant and undergo full review, including updated PPR screening." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:rationale> "Ensures educators who lost credentials due to professional misconduct undergo full re-evaluation." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "Suspended or revoked credentials cannot be renewed. A new application is required, and approval is subject to review of the suspension/revocation cause." .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Rule_IdpForPermitRenewals> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:BusinessRule> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:appliesTo> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:CredentialApplicationAggregate> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:DomainDoc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:enforcedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Op_SubmitRenewal> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:enforcedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Seq_RenewCredential> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:example> "Educator applies for 2nd FYBSP renewal; Professional Learning confirms 8 semester hours completed against a 6-hour requirement — renewal auto-approved. A second educator's renewal shows only 3 hours completed; the application is flagged InsufficientIDPProgress and a credential processor reviews." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Open Item (2026-08-27): proflearning-domain.md has no IndividualDevelopmentPlan aggregate, and proflearning-api.yml does not define the GET /educators/{uniqueId}/idp/status endpoint this rule assumes. credentialing-sequences.md's 'Renew Credential' sequence instead treats IDP as a manually-uploaded document with no Professional Learning API call at all — the two SDD documents disagree on the verification mechanism, and neither has been built. See the '14-professional-learning-admin' review, Discrepancy #1, and proflearning-domain.md Open Question #7. This rule's structured, API-driven model (matching FDD 17's specific per-renewal numeric requirements) reads as the intended design, but building it is proflearning-domain work, not resolved here." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:rationale> "Ensures temporary permit holders are actively working toward full credential, not indefinitely relying on substitute status." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "Full Year Basic Substitute Permit renewals require an approved Individual Development Plan (IDP) documenting professional growth and progress toward full certification. 1st Renewal: IDP must show enrollment in a state-approved teacher prep program. 2nd & 3rd Renewals: IDP must document a minimum of 6 semester hours completed since the previous renewal. Credentialing validates IDP requirements are met; Professional Learning manages IDP content and approval." .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Rule_ManualReviewTriggering> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:BusinessRule> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:appliesTo> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:CredentialApplicationAggregate> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:DomainDoc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:enforcedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Op_ApproveApplication> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:enforcedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Op_DenyApplication> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:enforcedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Seq_ApplicationAutoApproval> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:enforcedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Seq_ApplicationManualReviewAndApproval> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:example> "When processor makes a decision, they call POST /applications/{id}/approve or POST /applications/{id}/deny. Credentialing updates state to Approved or Denied and publishes corresponding events." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:rationale> "Separates business logic (what requires review?) from the processor's own workflow of finding and acting on flagged applications, while keeping both within Credentialing's own list/detail/approve/deny endpoints and permissions." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "Applications are flagged with ManualReviewRequired = true when: (1) ProfessionalPracticeStatus = Hold, Blocked, or ConditionalClearance; (2) required assessment results missing or failing; (3) required supporting documents not uploaded or rejected during scan; (4) application responses indicate policy exception scenario; (5) credential type requires specialist review (per CredentialDefinition configuration). When flagged, the system publishes ApplicationRequiresManualReview and the application becomes visible through Credentialing's own filtered application list endpoint (e.g. GET /applications?status=RequiresManualReview) — there is no separate task-routing or assignment service; a processor with the appropriate application-processing permission works the list directly." .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Rule_MentorAssignmentRequirementForPermits> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:BusinessRule> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:appliesTo> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:CredentialApplicationAggregate> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:DomainDoc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:enforcedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Op_AdminIssuePermit> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:enforcedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Seq_SubmitPermitApplication> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:example> "Applicant applies for Extended Daily Substitute Permit, enters Mentor Unique ID '12345678'; system verifies the mentor holds a valid Professional Teaching Certificate and the application proceeds. Contrast: a School Social Worker Permit applicant whose mentor is an external college professor selects 'Mentor is external', enters free-form details, and the application is flagged for manual verification." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Cross-Domain Endpoint Note (added during FDD 10 review, 2026-08-14): the GET /educators/{uniqueId} call this rule assumes on the Staffing API does not exist — staffing-api.yml's closest endpoint (GET /educators/search) only returns a free-text activeCredentialSummary string, and staffing-domain.md's own Dependencies table has Staffing calling Credentialing for this exact purpose, the reverse of what this rule assumes. See credentialing-technical-design.md Open Technical Question #8 / Question_StaffingMentorVerificationEndpoint — needs a decision, not a guess, since it determines which domain actually owns the mentor-credential check. Post-approval: Credentialing publishes CredentialIssued with mentor reference; Staffing consumes it to create the formal mentor-mentee assignment record. Ongoing mentorship compliance monitoring is out of scope for Credentialing (handled by the Compliance domain cross-referencing Staffing assignments)." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:rationale> "State requirements mandate mentorship for temporary permit holders. Credentialing validates the requirement is met during application; Staffing manages actual assignment tracking." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "Permit applications requiring mentorship (EDSP, EEDSP, SAP, SSWP) must capture mentor assignment information. Credentialing validates that a mentor reference is provided but does NOT manage the ongoing mentor-mentee relationship. Mentor information is captured either as a Mentor Unique ID (preferred — validated via Staffing) or free-form details for external mentors not in the system (flags the application for manual review, reason UnverifiedMentorAssignment). No mentor provided when required is a hard stop." .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Rule_PaymentRequirement> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:BusinessRule> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:appliesTo> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:CredentialApplicationAggregate> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:DomainDoc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:enforcedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Seq_ApplicationAutoApproval> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:example> "An educator pays $100 for a Daily Substitute Permit in September. In November, they apply for a Full Year Basic Substitute Permit; no additional fee is required because they've already paid the annual credential fee." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Enforced via Payments domain integration during application processing — 'per school year' definition (calendar/fiscal/academic year) is itself Open Question #24, unresolved. How Credentialing checks current payment status at all is a separate, related open question — see Question_PaymentStatusCheckEndpoint in credentialing-technical-design.ttl." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:rationale> "Reduces financial burden on educators making multiple applications in the same year." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "One permit/certificate fee per educator per school year, regardless of number of applications submitted." .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Rule_PermitDurationAndRenewalLimits> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:BusinessRule> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:appliesTo> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:CredentialApplicationAggregate> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:appliesTo> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:CredentialDefinitionAggregate> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:DomainDoc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:enforcedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:CredentialApplicationAggregate> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:enforcedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:CredentialDefinitionAggregate> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:enforcedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Seq_RenewCredential> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:example> "An educator on a Full Year Basic Substitute Permit applying for their 4th renewal is denied because the 3-renewal limit has been reached. They must either complete a teacher prep program for full certification or cannot continue teaching." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:rationale> "Permits are temporary measures; extended use requires demonstration of progress toward full certification or documented need." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "Each permit type has specific maximum duration and renewal limits: Daily Substitute Permit 90 days/assignment; Extended Daily +90 days (requires mentor, observation); Emergency Extended Daily +90 days (cannot exceed 270 total days combined); Full Year Basic Substitute max 3 renewals (4 years total); Full Year Shortage Substitute max 3 renewals (requires effective/highly effective ratings); School Administrator Permit not renewable; School Social Worker Permit max 1 renewal." .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Rule_ProfessionalPracticeClearance> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:BusinessRule> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:appliesTo> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:CredentialApplicationAggregate> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:DomainDoc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:enforcedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:CredentialApplicationAggregate> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:enforcedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Seq_ApplicationAutoApproval> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:enforcedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Seq_RenewCredential> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:enforcedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Seq_SubmitNewCertificateApplication> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:enforcedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Seq_SubmitPermitApplication> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:example> "An educator submits a certificate application. Professional Practices clears them (or holds/blocks/conditionally clears them) before the application can advance to auto-approval or manual review." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Integration Pattern (synchronous check on submission vs. purely event-driven) is UNRESOLVED — see credentialing-domain.md Open Question #33 and Question_PPRCheckTiming below." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:rationale> "State compliance requires conviction disclosure review and background check clearance before credential issuance." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "Applications cannot proceed to final approval if ProfessionalPracticeStatus = Blocked. Applications with ProfessionalPracticeStatus = Hold must wait for clearance from Professional Practices before proceeding. Applications with ProfessionalPracticeStatus = ConditionalClearance cannot auto-approve and are routed to manual review; if PPR's assessment sets RequiresFelonyAcknowledgment, the district must complete the felony disclosure acknowledgment before the application can proceed." .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Rule_PublicEducatorCredentialSearch> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:BusinessRule> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:appliesTo> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:IssuedCredentialAggregate> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:DomainDoc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:enforcedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Op_GetPublicEducatorCredentialHistory> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:enforcedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Op_SearchPublicEducatorCredentials> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:example> "An employer searches 'Jane Smith' and sees her held credential types; opening her detail view shows Active/Inactive credentials with blank dates and an adverse-action contact message (MDE-Professional-Practice@michigan.gov) for any Revoked/Suspended/PPR-Withdrawn entry." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Reuses the blank-issuance/expiration-date rule from Rule_CertificateDocumentGeneration and extends it to permits with PPR Withdrawn status in the active school year. Not modeled here: FDD 31.3's 'Legacy Reports' (pre-2014 Special Education Approvals, L2K/SCR reports from MOECS) — explicitly out of scope per the FDD; internal SOM users retrieve that historical data outside the system." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:rationale> "State transparency requirement — members of the public (employers, districts) need to verify an educator's credential status without an account. Not the same capability as credentialing.credential.view (scope-gated for authenticated users) — a separate, unauthenticated read path over a subset of the same data." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "Members of the public can search issued credentials with no authentication and no permission check (FDD 31.1/31.2). Search matches on educator name or credential_number (free-text, partial-match, whitespace-stripped, special characters ignored). Only credentials with a non-null CredentialStatus are returned (Pending excluded); results include Valid, Expired, Nullified, Revoked, and Suspended credentials, plus temporary permits Valid or PPR Withdrawn within the current academic school year. Results are grouped per educator; a detail view groups that educator's credentials into Active (Valid) and Inactive (Expired, Nullified, Revoked, Suspended, permit PPR Withdrawn) sections. Sort: multiple credentials descending by Issue Date; within the same Credential Type, ascending alphabetically by Status." .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Rule_SubjectAreaAssessmentValidation> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:BusinessRule> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:appliesTo> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:CredentialApplicationAggregate> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:appliesTo> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:EndorsementDefinitionAggregate> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:DomainDoc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:enforcedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:EndorsementDefinitionAggregate> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:enforcedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Seq_AddEndorsementToCertificate> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:enforcedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Seq_ValidateAssessmentResults> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:example> "A Secondary Mathematics endorsement requires assessment 'MTTC-022-Mathematics' with a passing score of 220. If the educator has a verified score of 225, the endorsement can proceed via auto-approval. If score is 219, the application is flagged for manual review. If the requirement changes to 'Praxis-5161' with passing score 157, existing applications are evaluated against the definition version active at submission time." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:rationale> "State/jurisdiction requirements mandate subject area competency verification through approved assessments. Assessment types and passing criteria are configurable to accommodate policy changes." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "Endorsement applications require passing assessment results for all required competency assessments. Assessment requirements can be combined with AND logic (all must pass) or OR logic (any one must pass). Passing criteria are defined in the AssessmentDefinition and may vary by assessment." .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:ScoreValue> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:ValueObject> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:description> "Numerical score or rubric rating achieved." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:name> "ScoreValue" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:ScoringScale> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:ValueObject> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:description> "Min/max possible scores and interpretation." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:name> "ScoringScale" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Seq_AddEndorsementToCertificate> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Sequence> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:belongsToContext> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:CredentialingContext> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:content> "sequenceDiagram\n    actor Educator\n    participant UI as Credentialing UI\n    participant AppService as Application Service\n    participant RefData as Reference Data API\n    participant BRM as Business Rule Engine\n    participant EventBus as Event Bus\n\n    Educator->>UI: Navigate to \"Add Endorsement\"\n    UI->>AppService: GET /endorsements/eligible?educatorId={id}\n    AppService->>AppService: Verify valid teaching certificate exists\n    AppService->>RefData: GET /endorsement-definitions\n    RefData-->>AppService: Available endorsements\n    AppService->>BRM: Filter by eligibility (prerequisites)\n    BRM-->>AppService: Eligible endorsements\n    AppService-->>UI: Endorsement options\n\n    Educator->>UI: Select endorsement(s)\n    UI->>AppService: GET /assessment-requirements?endorsementCodes={codes}\n    AppService->>RefData: Get assessment requirements for endorsements\n    RefData-->>AppService: Assessment requirements\n    AppService-->>UI: Required assessments\n\n    UI-->>Educator: Display assessment requirements\n\n    Educator->>UI: Answer endorsement application questions\n    Educator->>UI: Submit endorsement application\n    UI->>AppService: POST /applications/endorsements\n\n    AppService->>AppService: Retrieve educator's assessment results\n\n    alt Assessment results not found or insufficient\n        AppService->>AppService: Create application, flag for manual review\n        Note over AppService: State: Submitted > Awaiting Manual Review\n        AppService--)EventBus: ApplicationRequiresManualReview\n        AppService-->>UI: Application submitted - under review\n    else Assessment results meet requirements\n        AppService->>BRM: Validate all endorsement criteria\n        BRM-->>AppService: Validation passed\n\n        AppService->>AppService: Create CredentialApplication aggregate\n        Note over AppService: State: Submitted > Approved (auto)\n\n        AppService->>AppService: Create IssuedEndorsement aggregate\n        Note over AppService: State: Pending > Active\n\n        AppService--)EventBus: CredentialApplicationSubmitted\n        AppService--)EventBus: ApplicationApproved\n        AppService--)EventBus: EndorsementAdded\n\n        AppService-->>UI: Endorsement approved and added\n        UI-->>Educator: Confirmation\n    end\n" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:SequencesDoc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:errorScenarios> "No valid teaching certificate > Block application, display error. Assessment results insufficient > Flag for manual review, notify educator of review timeline." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:eventsPublished> "CredentialApplicationSubmitted - Application created. ApplicationApproved - Auto-approval occurred. EndorsementAdded - New endorsement now active on certificate. ApplicationRequiresManualReview - Manual review required by external workflow service." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:initiatedBy> "user" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:keyDecisions> "Assessment Validation: If results don't meet requirements, flag for external manual review. Auto-Approval: If all criteria met (assessment scores, prerequisites, payment), approve immediately. Multiple Endorsements: User may apply for multiple endorsements in single application. No PPR Check: Unlike new-certificate, permit, and renewal applications, endorsement-addition applications do not check ProfessionalPracticeStatus/PPR clearance at all — confirmed by FDD 29, whose Feature 29.3 narrative consistently omits PPR routing language present in every other application type. This is a deliberate business-rule difference, not an oversight." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "confirmed" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Add Endorsement to Certificate" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:whatWhenWho> "What: Educator applies to add a subject area endorsement to their existing teaching certificate. When: Educator has completed required coursework and subject area assessment for a new subject. Who: Authenticated educator with valid teaching certificate." .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Seq_ApplicationAutoApproval> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Sequence> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:belongsToContext> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:CredentialingContext> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:content> "sequenceDiagram\n    participant EventBus as Event Bus\n    participant AppService as Application Service\n    participant PPR as Professional Practices API\n    participant Payments as Payments API\n    participant BRM as Business Rule Engine\n    participant DocService as Document Service\n\n    EventBus->>AppService: CredentialApplicationSubmitted event\n    AppService->>AppService: Load CredentialApplication aggregate\n\n    AppService->>PPR: GET /educators/{id}/ppr-clearance\n    PPR-->>AppService: PPR status (Clear/ConditionalClearance/Hold/Blocked)\n\n    alt PPR status = Hold or Blocked\n        AppService->>AppService: Set status to Professional Practice Hold\n        Note over AppService: State: Submitted > Professional Practice Hold\n        AppService--)EventBus: ApplicationRequiresManualReview\n    else PPR status = ConditionalClearance\n        AppService->>AppService: Flag for manual review (cannot auto-approve); set felony acknowledgment requirement if indicated\n        Note over AppService: State: Submitted > Awaiting Manual Review\n        AppService--)EventBus: ApplicationRequiresManualReview\n    else PPR status = Clear\n        AppService->>AppService: Check locally cached PaymentStatus (NOTE: not yet resolved which endpoint/event backs this - see below)\n\n        alt Payment not received\n            AppService->>AppService: Update status\n            Note over AppService: State: Submitted > Pending Payment\n            Note over AppService: Wait for PaymentCompleted event (payments-capability.md), not the previously-referenced PaymentReceived, which does not exist\n        else Payment received\n            AppService->>DocService: GET /documents?applicationId={id}\n            DocService-->>AppService: Document verification\n\n            alt Required documents missing\n                AppService->>AppService: Update status\n                Note over AppService: State: Submitted > Pending Documents\n            else Documents complete\n                AppService->>BRM: Validate all business rules\n                BRM-->>AppService: Validation result\n\n                alt Assessment results or other validation fails\n                    AppService->>AppService: Flag for manual review\n                    Note over AppService: State: Submitted > Awaiting Manual Review\n                    AppService--)EventBus: ApplicationRequiresManualReview\n                else All validations pass\n                    AppService->>AppService: Auto-approve application\n                    Note over AppService: State: Submitted > Approved\n\n                    AppService->>AppService: Create IssuedCredential aggregate\n                    Note over AppService: State: Pending > Valid\n\n                    AppService--)EventBus: ApplicationApproved\n                    AppService--)EventBus: CredentialIssued\n                end\n            end\n        end\n    end\n" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:SequencesDoc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:errorScenarios> "Any validation failure > Set appropriate status or flag for external manual review." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:eventsPublished> "ApplicationApproved - Application auto-approved. CredentialIssued - Credential created and now valid. ApplicationRequiresManualReview - Manual review required (application becomes visible via Credentialing's own filtered application list)." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:initiatedBy> "internal-system" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:keyDecisions> "PPR Check: First gate - Hold or Blocked status triggers Professional Practice Hold; ConditionalClearance cannot auto-approve and always routes to manual review (with felony acknowledgment requirement if applicable); only Clear proceeds to payment/document/business-rule validation for possible auto-approval. Payment Check: Second gate - no payment means Pending Payment status. Unresolved: the endpoint/mechanism for checking current payment status isn't confirmed — payments-api.yml has no internal-service status-check endpoint; this gate may need to rely purely on the PaymentCompleted event subscription. Document Check: Third gate - missing docs means Pending Documents status. Business Rules: Final gate - assessment results, eligibility, etc.; if any fail, flag for manual review." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "confirmed" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Application Auto-Approval" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:whatWhenWho> "What: System automatically approves application when all business rules are satisfied. When: Application submitted and all validation checks pass (PPR clear, payment received, documents complete, assessment results verified). Who: System process." .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Seq_ApplicationManualReviewAndApproval> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Sequence> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:belongsToContext> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:CredentialingContext> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:content> "sequenceDiagram\n    participant ProcessorUI as Credential Processor UI\n    participant AppService as Application Service\n    participant DocService as Document Service\n    participant EventBus as Event Bus\n\n    ProcessorUI->>AppService: GET /applications/{id}/details\n    AppService-->>ProcessorUI: Full application details\n\n    ProcessorUI->>DocService: GET /documents?applicationId={id}\n    DocService-->>ProcessorUI: Uploaded documents\n\n    Note over ProcessorUI: Processor reviews application via<br/>Credentialing's own list/detail views\n\n    alt Processor approves application\n        ProcessorUI->>AppService: POST /applications/{id}/approve\n        AppService->>AppService: Update CredentialApplication aggregate\n        Note over AppService: State: Awaiting Manual Review > Approved\n\n        AppService->>AppService: Create IssuedCredential aggregate\n        Note over AppService: State: Pending > Valid\n\n        AppService--)EventBus: ApplicationApproved\n        AppService--)EventBus: CredentialIssued\n\n        AppService-->>ProcessorUI: Approval confirmed\n\n    else Processor denies application\n        ProcessorUI->>AppService: POST /applications/{id}/deny\n        AppService->>AppService: Update CredentialApplication aggregate\n        Note over AppService: State: Awaiting Manual Review > Denied\n\n        AppService--)EventBus: ApplicationDenied\n\n        AppService-->>ProcessorUI: Denial confirmed\n\n    else Processor places on hold\n        ProcessorUI->>AppService: POST /applications/{id}/on-hold\n        AppService->>AppService: Update CredentialApplication aggregate\n        Note over AppService: State: Awaiting Manual Review > On-Hold\n\n        AppService-->>ProcessorUI: Hold confirmed\n    end\n" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:SequencesDoc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:errorScenarios> "Application already processed > Display conflict error." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:eventsPublished> "ApplicationApproved - Manual approval. ApplicationDenied - Manual denial. CredentialIssued - Credential created and valid." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:initiatedBy> "user" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:keyDecisions> "Approve: Credential issued immediately, educator notified. Deny: Application rejected, educator notified with reason. On-Hold: Application remains flagged in the application list for follow-up." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "confirmed" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Application Manual Review and Approval" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:whatWhenWho> "What: Credential processor reviews application and takes action (approve/deny/hold). When: Application flagged for manual review due to PPR status, assessment failure, or other manual review trigger. Who: Credential processor, working the flagged-application list through Credentialing's own list/detail/approve/deny endpoints. Represents a processor's reviewer UI querying Credentialing's own filtered application list and detail endpoints, then acting via the existing approve/deny/hold endpoints — not a separate workflow or worklist system (see credentialing-domain.md Open Question #34 for the unresolved reviewer-to-application assignment question)." .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Seq_BulkRenewalInitiation> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Sequence> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:belongsToContext> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:CredentialingContext> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:content> "sequenceDiagram\n    actor Admin\n    participant UI as Credentialing Admin UI\n    participant AppService as Application Service\n    participant BRM as Business Rule Engine\n    participant EventBus as Event Bus\n\n    Admin->>UI: Navigate to \"Bulk Renewal\"\n    UI->>AppService: GET /credentials/expiring?filters={credentialType, expiryDateRange}\n    AppService-->>UI: List of expiring credentials\n\n    Admin->>UI: Select educators for renewal (individual or all)\n    Admin->>UI: Initiate bulk renewal\n\n    UI->>AppService: POST /applications/bulk-renewals\n\n    loop For each selected educator\n        AppService->>BRM: Evaluate renewal eligibility\n        BRM-->>AppService: Eligibility status\n\n        alt Eligible for renewal\n            AppService->>AppService: Create CredentialApplication (renewal)\n            Note over AppService: State: Draft > Submitted\n            AppService--)EventBus: CredentialApplicationSubmitted\n            Note over AppService: Application enters normal workflow:<br/>PPR check, payment, auto-approval if eligible\n        else Not eligible\n            AppService->>AppService: Log ineligible educator\n        end\n    end\n\n    AppService-->>UI: Bulk renewal summary\n    UI-->>Admin: Display: {processed, eligible, ineligible, errors}\n\n    Note over EventBus: Each application triggers:<br/>- Payment links<br/>- External workflow routing<br/>- Auto-approval if qualified\n" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:SequencesDoc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:errorScenarios> "Educator ineligible (PPR status, etc.) > Skip, log in summary. System error during processing > Rollback batch, display error." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:eventsPublished> "CredentialApplicationSubmitted - One event per renewal initiated." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:initiatedBy> "user" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:keyDecisions> "Eligibility Filtering: BRM evaluates PPR status, payment status, etc. Workflow Routing: Each renewal enters normal application workflow (may auto-approve or flag for external review)." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "confirmed" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Bulk Renewal Initiation" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:whatWhenWho> "What: Administrator initiates renewal process for multiple educators at once. When: Annual renewal cycle or targeted renewal for specific credential types. Who: User with credentialing.application.manual-submit permission." .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Seq_ConfigureAssessmentDefinition> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Sequence> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:belongsToContext> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:CredentialingContext> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:content> "sequenceDiagram\n    actor Admin\n    participant UI as Credentialing Admin UI\n    participant AppService as Application Service\n    participant IAM as Identity & Access API\n    participant EventBus as Event Bus\n\n    Admin->>UI: Navigate to \"Manage Assessment Definitions\"\n    UI->>IAM: Verify permission (credentialing.assessment-definition.manage)\n    IAM-->>UI: Permission confirmed\n\n    UI->>AppService: GET /assessment-definitions\n    AppService-->>UI: List of assessment definitions\n\n    alt Creating New Assessment\n        Admin->>UI: Click \"Create New Assessment\"\n\n        Admin->>UI: Enter assessment details\n        Note over Admin,UI: Enter: Assessment Identifier (e.g., MTTC-022),<br/>Assessment Name (e.g., Mathematics Secondary),<br/>Provider (e.g., Pearson-MTTC),<br/>Passing Criteria, Scoring Scale,<br/>Validity Period, Effective From\n\n        Admin->>UI: Submit new assessment\n        UI->>AppService: POST /assessment-definitions\n\n        AppService->>AppService: Create AssessmentDefinition aggregate\n        Note over AppService: State: Draft > Active\n\n        AppService--)EventBus: AssessmentDefinitionCreated\n        AppService-->>UI: Assessment created\n        UI-->>Admin: Confirmation - assessment now available\n\n    else Editing Existing Assessment\n        Admin->>UI: Select assessment definition to edit\n        UI->>AppService: GET /assessment-definitions/{id}\n        AppService-->>UI: Current definition and version history\n\n        Admin->>UI: Modify fields (e.g., update passing criteria, change validity period)\n        Admin->>UI: Set \"Effective From\" date for changes\n\n        Admin->>UI: Submit changes\n        UI->>AppService: PUT /assessment-definitions/{id}\n\n        AppService->>AppService: Create new version of AssessmentDefinition\n        Note over AppService: Old version preserved for historical reference\n\n        AppService--)EventBus: AssessmentDefinitionUpdated\n        AppService-->>UI: Assessment updated\n        UI-->>Admin: Confirmation with version info\n    end\n" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:SequencesDoc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:errorScenarios> "Assessment identifier already exists > Validation error. Passing criteria outside scoring scale bounds > Display error." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:eventsPublished> "AssessmentDefinitionCreated - New assessment type available. AssessmentDefinitionUpdated - Existing definition modified." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:initiatedBy> "user" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:keyDecisions> "Versioning: Changes create new versions to preserve historical passing criteria. Validity Period: Configurable per assessment (e.g., 5 years for MTTC, 10 years for Praxis)." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "confirmed" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Configure Assessment Definition" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:whatWhenWho> "What: Administrator creates or updates an assessment type definition with versioning. When: State adopts new assessment provider, changes passing criteria, or retires old assessments. Who: User with credentialing.assessment-definition.manage permission (System Admin)." .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Seq_ConfigureCredentialDefinition> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Sequence> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:belongsToContext> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:CredentialingContext> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:content> "sequenceDiagram\n    actor Admin\n    participant UI as Credentialing Admin UI\n    participant AppService as Application Service\n    participant IAM as Identity & Access API\n    participant RefData as Reference Data API\n    participant EventBus as Event Bus\n\n    Admin->>UI: Navigate to \"Manage Credential Definitions\"\n    UI->>IAM: Verify permission (credentialing.credential-definition.manage)\n    IAM-->>UI: Permission confirmed\n\n    UI->>AppService: GET /credential-definitions\n    AppService-->>UI: List of credential definitions\n\n    alt Creating New Definition\n        Admin->>UI: Click \"Create New Credential\"\n        UI->>RefData: GET /credential-categories\n        RefData-->>UI: Available categories\n\n        Admin->>UI: Select category and enter details\n        Note over Admin,UI: Enter: Print Name, Type, Category,<br/>IsPermanent, IsAdvanced, IsActive,<br/>CanApply, CanRenew, Fee, Effective From\n\n        Admin->>UI: Define requirement rules (degree, GPA, etc.)\n        Admin->>UI: Submit new definition\n\n        UI->>AppService: POST /credential-definitions\n        AppService->>AppService: Create CredentialDefinition aggregate\n        Note over AppService: State: Draft > Active (if Effective From is today or past)\n\n        AppService--)EventBus: CredentialDefinitionCreated\n        AppService-->>UI: Definition created\n        UI-->>Admin: Confirmation - credential type now available\n\n    else Editing Existing Definition\n        Admin->>UI: Select credential definition to edit\n        UI->>AppService: GET /credential-definitions/{id}\n        AppService-->>UI: Current definition details and version history\n\n        Admin->>UI: Modify fields (e.g., change fee, update requirements)\n        Admin->>UI: Set \"Effective From\" date for changes\n\n        alt Effective From = Today or Past\n            Note over Admin,UI: Changes take effect immediately\n        else Effective From = Future Date\n            Note over Admin,UI: Changes scheduled for future\n        end\n\n        Admin->>UI: Submit changes\n        UI->>AppService: PUT /credential-definitions/{id}\n\n        AppService->>AppService: Create new version of CredentialDefinition\n        Note over AppService: Old version remains for historical reference<br/>New version becomes active on Effective From date\n\n        AppService--)EventBus: CredentialDefinitionUpdated\n        AppService-->>UI: Definition updated\n        UI-->>Admin: Confirmation - version history preserved\n    end\n" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:SequencesDoc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:errorScenarios> "Admin lacks permission > Access denied. Overlapping effective date ranges > Validation error. Invalid configuration (e.g., IsPermanent=true but CanRenew=true) > Display validation errors." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:eventsPublished> "CredentialDefinitionCreated - New credential type available. CredentialDefinitionUpdated - Existing definition modified." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:initiatedBy> "user" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:keyDecisions> "Versioning: All changes create new versions rather than overwriting existing definitions. Effective Dating: Determines when changes become active; future dates allow scheduled updates. Historical Preservation: Old versions remain accessible for audit and in-progress applications." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "confirmed" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Configure Credential Definition" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:whatWhenWho> "What: Administrator creates a new credential definition or updates an existing one with versioning. When: State policy changes, new credential types introduced, or corrections needed. Who: User with credentialing.credential-definition.manage permission (System Admin)." .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Seq_ConfigureEndorsementDefinition> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Sequence> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:belongsToContext> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:CredentialingContext> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:content> "sequenceDiagram\n    actor Admin\n    participant UI as Credentialing Admin UI\n    participant AppService as Application Service\n    participant IAM as Identity & Access API\n    participant RefData as Reference Data API\n    participant EventBus as Event Bus\n\n    Admin->>UI: Navigate to \"Manage Endorsement Definitions\"\n    UI->>IAM: Verify permission (credentialing.endorsement-definition.manage)\n    IAM-->>UI: Permission confirmed\n\n    UI->>AppService: GET /endorsement-definitions\n    AppService-->>UI: List of endorsement definitions\n\n    alt Creating New Endorsement\n        Admin->>UI: Click \"Create New Endorsement\"\n\n        Admin->>UI: Enter endorsement details\n        Note over Admin,UI: Enter: Endorsement Code, Display Name,<br/>Grade Band (Low-High), Active Date Range,<br/>OutOfState, InitialEndorsementEligible,<br/>ProgressToProfessional\n\n        Admin->>UI: Define assessment requirements\n        UI->>RefData: GET /assessment-definitions\n        RefData-->>UI: Available assessments\n\n        Admin->>UI: Select assessments and logic (AND/OR)\n        Note over Admin,UI: Example: MTTC-022 (Math) OR MTTC-023 (Integrated Math)\n\n        Admin->>UI: Submit new endorsement\n        UI->>AppService: POST /endorsement-definitions\n\n        AppService->>AppService: Create EndorsementDefinition aggregate\n        Note over AppService: State: Draft > Active\n\n        AppService--)EventBus: EndorsementDefinitionCreated\n        AppService-->>UI: Endorsement created\n        UI-->>Admin: Confirmation - endorsement now available\n\n    else Editing Existing Endorsement\n        Admin->>UI: Select endorsement definition to edit\n        UI->>AppService: GET /endorsement-definitions/{id}\n        AppService-->>UI: Current definition and version history\n\n        Admin->>UI: Modify fields (e.g., update assessment codes, change grade band)\n        Admin->>UI: Set \"Active From\" date for changes\n\n        Admin->>UI: Submit changes\n        UI->>AppService: PUT /endorsement-definitions/{id}\n\n        AppService->>AppService: Create new version of EndorsementDefinition\n        Note over AppService: Old version preserved for historical reference\n\n        AppService--)EventBus: EndorsementDefinitionUpdated\n        AppService-->>UI: Endorsement updated\n        UI-->>Admin: Confirmation with version info\n    end\n" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:SequencesDoc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:errorScenarios> "Endorsement code already exists > Validation error. Invalid grade band range (High < Low) > Display error. Assessment logic misconfigured (e.g., AND with zero codes) > Validation error." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:eventsPublished> "EndorsementDefinitionCreated - New endorsement type available. EndorsementDefinitionUpdated - Existing definition modified." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:initiatedBy> "user" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:keyDecisions> "Assessment Logic: AND requires all assessments to pass; OR requires any one to pass. Grade Band: Must be contiguous range; system validates Low <= High. Versioning: Changes create new versions while preserving historical definitions." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "confirmed" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Configure Endorsement Definition" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:whatWhenWho> "What: Administrator creates a new endorsement definition or updates an existing one with versioning. When: New subject areas added, assessment requirements change, or corrections needed. Who: User with credentialing.endorsement-definition.manage permission (System Admin)." .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Seq_DeletePendingApplication> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Sequence> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:belongsToContext> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:CredentialingContext> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:content> "sequenceDiagram\n    actor Educator\n    participant UI as Credentialing UI\n    participant AppService as Application Service\n\n    Educator->>UI: Navigate to \"View Pending Applications\"\n    UI->>AppService: GET /applications?educatorId={id}&status=submitted\n    AppService-->>UI: List of pending applications\n\n    Educator->>UI: Select application to delete\n    UI->>AppService: GET /applications/{id}/status\n    AppService-->>UI: Current status\n\n    alt Status is \"Submitted\" (not yet processed)\n        Educator->>UI: Confirm deletion\n        UI->>AppService: DELETE /applications/{id}\n        AppService->>AppService: Soft delete CredentialApplication\n        Note over AppService: State: Submitted > Cancelled\n\n        AppService-->>UI: Application deleted\n        UI-->>Educator: Deletion confirmed\n\n    else Status is beyond \"Submitted\" (processing started)\n        AppService-->>UI: Cannot delete - processing has begun\n        UI-->>Educator: Cannot delete - contact support\n    end\n" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:SequencesDoc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:errorScenarios> "Application already processing > Display error, suggest contacting support. Application not found > Display error." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:eventsPublished> "None (or optional ApplicationCancelled for audit)." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:initiatedBy> "user" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:keyDecisions> "Deletion Window: Only applications in Submitted status can be deleted by educator. Soft Delete: Application marked as cancelled, not physically deleted (audit trail)." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "confirmed" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Delete Pending Application" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:whatWhenWho> "What: Educator deletes their own application before processing begins. When: Educator submitted application but wants to withdraw before review. Who: Authenticated educator (self-only)." .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Seq_ImportAssessmentResults> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Sequence> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:belongsToContext> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:CredentialingContext> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:content> "sequenceDiagram\n    actor Admin\n    participant UI as Credentialing Admin UI\n    participant AppService as Application Service\n    participant IAM as Identity & Access API\n    participant DocService as Document Service\n    participant EventBus as Event Bus\n\n    Admin->>UI: Navigate to \"Import Assessment Results\"\n    UI->>IAM: Verify permission (credentialing.assessment-result.import)\n    IAM-->>UI: Permission confirmed\n\n    Admin->>UI: Select provider (Pearson-MTTC, ETS-Praxis, etc.)\n    Admin->>UI: Upload CSV/XLSX file\n    UI->>DocService: POST /upload (staging area)\n    DocService-->>UI: File uploaded, file ID\n\n    Admin->>UI: Click \"Process Import\"\n    UI->>AppService: POST /assessment-results/import\n\n    AppService->>DocService: GET /files/{fileId}\n    DocService-->>AppService: File content\n\n    AppService->>AppService: Parse file (provider-specific schema)\n\n    loop For each row in file\n        AppService->>AppService: Validate educator ID exists\n        AppService->>AppService: Validate assessment identifier exists\n        AppService->>AppService: Validate score within scoring scale\n\n        alt Validation passes\n            AppService->>AppService: Create or update AssessmentResult aggregate\n            Note over AppService: If educator has existing score for same assessment,<br/>keep highest score\n            AppService--)EventBus: AssessmentResultImported\n        else Validation fails\n            AppService->>AppService: Log error for row\n        end\n    end\n\n    AppService-->>UI: Import summary\n    UI-->>Admin: Display: {total rows, successful, failed, errors}\n" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:SequencesDoc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:errorScenarios> "Invalid educator ID > Skip row, log error. Unknown assessment identifier > Skip row, log error. Malformed file > Abort import, display parsing error." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:eventsPublished> "AssessmentResultImported - One per successful row." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:initiatedBy> "user" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:keyDecisions> "Provider-Specific Parsing: Different CSV schemas for Pearson vs ETS. Highest Score Logic: If educator retakes, system keeps highest score automatically. Verification Status: Imported results are marked Verified (from official provider)." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "confirmed" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Import Assessment Results" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:whatWhenWho> "What: Administrator uploads assessment result file from provider and system imports scores. When: Assessment provider sends updated score report; admin downloads and uploads to system. Who: User with credentialing.assessment-result.import permission." .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Seq_IssueTemporaryPermitExceptional> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Sequence> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:belongsToContext> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:CredentialingContext> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:content> "sequenceDiagram\n    actor Admin\n    participant UI as Credentialing Admin UI\n    participant AppService as Application Service\n    participant IAM as Identity & Access API\n    participant PPR as Professional Practices API\n    participant BRM as Business Rule Engine\n    participant EventBus as Event Bus\n\n    Admin->>UI: Navigate to \"Issue Permit (Exceptional)\"\n    UI->>IAM: Verify permission (credentialing.permit.issue)\n    IAM-->>UI: Permission confirmed\n\n    Admin->>UI: Search for educator by Unique ID\n    UI->>IAM: GET /users/search?uniqueId={id}\n    IAM-->>UI: Educator profile\n\n    Admin->>UI: Select permit type\n    UI->>AppService: GET /permit-types\n    AppService-->>UI: Permit types\n\n    Admin->>UI: Complete permit application on behalf of educator\n    Admin->>UI: Enter dates, endorsements, mentor, attestations\n\n    Admin->>UI: Submit permit issuance\n    UI->>AppService: POST /applications/permits/admin-issue/exceptional (NOT YET DEFINED in credentialing-api.yml - see status note above)\n\n    AppService->>PPR: GET /educators/{id}/ppr-clearance\n    PPR-->>AppService: PPR status (Clear/ConditionalClearance/Hold/Blocked)\n\n    alt PPR status = Blocked\n        AppService-->>UI: Cannot issue - PPR hold required\n        UI-->>Admin: Display PPR block message\n    else PPR status = Hold\n        AppService-->>UI: Cannot expedite - must wait for Professional Practices clearance\n        UI-->>Admin: Display PPR hold message; admin may create application via standard path instead\n    else PPR status = Clear or ConditionalClearance\n        AppService->>BRM: Validate permit requirements\n        BRM-->>AppService: Validation result\n\n        alt Requirements not met\n            AppService-->>UI: Validation errors\n            UI-->>Admin: Display specific violations\n        else Requirements met\n            AppService->>AppService: Create CredentialApplication (admin-submitted, exceptional)\n            Note over AppService: State: Submitted > Approved (bypasses payment/workflow - unconfirmed)\n\n            AppService->>AppService: Create IssuedCredential aggregate\n            Note over AppService: State: Pending > Valid\n\n            AppService--)EventBus: CredentialApplicationSubmitted\n            AppService--)EventBus: CredentialIssued\n\n            AppService-->>UI: Permit issued successfully\n            UI-->>Admin: Confirmation with permit ID\n        end\n    end\n" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:SequencesDoc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:errorScenarios> "PPR status = Blocked > Block issuance, require specialist review. Eligibility validation fails > Display errors, allow admin to correct." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:eventsPublished> "CredentialApplicationSubmitted - Audit trail. CredentialIssued - Notifies downstream systems of new credential." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:initiatedBy> "user" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:keyDecisions> "Status: unconfirmed capability — models an expedited, bypass-payment, auto-approved admin issuance path with no FDD evidence found; FDD 17's eight permit-family documents and FDD 11's bulk permit-renewal wireframes describe every permit type (including bulk admin-initiated renewals) going through the standard payment-link/PPR/manual-review pipeline regardless of who submits. Do not build this expedited behavior without confirming a genuine business need first — removing it doesn't lose any FDD-described capability, since that's fully covered by 'Submit Permit Application'. Admin Authority: permission scope determines which educators the admin can issue permits for. PPR Override: admins cannot override Blocked or Hold PPR status via this path even in the exceptional flow. Bypass behavior: if retained, should require a distinct, more restrictive permission or explicit justification capture, not just credentialing.permit.issue (which now also gates the standard, non-bypassing path)." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "unconfirmed" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Issue Temporary Permit — Exceptional Cases (Admin)" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:whatWhenWho> "What: Authorized administrator issues a temporary permit outside the standard application pipeline, bypassing payment and/or manual review. When: Unconfirmed — no FDD source document reviewed so far describes a scenario requiring this. Who: User with credentialing.permit.issue permission at appropriate scope." .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Seq_NullifyEndorsement> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Sequence> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:belongsToContext> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:CredentialingContext> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:content> "sequenceDiagram\n    actor Admin\n    participant UI as Credentialing Admin UI\n    participant AppService as Application Service\n    participant IAM as Identity & Access API\n    participant EventBus as Event Bus\n\n    Admin->>UI: Search for educator credential\n    UI->>AppService: GET /credentials/search?educatorId={id}\n    AppService-->>UI: Credentials with endorsements\n\n    Admin->>UI: Select credential and endorsement to nullify\n    UI->>AppService: GET /endorsements/{id}/details\n    AppService-->>UI: Endorsement details\n\n    Admin->>UI: Enter reason for nullification\n    UI->>IAM: Verify permission (credentialing.endorsement.nullify)\n    IAM-->>UI: Permission confirmed\n\n    UI->>AppService: POST /endorsements/{id}/nullify\n    AppService->>AppService: Update IssuedEndorsement aggregate\n    Note over AppService: State: Active > Nullified\n\n    AppService--)EventBus: EndorsementNullified\n\n    AppService-->>UI: Endorsement nullified\n    UI-->>Admin: Nullification confirmed\n\n    Note over EventBus: Events consumed by:<br/>- Staffing (update assignment eligibility)<br/>- Communications (notify educator)<br/>- Audit (record action)\n" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:SequencesDoc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:errorScenarios> "Admin lacks permission > Access denied. Endorsement already nullified > Display current state." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:eventsPublished> "EndorsementNullified - Endorsement removed from certificate." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:initiatedBy> "user" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:keyDecisions> "Nullification Reason: Required for audit trail and educator notification." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "confirmed" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Nullify Endorsement" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:whatWhenWho> "What: Administrator removes an endorsement from an educator's certificate. When: Administrative error correction or compliance action. Who: User with credentialing.endorsement.nullify permission (System Admin)." .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Seq_PrintCertificate> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Sequence> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:belongsToContext> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:CredentialingContext> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:content> "sequenceDiagram\n    actor User\n    participant UI as Credentialing UI\n    participant AppService as Application Service\n    participant PrintService as Document Generation Service\n\n    User->>UI: Navigate to \"Print Certificate\"\n    UI->>AppService: GET /credentials?educatorId={id}&status=approved\n    AppService-->>UI: List of approved credentials\n\n    User->>UI: Select credential(s) to print\n    UI->>AppService: POST /credentials/print\n    AppService->>PrintService: Generate certificate PDF\n\n    Note over PrintService: Generates official certificate with:<br/>- Credential details<br/>- Endorsements<br/>- Validity dates<br/>- Security features (if applicable)\n\n    PrintService-->>AppService: PDF generated\n    AppService-->>UI: PDF download link\n    UI-->>User: Download/print certificate\n" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:SequencesDoc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:errorScenarios> "No approved credentials > Display message. PDF generation fails > Retry, display error." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:eventsPublished> "None (audit log may record print action)." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:initiatedBy> "user" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:keyDecisions> "Security Features: Certificates may include watermarks, security codes, or other anti-fraud measures. Multiple Selection: User can print multiple certificates in batch." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "confirmed" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Print Certificate" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:whatWhenWho> "What: Educator or administrator prints an official credential certificate. When: Credential issued or renewed, educator needs physical copy. Who: Authenticated educator (self) or admin with credentialing.credential.print permission." .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Seq_RenewCredential> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Sequence> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:belongsToContext> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:CredentialingContext> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:content> "sequenceDiagram\n    actor Educator\n    participant UI as Credentialing UI\n    participant AppService as Application Service\n    participant PPR as Professional Practices API\n    participant ProfLearning as Professional Learning API\n    participant BRM as Business Rule Engine\n    participant EventBus as Event Bus\n\n    Educator->>UI: Navigate to \"Renew Certificate\"\n    UI->>AppService: GET /credentials/renewable?educatorId={id}\n    AppService-->>UI: List of renewable credentials\n\n    Educator->>UI: Select credential to renew\n    UI->>AppService: GET /renewal-requirements?credentialId={id}\n    AppService->>BRM: Get renewal criteria for credential type\n    BRM-->>AppService: Requirements (SCECH hours, IDP, etc.)\n    AppService-->>UI: Renewal requirements\n\n    Educator->>UI: Review requirements\n    UI->>ProfLearning: GET /scech-hours?educatorId={id}&credentialType={type}\n    ProfLearning-->>UI: SCECH hours completed\n\n    alt Requirements not met (e.g., insufficient SCECH hours)\n        UI-->>Educator: Display unmet requirements - cannot proceed\n    else Requirements met\n        Educator->>UI: Answer renewal questions\n        Educator->>UI: Upload required documents (e.g., IDP for permit renewals)\n        Educator->>UI: Submit renewal application\n\n        UI->>AppService: POST /applications/renewals\n        AppService->>PPR: GET /educators/{id}/ppr-clearance\n        PPR-->>AppService: PPR status (Clear/ConditionalClearance/Hold/Blocked)\n\n        alt PPR status = Blocked\n            AppService-->>UI: Error: Must complete conviction disclosure\n            UI-->>Educator: Cannot proceed - redirect to PPR\n        else PPR status = Hold\n            AppService->>AppService: Create CredentialApplication aggregate (renewal type)\n            Note over AppService: State: Draft > Professional Practice Hold\n            AppService--)EventBus: CredentialApplicationSubmitted\n            AppService-->>UI: Renewal submitted, pending PPR review\n            UI-->>Educator: Confirmation - held pending Professional Practices review\n        else PPR status = Clear or ConditionalClearance\n            AppService->>BRM: Validate renewal eligibility\n            BRM-->>AppService: Validation result\n\n            alt Validation fails\n                AppService-->>UI: Renewal criteria not met\n                UI-->>Educator: Display specific issues\n            else Validation passes\n                AppService->>AppService: Create CredentialApplication aggregate (renewal type)\n                Note over AppService: State: Draft > Submitted\n\n                AppService--)EventBus: CredentialApplicationSubmitted\n                AppService-->>UI: Renewal application submitted\n                UI-->>Educator: Confirmation - payment link will be emailed\n            end\n        end\n    end\n" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:SequencesDoc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:errorScenarios> "Credential not renewable (suspended/revoked) > Display error, suggest new application. PPR status = Blocked > Block renewal, redirect to complete disclosure. SCECH hours insufficient > Block submission, display shortfall. Renewal window expired > Display error, may require new application instead." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:eventsPublished> "CredentialApplicationSubmitted - Triggers payment processing and external routing" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:initiatedBy> "user" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:keyDecisions> "Renewal Eligibility: System checks if credential is renewable (not suspended/revoked, within renewal window). PPR Status: same gating as new-certificate/permit submission — Blocked prevents the renewal from being created at all; Hold creates the renewal but holds it pending Professional Practices review; Clear/ConditionalClearance proceed to BRM eligibility validation. SCECH Requirements: Professional Learning domain provides hours completed; renewal blocked if insufficient. Open item (2026-08-27): the GET /scech-hours call shown in this sequence has no matching endpoint in proflearning-api.yml — proflearning-domain.md's own Downstream dependency table instead expects Credentialing to maintain a running SCECH balance via event subscription rather than a live query. Document Requirements: some permit renewals require IDP or other proof of progress; conflicts with credentialing-domain.md's IDP rule, which describes a structured GET /educators/{uniqueId}/idp/status validation call that doesn't exist on a domain with no IDP aggregate at all." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "confirmed" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Renew Credential" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:whatWhenWho> "What: Educator renews an expiring certificate or permit. When: Credential is approaching expiration or has expired (within grace period). Who: Authenticated educator with renewable credential." .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Seq_SubmitNewCertificateApplication> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Sequence> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:belongsToContext> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:CredentialingContext> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:content> "sequenceDiagram\n    actor Educator\n    participant UI as Credentialing UI\n    participant AppService as Application Service\n    participant PPR as Professional Practices API\n    participant EPP as Educator Prep API\n    participant BRM as Business Rule Engine\n    participant DocService as Document Service\n    participant EventBus as Event Bus\n\n    Educator->>UI: Navigate to \"Apply for Certificate\"\n    UI->>AppService: GET /certificate-types\n    AppService-->>UI: Available certificate types\n\n    Educator->>UI: Select certificate type\n    UI->>AppService: GET /eligibility-questions?type={certType}\n    AppService->>BRM: Get questions for certificate type\n    BRM-->>AppService: Question set\n    AppService-->>UI: Questions\n\n    Educator->>UI: Answer eligibility questions\n    UI->>AppService: POST /validate-eligibility\n    AppService->>PPR: GET /educators/{id}/ppr-clearance\n    PPR-->>AppService: PPR status (Clear/ConditionalClearance/Hold/Blocked)\n\n    alt PPR status = Blocked\n        AppService-->>UI: Error: Must complete conviction disclosure\n        UI-->>Educator: Cannot proceed - redirect to PPR\n    else PPR status = Hold\n        AppService->>AppService: Create CredentialApplication aggregate\n        Note over AppService: State: Draft > Professional Practice Hold\n        AppService--)EventBus: CredentialApplicationSubmitted\n        AppService-->>UI: Application submitted, pending PPR review\n        UI-->>Educator: Confirmation - held pending Professional Practices review\n    else PPR status = Clear or ConditionalClearance\n        AppService->>EPP: GET /candidates/{id}/enrollment-status\n        EPP-->>AppService: Enrollment verification (hasActiveEnrollment, per-EPP program detail)\n        AppService->>BRM: Validate all eligibility criteria\n        BRM-->>AppService: Eligibility result\n\n        alt Not Eligible\n            AppService-->>UI: Eligibility requirements not met\n            UI-->>Educator: Display unmet requirements\n        else Eligible\n            AppService-->>UI: Eligibility confirmed\n\n            Educator->>UI: Upload required documents\n            UI->>DocService: POST /upload\n            DocService-->>UI: Document IDs\n\n            Educator->>UI: Submit application\n            UI->>AppService: POST /applications\n            AppService->>AppService: Create CredentialApplication aggregate\n            Note over AppService: State: Draft > Submitted\n\n            AppService--)EventBus: CredentialApplicationSubmitted\n            AppService-->>UI: Application ID\n            UI-->>Educator: Confirmation with application number\n        end\n    end\n" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:SequencesDoc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:errorScenarios> "PPR status = Blocked > Block application, redirect to complete disclosure. Eligibility not met > Display specific unmet requirements, do not create application. Document upload fails > Allow retry, do not proceed to submission." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:eventsPublished> "CredentialApplicationSubmitted - Triggers payment link generation, external workflow routing evaluation" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:initiatedBy> "user" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:keyDecisions> "PPR Status: If status = Blocked, application is blocked entirely; if Hold, application is created but held pending Professional Practices review; Clear and ConditionalClearance both proceed to normal eligibility processing (ConditionalClearance is instead evaluated during auto-approval). Eligibility: BRM evaluates all criteria (degree, GPA, program enrollment, etc.). Document Requirements: Varies by certificate type and in-state vs out-of-state status." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "confirmed" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Submit New Certificate Application" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:whatWhenWho> "What: Educator submits an application for a new teaching, administrative, or specialist certificate. When: Educator meets eligibility requirements and wants to obtain initial certification. Who: Authenticated educator or admin submitting on educator's behalf." .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Seq_SubmitPermitApplication> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Sequence> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:belongsToContext> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:CredentialingContext> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:content> "sequenceDiagram\n    actor Admin as District/ISD/Staffing Agency User\n    participant UI as Credentialing UI\n    participant AppService as Application Service\n    participant IAM as Identity & Access API\n    participant PPR as Professional Practices API\n    participant Staffing as Staffing API\n    participant BRM as Business Rule Engine\n    participant EventBus as Event Bus\n\n    Admin->>UI: Navigate to \"Apply for a permit\"\n    UI->>IAM: Verify permission (credentialing.permit.issue)\n    IAM-->>UI: Permission confirmed\n\n    Admin->>UI: Search for educator by Unique ID\n    UI->>AppService: GET /educators/{id}/search\n    AppService->>PPR: GET /educators/{id}/ppr-clearance\n    PPR-->>AppService: PPR status (Clear/ConditionalClearance/Hold/Blocked)\n\n    alt PPR status = Blocked\n        AppService-->>UI: Error: adverse action on file - direct district to contact MDE-Professional-Practice\n        UI-->>Admin: Cannot proceed\n    else PPR status = Clear, ConditionalClearance, or Hold\n        AppService-->>UI: Educator profile + existing temporary credentials for this org\n        UI->>AppService: GET /permit-types?educatorId={id}&orgId={orgId}\n        AppService-->>UI: Eligible permit types (filtered by existing permits held for this org, same academic year)\n\n        Admin->>UI: Select permit type (e.g., Full Year Basic Substitute)\n        UI->>AppService: GET /permit-questions?type={permitType}\n        AppService->>BRM: Get permit-specific questions\n        BRM-->>AppService: Question set\n        AppService-->>UI: Questions\n\n        Admin->>UI: Answer permit questions\n        Admin->>UI: Enter required dates, endorsements, mentor info\n\n        Note over Admin,UI: Mentor search: dynamic lookup or free-form entry\n\n        Admin->>UI: Submit application\n        UI->>AppService: POST /applications/permits/admin-issue\n\n        alt PPR status = Hold\n            AppService->>AppService: Create CredentialApplication aggregate (org-submitted)\n            Note over AppService: State: Draft > Professional Practice Hold\n            AppService--)EventBus: CredentialApplicationSubmitted\n            AppService-->>UI: Application submitted, pending PPR review\n            UI-->>Admin: Confirmation - held pending Professional Practices review\n        else PPR status = Clear or ConditionalClearance\n            AppService->>BRM: Validate permit eligibility (degree, GPA, etc.)\n            BRM-->>AppService: Validation result\n\n            alt Hard stop violation (e.g., insufficient degree)\n                AppService-->>UI: Error: Eligibility requirements not met\n            else Eligible\n                AppService->>Staffing: Verify employment assignment (if required) [endpoint unconfirmed - see credentialing-technical-design.md Open Technical Question #8]\n                Staffing-->>AppService: Assignment verified\n\n                AppService->>AppService: Create CredentialApplication aggregate (org-submitted)\n                Note over AppService: State: Draft > Submitted\n\n                AppService--)EventBus: CredentialApplicationSubmitted\n                AppService-->>UI: Application ID\n                UI-->>Admin: Confirmation - payment link will be emailed to the educator\n            end\n        end\n    end\n" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:SequencesDoc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:errorScenarios> "Hard stop eligibility failure > Display error, do not create application. PPR status = Blocked > Block application, redirect to complete disclosure. PPR status = Hold > Application created but held pending Professional Practices review." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:eventsPublished> "CredentialApplicationSubmitted - Triggers payment processing and external routing evaluation" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:initiatedBy> "user" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:keyDecisions> "Permit Type: Determines eligibility criteria and required documents; the eligible-permit list is filtered by what the submitting org already holds for this individual in the current academic year. PPR Status: Blocked prevents application creation entirely; Hold routes to Professional Practice Hold instead of immediate processing; Clear and ConditionalClearance both proceed to eligibility validation. Hard Stops: Certain violations (degree requirements, GPA) block submission immediately. No expedited/bypass path: submission through this sequence always follows the standard payment/PPR/manual-review pipeline. Not yet modeled: bulk submission for initial permit applications." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "confirmed" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Submit Permit Application" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:whatWhenWho> "What: A district/ISD/staffing-agency user submits an application for a temporary teaching permit on behalf of an educator. This is the standard, everyday intake path for all temporary permit types — educators never self-submit a permit application. When: A school needs to place an individual who doesn't hold the applicable certificate/endorsement into a teaching assignment. Who: User with credentialing.permit.issue permission at District/ISD scope (or the appropriate Staffing Agency scope, pending resolution of client-questions.md #1)." .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Seq_SuspendOrRevokeCredential> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Sequence> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:belongsToContext> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:CredentialingContext> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:content> "sequenceDiagram\n    actor Admin\n    participant UI as Credentialing Admin UI\n    participant AppService as Application Service\n    participant IAM as Identity & Access API\n    participant EventBus as Event Bus\n\n    Admin->>UI: Search for educator credential\n    UI->>AppService: GET /credentials/search?educatorId={id}\n    AppService-->>UI: List of educator's credentials\n\n    Admin->>UI: Select credential to suspend/revoke\n    UI->>AppService: GET /credentials/{id}/details\n    AppService-->>UI: Credential details\n\n    Admin->>UI: Select action (Suspend / Revoke)\n    Admin->>UI: Enter reason for action\n\n    alt Admin selects Suspend\n        UI->>IAM: Verify permission (credentialing.credential.suspend)\n        IAM-->>UI: Permission confirmed\n\n        UI->>AppService: POST /credentials/{id}/suspend\n        AppService->>AppService: Update IssuedCredential aggregate\n        Note over AppService: State: Valid > Suspended\n\n        AppService--)EventBus: CredentialSuspended\n\n        AppService-->>UI: Credential suspended\n        UI-->>Admin: Suspension confirmed - takes effect immediately\n\n    else Admin selects Revoke\n        UI->>IAM: Verify permission (credentialing.credential.revoke)\n        IAM-->>UI: Permission confirmed\n\n        UI->>AppService: POST /credentials/{id}/revoke\n        AppService->>AppService: Update IssuedCredential aggregate\n        Note over AppService: State: Valid > Revoked\n\n        AppService--)EventBus: CredentialRevoked\n\n        AppService-->>UI: Credential revoked\n        UI-->>Admin: Revocation confirmed - takes effect immediately\n    end\n\n    Note over EventBus: Events consumed by:<br/>- Staffing (block assignments)<br/>- IAM (revoke credential-based permissions)<br/>- Public Portal (update verification)<br/>- Communications (notify educator)\n" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:SequencesDoc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:errorScenarios> "Admin lacks permission > Access denied. Credential already suspended/revoked > Display current state, prevent duplicate action." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:eventsPublished> "CredentialSuspended - Credential temporarily invalidated. CredentialRevoked - Credential permanently invalidated." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:initiatedBy> "user" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:keyDecisions> "Suspend vs. Revoke: Suspension is temporary (can be reinstated), revocation is permanent. Immediate Effect: State change must propagate to all systems as quickly as possible." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "confirmed" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Suspend or Revoke Credential" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:whatWhenWho> "What: Administrator suspends or permanently revokes an educator's credential. When: Professional misconduct, legal issues, or compliance violations identified. Who: User with credentialing.credential.suspend or credentialing.credential.revoke permission (System Admin)." .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Seq_ValidateAssessmentResults> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Sequence> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:belongsToContext> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:CredentialingContext> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:content> "sequenceDiagram\n    participant AppService as Application Service\n    participant AssessmentService as Assessment Service\n    participant BRM as Business Rule Engine\n    participant EventBus as Event Bus\n\n    Note over AppService: Triggered during endorsement application processing\n\n    AppService->>AppService: Load CredentialApplication\n    AppService->>AppService: Get required assessments from EndorsementDefinition\n\n    Note over AppService: Required assessments may use AND/OR logic\n\n    AppService->>AssessmentService: GET /assessment-results?educatorId={id}\n    AssessmentService-->>AppService: All verified, non-expired results for educator\n\n    loop For each required assessment\n        AppService->>AppService: Find matching result by AssessmentIdentifier\n\n        alt Result found\n            AppService->>AppService: Check if score >= PassingCriteria\n            AppService->>AppService: Check if result not expired\n\n            alt Score passes and not expired\n                Note over AppService: Assessment requirement met\n            else Score insufficient or expired\n                Note over AppService: Assessment requirement NOT met\n            end\n        else Result not found\n            Note over AppService: Assessment requirement NOT met\n        end\n    end\n\n    AppService->>BRM: Evaluate combination logic (AND/OR)\n    BRM-->>AppService: Overall assessment validation result\n\n    alt All requirements met\n        AppService--)EventBus: AssessmentResultsValidated (passed=true)\n        Note over AppService: Proceed to auto-approval\n    else Requirements not met\n        AppService--)EventBus: AssessmentResultsValidated (passed=false)\n        Note over AppService: Flag for manual review\n    end\n" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:SequencesDoc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:errorScenarios> "No results on file > Validation fails, flag for manual review. Mixed results (some pass, some fail with AND logic) > Validation fails." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:eventsPublished> "AssessmentResultsValidated - Records validation outcome." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:initiatedBy> "internal-system" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:keyDecisions> "AND Logic: ALL specified assessments must pass. OR Logic: ANY ONE specified assessment must pass. Expiration Check: Expired results (ValidityPeriod exceeded) are treated as missing." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "confirmed" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Validate Assessment Results" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:whatWhenWho> "What: System validates educator's assessment scores against endorsement requirements. When: During endorsement application processing or auto-approval workflow. Who: System (automated)." .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Seq_ViewDefinitionHistory> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Sequence> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:belongsToContext> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:CredentialingContext> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:content> "sequenceDiagram\n    actor Admin\n    participant UI as Credentialing Admin UI\n    participant AppService as Application Service\n    participant IAM as Identity & Access API\n\n    Admin->>UI: Navigate to definitions (credential/endorsement/assessment)\n    UI->>IAM: Verify permission (appropriate .view permission)\n    IAM-->>UI: Permission confirmed\n\n    UI->>AppService: GET /{definition-type}\n    AppService-->>UI: List of definitions\n\n    Admin->>UI: Select definition to view history\n    UI->>AppService: GET /{definition-type}/{id}/history\n    AppService-->>UI: All versions with change details\n\n    Note over UI: Display table:<br/>- Version #<br/>- Effective From / To dates<br/>- Changed By<br/>- Changed At<br/>- What Changed (diff view)\n\n    Admin->>UI: Select specific version to view\n    UI->>AppService: GET /{definition-type}/{id}/versions/{versionId}\n    AppService-->>UI: Complete definition as it existed in that version\n\n    UI-->>Admin: Display historical definition snapshot\n\n    Note over Admin,UI: Admin can see:<br/>- Requirement rules at that time<br/>- Fee schedules / Passing criteria<br/>- Configuration flags<br/>- Associated applications using this version\n" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:SequencesDoc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:errorScenarios> "Definition not found > Display error. Version not found > Display error." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:eventsPublished> "None (or optional audit log entry for view access)." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:initiatedBy> "user" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:keyDecisions> "Read-Only: History view is read-only; cannot edit historical versions. Version Comparison: UI may offer diff view showing what changed between versions. Application Association: Can see which applications were evaluated against which version." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "This one sequence generically covers all three definition types (credential/endorsement/assessment) via a templated '/{definition-type}/...' path — not modeled as SequenceReferences to any one of the three specific *-definitions/{id}/history operations, since none of them is a literal path match on its own." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "confirmed" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "View Definition History" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:whatWhenWho> "What: Administrator reviews the complete version history and change audit trail for credential, endorsement, or assessment definitions. When: Investigating policy changes, compliance audits, or troubleshooting application issues. Who: User with credentialing.credential-definition.view, credentialing.endorsement-definition.view, or credentialing.assessment-definition.view permission." .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:SequencesDoc> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:SourceDocument> ;
