<urn:solutiondesign:instance:dashboards:Fdd03Doc> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:SourceDocument> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:docType> "fdd" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Covers Features 3.0(Addendum baseline)-3.7 (the document's own subtitle: 'Dashboards (3.1-3.7)'). Approved by Beth Dontje (MDE) and Caitlin Groom (CEPI), both 08/01/2025 per the Review & Sign Offs table, but comments.xml carries entries dated into 2026-03 (Caswell, DTMB-Contractor) — same 'kept revising after nominal signoff' pattern already noted in the FDD 29 review's header, not resolved here beyond flagging it. The folder's other two .docx files ('Dashboard.docx', 'Worklist, Dashboard.docx') are Professional Learning reference material, not part of this FDD — see this file's header comment." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:section> "functional-design-docs/03 - Dashboards/3 - Dashboard.docx" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:dashboards:Question_DashboardCmsNotModeled> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Features 12.3.1-12.3.5 describe a concrete admin CMS for the internal (authenticated-user) dashboard: hyperlink maintenance, text/heading/subheading content, broadcast system messages with an effective date range, alert-aging parameter configuration, and an audit trail over all of it. dash:DashboardsContext is a stub-only sd:BoundedContext (declared centrally in solution.ttl per CONVENTIONS.md's registry, sd:status \"stub\") with no Aggregate, ApiOperation, or Sequence of its own — consistent with how the FDD 11/16 and FDD 29 passes already found this same stub referenced only passively (rendering credential-landing-page content, persisting per-user widget-arrangement preferences) and never as something with its own admin-configuration surface. This FDD is the first pass to describe that admin surface directly and in a comparable amount of detail to a real Feature (5 numbered stories, 2 wireframes viewed including a real drag-and-drop widget-layout builder) — worth flagging for whoever eventually picks up an actual Dashboards/FDD-03 conversion, since this content-administration half is currently invisible to anyone who only reads the FDD 02/03-family Dependencies chain." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:dashboards:Req_12_3_1> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:dashboards:Req_12_3_2> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:dashboards:Req_12_3_3> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:dashboards:Req_12_3_4> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:dashboards:Req_12_3_5> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd12Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "coverage-gap" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:impact> "M" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "open" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:dashboards:Req_03_0_1> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:UserStory> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "The system identifies the user's assigned role (e.g., System Administrator, Staffing Administrator, or Credentialing Administrator). The system immediately directs the user to the Dashboard, which serves as the system home page. The system populates dynamic tiles and summaries specific to that role, including progress tracking for tasks and statuses of pending applications. The dashboard must present an initial summary of tasks relevant to the user's role, after submitting any required information." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:dashboards:Fdd03Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "No satisfiedBy: no dashboard-rendering, tile-population, or post-login-routing concept exists anywhere in the graph outside this stub file. Comment thread on the 'identifies the user's assigned role' clause (Groom, 351671444: 'Is this where we would need to define that users can have multiple roles and will need ability to set default views, and ability to see tiles across multiple roles?' -> Caswell, 1445230173: 'Yes, this is the place to incorporate that functionality. The handling of multiple roles is also defined under Epic 1 User Mgmt. It was discussed that users would toggle between roles and that the dashboard would update to reflect that user's context.') confirms multi-role toggle behavior belongs here, feeding into Req_03_0_6's own 'switch roles' criterion, and cross-references iam (Epic 1/FDD 01) for the role-holding side. iam:RoleDefinitionAggregate/iam:UserAuthorizationAggregate (already real, mied-v3/iam) model WHICH roles a user holds and WHAT they permit, but neither iam nor anything else models the act of selecting/toggling a current active role for dashboard-rendering purposes or the rendering itself — noted as adjacent infrastructure, not asserted as satisfiedBy since it doesn't actually carry this story out." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "3.0.1" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As an authorized MiEdWorkforce User, I need the dashboard to display immediately upon login so I have an initial summary of my essential tasks." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Dashboard displays immediately upon login with role-based summary" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:dashboards:Req_03_0_2> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:UserStory> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "The user enters the customization mode of the dashboard. A predefined list of available section layouts will display. The user is able to drag predefined section layouts onto the dashboard." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:dashboards:Fdd03Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "3.0.2" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As an authorized MiEdWorkforce User, I need to be able to customize my dashboard \"sections\" by adding, removing, and modifying \"sections\" within the dashboard layout, so that I can organize my workspace to highlight the most critical visualizations and task management tools for my daily workflow." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Customize dashboard by adding/removing/modifying sections" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:dashboards:Req_03_0_3> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:UserStory> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "The user enters the customization mode of the dashboard. The user selects the Kebab Menu (three dots) within the section that needs to be edited or removed. A menu will pop up with the options to either \"Edit Layout Section\" or \"Remove Section\"." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:dashboards:Fdd03Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Story's own stem text ('removing and modifying \"widgets\"') and its acceptance criteria (which describe editing/removing a SECTION, not a widget) don't match each other — likely a copy/paste of 3.0.5's stem onto 3.0.3's slot; not corrected here per this project's 'quote as-is, don't smooth over' convention, but worth flagging since it could confuse a reader expecting 3.0.3 to be about widgets specifically." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "3.0.3" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As an authorized MiEdWorkforce User, I need to be able to customize my dashboard \"sections\" by removing and modifying \"widgets\" within the \"sections\" layout, so that I can organize my workspace to highlight the most critical visualizations and task management tools for my daily workflow." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Remove or modify dashboard sections via a Kebab menu" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:dashboards:Req_03_0_4> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:UserStory> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "The user is able to add a widget by selecting \"Add Widget\" within a section. The system will offer predefined widgets for selection. The user must have the ability to add predefined widgets. Mandatory tiles, such as those displaying action items and upcoming deadlines, must be protected from removal." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:dashboards:Fdd03Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "'Mandatory tiles ... protected from removal' is a business rule embedded in this story's own AC, not promoted to a standalone sd:BusinessRule — no Aggregate exists yet for it to enforcedBy/appliesTo against, so promoting it now would be a rule pointing at nothing; left as prose here per 'prefer honest gaps over fabrication'." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "3.0.4" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a MiEdWorkforce User, I need to customize my dashboard by adding predefined widgets and visualizations, so that I can view the specific data summaries and task management tools relevant to my daily workflow." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Add predefined widgets to a dashboard section" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:dashboards:Req_03_0_5> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:UserStory> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "The user selects the Kebab Menu (three dots) within the widget that needs to be edited or removed. A menu will pop up with the options to either \"Edit Widget\" or \"Remove Widget\"." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:dashboards:Fdd03Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "3.0.5" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a MiEdWorkforce User, I need to customize my dashboard by removing, and modifying predefined widgets and visualizations, so that I can view the specific data summaries and task management tools relevant to my daily workflow." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Remove or modify predefined widgets via a Kebab menu" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:dashboards:Req_03_0_6> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:UserStory> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "The system must save the dashboard preferences and customizations defined by the user. The system must automatically populate the dashboard using saved preferences and customizations upon log in. If the user toggles between roles (if they possess multiple roles), the system must apply the saved preferences specific to the newly selected role." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:dashboards:Fdd03Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "This is the exact capability BOTH cred:Req_29_1_8 (FDD 29, 'Persistent certificate dashboard state') and cred:Req_11_7 (FDD 11/16) already pointed at when deferring their own dashboard-preference concerns as out-of-scope for Credentialing. Confirms, on the receiving end, that the deferral target is genuinely empty — not a documentation lag on Credentialing's side." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "3.0.6" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a MiEdWorkforce User, I need my dashboard preferences (layout and tile selection) to be saved and re-applied every time I log in or switch roles." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Persist and re-apply dashboard preferences per login and per role" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:dashboards:Req_03_0_7> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:UserStory> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "The dashboard tiles must provide the option to refresh automatically at a set interval. The system must automatically refresh dashboard tiles at a standardized, system-defined interval without requiring manual administrative configuration." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:dashboards:Fdd03Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "AC's second sentence is the RESULT of a live tracked-change edit, not the document's original text: the original read '...at a set interval. The system must allow administrators to define the set interval for automatic tile refreshing (e.g., 15 minutes).' — Groom's comment on that exact clause (1065075332: 'This should be a set standard without admin control to set interval.') led Caswell to delete it (w:del, 2026-03-05) and insert the current 'standardized, system-defined interval without requiring manual administrative configuration' text (w:ins, same timestamp; a second comment, 863305758, 'Revised. Please resolve this comment if nothing further is needed.', confirms the edit was the intended resolution) — even though neither comment thread was formally marked done in commentsExtended.xml. Quoted here as the POST-edit (current) text, which is also what the .md plain-text extraction garbles ('The system must' then truncates, having apparently rendered the deleted run and dropped the inserted one) — read from document.xml directly to get this right. Also note: this final text now mildly CONTRADICTS the FDD's own Business Specifications section, which still says 'an available tile to refresh automatically at a set interval (e.g. 15 minutes) OR refreshing upon navigation' (implying a user- or admin-configurable interval) — the prose section was never updated to match the Addendum story's own tracked-change revision. Not modeled as a discrepancy Annotation given how minor and clearly-resolved-in-intent it is; noted here instead." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "3.0.7" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a MiEdWorkforce User, I need to have my dashboard tiles automatically refresh upon navigating to the dashboard and when new data is available." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Automatic dashboard tile refresh" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:dashboards:Req_03_1> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Requirement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:dashboards:Fdd03Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "3.1" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "While the framework for widget selection is defined, the specific catalog of available predefined widgets is to be determined." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Dashboard - School District" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:dashboards:Req_03_2> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Requirement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:dashboards:Fdd03Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "3.2" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "While the framework for widget selection is defined, the specific catalog of available predefined widgets is to be determined." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Dashboard - Educational Staff" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:dashboards:Req_03_3> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Requirement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:dashboards:Fdd03Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "3.3" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "While the framework for widget selection is defined, the specific catalog of available predefined widgets is to be determined. Additional user stories, as they relate to dashboards relevant to this feature, can be found under feature 19.3 Data Quality Review & Processing – Dashboard." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Dashboard - ISD/Auditor" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:dashboards:Req_03_4> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Requirement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:dashboards:Fdd03Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "3.4" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "While the framework for widget selection is defined, the specific catalog of available predefined widgets is to be determined. Additional user stories, as they relate to dashboards relevant to this feature, can be found under feature 13.5 Educator Preparation Providers – Dashboard." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Dashboard - Educational Preparation Providers" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:dashboards:Req_03_5> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Requirement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:dashboards:Fdd03Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "3.5" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "While the framework for widget selection is defined, the specific catalog of available predefined widgets is to be determined. Additional user stories, as they relate to dashboards relevant to this feature, can be found under feature 14.5 Professional Learning – Dashboard." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Dashboard - Professional Learning Coordinator" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:dashboards:Req_03_6> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Requirement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:dashboards:Fdd03Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "See Question_CircularDashboardContentDeferral below — 11.7 does not actually contain this content; it points back here." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "3.6" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "While the framework for widget selection is defined, the specific catalog of available predefined widgets is to be determined. Additional user stories, as they relate to dashboards relevant to this feature, can be found under feature 11.7 Educator Credentialing – Dashboard." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Dashboard - Credential admin" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:dashboards:Req_03_7> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Requirement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:dashboards:Fdd03Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "3.7" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "While the framework for widget selection is defined, the specific catalog of available predefined widgets is to be determined. Additional user stories, as they relate to dashboards relevant to this feature, can be found under feature 10.6 Data Collection & Compliance - Staffing – Dashboard." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Dashboard - Staffing admin" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:dashboards:Req_03_BizSpec_AlertsInbox> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Requirement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "Message preview with Sender, Date Received, Un/Read indicator, and Subject; ability to select and view an entire message; ability to select message(s) to mark as Un/Read; ability to select message(s) to delete; display aging of unread messages based on a specified timeframe (defined by MiEdWorkforce System Administrator, Credentialing Administrator, or Staffing Administrator); Alerts examples given are task-assignment and expiration-window reminders (3/1/6 months out), Emails examples are application-confirmation and expiration-reminder emails, Notifications examples are non-critical FYI items." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:dashboards:Fdd03Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Real, substantive partial match — communications-capability.ttl's comm:AlertAggregate is explicitly dashboard-targeted (comm:AlertRoleTarget; its own invariants say 'Dashboard alerts persist until explicitly resolved or expired'), and comm:Seq_DashboardAlertCreationAndDisplay/comm:Seq_UserResolvesDashboardAlert plus comm:Op_ListAlerts/Op_CreateAlert/Op_ResolveAlert carry the creation/display/resolve lifecycle end to end. Partial, not full, satisfaction per the 'partial satisfaction is normal' rule: this Requirement's own richer inbox-UX detail — per-message Un/Read toggling, delete, sender/date-received/subject preview fields, and admin-configurable unread-aging display — has no corresponding entity/field/operation in comm:AlertAggregate or its API (which models Draft/Pending/Active/Resolved/Expired states and a single Resolve action, not a message-inbox CRUD/read-state surface). Also: this business-spec item bundles Alerts, Emails, and Notifications as one inbox, but comm:AlertAggregate is Alert-specific — comm:EmailInstanceAggregate is a separate, distinct aggregate for the Email side, and nothing named 'Notification' as a third, distinct concept from Alert exists at all — a minor terminology/structure gap worth a note, not a separate Annotation." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "3.BizSpec.Alerts" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:AlertAggregate> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:Op_ListAlerts> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:Seq_DashboardAlertCreationAndDisplay> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:Seq_UserResolvesDashboardAlert> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "(Business Specifications prose, never promoted to a numbered Addendum story.) The dashboard will display a summary of all alerts and notifications for a specified MiEdWorkforce user, by role, and contain a hyperlink to navigate the user to an Alerts, Emails, and Notifications Inbox." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Dashboard alerts/notifications summary and linked inbox" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:dashboards:Req_03_BizSpec_PersonnelSearchTile> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Requirement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:dashboards:Fdd03Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "No satisfiedBy: this FDD's own Dependencies section names 'User Management-Identity Management Person/ID Search 15.4' as the source of the underlying search itself, but iam-domain.ttl/iam-api.ttl (already real, mied-v3/iam) has no Person/ID-search-named Aggregate, ApiOperation, or Sequence at all (checked directly — no match for 'Personnel'/'Person Search'/'Identity Search' anywhere in iam/), and FDD 15 has not been reviewed in this session. Both halves of this Requirement are therefore currently unaccounted-for: the dashboard TILE (Dashboards' own gap) and the search mechanism it embeds (an iam gap, or an iam FDD-15-review gap — unconfirmed which)." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "3.BizSpec.PersonnelSearchTile" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "(Business Specifications prose, never promoted to a numbered Addendum story.) The dashboard will have an available tile to allow SOM and Business users to perform a Personnel Search as defined in User Management-Identity Management Person/ID Search 15.4. The Personnel Search will not be viewable to MiLogin Citizen users. Upon clicking search, the system will navigate the user to a detailed view to display the results, in a table, with sorting and filtering." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Personnel Search dashboard tile (SOM/Business users only)" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:dashboards:Req_03_BizSpec_PresetAdminDesign> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Requirement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:dashboards:Fdd03Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "No satisfiedBy: distinct admin-side authoring capability (design a preset dashboard template per role/function) from the end-user customization already covered by Req_03_0_2 through Req_03_0_5 — no preset/template concept, admin-facing or otherwise, exists in the graph." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "3.BizSpec.PresetAdmin" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "(Business Specifications prose, never promoted to a numbered Addendum story.) The MiEdWorkforce System Administrator will have the ability to define/design preset dashboards for specific functions or roles, in which the user can customize from the presets for their role. The predefined and designed dashboards will include the major functions of the assigned user role and permissions." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "System Administrator authors preset role/function dashboards" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:dashboards:Req_03_BizSpec_ReportsSummary> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Requirement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:dashboards:Fdd03Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "No satisfiedBy: reporting-capability.ttl (rpt:, already real, reviewed as FDD 02) models rpt:ReportDefinitionAggregate and an embed-token/Power-BI-link delivery mechanism, but nothing resembling a scheduled/due-date concept, or a report-preview-data summary distinct from opening the full report itself. This is a genuinely new capability neither Dashboards nor Reporting currently models, not merely an integration gap between two existing pieces." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "3.BizSpec.ReportsSummary" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "(Business Specifications prose, never promoted to a numbered Addendum story.) The dashboard will display a summary of upcoming reports and approximate due dates, along with preview data, for a specified MiEdWorkforce user, by role. Examples: MiSchoolData, school index score, aggregate counts of staff." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Dashboard summary of upcoming reports with preview data" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:dashboards:Req_12_3_1> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:UserStory> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "When the System Administrator has the appropriate role permissions and accesses the dashboard maintenance area, the system allows selection of hyperlink content for update. The system allows the System Administrator to enter or modify a hyperlink URL. The system validates the hyperlink format before allowing the change to be saved. If the hyperlink URL is malformed, the system displays a validation error and prevents saving. Upon saving a valid hyperlink, the system updates the hyperlink for all relevant internal users. The system records audit details for the hyperlink update." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd12Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "No satisfiedBy asserted — see Question_DashboardCmsNotModeled below." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "12.3.1" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a MiEdWorkforce System Administrator, I want to update hyperlinks displayed on the internal dashboard, so that internal users are routed correctly to relevant internal system pages and resources." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Update internal-dashboard hyperlinks" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:dashboards:Req_12_3_2> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:UserStory> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "When the System Administrator accesses the dashboard maintenance area with appropriate permissions, the system allows selection of text, heading, or subheading content for update. The system allows the System Administrator to enter or edit dashboard text content. The system enforces system-defined character limits on text and verbiage fields. If the entered text exceeds the allowed character limit, the system displays a validation error and prevents saving. Upon saving valid content, the system updates the dashboard display for all relevant internal users. The system stores audit details capturing Modified By, Modified On, and the content changes." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd12Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "No satisfiedBy asserted — see Question_DashboardCmsNotModeled below. Embedded wireframe (image7.png, viewed but not extracted) shows a real drag-and-drop dashboard-section/widget-layout builder ('Add Section' with 1/2/3-column layouts, 'Add Widget' placeholders) — further evidence this is a concretely designed feature, not narrative text." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "12.3.2" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a MiEdWorkforce System Administrator, I want to define and manage text, headings, and subheadings displayed on the internal dashboard, so that administrative announcements and informational content are communicated effectively to internal users." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Manage internal-dashboard text, headings, and subheadings" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:dashboards:Req_12_3_3> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:UserStory> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "When the System Administrator navigates to the dashboard messaging maintenance area, the system allows selection of system message or notification content for update. The system allows the System Administrator to define or modify the message text displayed on the dashboard. The system allows the System Administrator to define optional effective start and end dates for the message. If an effective start date/time is not provided, the system shall default to the current system date and time, making the message active immediately upon saving. If an effective end date/time is not provided, the system shall leave the message active indefinitely until it is manually deactivated or removed by an administrator. The system applies the message configuration only within the defined effective date range, when provided. Upon saving, the system updates the dashboard messaging for all relevant internal users. The system records audit details for the message configuration change, specifically capturing the 'Modified By' user and 'Modified On' date/timestamp." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd12Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "No satisfiedBy asserted — see Question_DashboardCmsNotModeled below. Note for the record (not itself a gap): the default-date AC lines here (start defaults to now, end defaults to indefinite) were added mid-review per comment thread id 39/340970065 (Dontje asks 'what happens if optional dates aren't selected?'; Doherty/Yashi confirms the defaults and states the AC was updated accordingly) — a resolved clarification captured directly in the visible text above, not an open question. This story's own 'system messages/notifications' concept is distinct from, but adjacent to, comm:AlertAggregate's dashboard-alert model (Feature 12.1.5/12.1.6's satisfiedBy) — a targeted, per-user, action-oriented alert vs. this story's untargeted, broadcast-to-all-internal-users banner message with an effective date range; not the same aggregate, and comm:AlertAggregate has no all-users broadcast mode or date-range-based (vs. expiration-based) activity window, so it would not by itself satisfy this story even if credited." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "12.3.3" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a MiEdWorkforce System Administrator, I want to update system messages and notifications displayed on the internal dashboard, so that internal users receive timely and relevant system information upon login." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Update internal-dashboard system messages and notifications" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:dashboards:Req_12_3_4> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:UserStory> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "When the System Administrator has appropriate permissions and accesses the alert parameter configuration area, the system allows selection of system-defined alert parameters. The system allows the System Administrator to enter or select a value for the alert aging timeframe. If the entered value is non-numeric or outside allowed limits, the system displays a validation error and prevents saving. Upon saving a valid value, the system applies the updated parameter to govern how alerts and messages are displayed on dashboards. The system records audit details for the parameter change." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd12Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "No satisfiedBy asserted. This one is closer to comm:AlertAggregate territory than 12.3.1-12.3.3 (comm:Seq_DashboardAlertCreationAndDisplay's own key decision already states a configured default expiration period of 30 days) — but that expiration value is documented as a fixed sequence-level default, not an admin-configurable system parameter exposed via any ApiOperation, so still no real satisfiedBy target. Grouped with 12.3.1-12.3.3/12.3.5 under Question_DashboardCmsNotModeled below rather than called out as a narrower, closer-to-satisfied gap, since no operation exists either way." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "12.3.4" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a MiEdWorkforce System Administrator, I want to configure the aging parameters for unread alerts and messages on the internal dashboard, so that users are presented with relevant and recent notifications." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Configure aging parameters for unread dashboard alerts" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:dashboards:Req_12_3_5> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:UserStory> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "The system records audit details for each dashboard configuration change, including hyperlinks, text, headings, messages, and alert parameters. The system associates each change with the System Administrator role; the Modified By and Modified On will be stored. The system retains audit records for historical review and compliance purposes. Audit records are read-only and cannot be modified by administrators." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Fdd12Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "No satisfiedBy asserted: an audit trail over dashboard-configuration changes presupposes the configuration entities themselves, which don't exist — see Question_DashboardCmsNotModeled below." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "12.3.5" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a MiEdWorkforce System Administrator, I want the system to store audit history for all dashboard structure and messaging configuration changes, so that traceability and compliance requirements are met." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Retain audit history for dashboard configuration changes" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:dataquality:DataQualityContext> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:BoundedContext> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:displayName> "Data Quality" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:displayName> "Data Qualitye" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:identifier> "dataquality" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:kind> "PlatformCapability" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Stub-only bounded context per CONVENTIONS.md's registry (no source documents of its own anywhere in this repo). Referenced directly by communications-capability.md's Dependencies table (DataQualityIssueDetected events) and the Mass Email with Consolidation sequence, so a minimal placeholder is minted here rather than left dangling." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "stub" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:dataquality:DataQualityIssueDetectedEvent> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:DomainEvent> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Stub — dataquality is a stub-only registry context (no source docs anywhere); see dq:DataQualityContext's own notes." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:payloadHighlights> "issue_id (per communications-sequences.md's Mass Email with Consolidation sequence, which queries GET /api/data-quality/issues?ids=... for issue detail)" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:trigger> "Data quality check identifies an issue" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:dataquality:Fdd19Doc> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:SourceDocument> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:docType> "fdd" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Author Caitlin Groom (CEPI); approved by Beth Dontje (MDE) and Caitlin Groom (CEPI) both 08/04/2025 per the signoff table. Review comments in comments.xml carry dates from 2025-12-19 through 2026-03-16, well after the nominal approval date — same pattern the FDD 29 pass already found (approval date is not 'nothing changed after this')." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:section> "functional-design-docs/19 - Data Quality Review & Processing/19 - Data Quality Review & Processing.docx" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:dataquality:Fdd20Doc> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:SourceDocument> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:docType> "fdd" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Author Caitlin Groom (CEPI); approved by Beth Dontje (MDE) and Caitlin Groom (CEPI), both 08/04/2025. Confirmed via unzip: no comments.xml, no word/media — a genuinely clean, comment-free, wireframe-free document, unlike almost every other FDD reviewed in this project so far." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:section> "functional-design-docs/20 - Data Quality Review & Processing - Comments & Flags/20.0 - Data Quality Review & Processing - Comments and Flags.docx" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:dataquality:GetIssuesOperation> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:ApiOperation> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:accessType> "internal-service" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:exposedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:dataquality:DataQualityContext> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:method> "GET" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Stub, path taken literally from communications-sequences.md's Mass Email with Consolidation sequence (GET /api/data-quality/issues?ids=101,102,103). dataquality has no source docs of its own anywhere in this repo — see dq:DataQualityContext's own notes." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:path> "/api/data-quality/issues" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:scopeSensitive> false ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:summary> "Returns issue detail for a set of data-quality issue IDs, for variable resolution in a consolidated notification." .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:dataquality:Req_19_1_1> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:UserStory> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "The user must possess District level access to view the Data Quality Dashboard widget. The main dashboard displays a clearly labeled Data Quality Dashboard widget. The Data Quality Dashboard displays dynamic reports reflecting the district's submitted data, including the results of Data Quality checks." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:dataquality:Fdd19Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "No satisfiedBy: dq:DataQualityContext and dash:DashboardsContext are both stub-only (sd:status \"stub\"), and Wireframe19_2 (confirmed by viewing) shows only a generic, content-free empty-widget dashboard shell — no DQ-specific widget design exists. A tracked-change-inserted AC bullet on this exact story ('The system immediately directs the user to the main Dashboard, which serves as the system home page') was flagged in review by comment 27 (Groom: 'This requirement does not belong with this story, the login and dashboard availability should be defined within 1.0 User Management and 3.0 Dashboard') — a narrower, already-resolved out-of-scope finding on one AC clause, not the whole story, so not modeled as its own Annotation target; the surviving AC text above already excludes that flagged clause." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "19.1.1" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a MiEdWorkforce user with District level access, I want a link on my main dashboard to navigate to the Data Quality Dashboard." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "District-level dashboard link to Data Quality Dashboard" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:dataquality:Req_19_1_2> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:UserStory> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "The Data Quality Dashboard widget includes an accessible option for the authorized user to initiate Data Quality checks. The system executes the Data Quality checks against the current system data immediately upon the user's request (on-demand/ad-hoc functionality)." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:dataquality:Fdd19Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "No satisfiedBy: no generic, cross-domain on-demand check-execution capability exists. The closest real analog anywhere in mied-v3 is staff:Seq_CertifyCollection's user-triggered 'Run Quality Review' step, but that is scoped entirely to Staffing's own collection-certification workflow (triggered by a District user preparing to certify one collection), not a general-purpose 'run any DQ check on demand' capability spanning every domain the way this story describes — see the consolidated coverage-gap Annotation below." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "19.1.2" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As an authorized user, I want the ability to run Data Quality checks against the current system data on-demand (ad-hoc) via the Data Quality Dashboard." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "On-demand/ad-hoc Data Quality check execution from the dashboard" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:dataquality:Req_19_1_3> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:UserStory> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "The Data Quality Dashboard widget provides a function to extract the results of the Data Quality checks. The extracted results are produced in a common, consumable file format, such as Excel. The extraction includes all Data Quality check information and associated metadata." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:dataquality:Fdd19Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "No satisfiedBy: dq:GetIssuesOperation exists only as a stub minted from communications-sequences.ttl's own cross-domain call detail (GET /api/data-quality/issues?ids=...) — a placeholder acknowledging the endpoint's existence for Communications' variable-resolution purposes, not a real, built extraction capability, so not used as a satisfiedBy target (would overclaim coverage that isn't real)." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "19.1.3" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As an authorized user, I want the option to extract Data Quality results to a consumable file format (i.e., Excel)." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Extract Data Quality results to a consumable file format" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:dataquality:Req_19_1_4> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:UserStory> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "The Data Quality Dashboard widget presents an option to view individual level records that are flagged for issues as interactive elements (e.g., hyperlinks). Selecting an individual record from the report view navigates the user directly to the individual level record within the data submission component. The user can perform necessary corrections or reviews on the accessed individual record." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:dataquality:Fdd19Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "No satisfiedBy: depends on both an unbuilt DQ report view AND, per its own Dependencies section ('Data used by...Data Quality Review & Processing is dependent upon Collection & Compliance (22)'), on FDD 22 (Data Collection & Compliance - Assignment Details), itself one of several unconverted 'Data Collection & Compliance' FDD folders per mied-v3/CONVENTIONS.md — a two-layer gap, neither layer built." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "19.1.4" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As an authorized user, I want to be able to access the individual level record for data submission correction directly from the Data Quality report view." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Navigate from a Data Quality report to the underlying individual-level record" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:dataquality:Req_19_1_5> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:UserStory> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "When the authorized user views a Data Quality violation, the system displays descriptive text defined by the Data Quality Administrator. The displayed descriptive text includes components such as Problem, Impact, and Resolution statements." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:dataquality:Fdd19Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "No satisfiedBy: Wireframe19_1 (the real legacy CEPI MSDS screenshot, confirmed by viewing) shows this exact DESCRIPTION/IMPACT/ACTION three-part text pattern already working in production for the state's current tooling — corroborating that this is a real, well-understood requirement, not speculative — but nothing in mied-v3's own graph models a DQ-check-authored text field of any kind." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "19.1.5" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As an authorized user, I want to be provided with the associated text defined by the Data Quality Administrator (i.e., Problem, Impact, Resolution) when viewing a violation." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Display administrator-defined Problem/Impact/Resolution text for a violation" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:dataquality:Req_19_1_6> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:UserStory> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "The system allows the user to formally acknowledge a specific Data Quality check violation. The system provides a text field for the user to enter comments/explanations to justify the offending data. The system enforces justification requirements (Required vs. Optional) based on the settings defined by the DQ Administrator. Submitted justifications are stored and associated with the violation record." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:dataquality:Fdd19Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "No satisfiedBy at the generic level this story describes (any DQ check, any domain), but staff:Seq_CertifyCollection already implements the identical acknowledge-plus-justification pattern ('Justification-required conditions exist -> Display justification-required items -> Enter justification text...POST /collections/{id}/justifications...Store justifications linked to collection') scoped entirely to Staffing's own collection certification — the single closest real analog anywhere in mied-v3, not asserted as satisfiedBy since it doesn't implement THIS story's cross-domain scope. See the consolidated coverage-gap Annotation below." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "19.1.6" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As an authorized user, I want to acknowledge Data Quality checks and provide required justifications or comments, so that I can explain data anomalies without changing the data." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Acknowledge a Data Quality check violation with justification, without changing data" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:dataquality:Req_19_1_7> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:UserStory> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "The system clears the Action Item automatically if the user corrects the data and the check passes upon re-run. The system clears the Action Item if the user submits a justification (for checks where justification is allowed). Simply viewing the dashboard does not clear the Action Item if the violation persists without justification." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:dataquality:Fdd19Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "No satisfiedBy: no 'Action Item' entity/aggregate of any kind is modeled anywhere in mied-v3 (confirmed by grep across abox/mied-v3/*/*.ttl — zero hits for 'ActionItem'). staff:Seq_CertifyCollection's 'loop until all errors resolved' plus its justification-store step are the same underlying shape (re-run-clears, justification-clears) but, again, scoped to Staffing collection certification only, and that sequence has no explicit 'passive viewing does not clear' negative-case language the way this story does." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "19.1.7" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As an authorized user, I want the system to clear the associated Action Item when I resolve the issue, so that my worklist accurately reflects remaining tasks." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Auto-clear the Action Item when the violation is resolved" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:dataquality:Req_19_1_8> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:UserStory> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "The authorized user can access a view displaying historical Data Quality checks. The historical view includes the details of the status of past checks. The view provides access to audit details (historical notes) related to the checks." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:dataquality:Fdd19Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "No satisfiedBy: no versioning/audit-history concept exists for a DQ check (there is no DQ check node at all to version). comm:EmailTemplateAggregate/comm:AlertAggregate both show what a versioned, stateful, audited configuration entity looks like elsewhere in this graph (TemplateVersion, AlertVersion, explicit StateDefinition lifecycles) — cited here only as a structural pattern this capability could follow if built, not as coverage." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "19.1.8" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As an authorized user, I want to view historical Data Quality checks and include the details of status and changes." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "View historical Data Quality checks with status and change details" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:dataquality:Req_19_1_9> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:UserStory> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "All comments and explanations provided by users are permanently stored and retrievable by the Data Quality Administrator. The stored comments are accessible during the review of historical data quality checks. The Data Quality Administrator has the ability to publish these stored comments as needed." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:dataquality:Fdd19Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "PARTIAL match, genuinely close: comm:CommentAggregate is a real (non-stub), already-converted, generic comment framework whose own invariants already say almost exactly this ('Deleted comments remain in the audit trail but are hidden from the UI'; comm:CommentEmailHistory tracks which sent emails included a given comment, which is the closest real analog to 'publish as needed'). The one concrete gap: comm:CommentAggregate's invariant explicitly enumerates the process-item types it applies to as 'CredentialApplication, StaffingRecord, EPPEnrollment' — a Data Quality violation/check is not among them, so extending Comments to cover DQ violations specifically is a small, well-understood addition to an existing real aggregate rather than a from-scratch build. This is genuinely different in kind from every other Feature 19.1/19.2/19.3 story above, which have no real analog at all." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "19.1.9" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:CommentAggregate> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a Data Quality Administrator, I want the user-provided comments/explanations to be stored and accessible for historical data reviews." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Store user comments/explanations for historical review and publication" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:dataquality:Req_19_2_1> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:UserStory> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "The system provides an administrative page for the DQ Administrator role to define and manage data quality processing. The DQ Administrator is granted both View and View/Edit access for this administrative page. The page displays all configured data quality checks in a sortable table. The sortable table includes the Data Quality ID, DQ Category, Title, Description, and Status for each check." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:dataquality:Fdd19Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "No satisfiedBy: no admin-configuration surface for defining a DQ check exists anywhere. Wireframe19_3 (confirmed by viewing) — the image actually embedded at this exact story — depicts an unrelated Credentialing > Business Rules admin table, not a Data Quality screen; see Question_DqAdminOverlapsBusinessRuleManagement below, which treats this as significant evidence rather than noise." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "19.2.1" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a DQ Administrator, I want an administrative page to define and manage data quality processing." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "DQ Administrator administrative page to define and manage data quality processing" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:dataquality:Req_19_2_2> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:UserStory> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "The system automatically versions data quality checks when changes are applied. The system stores all audit data for changes made by the Data Quality Administrator. The DQ check details page allows viewing of historical notes and audit details. Notes are required to be entered and stored when submitting changes to a DQ check." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:dataquality:Fdd19Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "No satisfiedBy — same whole-capability gap as 19.1.8/19.2.1; there is no DQ check node to version. See Question_DqAdminOverlapsBusinessRuleManagement below." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "19.2.2" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a DQ Administrator, I want the system to version data quality checks and store all audit data for changes applied." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Version data quality checks and store audit data for changes" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:dataquality:Req_19_2_3> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:UserStory> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "The DQ Administrator can set the intervals or schedules for running Data Quality checks against system data. The system runs the Data Quality checks against the current system data based on the set interval/schedule. The DQ Administrator sets the associated Action Item and specifies the users or user roles who will receive the task. The DQ Administrator can configure options for pausing a check, defining justification requirements, and setting a pause/sleep duration." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:dataquality:Fdd19Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "No satisfiedBy: this is precisely the shape sd:BatchJob exists for in the ontology (a scheduled/triggered automated process, sd:schedule property) — but no dq:BatchJob or equivalent scheduled check-runner is modeled anywhere; cited here only to note that the ontology already has the right vocabulary position waiting for this, unlike the admin-console pieces above which have no obvious modeling slot yet either." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "19.2.3" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a DQ Administrator, I want to set intervals/schedules for running Data Quality checks against system data." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Set intervals/schedules for running Data Quality checks" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:dataquality:Req_19_2_4> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:UserStory> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "The DQ Administrator can perform analysis on data submitted within MiEdWorkforce to identify violations of the Data Quality validation condition. Data Quality checks performed can reference current MiEdWorkforce system data, historical data, and data from other data systems. The analysis results are displayed within the Data Quality Dashboard in the MiEdWorkforce system. The DQ Administrator dashboard includes summary information about the results, including frequency counts of DQ checks and details of communications and action items sent to users. The DQ Administrator can initiate analysis both at set intervals and on-demand (ad-hoc)." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:dataquality:Fdd19Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "The ONE genuinely real, well-sourced partial match in this whole file: staff:Seq_CertifyCollection's 'Run Quality Review' step literally executes 'validation rules (record-level, cross-record, historical, EEM alignment)' — current data, historical data, AND an external data system (EEM), matching this story's own three-way reference list almost exactly — and staff:Perm_CollectionValidate's own description is 'Run data quality checks before certification.' A review comment on this exact FDD (comment 30: 'This DQ Admin functionality is needed within the system, this was originally defined within 10.3- Staffing Admin- Data Quality Monitoring & Review. I am ok to leave it here, but we also need the BR Validation functionality...') independently confirms this domain-specific origin, in the reviewer's own words, not an inference made here. What is NOT covered: the admin-configurable, cross-domain, dashboard-displayed generality this story also asks for (frequency counts, communications/action-item summaries, on-demand-vs-scheduled toggle) — Staffing's version is a fixed, hardcoded rule set run at one fixed point in one domain's workflow, not an administrator-authored, reusable check definition." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "19.2.4" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:staffing:Perm_CollectionValidate> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:staffing:Seq_CertifyCollection> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a DQ Administrator, I want the ability to perform analysis on data referencing current MiEdWorkforce system data, historical data, and data from other data systems." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Analyze current, historical, and cross-system data for Data Quality violations" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:dataquality:Req_19_2_5> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:UserStory> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "The Admin can define basic details: Category, Title, Description, Status, Effective Dates, and Associated Data Elements. The Admin can define Data Quality Specifications (logic/thresholds). The Admin can set Justification Expectations (Required vs. Optional) for the check. The Admin can define the Level of Aggregation for the check (Statewide, ISD, District, Building, or Individual). The Admin can define the Text displayed to users (Problem, Impact, Resolution)." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:dataquality:Fdd19Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "No satisfiedBy — same admin-configuration-surface gap as 19.2.1/19.2.2. Wireframe19_1's real legacy-system example independently corroborates that a per-entity Level-of-Aggregation breakdown (its table is per-entity/per-FPL-band) and a Problem/Impact/Action text triad are both real, already-practiced requirements in the state's current tooling, not speculative asks — reinforcing that this gap is worth taking seriously for GAPS.md, not a nice-to-have." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "19.2.5" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a DQ Administrator, I want to configure detailed attributes for each Data Quality check, so that the system accurately identifies and routes specific data issues." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Configure detailed attributes for each Data Quality check" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:dataquality:Req_19_2_6> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:UserStory> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "The system provides a function to easily extract all Data Quality Check information and associated metadata. The extracted information is available in consumable file formats, such as Excel and SQL." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:dataquality:Fdd19Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "No satisfiedBy — same admin-configuration-surface gap; duplicate of 19.1.3's extraction ask but for check DEFINITIONS/metadata rather than check RESULTS." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "19.2.6" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a DQ Administrator, I want to be able to extract all Data Quality Check information and metadata easily (i.e., Excel, SQL)." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Extract all Data Quality check information and metadata" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:dataquality:Req_19_3_1> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:UserStory> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "The Data Quality Administrator dashboard successfully loads upon request. The dashboard displays summary information derived from the results of the Data Quality checks." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:dataquality:Fdd19Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "No satisfiedBy: Wireframe19_2 (the image embedded here, byte-identical to the one at 19.1.1 per the reviewer's own comment 33) is a generic content-free widget shell, not a DQ-specific dashboard design; dash:DashboardsContext remains stub-only." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "19.3.1" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a DQ Administrator, I want the Data Quality Administrator dashboard to display summary information about the results of the Data Quality checks." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Data Quality Administrator dashboard displays summary information" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:dataquality:Req_19_3_2> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:UserStory> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "The summary information displayed includes details of communications sent regarding Data Quality issues. The summary information displays details regarding assigned action items and identifies which users were contacted. The dashboard provides frequency counts of the Data Quality checks performed." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:dataquality:Fdd19Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "No satisfiedBy, though the raw ingredients for the 'communications sent' half are real elsewhere (comm:EmailInstanceAggregate's full historical send record, comm:AlertAggregate's resolution tracking) — nothing assembles them into a Data-Quality-specific summary dashboard the way this story asks; not asserted as satisfiedBy since neither aggregate is DQ-aware (see 19.1.9's own note on the same enumerated-process-item-types limitation)." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "19.3.2" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a DQ Administrator, I want the summary information to include details of communications, assigned action items, and frequency counts of DQ checks." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Dashboard summary includes communications, action items, and frequency counts" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:dataquality:Req_19_3_3> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:UserStory> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "When data submitted by an authorized organization violates Data Quality check specifications, the system automatically assigns an Action Item to the authorized user. The assigned Action Item populates and is viewable on the user's landing page or dashboard. The system notifies the authorized user of the assigned Action Item via email, using the template defined by the Data Quality Administrator." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:dataquality:Fdd19Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Real, well-sourced PARTIAL match: communications-capability.ttl already declares a live sd:Dependency (fromContext comm:CommunicationsContext, toContext dq:DataQualityContext, mechanism event-subscription, viaEvent dq:DataQualityIssueDetectedEvent) whose own sd:notes cites 'communications-capability.md BRD 19.4' by number — i.e. Communications' own conversion already read and is designed against this exact FDD feature. comm:AlertAggregate (dashboard alerts with role-based targeting and resolution tracking) is the real, generic landing-page/dashboard notification mechanism. What's NOT covered: comm:AlertAggregate targets individual users/roles, not 'the submitting organization' as this story specifically asks, and — as with every other Feature 19.x story — the upstream half (a real dq:BusinessRule that actually evaluates a check and fires dq:DataQualityIssueDetectedEvent) doesn't exist; the event is currently only a typed placeholder Communications subscribes to." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "19.3.3" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:AlertAggregate> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:DashboardAlertCreatedEvent> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As an authorized user, I want Action Items to populate on my landing page/dashboard when a data quality violation occurs." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Action Items populate on the landing page/dashboard when a violation occurs" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:dataquality:Req_19_4_1> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:UserStory> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "The system runs Data Quality checks against system data at the interval set by the DQ Administrator. When submitted data is in violation of the Data Quality check specifications, the system automatically assigns an \"Action Item\" for the submitting organization. Action Items are assigned upon the return of the Data Quality results. The assigned Action Item is automatically populated on the authorized user's landing page or dashboard." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:dataquality:Fdd19Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Same partial match and same caveats as 19.3.3 (near-duplicate story, different Feature grouping) — review comment 34 on this exact document, anchored to the 'Feature: 19.4 Email/Communication' heading itself, reads 'Other functionality already covered in epic 6' (epic 6 = Alerts, Emails and Communications, i.e. the real comm: domain), independently confirming from the reviewer's own side that this Feature's notification half is considered already-covered elsewhere rather than a fresh Communications-side build. Not modeled as a separate out-of-scope Annotation since the coverage is real (sd:satisfiedBy asserted) rather than merely deferred — 'covered elsewhere' and 'out of scope for lack of any owner' are different findings, and comment 34 describes the former." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "19.4.1" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:AlertAggregate> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:DashboardAlertCreatedEvent> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a MiEdWorkforce system, I will assign \"Action Items\" to submitting organizations when data violates Data Quality check specifications." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Assign Action Items to submitting organizations on violation" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:dataquality:Req_19_4_2> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:UserStory> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "The system automatically uses the specific email templates that were defined by the Data Quality Administrator to handle notifications for assigned Action Items. The authorized user receives an email notification alerting them of the assigned Action Item." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:dataquality:Fdd19Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Strong, direct match on the 'use defined email templates to notify' mechanism itself — comm:EmailTemplateAggregate/comm:Seq_EventTriggeredEmailSend is exactly this pattern (event fires -> template resolved -> variables substituted -> sent), and communications-technical-design.ttl's comm:TP_EventConsolidation batches multiple DQ issues into one email per the same BRD-19.4-cited Dependency noted at 19.3.3, matching this story's own implicit 'Data Quality Category Email Templates' concept from the main Business Specifications prose. The one remaining gap, as elsewhere in this file, is upstream: 'defined by the Data Quality Administrator' implies a DQ-specific template-authoring/category surface that doesn't exist (comm:EmailTemplateAggregate's own template authoring is generic across all of Communications' consumers, not a DQ Administrator's own tool)." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "19.4.2" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:EmailTemplateAggregate> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:Rule_EventPayloadStructureAndVariableResolution> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:Seq_EventTriggeredEmailSend> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a MiEdWorkforce system, I will use the defined email templates to notify authorized users of the assigned Action Item." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Use defined email templates to notify users of assigned Action Items" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:dataquality:Req_19_5> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Requirement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:dataquality:Fdd19Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Modeled as a plain sd:Requirement, not sd:UserStory, since the FDD supplies no narrative/AC content at all to type further — the rejection IS the entire content of this section. The ADA/WCAG 2.0 compliance standard itself remains asserted as a project-wide Assumption in both FDD 19 and FDD 20's own Assumptions sections (not modeled as a separate Requirement here — see sd:nonFunctionalRequirement's own escape-hatch guidance for project-wide NFRs asserted at sd:Solution level, out of scope for a per-domain FDD-review pass to re-litigate)." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "19.5" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "(No narrative or acceptance criteria given — the entire Feature 19.5 section consists of one sentence: 'It has been determined that this feature is no longer necessary.')" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "MiEdWorkforce ADA Compliance (Feature 19.5)" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:dataquality:Req_20_0_1> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:UserStory> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "The Administrator accesses the comment input field (standard free-form text box) within the specific functional area (including, but not limited to, Educator Credentialing, Professional Practice Review (PPR), Professional Learning). The Administrator enters the justification or feedback text. The system saves the comment with details (Created by/Date Created). The system displays the \"External\" comment to the User, as external comments may be viewed with permissions." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:dataquality:Fdd20Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Direct, strong match: comm:CommentAggregate's own invariants already state 'External comments are eligible for inclusion in outbound emails' and require an explicit visibility distinction created-by/created-at audit fields (comm:CommentEmailHistory), matching this story's AC almost verbatim. See the file-header finding (Question_CommentFrameworkModeledRedundantlyAcrossDomains below) on how this generic framework relates to profpractices' and EPP's own separately-modeled internal/external remarks fields." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "20.0.1" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:CommentAggregate> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:Op_CreateComment> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:Perm_CommentsCreateExternal> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a MiEdWorkforce Administrator, I want the workflow to allow me to input specific comments as \"External\" within a functional area, so that Users can view relevant feedback and justifications regarding their records while logged into the system." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Administrator inputs an External comment visible to the user" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:dataquality:Req_20_0_2> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:UserStory> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "The System Administrator accesses the comment input field during a review process, within the specific functional area (including, but not limited to, Educator Credentialing, Professional Practice Review (PPR), Rap backs, Education Preparation Provider). The Administrator enters text into the comment box. The system saves the comment and enforces role-based restrictions. If a Business or Citizen User views the record, the system hides the \"Internal\" comment from their view. Only select state staff with appropriate privileges and functional area authorization can view the comment." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:dataquality:Fdd20Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Direct, strong match: comm:CommentAggregate's invariant 'Internal comments are never visible to external users' is exactly this story's core requirement, and comm:Perm_CommentsViewInternal's own conditional PermissionRequirement on comm:Op_ListComments already encodes the role-gated visibility this AC describes." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "20.0.2" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:CommentAggregate> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:Op_CreateComment> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:Perm_CommentsCreateInternal> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:Perm_CommentsViewInternal> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a MiEdWorkforce Administrator, I want the workflow to support marking comments as \"Internal,\" so that sensitive discussions and decision-making details are restricted from Business and Citizen users and are only viewable by authorized state staff." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Administrator marks a comment as Internal, restricted from external view" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:dataquality:Req_20_0_3> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:UserStory> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "The system displays status options including \"Hold,\" \"Cancel,\" and \"Deny\" within the application processing screen. Selecting a status flag triggers a mandatory comment input field. The system defaults the comment visibility setting to \"External\" for these specific status flags. The entered justification is visible to the applicant when viewing their application status. The system stores the new status, the external comment, and the audit details (Created by and Date Created)." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:dataquality:Fdd20Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "PARTIAL, and asymmetric across the two domains this story itself names as examples. EPP already enforces almost exactly this rule TWICE, independently: epp:CredentialApplicationReviewAggregate's own invariant states 'Application Remarks (external, visible to applicant) required when action is Deny or Hold', and epp:ApprovalApplicationReviewAggregate's states 'Denial requires Remarks to be provided' — both a real, mandatory-on-status-change, externally-visible remarks requirement, matching this story closely. Credentialing, however, has the STATUS-FLAG structural half (cred:AppState_Denied, cred:AppState_Cancelled, cred:Op_DenyApplication all real) but NO equivalent 'remarks required on deny/cancel' invariant anywhere in credentialing-domain.ttl — a genuine cross-domain INCONSISTENCY worth flagging on its own terms (see Question_CommentFrameworkModeledRedundantlyAcrossDomains below): the same story names Credentialing and EPP as equally-applicable examples, but only EPP actually enforces it today. 'Hold' as a distinct citizen-facing status flag (vs. Credentialing's internal-only ProfessionalPracticeStatus=Hold, which is not the same concept) is not modeled in Credentialing at all." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "20.0.3" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:CommentAggregate> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:AppState_Cancelled> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:AppState_Denied> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Op_DenyApplication> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:epp:ApprovalApplicationReviewAggregate> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:epp:CredentialApplicationReviewAggregate> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a MiEdWorkforce Administrator (e.g., Credentialing or EPP Administrator), I want the system to require an external comment when I apply a status flag like \"Hold,\" \"Cancel,\" or \"Deny\" to an application, so that the applicant (Citizen or Business User) receives a clear explanation for the status change on their record." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Require an External comment when applying a status flag (Hold/Cancel/Deny)" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:dataquality:Req_20_0_4> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:UserStory> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "The system allows authorized administrators to apply internal-only flags (e.g., Professional Practice Flag) to a record. Applying an internal flag will also allow the option to add an internal remark by navigating to the \"internal remarks\" tab. The Administrator enters sensitive or administrative text into the comment box. The system automatically restricts the visibility of this comment to \"Internal.\" Business and Citizen users are prevented from viewing the flag or the associated comment on their record. Only State Staff with appropriate security privileges can view the internal flag and comment. The system captures and stores the flag application, the internal comment, and user in the audit history." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:dataquality:Fdd20Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Direct, strong match, and the story's own worked example (a 'Professional Practice Review flag') names the EXACT real mechanism this maps to: profp:Seq_ReviewDisclosureAndUpdateStatus's own sequence diagram literally shows 'Reviewer->>WorklistUI: Add internal remarks (staff notes)' / 'PPRService->>PPRService: Add InternalRemarks' as a real step, and profp:DisclosureInternalRemarks is a real ValueObject on the Disclosure aggregate whose own sd:keyDecisions elsewhere states 'internal remarks are not' visible externally. This is the strongest single satisfiedBy match in this entire file, precisely because the story described the PPR case by name rather than generically." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "20.0.4" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:CommentAggregate> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:Perm_CommentsCreateInternal> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:profpractices:DisclosureInternalRemarks> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:profpractices:Seq_ReviewDisclosureAndUpdateStatus> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a MiEdWorkforce Administrator (e.g. Professional Practices Reviewer), I want the system to require an internal comment when I apply a sensitive flag (such as a Professional Practice Review flag) to a record, so that internal staff can track the reason for the investigation or audit without revealing sensitive details to the public user." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Require an Internal comment when applying a sensitive internal flag (e.g. PPR flag)" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:dataquality:Wireframe19_1> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:SourceDocument> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:dataquality:Fdd19Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:docType> "wireframe" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Confirmed by viewing: NOT a MiEdWorkforce mockup — a live screenshot of the EXISTING legacy CEPI MSDS system ('MSDS - 2024-25 Early Childhood Fall - Kent ISD', 'Collection & Data Quality Summary'), embedded in the Business Specifications prose right after the line 'Example from CEPI MSDS Early Childhood.' Shows exactly the Problem/Impact/Action three-part text structure that 19.1.5/19.2.5 describe in the abstract, and the per-entity/per-category aggregation table 19.2.5's 'Level of Aggregation' criterion describes — i.e. this is reference material showing what MDE/CEPI's CURRENT tooling already does, which MiEdWorkforce is meant to replicate/replace, not a proposed new screen. Also independently explains what the sibling 'Copy of EOY 2024 REP Comparison and Review' workbook (not opened, per this file's header) most likely refers to (REP = the same Early Childhood reporting cycle), without needing to open it." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:section> "abox/mied-v3/fdd-review/19-20-data-quality-review-and-processing/wireframes/19-1-msds-early-childhood-example.jpg" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:dataquality:Wireframe19_2> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:SourceDocument> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:dataquality:Fdd19Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:docType> "wireframe" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Confirmed by viewing: a completely generic, content-free 'Dashboard / Manage Layout' screen — three empty 'Section Name' rows of '+ Add Widget' placeholder tiles, no Data-Quality-specific content of any kind. Embedded once inline within 19.1.1's acceptance criteria (between the District-access bullet and the 'displays a clearly labeled Data Quality Dashboard widget' bullet) and reused VERBATIM (byte-for-byte identical layout, confirmed by direct visual comparison, not just taken on the reviewer's word) as the image embedded at 19.3.1. Reviewer's own comment 33 on the second occurrence says as much ('representative of the general layout of a user's dashboard...applicable to all user stories under feature 19.3') — corroborated here, not merely trusted. The practical implication: no DQ-specific dashboard visual design exists anywhere in this FDD; only a generic, dashboards-capability-owned empty-widget shell." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:section> "abox/mied-v3/fdd-review/19-20-data-quality-review-and-processing/wireframes/19-1-1-empty-dashboard-widget-shell.png" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:dataquality:Wireframe19_3> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:SourceDocument> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:dataquality:Fdd19Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:docType> "wireframe" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Confirmed by viewing: NOT a Data Quality screen. Breadcrumb reads 'Dashboard > Credentialing > Credential Data & Management > Business Rules', a generic sortable/paginated 'Business Rules' list table (redacted placeholder text, 6115 items, filter+export icons) inside the CREDENTIALING module. Embedded directly within 19.2.1's acceptance criteria ('administrative page...displays all configured data quality checks in a sortable table') despite depicting an unrelated Business Rules admin screen. This is significant, independent visual corroboration of comment 30's own point (see Question_DqAdminOverlapsBusinessRuleManagement below): the FDD's own wireframe author reached for a Business Rule Management mockup to illustrate the Data Quality admin console, suggesting the two capabilities may have been conceived as the same underlying admin-configuration surface (per-domain rule/check definitions, versioned, sortable/filterable table, export) rather than genuinely distinct ones — not a captioning error, since no other 'DQ admin table' mockup appears anywhere in the document." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:section> "abox/mied-v3/fdd-review/19-20-data-quality-review-and-processing/wireframes/19-2-1-credentialing-business-rules-page.png" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:AllowableFormatsVO> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:ValueObject> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:description> "Whitelist of permitted file extensions and MIME types." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:name> "AllowableFormats" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:ApiDoc> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:SourceDocument> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:docType> "api-spec" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:section> "abox-tests/mied/documents/documents-api.yml" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:ApiSpec> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:ApiSpec> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:ApiDoc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:version> "1.0.0" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:BatchJob_HardDeleteProcessing> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:BatchJob> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:TechnicalDesignDoc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:enforcedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:DocumentAggregate> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:errorScenarios> "Retry failed deletions the next night (max 3 consecutive failures per document). Never delete metadata even if blob deletion fails, to preserve the audit trail. Alert admins if the deletion failure rate exceeds 5%." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:initiatedBy> "internal-system" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Performance targets: batch size 100, total runtime <10 minutes for 10,000 deletions; if it exceeds 10 minutes, pause and resume the next night." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:schedule> "Nightly at 2:00 AM EST (Azure Function Timer Trigger)" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:steps> "1) Query soft-deleted documents where retention period has expired and no legal hold is active. 2) Process in batches of 100. 3) Delete blob from Azure Storage. 4) Update metadata: hard_deleted=true, hard_deleted_at=NOW(). 5) Publish DocumentHardDeleted. 6) Generate a summary report: total evaluated, deleted, skipped, errors." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Hard Delete Background Job" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:BatchJob_StagingFileCleanup> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:BatchJob> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:TechnicalDesignDoc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:enforcedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:StagingFileAggregate> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:errorScenarios> "Not detailed in source; staging files that fail cleanup are not explicitly addressed in documents-technical-design.md or documents-sequences.md — contrast with docs:BatchJob_HardDeleteProcessing's explicit retry/alert policy. See docs:Question_StagingCleanupJobErrorHandling." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:initiatedBy> "internal-system" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:schedule> "Daily" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:steps> "Query staging files where uploaded_at is older than 7 days; delete the blob for each; update StagingFile.blob_deleted=true. Runs regardless of processing status (processed, failed, or still pending)." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Bulk-Import Staging File Cleanup Job" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:BlobReference> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:ValueObject> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:description> "Azure Blob Storage coordinates (container, path, SAS token generation metadata)." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:name> "BlobReference" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:BulkFileUploadedEvent> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:DomainEvent> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:payloadHighlights> "upload_id, functional_area, import_type, blob_path" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:publishedToTopic> "miedworkforce-domain-events" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:trigger> "Staged bulk-import file scanned clean" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:BulkOpState_Cancelled> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:StateDefinition> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:isTerminal> true ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:name> "Cancelled" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:BulkOpState_Completed> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:StateDefinition> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:isTerminal> true ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:name> "Completed" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:BulkOpState_Failed> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:StateDefinition> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:isTerminal> true ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:name> "Failed" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:BulkOpState_InProgress> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:StateDefinition> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:isTerminal> false ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:name> "In Progress" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:BulkOpState_PartiallyFailed> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:StateDefinition> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:isTerminal> true ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:name> "Partially Failed" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:BulkOpState_Queued> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:StateDefinition> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:isTerminal> false ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:name> "Queued" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:BulkOperationAggregate> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Aggregate> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:CapabilityDoc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:description> "Tracks batch upload or delete operations, providing progress monitoring, error handling, and rollback capabilities." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:emits> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:BulkOperationCompletedEvent> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:hasEntity> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:BulkOperationItem> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:hasState> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:BulkOpState_Cancelled> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:hasState> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:BulkOpState_Completed> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:hasState> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:BulkOpState_Failed> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:hasState> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:BulkOpState_InProgress> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:hasState> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:BulkOpState_PartiallyFailed> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:hasState> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:BulkOpState_Queued> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:hasValueObject> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:BulkOperationSummary> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:invariants> "Bulk operations must have at least one item. Operation cannot transition to Completed until all items processed. Failed items must include error reason. Bulk delete must validate retention policies and legal holds for all items before starting. If any item in bulk delete violates retention policy, entire operation marked Partially Failed. Bulk upload malware scan failures mark individual items as Failed but don't block other items. Each BulkOperationItem references its created Document ID once upload succeeds." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:rootEntity> "BulkOperation" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:BulkOperationCompletedEvent> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:DomainEvent> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:payloadHighlights> "operation_id, type, total_count, succeeded_count, failed_count" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:publishedToTopic> "miedworkforce-domain-events" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:trigger> "Batch operation finished" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:BulkOperationItem> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:DomainEntity> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:description> "Individual document in a batch with success/failure status, error message, and document reference." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:name> "BulkOperationItem" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:BulkOperationSummary> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:ValueObject> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:description> "Aggregate statistics: total count, succeeded, failed, skipped." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:name> "BulkOperationSummary" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:CapabilityDoc> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:SourceDocument> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:docType> "domain" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:section> "abox-tests/mied/documents/documents-capability.md" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:CatState_Active> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:StateDefinition> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:isTerminal> false ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:name> "Active" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:CatState_Deprecated> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:StateDefinition> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:description> "No new uploads allowed; existing documents remain accessible." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:isTerminal> true ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:name> "Deprecated" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:Cat_AdminOperations> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:PermissionCategory> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:label> "Admin Operations" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:Cat_AuditReporting> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:PermissionCategory> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:label> "Audit & Reporting" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:Cat_CategoryManagement> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:PermissionCategory> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:label> "Category Management" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:Cat_LegalHold> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:PermissionCategory> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:label> "Legal Hold" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:Cat_RetentionOverride> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:PermissionCategory> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:label> "Retention Override" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:DocState_Archived> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:StateDefinition> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:isTerminal> false ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:name> "Archived" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:DocState_Available> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:StateDefinition> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:isTerminal> false ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:name> "Available" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:DocState_HardDeleted> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:StateDefinition> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:isTerminal> true ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:name> "Hard Deleted" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:DocState_Infected> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:StateDefinition> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:isTerminal> true ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:name> "Infected" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:DocState_ScanFailed> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:StateDefinition> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:isTerminal> true ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:name> "Scan Failed" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:DocState_Scanning> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:StateDefinition> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:isTerminal> false ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:name> "Scanning" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:DocState_SoftDeleted> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:StateDefinition> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:isTerminal> false ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:name> "Soft Deleted" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:DocState_Uploading> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:StateDefinition> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:isTerminal> false ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:name> "Uploading" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:DocumentAccessLog> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:DomainEntity> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:description> "Audit entry for each document interaction (view, download, upload, replace, delete) with user ID, timestamp, IP address, and user agent." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:name> "DocumentAccessLog" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:DocumentAggregate> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Aggregate> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:CapabilityDoc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:description> "Manages the complete lifecycle of a single file from upload through deletion, enforcing security, retention, and audit requirements." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:emits> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:DocumentArchivedToBlobEvent> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:emits> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:DocumentHardDeletedEvent> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:emits> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:DocumentMalwareDetectedEvent> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:emits> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:DocumentReplacedEvent> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:emits> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:DocumentSoftDeletedEvent> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:emits> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:DocumentUploadedEvent> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:emits> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:DocumentViewedEvent> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:emits> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:LegalHoldAppliedEvent> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:emits> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:LegalHoldReleasedEvent> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:hasEntity> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:DocumentAccessLog> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:hasEntity> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:DocumentVersion> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:hasState> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:DocState_Archived> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:hasState> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:DocState_Available> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:hasState> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:DocState_HardDeleted> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:hasState> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:DocState_Infected> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:hasState> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:DocState_ScanFailed> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:hasState> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:DocState_Scanning> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:hasState> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:DocState_SoftDeleted> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:hasState> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:DocState_Uploading> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:hasValueObject> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:BlobReference> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:hasValueObject> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:LegalHoldVO> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:hasValueObject> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:MalwareScanResultVO> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:hasValueObject> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:RetentionPolicyVO> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:invariants> "Document must belong to exactly one category. Document must have valid blob reference in Azure Storage. Malware-infected documents cannot transition to Available status. Soft-deleted documents cannot be accessed by users (admin override allowed). Hard delete blocked if legal hold is active. Hard delete blocked if retention period has not expired. Document replacement creates new version record; old version soft-deleted or archived per category policy. Original filename preserved in metadata even if blob path uses UUID-based naming. MIME type must match allowable formats for category. File size must not exceed category-specific file size limit." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:rootEntity> "Document" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:DocumentArchivedToBlobEvent> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:DomainEvent> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:payloadHighlights> "document_id, archived_at, archive_tier" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:publishedToTopic> "miedworkforce-domain-events" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:trigger> "Document moved to archive tier by Azure lifecycle policy" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:DocumentCategoryAggregate> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Aggregate> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:CapabilityDoc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:description> "Defines storage, security, retention, and file size rules for groups of documents with similar business purposes and compliance requirements." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:emits> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:DocumentCategoryCreatedEvent> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:emits> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:RetentionPolicyUpdatedEvent> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:hasState> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:CatState_Active> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:hasState> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:CatState_Deprecated> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:hasValueObject> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:AllowableFormatsVO> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:hasValueObject> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:FileSizeLimitVO> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:hasValueObject> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:RetentionConfiguration> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:hasValueObject> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:SecurityConfiguration> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:hasValueObject> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:StoragePolicy> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:invariants> "Category slug must be unique and follow naming convention: lowercase, hyphen-separated. Retention period must be >= 0 (0 = immediate deletion after soft delete). Allowable formats list cannot be empty. File size limit must be between 1 MB and 500 MB (never exceed 500 MB due to scan performance and Defender limitations). Blob container name derived from category slug: documents-{category-slug}. Categories cannot be deleted if documents exist in that category. Retention period changes apply only to new documents (existing documents retain original expiry date)." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:rootEntity> "DocumentCategory" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:DocumentCategoryCreatedEvent> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:DomainEvent> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:payloadHighlights> "category_id, category_slug, retention_years" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:publishedToTopic> "miedworkforce-domain-events" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:trigger> "New category configured" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:DocumentHardDeletedEvent> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:DomainEvent> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:payloadHighlights> "document_id, deleted_at, deletion_reason" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:publishedToTopic> "miedworkforce-domain-events" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:trigger> "Blob permanently removed" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:DocumentMalwareDetectedEvent> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:DomainEvent> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:payloadHighlights> "document_id, threat_type, threat_name, scan_service, uploaded_by_user_id" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:publishedToTopic> "miedworkforce-domain-events" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:trigger> "Malware scan identifies threat" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:DocumentReplacedEvent> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:DomainEvent> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:payloadHighlights> "document_id, new_version_id, replaced_by_user_id, old_version_archived" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:publishedToTopic> "miedworkforce-domain-events" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:trigger> "User uploads new version (scan clean)" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:DocumentSoftDeletedEvent> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:DomainEvent> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:payloadHighlights> "document_id, deleted_by_user_id, retention_expiry_date" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:publishedToTopic> "miedworkforce-domain-events" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:trigger> "Document marked as deleted" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:DocumentUploadedEvent> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:DomainEvent> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:payloadHighlights> "document_id, category, attachment_type, attachment_id, uploaded_by_user_id, file_size, mime_type" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:publishedToTopic> "miedworkforce-domain-events" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:trigger> "Upload completed and malware scan clean" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:DocumentVersion> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:DomainEntity> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:description> "Historical record of a document replacement with version number and archived blob reference. Maximum 10 versions per document." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:name> "DocumentVersion" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:DocumentViewedEvent> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:DomainEvent> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:payloadHighlights> "document_id, viewed_by_user_id, viewed_at" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:publishedToTopic> "miedworkforce-domain-events" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:trigger> "User downloads/views document" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:DocumentsContext> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:BoundedContext> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:CapabilityDoc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:displayName> "Documents" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:hasAggregate> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:BulkOperationAggregate> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:hasAggregate> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:DocumentAggregate> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:hasAggregate> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:DocumentCategoryAggregate> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:hasAggregate> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:OverrideRequestAggregate> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:hasAggregate> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:StagingFileAggregate> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:identifier> "documents" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:kind> "PlatformCapability" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Explicitly does NOT own: authorization of upload/download requests (calling domain's responsibility), business rules determining which documents are required for a workflow (domain-specific), evaluation of document content quality (domain-specific), malware scanning infrastructure itself (Azure Defender for Storage), upload-form UI (UI framework / domain UIs), authorization rules for who may upload to a context (iam), workflow state transitions requiring uploads (domain-specific workflow engines), long-term data warehouse archival (Azure Synapse / Data Lake), scheduled ETL (Azure Synapse / Data Factory), storage tier transition logic (Azure Blob Storage Lifecycle Management, infrastructure-managed)." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:purpose> "Provides centralized file storage and lifecycle management infrastructure across MiEdWorkforce, enabling functional areas to support secure document uploads, version control, malware scanning, retention policies, and bulk file operations. Manages the complete document lifecycle from upload through storage, retrieval, archival, and deletion while maintaining compliance with security, audit, and retention requirements." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "documented" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:subscribesTo> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:external:BulkFileProcessedEvent> .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:FileSizeLimitVO> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:ValueObject> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:description> "Maximum file size allowed for uploads in this category, in MB (1-500)." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:name> "FileSizeLimit" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:LegalHoldAppliedEvent> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:DomainEvent> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:payloadHighlights> "document_id, applied_by_user_id, justification" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:publishedToTopic> "miedworkforce-domain-events" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:trigger> "Legal hold flag set" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:LegalHoldReleasedEvent> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:DomainEvent> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:payloadHighlights> "document_id, released_by_user_id, release_reason" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:publishedToTopic> "miedworkforce-domain-events" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:trigger> "Legal hold removed" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:LegalHoldVO> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:ValueObject> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:description> "Flag with justification, case number, and hold-placed/released timestamps." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:name> "LegalHold" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:MalwareScanResultVO> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:ValueObject> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:description> "Outcome of the security scan with threat details if infected." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:fields> "scanResultType (No threats found|Malicious|Error|Not scanned), scannedAt, threatDetails" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:name> "MalwareScanResult" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:Op_ApplyLegalHold> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:ApiOperation> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:accessType> "internal-user" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:consumesShape> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:LegalHoldVO> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:exposedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:DocumentsContext> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:method> "POST" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:operationId> "applyLegalHold" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:partOfSpec> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:ApiSpec> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:path> "/documents/legal-hold/apply" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:projection> "documentIds[] + justification/caseNumber/holdReason — batch application of LegalHold value-object fields across multiple documents in one call, rather than one LegalHold per request." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:responseSchema> "{appliedCount} — a simple count, not an entity projection." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:scopeSensitive> false ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:summary> "Apply legal hold to documents" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:tags> "LegalHold" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:Op_ApproveOverrideRequest> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:ApiOperation> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:accessType> "internal-user" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:consumesShape> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:OverrideApproval> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:exposedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:DocumentsContext> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:method> "POST" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Approvers cannot approve their own requests (enforced at execution time, not expressible as a static permission)." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:operationId> "approveOverrideRequest" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:partOfSpec> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:ApiSpec> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:path> "/documents/override-requests/{requestId}/approve" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:producesShape> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:OverrideRequestAggregate> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:projection> "Request carries only approvalComments — server fills approvedByUserId/approvedAt from the authenticated caller and current time." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:projection> "{requestId, status (Approved|Pending), approvalsReceived} — a status-transition confirmation subset of OverrideRequest." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:scopeSensitive> false ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:summary> "Approve override request" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:tags> "RetentionOverride" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:Op_BulkDeleteDocuments> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:ApiOperation> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:accessType> "internal-user" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:consumesShape> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:BulkOperationAggregate> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:exposedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:DocumentsContext> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:method> "POST" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:operationId> "bulkDeleteDocuments" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:partOfSpec> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:ApiSpec> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:path> "/documents/bulk-delete" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:producesShape> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:BulkOperationAggregate> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:projection> "Request is just {documentIds[], mode} — the scope of the batch, not a full BulkOperation; the BulkOperation record itself (operation_type, status, counts) is created server-side." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:projection> "Response mirrors BulkOperationSummary fields (succeededCount, skippedCount) plus per-item skipReason (legal_hold|retention_not_expired), a subset of BulkOperationItem." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:scopeSensitive> false ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:summary> "Bulk soft delete documents with retention validation" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:tags> "BulkOperations" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:Op_CreateDocumentCategory> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:ApiOperation> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:accessType> "internal-user" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:consumesShape> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:DocumentCategoryAggregate> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:exposedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:DocumentsContext> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:method> "POST" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:operationId> "createDocumentCategory" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:partOfSpec> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:ApiSpec> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:path> "/documents/categories" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:producesShape> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:DocumentCategoryAggregate> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:projection> "DocumentCategoryCreate carries categorySlug/displayName/description/allowableFormats/fileSizeLimitMb; blobContainerName is derived server-side from the slug (documents-{category-slug}) and categoryId is server-generated." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:projection> "{categoryId, categorySlug, blobContainerName} — creation-confirmation subset." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:scopeSensitive> false ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:summary> "Create document category" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:tags> "CategoryManagement" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:Op_DeprecateDocumentCategory> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:ApiOperation> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:accessType> "internal-user" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:exposedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:DocumentsContext> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:method> "POST" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Cannot be reversed via API." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:operationId> "deprecateDocumentCategory" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:partOfSpec> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:ApiSpec> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:path> "/documents/categories/{categorySlug}/deprecate" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:producesShape> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:DocumentCategoryAggregate> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:projection> "Transitions the category to docs:CatState_Deprecated; 200 response body is empty per the spec (no explicit projection returned)." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:scopeSensitive> false ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:summary> "Deprecate document category" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:tags> "CategoryManagement" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:Op_DownloadDocument> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:ApiOperation> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:accessType> "internal-service" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:exposedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:DocumentsContext> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:method> "GET" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "x-permissions-required: [] — the calling domain is responsible for verifying the user may access this document; Documents does not re-check business authorization." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:operationId> "downloadDocument" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:partOfSpec> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:ApiSpec> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:path> "/documents/{documentId}/download" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:producesShape> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:DocumentAggregate> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:projection> "200 response mirrors Document's originalFilename/fileSize/mimeType fields, with sasUrl and expiresAt added — pure technical fields with no Document-field counterpart (a time-limited storage token, not persisted state)." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:scopeSensitive> false ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:summary> "Generate download SAS token for document" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:tags> "Documents" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:Op_ExecuteOverrideRequest> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:ApiOperation> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:accessType> "internal-user" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:exposedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:DocumentsContext> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:method> "POST" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Per the spec, the requester executes their own approved request. Gated on the same request permission rather than a distinct execute permission." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:operationId> "executeOverrideRequest" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:partOfSpec> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:ApiSpec> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:path> "/documents/override-requests/{requestId}/execute" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:responseSchema> "{deletedCount} — a simple count, not an entity projection." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:scopeSensitive> false ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:summary> "Execute approved override" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:tags> "RetentionOverride" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:Op_ExportAuditLogs> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:ApiOperation> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:accessType> "internal-user" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:exposedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:DocumentsContext> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:method> "POST" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Async export; returns a job ID, poll for completion and download URL." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:operationId> "exportAuditLogs" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:partOfSpec> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:ApiSpec> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:path> "/documents/audit/logs/export" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requestBodySchema> "{format (csv|xlsx, default csv), after, before, documentId, userId} — filter/export-job parameters overlapping DocumentAccessLog's own filterable fields, but shaped as an async export request rather than a document entity; escape hatch used since the whole point of the body is job configuration, not a DocumentAccessLog instance." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:responseSchema> "{jobId, statusUrl} — an async job handle, not an entity projection." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:scopeSensitive> false ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:summary> "Export audit log data" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:tags> "Audit" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:Op_GetAuditLogs> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:ApiOperation> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:accessType> "internal-user" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:exposedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:DocumentsContext> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:method> "GET" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:operationId> "getAuditLogs" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:parameters> "documentId, userId, action, after, before, page (default 1), pageSize (default 20, max 100) — all query filters/pagination." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:partOfSpec> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:ApiSpec> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:path> "/documents/audit/logs" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:producesShape> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:DocumentAccessLog> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:projection> "AuditLogEntry mirrors DocumentAccessLog's fields directly (accessLogId, documentId, action, userId, actionTimestamp, ipAddress, userAgent) — no material reshaping." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:scopeSensitive> false ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:summary> "View document access and lifecycle audit logs" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:tags> "Audit" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:Op_GetBulkOperationStatus> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:ApiOperation> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:accessType> "internal-service" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:exposedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:DocumentsContext> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:method> "GET" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "x-permissions-required: []. Used by both domain UIs (polling upload progress) and the Documents admin UI." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:operationId> "getBulkOperationStatus" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:partOfSpec> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:ApiSpec> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:path> "/documents/bulk-operations/{operationId}" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:producesShape> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:BulkOperationAggregate> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:projection> "BulkOperationDetail closely mirrors the aggregate's own fields (operationType, status, totalCount, succeededCount, failedCount, skippedCount, initiatedByUserId, initiatedAt, completedAt) plus an items[] array of BulkOperationItem." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:scopeSensitive> false ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:summary> "Get bulk operation status" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:tags> "BulkOperations" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:Op_GetDocumentCategory> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:ApiOperation> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:accessType> "internal-user" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:exposedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:DocumentsContext> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:method> "GET" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:operationId> "getDocumentCategory" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:partOfSpec> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:ApiSpec> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:path> "/documents/categories/{categorySlug}" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:producesShape> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:DocumentCategoryAggregate> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:projection> "DocumentCategoryDetail is the full category shape (Summary fields plus description, blobContainerName, allowableFormats, createdAt, deprecatedAt) — mirrors the aggregate essentially as-is." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:scopeSensitive> false ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:summary> "Get document category details" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:tags> "CategoryManagement" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:Op_GetDocumentMetadata> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:ApiOperation> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:accessType> "internal-service" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:exposedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:DocumentsContext> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:method> "GET" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "x-permissions-required: []." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:operationId> "getDocumentMetadata" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:partOfSpec> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:ApiSpec> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:path> "/documents/{documentId}" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:producesShape> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:DocumentAggregate> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:projection> "DocumentMetadata schema closely mirrors Document's own fields (status, fileSize, mimeType, uploadedAt, currentVersion, versionCount, retentionExpiryDate, legalHold, softDeleted) plus a nested malwareScanResult object mapping to docs:MalwareScanResultVO. Excludes internal-only blob path/container fields. Returns metadata only, no download URL." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:scopeSensitive> false ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:summary> "Get document metadata" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:tags> "Documents" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:Op_GetOverrideRequest> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:ApiOperation> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:accessType> "internal-user" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:exposedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:DocumentsContext> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:method> "GET" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Same OR relationship as listOverrideRequests above." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:operationId> "getOverrideRequest" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:partOfSpec> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:ApiSpec> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:path> "/documents/override-requests/{requestId}" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:producesShape> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:OverrideRequestAggregate> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:projection> "OverrideRequestDetail extends Summary with documents[] (DocumentSummary, i.e. docs:DocumentAggregate projections) and approvals[] (docs:OverrideApproval entity: approvedByUserId, approvedAt, approvalComments)." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:scopeSensitive> false ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:summary> "Get override request details" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:tags> "RetentionOverride" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:Op_InitiateBulkUpload> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:ApiOperation> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:accessType> "internal-service" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:consumesShape> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:BulkOperationAggregate> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:exposedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:DocumentsContext> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:method> "POST" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "x-permissions-required: []. If a user is authorized to upload a document for a given purpose, they are authorized to upload multiple — same authorization boundary as single upload, enforced entirely by the calling domain." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:operationId> "initiateBulkUpload" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:partOfSpec> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:ApiSpec> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:path> "/documents/bulk-upload/request" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:projection> "Request's files[] array (filename/fileSize/mimeType per item) plus shared category/attachmentType/attachmentId maps to BulkOperation's initiating fields and each item's Document-shaped upload metadata; BulkOperationItem records and per-file Document records are server-created, not part of the request." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:responseSchema> "{operationId, uploadUrls: [{documentId, uploadUrl, filename}]} — a SAS upload-handshake envelope per file, same escape-hatch reasoning as requestDocumentUpload." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:scopeSensitive> false ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:summary> "Initiate bulk document upload" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:tags> "BulkOperations" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:Op_ListDocumentCategories> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:ApiOperation> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:accessType> "internal-user" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:exposedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:DocumentsContext> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:method> "GET" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:operationId> "listDocumentCategories" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:partOfSpec> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:ApiSpec> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:path> "/documents/categories" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:producesShape> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:DocumentCategoryAggregate> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:projection> "Returns DocumentCategorySummary — a list-view projection of DocumentCategory (categorySlug, displayName, isActive, fileSizeLimitMb, retentionPeriodDays), excluding description/allowableFormats/blobContainerName." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:scopeSensitive> false ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:summary> "List document categories" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:tags> "CategoryManagement" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:Op_ListOverrideRequests> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:ApiOperation> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:accessType> "internal-user" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:exposedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:DocumentsContext> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:method> "GET" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Accessible to users holding EITHER documents.retention-override.request OR documents.retention-override.approve (an OR, not an AND) — modeled below as two independent, non-conditional PermissionRequirement nodes since the ontology has no direct way to express 'either of these two satisfies access'; do not read the two nodes together as requiring both." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:operationId> "listOverrideRequests" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:partOfSpec> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:ApiSpec> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:path> "/documents/override-requests" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:producesShape> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:OverrideRequestAggregate> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:projection> "Returns OverrideRequestSummary — a list-view projection of OverrideRequest (status, documentCount, justification, businessReason, requestedByUserId, requestedAt, approvalsRequired, approvalsReceived, expiresAt)." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:scopeSensitive> false ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:summary> "List retention override requests" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:tags> "RetentionOverride" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:Op_ReceiveScanResult> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:ApiOperation> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:accessType> "internal-service" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:exposedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:DocumentsContext> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:method> "POST" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "x-permissions-required: []. Not a user-facing or domain-service endpoint — secured via Azure Event Grid webhook signature validation, a third distinct trust mechanism alongside MiLogin and Managed Identity that documents-api.yml itself calls out but that x-access's two-value vocabulary (internal-service/internal-user) doesn't distinguish from the Managed-Identity-secured domain-to-domain endpoints above. Recorded as internal-service (matching the spec's own x-access value) with this note flagging the distinction." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:operationId> "receiveScanResult" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:partOfSpec> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:ApiSpec> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:path> "/webhooks/defender-scan-result" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requestBodySchema> "Array of Azure Event Grid event objects: {id, eventType, subject, data: {blobUri, scanResultType, scanResultDetails: {malwareNamesFound[]}}} — an opaque third-party webhook envelope (Event Grid's own event schema, not a Documents domain-model shape); escape hatch is the only reasonable option here." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:scopeSensitive> false ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:summary> "Receive Azure Defender malware scan result" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:tags> "Webhooks" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:Op_ReleaseLegalHold> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:ApiOperation> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:accessType> "internal-user" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:consumesShape> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:LegalHoldVO> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:exposedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:DocumentsContext> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:method> "POST" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:operationId> "releaseLegalHold" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:partOfSpec> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:ApiSpec> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:path> "/documents/legal-hold/release" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:projection> "documentIds[] + releaseReason/caseClosureDate — batch clearing of LegalHold value-object fields across multiple documents." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:responseSchema> "{releasedCount} — a simple count, not an entity projection." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:scopeSensitive> false ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:summary> "Release legal hold from documents" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:tags> "LegalHold" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:Op_RequestDocumentReplacement> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:ApiOperation> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:accessType> "internal-service" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:consumesShape> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:DocumentVersion> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:exposedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:DocumentsContext> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:method> "POST" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "x-permissions-required: []. See documents-capability.ttl's docs:Rule_DocumentReplacementVersioning note for the capability.md/permissions.md discrepancy over whether a documents.document.replace permission exists (it doesn't, per documents-permissions.md, which treats replacement as an implicit baseline capability)." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:operationId> "requestDocumentReplacement" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:partOfSpec> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:ApiSpec> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:path> "/documents/{documentId}/replace/request" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:projection> "Request carries only filename/fileSize/mimeType for the replacement file — the fields that seed a new DocumentVersion/Document record; version numbering and archival of the prior version are server-computed." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:responseSchema> "{newDocumentId, uploadUrl, versionNumber, expiresAt} — same SAS upload-handshake envelope shape as requestDocumentUpload's response; escape hatch for the same reason." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:scopeSensitive> false ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:summary> "Request upload SAS token for document replacement" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:tags> "Documents" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:Op_RequestDocumentUpload> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:ApiOperation> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:accessType> "internal-service" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:consumesShape> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:DocumentAggregate> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:exposedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:DocumentsContext> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:method> "POST" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "x-permissions-required: [] — secured by Managed Identity / mTLS at the platform level, not an application permission. Calling domain is solely responsible for business authorization." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:operationId> "requestDocumentUpload" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:partOfSpec> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:ApiSpec> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:path> "/documents/upload/request" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:projection> "Request carries only initial upload metadata (filename, fileSize, mimeType, category, attachmentType, attachmentId) — a subset of Document's fields. Server generates documentId, blob path, and status; these are not part of the request." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:responseSchema> "{documentId, uploadUrl (write-only SAS URL, 15 min expiry), status: Scanning, expiresAt} — a SAS upload-handshake envelope, not a Document projection: uploadUrl/expiresAt have no domain-model counterpart (they're a storage-layer token, not persisted document state). Escape hatch used deliberately, per the ontology's own note that upload/download responses are a likely legitimate case for it." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:scopeSensitive> false ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:summary> "Request upload SAS token for document" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:tags> "Documents" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:Op_RequestRetentionOverride> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:ApiOperation> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:accessType> "internal-user" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:consumesShape> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:OverrideRequestAggregate> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:exposedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:DocumentsContext> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:method> "POST" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:operationId> "requestRetentionOverride" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:partOfSpec> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:ApiSpec> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:path> "/documents/override-requests" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:producesShape> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:OverrideRequestAggregate> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:projection> "documentIds[] + justification/businessReason/urgency maps to OverrideRequest's initiating fields; approvalsRequired/status/expiresAt are server-computed, not part of the request." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:projection> "{requestId, status: Pending, approvalsRequired} — a creation-confirmation subset of OverrideRequest." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:scopeSensitive> false ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:summary> "Request retention policy override" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:tags> "RetentionOverride" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:Op_SearchDocuments> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:ApiOperation> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:accessType> "internal-service" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:exposedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:DocumentsContext> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:method> "GET" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "x-permissions-required: []. Used both by domain APIs for attachment-context lookups and by the Documents admin UI's legal hold/override workflows — the admin UI usage is gated upstream by whatever permission gets the admin into that workflow (e.g. documents.legal-hold.apply), not by a permission on this endpoint itself." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:operationId> "searchDocuments" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:parameters> "attachmentType, attachmentId, category, status, uploadedAfter, page (default 1), pageSize (default 20, max 100) — all query parameters." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:partOfSpec> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:ApiSpec> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:path> "/documents/search" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:producesShape> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:DocumentAggregate> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:projection> "Returns DocumentSummary — a reduced list-view projection of Document (documentId, originalFilename, category, status, fileSize, uploadedAt, currentVersion). Query parameters (attachmentType, attachmentId, category, status, uploadedAfter, page, pageSize) are opaque filter/pagination text, captured via sd:parameters rather than sd:consumesShape (they don't constitute a request body shaped like a domain entity)." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:scopeSensitive> false ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:summary> "Search documents by attachment or category" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:tags> "Documents" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:Op_SoftDeleteDocument> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:ApiOperation> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:accessType> "internal-service" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:exposedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:DocumentsContext> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:method> "DELETE" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "x-permissions-required: []. Documents enforces that legal holds block deletion; the calling domain is responsible for verifying the user may delete this document. This is the 'Soft-delete an uploaded document' implicit baseline capability from documents-permissions.md, not the same as documents.admin.bulk-delete's batch path." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:operationId> "softDeleteDocument" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:partOfSpec> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:ApiSpec> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:path> "/documents/{documentId}" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:producesShape> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:DocumentAggregate> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:projection> "Response is {documentId, retentionExpiryDate} only — a minimal confirmation subset of Document's fields, not a full projection." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:scopeSensitive> false ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:summary> "Soft delete document" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:tags> "Documents" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:Op_UpdateDocumentCategory> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:ApiOperation> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:accessType> "internal-user" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:consumesShape> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:DocumentCategoryAggregate> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:exposedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:DocumentsContext> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:method> "PATCH" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:operationId> "updateDocumentCategory" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:partOfSpec> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:ApiSpec> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:path> "/documents/categories/{categorySlug}" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:producesShape> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:DocumentCategoryAggregate> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:projection> "Request may update displayName/description/allowableFormats/fileSizeLimitMb only — a narrow, mutable subset of DocumentCategory. Retention period and storage tier changes are managed via infrastructure-as-code (docs:RetentionConfiguration/docs:StoragePolicy are both explicitly read-only value objects) and are not exposed here." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:projection> "Returns the full updated DocumentCategoryDetail, same shape as getDocumentCategory." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:scopeSensitive> false ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:summary> "Update document category configuration" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:tags> "CategoryManagement" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:Op_UploadToStaging> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:ApiOperation> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:accessType> "internal-service" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:consumesShape> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:StagingFileAggregate> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:exposedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:DocumentsContext> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:method> "POST" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "x-permissions-required: []. functionalArea constrained to {staffing, epp, proflearning} by the request schema." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:operationId> "uploadToStaging" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:partOfSpec> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:ApiSpec> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:path> "/documents/staging/upload/request" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:projection> "Request carries filename/fileSize/mimeType/functionalArea/importType — initial StagingFile metadata; server generates upload_id and the staging blob path." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:responseSchema> "{uploadId, uploadUrl, status: Scanning} — SAS upload-handshake envelope, same escape-hatch reasoning as requestDocumentUpload." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:scopeSensitive> false ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:summary> "Upload file to staging area for Synapse pipeline processing" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:tags> "Staging" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:OverrideApproval> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:DomainEntity> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:description> "Business owner approval with timestamp and comments. Approvers cannot approve their own requests." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:name> "OverrideApproval" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:OverrideAudit> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:ValueObject> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:description> "Complete trail of request, approval, and execution." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:name> "OverrideAudit" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:OverrideRequestAggregate> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Aggregate> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:CapabilityDoc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:description> "Manages administrator requests to bypass retention policies or legal holds, enforcing approval workflows and audit trails." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:emits> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:OverrideRequestApprovedEvent> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:emits> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:OverrideRequestCreatedEvent> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:emits> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:OverrideRequestExecutedEvent> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:hasEntity> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:OverrideApproval> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:hasState> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:OverrideState_Approved> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:hasState> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:OverrideState_Executed> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:hasState> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:OverrideState_Expired> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:hasState> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:OverrideState_Pending> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:hasState> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:OverrideState_Rejected> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:hasValueObject> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:OverrideAudit> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:invariants> "Override request must include business justification. Request requires at least one business owner approval. High-value overrides (legal holds, retention >5 years) require dual approval. Approved overrides expire after 7 days if not executed. Executed overrides cannot be reversed (deletion is permanent). All override actions logged to compliance audit system." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:rootEntity> "OverrideRequest" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:OverrideRequestApprovedEvent> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:DomainEvent> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:payloadHighlights> "request_id, document_ids[], approved_by_user_id" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:publishedToTopic> "miedworkforce-domain-events" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:trigger> "Business owner approves override" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:OverrideRequestCreatedEvent> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:DomainEvent> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:payloadHighlights> "request_id, requested_by, document_ids[], approval_count_required" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:publishedToTopic> "miedworkforce-domain-events" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:trigger> "Admin submits a retention/legal-hold override request" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:OverrideRequestExecutedEvent> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:DomainEvent> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:payloadHighlights> "request_id, executed_at, executed_by" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:publishedToTopic> "miedworkforce-domain-events" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:trigger> "Admin executes an approved override, soft-deleting its documents" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:OverrideState_Approved> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:StateDefinition> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:isTerminal> false ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:name> "Approved" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:OverrideState_Executed> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:StateDefinition> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:isTerminal> true ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:name> "Executed" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:OverrideState_Expired> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:StateDefinition> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:isTerminal> true ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:name> "Expired" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:OverrideState_Pending> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:StateDefinition> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:isTerminal> false ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:name> "Pending" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:OverrideState_Rejected> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:StateDefinition> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:isTerminal> true ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:name> "Rejected" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:Perm_AdminBulkDelete> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Permission> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:description> "Soft-delete multiple documents in a single batch operation" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:hasCategory> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:Cat_AdminOperations> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:hasScope> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:shared:scope:SystemWide> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Document Admin; retention and legal hold status validated per item before executing." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:permissionId> "documents.admin.bulk-delete" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:Perm_AdminForceHardDelete> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Permission> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:description> "Immediately hard-delete a document outside the normal retention cycle" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:hasCategory> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:Cat_AdminOperations> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:hasScope> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:shared:scope:SystemWide> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "System Admin only; requires an approved override request; irreversible; audit logged. No matching endpoint in documents-api.yml — the closest existing endpoint, POST /documents/override-requests/{requestId}/execute, performs a soft delete per its own spec ('Performs soft delete for all documents ... bypassing retention policy checks'), not a hard delete. Documented gap between the permission catalog's description and the API's actual behavior." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:permissionId> "documents.admin.force-hard-delete" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:Perm_AdminOverrideScan> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Permission> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:description> "Mark a quarantined document as a false positive" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:hasCategory> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:Cat_AdminOperations> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:hasScope> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:shared:scope:SystemWide> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Security Admin only; requires justification; audit logged. No matching endpoint in documents-api.yml — documented gap." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:permissionId> "documents.admin.override-scan" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:Perm_AdminViewAll> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Permission> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:description> "View and download any document regardless of attachment context" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:hasCategory> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:Cat_AdminOperations> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:hasScope> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:shared:scope:SystemWide> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Document Admin, Compliance Officer; for audit and compliance investigations. No matching endpoint in documents-api.yml — GET /documents/search and GET /documents/{documentId}/download are both internal-service (called by domain APIs, not gated by this or any Documents-owned permission directly). Documented gap." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:permissionId> "documents.admin.view-all" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:Perm_AdminViewQuarantine> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Permission> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:description> "View documents flagged by malware scanner" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:hasCategory> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:Cat_AdminOperations> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:hasScope> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:shared:scope:SystemWide> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Security Admin, Document Admin; regular users receive only a generic upload failure message. No matching endpoint in documents-api.yml — documented gap." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:permissionId> "documents.admin.view-quarantine" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:Perm_AuditExport> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Permission> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:description> "Export document access log data for compliance reporting" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:hasCategory> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:Cat_AuditReporting> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:hasScope> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:shared:scope:SystemWide> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Not present in documents-permissions.md's permission catalog table — inferred solely from documents-api.yml's exportAuditLogs x-permissions-required. Documented discrepancy, not a fabricated permission: the API clearly expects a distinct export permission separate from documents.audit.view, but the permissions catalog was never updated to define it." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:permissionId> "documents.audit.export" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:Perm_AuditView> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Permission> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:description> "View and export document access logs and audit trail" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:hasCategory> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:Cat_AuditReporting> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:hasScope> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:shared:scope:SystemWide> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Document Admin, Compliance Officer, Auditor." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:permissionId> "documents.audit.view" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:Perm_CategoryCreate> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Permission> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:description> "Create a new document category" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:hasCategory> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:Cat_CategoryManagement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:hasScope> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:shared:scope:SystemWide> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "System Admin, Document Admin." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:permissionId> "documents.category.create" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:Perm_CategoryDeprecate> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Permission> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:description> "Mark a category as deprecated; prevents new uploads, existing documents unaffected" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:hasCategory> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:Cat_CategoryManagement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:hasScope> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:shared:scope:SystemWide> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "System Admin only." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:permissionId> "documents.category.deprecate" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:Perm_CategoryEdit> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Permission> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:description> "Modify category configuration (display name, allowable formats, file size limit)" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:hasCategory> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:Cat_CategoryManagement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:hasScope> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:shared:scope:SystemWide> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "System Admin, Document Admin; retention period and storage tier changes are backend config only." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:permissionId> "documents.category.edit" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:Perm_CategoryView> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Permission> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:description> "View document category configurations" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:hasCategory> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:Cat_CategoryManagement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:hasScope> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:shared:scope:SystemWide> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Document Admin, Compliance Officer." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:permissionId> "documents.category.view" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:Perm_LegalHoldApply> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Permission> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:description> "Apply legal hold to one or more documents" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:hasCategory> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:Cat_LegalHold> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:hasScope> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:shared:scope:SystemWide> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Legal Counsel, Compliance Officer; requires justification; audit logged." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:permissionId> "documents.legal-hold.apply" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:Perm_LegalHoldRelease> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Permission> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:description> "Release legal hold from document(s)" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:hasCategory> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:Cat_LegalHold> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:hasScope> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:shared:scope:SystemWide> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Legal Counsel, Compliance Officer; requires case closure justification; audit logged." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:permissionId> "documents.legal-hold.release" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:Perm_LegalHoldView> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Permission> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:description> "View documents with active legal holds" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:hasCategory> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:Cat_LegalHold> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:hasScope> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:shared:scope:SystemWide> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Legal Counsel, Compliance Officer, Document Admin. No matching endpoint in documents-api.yml — GET /documents/search is the closest fit but is generic and ungated, not scoped to legal-hold-only results. Documented gap, not a fabricated resolution." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:permissionId> "documents.legal-hold.view" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:Perm_RetentionOverrideApprove> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Permission> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:description> "Approve a retention override request" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:hasCategory> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:Cat_RetentionOverride> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:hasScope> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:shared:scope:SystemWide> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Business Owner, Compliance Officer; dual approval required for high-value documents; audit logged." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:permissionId> "documents.retention-override.approve" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:Perm_RetentionOverrideRequest> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Permission> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:description> "Request early deletion before retention expiry" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:hasCategory> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:Cat_RetentionOverride> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:hasScope> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:shared:scope:SystemWide> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Document Admin; requires business justification; audit logged." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:permissionId> "documents.retention-override.request" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:PermissionsDoc> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:SourceDocument> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:docType> "permissions" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:section> "abox-tests/mied/documents/documents-permissions.md" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:Question_ArchiveTierUserNotification> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Should users be informed when a document has moved to archive storage tier, given that retrieval may take longer (up to 15 hours for standard rehydration priority, per documents-technical-design.md)? docs:DocumentArchivedToBlobEvent's only asserted consumer today is audit." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:DocumentArchivedToBlobEvent> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#questioning> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:CapabilityDoc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:impact> "L" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "open" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:Question_CascadeDeleteOnAttachmentRemoval> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "How should the system handle documents attached to a record that is later deleted or withdrawn — should associated documents be cascade soft-deleted? Documents has no knowledge of the calling domain's own lifecycle (per its explicit scope boundary: 'workflow state transitions that require document uploads' are the calling domain's responsibility), so a cascade behavior would need to be initiated by the calling domain calling Documents' soft-delete endpoint per document, not something Documents can infer on its own from an attachment_id going stale." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:DocumentAggregate> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#questioning> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:CapabilityDoc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:impact> "H" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "open" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:Question_CategorySpecificTierOverrideCriteria> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The 'Category-Specific Overrides' subsection of Storage Tier Management names 'Active Employment Records' as an example category needing longer Hot-tier retention via a separate container with a custom lifecycle policy, but does not specify the actual duration, the criteria for which categories qualify for an override, or an approval process for requesting one. Not enough to model as anything beyond this placeholder mention until infrastructure/business input narrows it down." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:StoragePolicy> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#reviewing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:TechnicalDesignDoc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:findingType> "unconfirmed-assumption" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:impact> "L" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "open" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:Question_DocumentTaggingSupport> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Should the system support document tagging or custom metadata fields per category? No such capability exists in the current domain model (DocumentCategory's configuration is limited to retention/format/size/security rules, with no extensible metadata schema)." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:DocumentCategoryAggregate> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#questioning> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:CapabilityDoc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:impact> "L" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "open" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:Question_MalwareNotificationChannel> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Should users receive email notifications when their uploaded documents are flagged as malware? documents-sequences.md's malware-detected path only confirms an in-UI notification and a security-team alert; docs:DocumentMalwareDetectedEvent's consumers are 'security, monitoring' — no consumer resolves to comm:CommunicationsContext today." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:DocumentMalwareDetectedEvent> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#questioning> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:CapabilityDoc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:impact> "L" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "open" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:Question_PostSubmissionDocumentDeletion> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Can users delete documents after they've been submitted as part of a workflow (e.g., a credential application that has already been submitted)? documents-permissions.md's Upload Permission Model says viewing/uploading follows the calling domain's permission, but doesn't say whether that calling-domain gate also covers post-submission deletion, or whether Documents' own soft-delete baseline capability should be blocked once a workflow has consumed the document." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:DocumentAggregate> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#questioning> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:CapabilityDoc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:impact> "M" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "open" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:Question_RetentionScheduleOwnership> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "What are the official retention schedules for each document category? Business owner input is needed per functional area — documents-capability.md only asserts a 7-year default and a handful of illustrative examples (50 MB/50-500MB size tiers, 90-day and 'indefinite' special cases), not a confirmed per-category schedule." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:DocumentCategoryAggregate> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#questioning> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:CapabilityDoc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:impact> "M" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:owner> "Business Owner (per functional area)" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "open" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:Question_RetroactiveLegalHold> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Can legal holds be applied retroactively to documents that are already past their retention expiry but not yet hard-deleted? docs:Rule_RetentionPeriodEnforcement establishes that legal holds override retention expiry going forward, but doesn't address the narrower race-condition case of a document sitting in the window between 'expired' and 'actually processed by the nightly hard-delete job.'" ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:LegalHoldVO> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#questioning> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:CapabilityDoc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:impact> "M" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "open" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:Question_StagingCleanupJobErrorHandling> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Annotation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "documents-technical-design.md's 'Bulk Upload Staging for Synapse' section states 'Pipeline failure: File remains in staging for manual retry' and 'Alert if files accumulate,' but the daily cleanup job's own error handling for failed blob deletions is never specified anywhere in the source — contrast with the Hard Delete Job's explicit 'retry next night, max 3 consecutive failures, alert admins if failure rate exceeds 5%' policy. Left open rather than silently assumed to mirror the Hard Delete Job's policy." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#hasTarget> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:BatchJob_StagingFileCleanup> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#motivatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#questioning> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:TechnicalDesignDoc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:impact> "L" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "open" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:RetentionConfiguration> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:ValueObject> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:description> "Retention period (years/days). Archive tier transition rules are read-only, managed by infrastructure." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:name> "RetentionConfiguration" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:RetentionPolicyUpdatedEvent> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:DomainEvent> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:payloadHighlights> "category_id, old_retention_years, new_retention_years" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:publishedToTopic> "miedworkforce-domain-events" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:trigger> "Category retention rules changed" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:RetentionPolicyVO> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:ValueObject> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:description> "Category-specific retention rules with expiry date calculation, as applied to a specific document." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:name> "RetentionPolicy" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:Rule_BulkOperationRetentionValidation> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:BusinessRule> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:appliesTo> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:BulkOperationAggregate> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:CapabilityDoc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:enforcedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:BulkOperationAggregate> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:example> "Admin selects 100 documents for bulk soft delete; 2 have active legal holds; permissive mode proceeds with the 98 eligible and marks the operation Partially Failed, listing the 2 skipped." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:rationale> "Prevents accidental bulk deletion of documents still under retention or legal hold, which could violate compliance requirements." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "Bulk delete operations must validate retention policies and legal holds for ALL documents in the batch before starting. If any document violates retention rules, the operation is blocked (strict mode) or marked partially failed (permissive mode, the default)." .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:Rule_DocumentReplacementVersioning> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:BusinessRule> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:appliesTo> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:DocumentAggregate> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:CapabilityDoc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:enforcedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:DocumentAggregate> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:example> "official_transcript.pdf v1.0 uploaded Jan 1 2026; user replaces it Jan 5 2026; v1.0 archived and soft-deleted, v2.0 becomes current; user can only view v2.0, admin can view version history." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "documents-capability.md's own Constraints list for this rule states replacement 'is only allowed if the user has documents.document.replace permission' — but documents-permissions.md's permission catalog defines no such permission; its own 'Implicit Baseline (All Authenticated Users)' section instead describes replacement as NOT requiring an explicit permission grant at all, gated only by technical constraints (max versions, not soft-deleted, format/size) plus whatever the calling domain has already authorized. A genuine contradiction between capability.md and permissions.md, left unresolved here — see documents-permissions.ttl's PermissionRequirement notes for the API side of this same gap." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:rationale> "Maintains audit trail of document changes while ensuring users always access the most current file. Protects against accidental data loss from replacements." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "When a user replaces a document, the previous version is soft-deleted (or archived per category policy) and a new version record is created; the new document becomes the active version with an incremented version number. Maximum 10 versions per document." .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:Rule_FileSizeLimitEnforcement> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:BusinessRule> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:appliesTo> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:DocumentAggregate> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:CapabilityDoc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:enforcedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:DocumentAggregate> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:example> "Category configured with 50 MB limit; user attempts to upload a 75 MB PDF; system rejects with 400 Bad Request before blob upload." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:rationale> "Ensures malware scan performance, prevents storage abuse, and aligns with practical document needs." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "Documents cannot exceed the category-specific file size limit. Maximum configurable limit is 500 MB across all categories. Uploads exceeding the limit are rejected before SAS token generation." .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:Rule_MalwareScanBlocking> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:BusinessRule> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:appliesTo> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:DocumentAggregate> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:CapabilityDoc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:enforcedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:DocumentAggregate> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:example> "Azure Defender detects an embedded macro in transcript.pdf with suspicious behavior; system returns MalwareScanResult.Infected with threat type 'Macro.Trojan'; upload fails, document not saved; user notified; security team alerted via DocumentMalwareDetected." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:rationale> "Prevents introduction of ransomware, viruses, or spyware into the system, protecting data integrity and system security. No fallback scanner ensures consistent security posture." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "Documents detected as malware-infected during upload scanning must be blocked from storage and user access; the upload transaction fails and the user is notified. If malware scanning is unavailable, ALL uploads are blocked." .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:Rule_OriginalFilenamePreservation> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:BusinessRule> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:appliesTo> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:DocumentAggregate> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:CapabilityDoc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:enforcedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:DocumentAggregate> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:example> "User uploads John_Doe_Official_Transcript_2025.pdf; blob is stored under a UUID-based path; the UI and downloads still show the original filename." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:rationale> "Enables users to identify documents by their original names in UI, supports audit trails, and allows downloads to use recognizable filenames." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "The original filename uploaded by the user is stored in document metadata, even if the blob is renamed using UUIDs or standardized naming conventions in storage." .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:Rule_RetentionPeriodEnforcement> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:BusinessRule> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:appliesTo> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:DocumentAggregate> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:CapabilityDoc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:enforcedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:BatchJob_HardDeleteProcessing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:example> "Document uploaded Jan 1 2026 with 7-year retention (expiry Jan 1 2033); soft-deleted Mar 15 2026; nightly hard-delete job leaves it alone until Jan 2 2033, and even then only if no legal hold is active." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:rationale> "Ensures compliance with Michigan state records retention schedules and protects against premature deletion of legally required documentation." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "Documents cannot be hard-deleted until their retention period has expired, calculated from upload date plus category-specific retention years/days. Legal holds override retention expiry." .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:Rule_SoftDeleteHardDeleteSeparation> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:BusinessRule> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:appliesTo> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:DocumentAggregate> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:CapabilityDoc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:enforcedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:BatchJob_HardDeleteProcessing> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:enforcedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:DocumentAggregate> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:example> "User soft-deletes a document Jan 1 2026 (90-day retention); nightly job hard-deletes it Apr 2 2026 once no legal hold is active; hard-deleted documents cannot be recovered." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:rationale> "Protects against accidental permanent data loss, ensures compliance with retention schedules, and provides a recovery window for deleted documents." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "Soft delete is a user-facing action that marks a document as inaccessible. Hard delete is a system-automated process that permanently removes blobs after retention/legal hold clearance. Users never directly trigger hard delete." .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:SecurityConfiguration> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:ValueObject> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:description> "Encryption requirements, access control defaults, malware scan settings." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:name> "SecurityConfiguration" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:Seq_AdministratorRequestsRetentionOverride> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Sequence> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:belongsToContext> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:DocumentsContext> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:content> "sequenceDiagram\n    actor DocAdmin as Document Admin\n    actor BusinessOwner as Business Owner\n    participant UI\n    participant DocsAPI as Documents API\n    participant MetadataDB as SQL Metadata DB\n    participant EventBus\n    participant NotificationService as Notifications\n\n    Note over DocAdmin,UI: REQUEST OVERRIDE\n    DocAdmin->>UI: Select documents blocked by retention\n    DocAdmin->>UI: Click \"Request Deletion Override\"\n    UI->>DocsAPI: POST /api/documents/override-requests\n    Note over UI,DocsAPI: {document_ids[], justification,<br/>urgency, business_reason}\n\n    DocsAPI->>DocsAPI: Validate: user has documents.retention.override.request\n    DocsAPI->>DocsAPI: Determine approval requirements\n    Note over DocsAPI: High-value docs (legal hold history,<br/>>5 years retention) = dual approval<br/>Standard = single approval\n\n    DocsAPI->>MetadataDB: Create OverrideRequest\n    Note over MetadataDB: {status: Pending, requested_by,<br/>document_ids[], approval_count_required,<br/>justification, expires_at: NOW() + 7 days}\n    MetadataDB-->>DocsAPI: request_id\n\n    DocsAPI--)EventBus: OverrideRequestCreated\n    DocsAPI->>NotificationService: Notify Business Owner(s)\n    NotificationService-->>BusinessOwner: Email: \"Override request pending review\"\n\n    DocsAPI-->>UI: 200 OK {request_id}\n    UI-->>DocAdmin: \"Override request submitted, awaiting approval\"\n\n    Note over BusinessOwner,UI: APPROVE OVERRIDE\n    BusinessOwner->>UI: Review override request\n    UI->>DocsAPI: GET /api/documents/override-requests/{request_id}\n    DocsAPI->>MetadataDB: Get OverrideRequest with documents\n    MetadataDB-->>DocsAPI: Request details\n    DocsAPI-->>UI: Request + document list + retention info\n\n    BusinessOwner->>UI: Review justification, click \"Approve\"\n    UI->>DocsAPI: POST /api/documents/override-requests/{request_id}/approve\n    Note over UI,DocsAPI: {approval_comments}\n\n    DocsAPI->>DocsAPI: Validate: user has documents.retention.override.approve\n\n    DocsAPI->>MetadataDB: Create OverrideApproval\n    Note over MetadataDB: {request_id, approved_by, approved_at,<br/>comments}\n\n    DocsAPI->>MetadataDB: Update OverrideRequest\n    Note over MetadataDB: approval_count += 1\n\n    alt Sufficient approvals received\n        DocsAPI->>MetadataDB: Update OverrideRequest\n        Note over MetadataDB: status: Approved\n        DocsAPI--)EventBus: OverrideRequestApproved\n        DocsAPI->>NotificationService: Notify requester\n        NotificationService-->>DocAdmin: Email: \"Override approved, execute within 7 days\"\n    else More approvals needed (dual approval)\n        DocsAPI->>NotificationService: Notify second approver\n        Note over DocsAPI: Awaiting second approval\n    end\n\n    DocsAPI-->>UI: 200 OK\n    UI-->>BusinessOwner: \"Override approved\"\n\n    Note over DocAdmin,UI: EXECUTE OVERRIDE (Within 7 days)\n    DocAdmin->>UI: View approved override, click \"Execute\"\n    UI->>DocsAPI: POST /api/documents/override-requests/{request_id}/execute\n\n    DocsAPI->>MetadataDB: Get OverrideRequest\n    MetadataDB-->>DocsAPI: {status: Approved, document_ids[], expires_at}\n\n    DocsAPI->>DocsAPI: Validate: not expired (< 7 days since approval)\n\n    loop For each document_id\n        DocsAPI->>MetadataDB: Force soft delete (bypass retention check)\n        Note over MetadataDB: soft_deleted = true<br/>deletion_override_request_id = request_id\n        DocsAPI--)EventBus: DocumentSoftDeleted {override: true}\n    end\n\n    DocsAPI->>MetadataDB: Update OverrideRequest\n    Note over MetadataDB: status: Executed, executed_at, executed_by\n\n    DocsAPI--)EventBus: OverrideRequestExecuted\n    DocsAPI-->>UI: 200 OK\n    UI-->>DocAdmin: \"Override executed, documents deleted\"\n" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:SequencesDoc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:errorScenarios> "Override expired (>7 days) -> 400 Bad Request 'Override expired, request new approval'. Insufficient approvals -> 403 Forbidden 'Awaiting second approval'. Request already executed -> 409 Conflict 'Override already executed'. Approver is same as requester -> 403 Forbidden 'Cannot approve own request'." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:eventsPublished> "OverrideRequestCreated - Admin submits request. OverrideRequestApproved - Business owner approves. OverrideRequestExecuted - Admin executes deletion. DocumentSoftDeleted - Per document, flagged as override deletion." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:initiatedBy> "user" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:keyDecisions> "Dual approval for high-value: documents with legal hold history or >5 year retention require 2 approvals. 7-day execution window: approved overrides expire if not executed within 7 days. Justification mandatory: all overrides require a business reason for audit trail. Cannot be reversed: once executed, deletion is permanent (standard retention applies to hard delete)." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "confirmed" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Administrator Requests Retention Override" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:whatWhenWho> "What: Admin requests exception to retention policy, business owner approves. When: Need to delete documents before retention expiry (e.g., GDPR request, legal mandate, storage emergency). Who: Document Administrator (requestor), Business Owner (approver)." .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:Seq_BulkDocumentSoftDeleteWithValidation> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Sequence> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:belongsToContext> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:DocumentsContext> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:content> "sequenceDiagram\n    actor Admin\n    participant UI\n    participant DocsAPI as Documents API\n    participant MetadataDB as SQL Metadata DB\n    participant EventBus\n\n    Admin->>UI: Select multiple documents, click \"Delete Selected\"\n    UI->>DocsAPI: POST /api/documents/bulk-delete\n    Note over UI,DocsAPI: {document_ids[], mode: permissive}\n\n    DocsAPI->>DocsAPI: Validate: user has documents.document.bulk-delete\n\n    Note over DocsAPI: Pre-validation phase\n    DocsAPI->>MetadataDB: Query documents\n    MetadataDB-->>DocsAPI: Document list with retention/legal hold status\n\n    DocsAPI->>DocsAPI: Validate retention and legal holds\n    Note over DocsAPI: Separate into:<br/>- Eligible (no restrictions)<br/>- Ineligible (legal hold or retention not expired)\n\n    alt Strict mode AND any ineligible\n        DocsAPI-->>UI: 400 Bad Request\n        Note over UI: \"Cannot delete: 2 documents have legal holds\"\n        UI-->>Admin: Error message with ineligible document list\n    else Permissive mode (default)\n        DocsAPI->>MetadataDB: Create BulkOperation\n        Note over MetadataDB: {operation_type: delete, status: In Progress,<br/>total_count, eligible_count, ineligible_count}\n        MetadataDB-->>DocsAPI: operation_id\n\n        loop For each eligible document\n            DocsAPI->>MetadataDB: Update Document\n            Note over MetadataDB: soft_deleted = true<br/>soft_deleted_at = NOW()<br/>soft_deleted_by_user_id = admin_id\n\n            DocsAPI->>MetadataDB: Create BulkOperationItem\n            Note over MetadataDB: {document_id, status: Succeeded}\n\n            DocsAPI--)EventBus: DocumentSoftDeleted\n        end\n\n        loop For each ineligible document\n            DocsAPI->>MetadataDB: Create BulkOperationItem\n            Note over MetadataDB: {document_id, status: Skipped,<br/>skip_reason: legal hold or retention}\n        end\n\n        DocsAPI->>MetadataDB: Update BulkOperation\n        Note over MetadataDB: status: Completed or Partially Failed<br/>succeeded_count, skipped_count\n\n        DocsAPI--)EventBus: BulkOperationCompleted\n        DocsAPI-->>UI: 200 OK {operation_id, succeeded, skipped}\n        UI-->>Admin: \"98 documents deleted, 2 skipped (legal hold)\"\n    end\n" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:SequencesDoc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:errorScenarios> "All documents have legal holds -> Operation status Failed (0 succeeded). User lacks scope permission -> 403 Forbidden. Strict mode with ineligible docs -> 400 Bad Request, operation blocked." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:eventsPublished> "DocumentSoftDeleted - Per successfully deleted document. BulkOperationCompleted - Summary with skipped count." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:initiatedBy> "user" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:keyDecisions> "Pre-validation required: check all retention/legal hold before starting. Permissive mode default: skip ineligible documents, delete eligible ones. Strict mode optional: admin can require all-or-nothing deletion." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "confirmed" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Bulk Document Soft Delete with Validation" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:whatWhenWho> "What: Administrator marks multiple documents for soft delete, system validates retention policies. When: Cleanup of obsolete documents, removing test data, or bulk document management. Who: Document Administrator, District Admin (scoped to their documents)." .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:Seq_BulkDocumentUpload> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Sequence> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:belongsToContext> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:DocumentsContext> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:content> "sequenceDiagram\n    actor Admin\n    participant UI\n    participant DocsAPI as Documents API\n    participant MetadataDB as SQL Metadata DB\n    participant BlobStorage as Azure Blob Storage\n    participant Defender as Azure Defender\n    participant EventGrid\n    participant BulkProcessor as Bulk Processor (async)\n    participant EventBus\n\n    Admin->>UI: Select multiple files, click \"Upload All\"\n    Note over UI,DocsAPI: Bulk vs. single upload is a UX distinction only.<br/>Authorization is governed by the same source domain permission<br/>that controls single uploads for this context.\n    UI->>DocsAPI: POST /api/documents/bulk-upload/request\n    Note over UI,DocsAPI: {files: [{filename, size, mime_type}],<br/>category, attachment_type, attachment_id}\n\n    DocsAPI->>DocsAPI: Validate: all files match allowable formats\n    DocsAPI->>DocsAPI: Validate: all files within size limits\n\n    DocsAPI->>MetadataDB: Create BulkOperation\n    Note over MetadataDB: {operation_type: upload, status: Queued,<br/>total_count: file count,<br/>initiated_by_user_id}\n    MetadataDB-->>DocsAPI: operation_id\n\n    loop For each file\n        DocsAPI->>DocsAPI: Generate document_id, build blob path\n        DocsAPI->>MetadataDB: Create Document (status: Scanning)\n        DocsAPI->>MetadataDB: Create BulkOperationItem\n        Note over MetadataDB: {operation_id, document_id, filename, status: Queued}\n        DocsAPI->>BlobStorage: Generate upload SAS token\n    end\n\n    DocsAPI-->>UI: 200 OK {operation_id, upload_urls[]}\n    UI-->>Admin: \"Upload started, processing X files...\"\n\n    loop For each file (parallel, max 10 concurrent)\n        UI->>BlobStorage: Upload file via SAS token\n        BlobStorage-->>UI: Upload complete\n\n        Defender->>BlobStorage: Scan blob in-place\n        Defender--)EventGrid: MalwareScanningResult\n\n        alt Scan clean\n            EventGrid->>BulkProcessor: Webhook: Clean\n            BulkProcessor->>MetadataDB: Update Document status = Available\n            BulkProcessor->>MetadataDB: Update BulkOperationItem status = Succeeded\n            BulkProcessor--)EventBus: DocumentUploaded\n        else Scan infected or failed\n            EventGrid->>BulkProcessor: Webhook: Malware/Error\n            BulkProcessor->>BlobStorage: Delete blob\n            BulkProcessor->>MetadataDB: Update Document status = Infected/Scan Failed\n            BulkProcessor->>MetadataDB: Update BulkOperationItem\n            Note over MetadataDB: status: Failed<br/>error_message: scan result\n        end\n\n        BulkProcessor->>UI: Progress update (SSE/polling)\n        UI-->>Admin: \"12 of 50 files processed...\"\n    end\n\n    BulkProcessor->>MetadataDB: Update BulkOperation\n    Note over MetadataDB: status: Completed or Partially Failed<br/>succeeded_count, failed_count\n\n    BulkProcessor--)EventBus: BulkOperationCompleted\n    BulkProcessor->>UI: Completion notification\n    UI-->>Admin: \"Upload complete: 48 succeeded, 2 failed\"\n" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:SequencesDoc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:errorScenarios> "Malware detected in 1 file -> That file fails, others continue. All files fail scan -> Operation status Failed. User cancels mid-upload -> Operation status Cancelled, uploaded files remain." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:eventsPublished> "DocumentUploaded - Per successfully uploaded file. BulkOperationCompleted - Summary of entire operation." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:initiatedBy> "user" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:keyDecisions> "Browser-based bulk upload: each file gets its own SAS token, uploaded directly from browser. Scan in-place: files scanned in target containers (no quarantine). Parallel uploads: max 10 concurrent to avoid overwhelming scan service (2,000 files/min limit). Individual item tracking: each file has success/failure status. Partial success allowed: some files can fail without failing the entire operation." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "BulkProcessor is an internal async component distinct from DocsAPI in this diagram, but not separately modeled here — it doesn't correspond to a distinct sd:ApiOperation, matching how credentialing left its own unmodeled internal collaborators (BRM, etc.) out of SequenceReferences." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "confirmed" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Bulk Document Upload" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:whatWhenWho> "What: Administrator uploads multiple files simultaneously, system processes batch with malware scanning. When: District uploads employee roster CSV, EPP uploads candidate tracking file, Sponsor uploads attendee list. Who: District Admin, EPP Admin, Professional Learning Sponsor." .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:Seq_DocumentDownloadWithSasToken> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Sequence> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:belongsToContext> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:DocumentsContext> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:content> "sequenceDiagram\n    actor User\n    participant UI\n    participant DocsAPI as Documents API\n    participant MetadataDB as SQL Metadata DB\n    participant BlobStorage as Azure Blob Storage\n    participant EventBus\n\n    Note over UI,DocsAPI: Caller has already verified the user may access<br/>this document. Documents does not re-check business authorization.\n\n    User->>UI: Click \"View Document\"\n    UI->>DocsAPI: GET /api/documents/{document_id}/download\n\n    DocsAPI->>MetadataDB: Get Document metadata\n    MetadataDB-->>DocsAPI: {blob_path, status, original_filename}\n\n    alt Document not available\n        DocsAPI-->>UI: 404 Not Found OR 410 Gone (if soft-deleted)\n        UI-->>User: \"Document not available\"\n    else Document still scanning\n        DocsAPI-->>UI: 202 Accepted {status: Scanning}\n        UI-->>User: \"Document is being processed, please try again shortly\"\n    else Document available\n        DocsAPI->>BlobStorage: Generate download SAS token (read-only, 15 min)\n        BlobStorage-->>DocsAPI: SAS URL\n\n        DocsAPI->>MetadataDB: Log access\n        Note over MetadataDB: DocumentAccessLog:<br/>{document_id, user_id, action: view, timestamp}\n\n        DocsAPI--)EventBus: DocumentViewed\n\n        DocsAPI-->>UI: 200 OK {sas_url, original_filename}\n        UI->>BlobStorage: Direct download via SAS URL\n        BlobStorage-->>UI: Blob content\n        UI-->>User: Browser downloads file as original_filename\n    end\n" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:SequencesDoc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:errorScenarios> "Document soft-deleted -> 410 Gone. Document still scanning -> 202 Accepted (try again). SAS token expired -> UI requests new token." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:eventsPublished> "DocumentViewed - Track document access for analytics." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:initiatedBy> "user" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:keyDecisions> "Direct blob access: UI downloads directly from blob storage using SAS token (no proxy through API). Time-limited tokens: 15-minute expiry prevents URL sharing. Access logging: all views logged for compliance audit. Status check: prevent download while still scanning." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Caller has already verified the user may access this document; Documents does not re-check business authorization (matches Op_DownloadDocument's own x-permissions-required: [])." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "confirmed" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Document Download with SAS Token" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:whatWhenWho> "What: User requests document, system generates time-limited access URL. When: User views document from a credential application, a filtered pending-items list view, or document library. Who: Educator, District Staff, Administrator." .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:Seq_DocumentReplacementAndVersioning> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Sequence> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:belongsToContext> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:DocumentsContext> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:content> "sequenceDiagram\n    actor User\n    participant UI\n    participant DocsAPI as Documents API\n    participant MetadataDB as SQL Metadata DB\n    participant BlobStorage as Azure Blob Storage\n    participant ArchiveContainer as Archive Container\n    participant Defender as Azure Defender\n    participant EventGrid\n    participant EventBus\n\n    User->>UI: Upload new version of document\n    UI->>DocsAPI: POST /api/documents/{document_id}/replace/request\n    Note over UI,DocsAPI: {filename, size, mime_type}\n\n    DocsAPI->>MetadataDB: Get current Document\n    MetadataDB-->>DocsAPI: {current_version, blob_path, category}\n\n    DocsAPI->>DocsAPI: Validate: max 10 versions not exceeded\n    DocsAPI->>DocsAPI: Validate: document not soft-deleted\n\n    DocsAPI->>DocsAPI: Generate new document_id for version\n    DocsAPI->>DocsAPI: Increment version number (e.g., 1.0 -> 2.0)\n\n    Note over DocsAPI: Archive old version\n    DocsAPI->>BlobStorage: Read current blob\n    BlobStorage-->>DocsAPI: Blob content\n    DocsAPI->>ArchiveContainer: Copy to archive\n    Note over ArchiveContainer: document-versions/{original_doc_id}/v1.0\n\n    DocsAPI->>MetadataDB: Create DocumentVersion record\n    Note over MetadataDB: {original_document_id, version: 1.0,<br/>archived_blob_path, replaced_at}\n\n    DocsAPI->>MetadataDB: Update original Document\n    Note over MetadataDB: current_version = false<br/>soft_deleted = true<br/>replaced_by_version_id = new_doc_id\n\n    Note over DocsAPI: Upload new version (follows standard upload flow)\n    DocsAPI->>DocsAPI: Build new blob path\n    DocsAPI->>MetadataDB: Create new Document record\n    Note over MetadataDB: {document_id: new_doc_id, version: 2.0,<br/>replaces_version_id: original_doc_id,<br/>status: Scanning}\n\n    DocsAPI->>BlobStorage: Generate upload SAS token\n    BlobStorage-->>DocsAPI: SAS URL\n\n    DocsAPI-->>UI: 200 OK {new_document_id, upload_url, version: 2.0}\n\n    UI->>BlobStorage: Upload new file via SAS\n    BlobStorage-->>UI: Upload complete\n\n    Note over Defender: Scan new version in-place\n    Defender->>BlobStorage: Scan blob\n    Defender--)EventGrid: MalwareScanningResult\n\n    alt Clean scan\n        EventGrid->>DocsAPI: Webhook: Clean\n        DocsAPI->>MetadataDB: Update new Document status = Available\n        DocsAPI--)EventBus: DocumentReplaced\n        DocsAPI->>UI: Notification\n        UI-->>User: \"Document updated successfully\"\n    else Malware detected\n        EventGrid->>DocsAPI: Webhook: Malware\n        DocsAPI->>BlobStorage: Delete infected blob\n        DocsAPI->>MetadataDB: Update new Document status = Infected\n        DocsAPI->>UI: Notification\n        UI-->>User: \"Replacement file rejected - original version remains\"\n        Note over DocsAPI: Original version restored as current\n    end\n" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:SequencesDoc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:errorScenarios> "Max 10 versions exceeded -> 400 Bad Request 'Maximum versions reached'. Document soft-deleted -> 400 Bad Request 'Restore document before replacing'. New file infected -> Upload fails, old version remains current." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:eventsPublished> "DocumentReplaced - Includes old and new document IDs (only if new version scan clean)." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:initiatedBy> "user" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:keyDecisions> "New document ID for new version: each version is a separate Document record. Archive old version: old blob moved to archive container, not deleted. Version numbering: incremental (1.0, 2.0, 3.0) for simplicity. Malware scan new version: replacement goes through the full scan-in-place workflow. Rollback on failure: if the new version fails scan, the old version remains current." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "confirmed" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Document Replacement and Versioning" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:whatWhenWho> "What: User replaces existing document, old version archived. When: User uploads wrong file or needs to update a supporting document. Who: Educator (own documents), Administrator (any document in scope)." .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:Seq_DocumentUploadWithMalwareScanning> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Sequence> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:belongsToContext> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:DocumentsContext> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:content> "sequenceDiagram\n    actor User\n    participant UI\n    participant DocsAPI as Documents API\n    participant BlobStorage as Azure Blob Storage\n    participant Defender as Azure Defender\n    participant EventGrid\n    participant MetadataDB as SQL Metadata DB\n    participant EventBus\n\n    User->>UI: Select file for upload\n    UI->>DocsAPI: POST /api/documents/upload/request\n    Note over UI,DocsAPI: {filename, size, mime_type, category, attachment_type, attachment_id}\n\n    Note over DocsAPI: Calling domain has already authorized this action.<br/>Documents validates technical constraints only.\n    DocsAPI->>DocsAPI: Validate file type against allowable formats\n    DocsAPI->>DocsAPI: Validate file size against category limit\n\n    DocsAPI->>DocsAPI: Generate document_id (UUID)\n    DocsAPI->>DocsAPI: Sanitize original filename\n    DocsAPI->>DocsAPI: Build blob path\n    Note over DocsAPI: documents-{category}/{year}/{month}/<br/>{attachment-type}/{attachment-id}/{doc-id}\n\n    DocsAPI->>MetadataDB: Create Document record\n    Note over MetadataDB: Status: Scanning<br/>blob_path, original_filename\n    MetadataDB-->>DocsAPI: document_id\n\n    DocsAPI->>BlobStorage: Generate upload SAS token (write-only, 15 min)\n    BlobStorage-->>DocsAPI: SAS URL\n\n    DocsAPI-->>UI: 200 OK {document_id, upload_url, status: Scanning}\n\n    UI->>BlobStorage: Upload file directly to blob storage via SAS\n    BlobStorage-->>UI: Upload complete\n    UI-->>User: \"File uploaded, scanning for malware...\"\n\n    Note over Defender: Azure Defender detects blob upload<br/>and scans in-place\n    Defender->>BlobStorage: Scan blob for malware\n    Defender->>BlobStorage: Write blob index tags\n\n    alt Clean Scan Result\n        Defender--)EventGrid: MalwareScanningResult {scanResultType: \"No threats found\"}\n        EventGrid->>DocsAPI: Webhook: /api/webhooks/defender-scan-result\n\n        DocsAPI->>MetadataDB: Update Document\n        Note over MetadataDB: Status: Available\n\n        DocsAPI--)EventBus: DocumentUploaded\n        DocsAPI->>UI: Notification (SSE/webhook)\n        UI-->>User: \"File uploaded successfully\"\n\n    else Malware Detected\n        Defender--)EventGrid: MalwareScanningResult {scanResultType: \"Malicious\", threatName}\n        EventGrid->>DocsAPI: Webhook: Malware detected\n\n        DocsAPI->>BlobStorage: Delete infected blob\n\n        DocsAPI->>MetadataDB: Update Document\n        Note over MetadataDB: Status: Infected<br/>threat_details\n\n        DocsAPI--)EventBus: DocumentMalwareDetected\n        DocsAPI->>UI: Notification (SSE/webhook)\n        UI-->>User: \"File rejected due to security concerns\"\n\n        Note over DocsAPI: Alert security team\n\n    else Scan Timeout/Failure\n        Note over DocsAPI: Background job detects no webhook<br/>received within 60 seconds\n\n        DocsAPI->>BlobStorage: Delete blob\n        DocsAPI->>MetadataDB: Update Document\n        Note over MetadataDB: Status: Scan Failed\n        DocsAPI->>UI: Notification (SSE/webhook)\n        UI-->>User: \"Upload failed, please try again\"\n    end\n" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:SequencesDoc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:errorScenarios> "Invalid file type -> 400 Bad Request, upload rejected before SAS generation. File size exceeds limit -> 400 Bad Request. Blob storage quota exceeded -> 503 Service Unavailable, alert admins. Scan timeout (>60 seconds) -> Mark as Scan Failed, delete blob." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:eventsPublished> "DocumentUploaded - Scan clean, document available. DocumentMalwareDetected - Malware found, security alert." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:initiatedBy> "user" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:keyDecisions> "Browser-based upload: file uploaded directly from browser to blob storage via SAS token (no proxy through API). Scan in-place: Azure Defender scans blob in target container (no quarantine/copy required). Async notification: UI uses SSE or polling for scan result (don't block user during scan). Timeout handling: background job marks as Scan Failed if no webhook received within 60 seconds." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "confirmed" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Document Upload with Malware Scanning" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:whatWhenWho> "What: User uploads file, system scans for malware, stores if clean. When: User needs to attach a supporting document to a credential application, PPR disclosure, or other context. Who: Educator, District Staff, Administrator." .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:Seq_IntegrationPatternDomainApiCallingDocuments> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Sequence> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:belongsToContext> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:DocumentsContext> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:content> "sequenceDiagram\n    actor User\n    participant DomainUI as Domain UI (e.g. Credentialing)\n    participant DomainAPI as Domain API (e.g. Credentialing API)\n    participant DocsAPI as Documents API\n    participant BlobStorage as Azure Blob Storage\n\n    User->>DomainUI: Initiate upload (e.g. attach transcript to application)\n    DomainUI->>DomainAPI: Request upload token\n    Note over DomainUI,DomainAPI: Domain-specific request context\n\n    DomainAPI->>DomainAPI: Validate: user has [domain permission]\n    Note over DomainAPI: e.g. credentialing.application.submit<br/>This is the only authorization check for this upload.\n\n    DomainAPI->>DocsAPI: POST /api/documents/upload/request\n    Note over DomainAPI,DocsAPI: Authenticated service-to-service call (Managed Identity)<br/>{filename, size, mime_type, category, attachment_type, attachment_id}\n\n    DocsAPI->>DocsAPI: Validate file type and size against category limits\n    DocsAPI-->>DomainAPI: {document_id, upload_url}\n\n    DomainAPI-->>DomainUI: {document_id, upload_url}\n    DomainUI->>BlobStorage: Upload file via SAS token\n" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:SequencesDoc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:errorScenarios> "Domain API authorization fails -> Domain API returns 403 to UI; Documents is never called. File type not in category allowlist -> Documents returns 400 to domain API; domain API surfaces error to UI. File size exceeds category limit -> Documents returns 400 to domain API; domain API surfaces error to UI. Managed Identity auth failure -> Documents returns 401; domain API should alert on this as it indicates a misconfiguration, not a user error." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:eventsPublished> "None — this diagram represents the handoff into Documents; see the per-flow sequences below for what Documents itself publishes." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:initiatedBy> "user" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:keyDecisions> "Single authorization check: the domain API is the only place business authorization is enforced; Documents trusts authenticated internal callers. Service-to-service auth: Domain APIs call Documents using Managed Identity; Documents does not accept direct unauthenticated calls from browsers. Technical validation only: Documents enforces file size, format, and category rules, not business rules about who may upload what. Bulk vs. single is a UX concern only: no separate permission for bulk uploads." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "documents-sequences.md calls this out as THE canonical integration pattern for all upload/download flows: 'The sequences that follow ... are Documents-internal views of what happens after this handoff.'" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "confirmed" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Integration Pattern: Domain API Calling Documents" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:whatWhenWho> "What: A domain API authorizes an upload or download action, then delegates file mechanics to the Documents API. When: Any time a domain feature requires a user to attach, retrieve, or manage a file. Who: Any domain API acting on behalf of an authenticated user (Credentialing, Staffing, Professional Learning, EPP, Audit)." .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:Seq_LegalHoldApplicationAndRelease> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Sequence> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:belongsToContext> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:DocumentsContext> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:content> "sequenceDiagram\n    actor LegalCounsel as Legal Counsel\n    participant UI\n    participant DocsAPI as Documents API\n    participant MetadataDB as SQL Metadata DB\n    participant EventBus\n\n    Note over LegalCounsel,UI: APPLY LEGAL HOLD\n    LegalCounsel->>UI: Search documents for case\n    UI->>DocsAPI: GET /api/documents/search?attachment=application-12345\n    DocsAPI->>MetadataDB: Query documents\n    MetadataDB-->>DocsAPI: List of documents\n    DocsAPI-->>UI: Document list\n\n    LegalCounsel->>UI: Select documents, \"Apply Legal Hold\"\n    UI->>DocsAPI: POST /api/documents/legal-hold/apply\n    Note over UI,DocsAPI: {document_ids[], justification,<br/>case_number, hold_reason}\n\n    DocsAPI->>DocsAPI: Validate: user has documents.legal-hold.apply\n\n    loop For each document_id\n        DocsAPI->>MetadataDB: Update Document\n        Note over MetadataDB: legal_hold = true<br/>legal_hold_applied_at = NOW()<br/>legal_hold_applied_by = user_id<br/>legal_hold_justification = text<br/>legal_hold_case_number = case_number\n\n        DocsAPI--)EventBus: LegalHoldApplied\n    end\n\n    DocsAPI-->>UI: 200 OK {applied_count}\n    UI-->>LegalCounsel: \"Legal hold applied to X documents\"\n\n    Note over MetadataDB: Documents cannot be hard-deleted<br/>even if retention period expires\n\n    Note over LegalCounsel,UI: RELEASE LEGAL HOLD (Later)\n    LegalCounsel->>UI: View legal hold documents\n    LegalCounsel->>UI: Select documents, \"Release Legal Hold\"\n    UI->>DocsAPI: POST /api/documents/legal-hold/release\n    Note over UI,DocsAPI: {document_ids[], release_reason,<br/>case_closure_date}\n\n    DocsAPI->>DocsAPI: Validate: user has documents.legal-hold.release\n\n    loop For each document_id\n        DocsAPI->>MetadataDB: Update Document\n        Note over MetadataDB: legal_hold = false<br/>legal_hold_released_at = NOW()<br/>legal_hold_released_by = user_id<br/>legal_hold_release_reason = text\n\n        DocsAPI--)EventBus: LegalHoldReleased\n\n        alt Document was soft-deleted\n            Note over DocsAPI: Document now eligible for hard delete<br/>if retention period expired\n        end\n    end\n\n    DocsAPI-->>UI: 200 OK {released_count}\n    UI-->>LegalCounsel: \"Legal hold released for X documents\"\n" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:SequencesDoc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:errorScenarios> "Non-legal user attempts hold -> 403 Forbidden. Release without justification -> 400 Bad Request 'Release reason required'." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:eventsPublished> "LegalHoldApplied - Per document, includes case number. LegalHoldReleased - Per document, includes release reason." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:initiatedBy> "user" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:keyDecisions> "Legal hold overrides retention: documents with hold cannot be hard-deleted regardless of age. Justification required: must include case number and reason for audit trail. Release doesn't delete: releasing hold allows retention policy to resume, but doesn't immediately delete." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "confirmed" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Legal Hold Application and Release" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:whatWhenWho> "What: Administrator applies legal hold preventing deletion, later releases after the legal matter concludes. When: Litigation, investigation, or audit requires document preservation. Who: Legal Counsel, Compliance Officer." .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:Seq_SoftDeleteAndHardDeleteLifecycle> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Sequence> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:belongsToContext> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:DocumentsContext> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:content> "sequenceDiagram\n    actor User\n    participant UI\n    participant DocsAPI as Documents API\n    participant MetadataDB as SQL Metadata DB\n    participant EventBus\n    participant HardDeleteJob as Hard Delete Job (nightly)\n    participant BlobStorage as Azure Blob Storage\n\n    Note over User,UI: SOFT DELETE (User-Initiated)\n    User->>UI: Click \"Delete Document\"\n    UI->>DocsAPI: DELETE /api/documents/{document_id}\n\n    DocsAPI->>MetadataDB: Get Document\n    MetadataDB-->>DocsAPI: {status, retention_expiry_date, legal_hold}\n\n    DocsAPI->>MetadataDB: Update Document\n    Note over MetadataDB: soft_deleted = true<br/>soft_deleted_at = NOW()<br/>soft_deleted_by_user_id = user_id<br/>Status: Soft Deleted\n\n    DocsAPI--)EventBus: DocumentSoftDeleted\n    DocsAPI-->>UI: 200 OK\n    UI-->>User: \"Document deleted\"\n\n    Note over MetadataDB: Document hidden from user queries<br/>but blob remains in storage\n\n    Note over HardDeleteJob: HARD DELETE (System-Automated)\n    loop Nightly at 2:00 AM EST\n        HardDeleteJob->>MetadataDB: Query eligible documents\n        Note over MetadataDB: WHERE soft_deleted = true<br/>AND soft_deleted_at + retention_days < NOW()<br/>AND legal_hold = false\n        MetadataDB-->>HardDeleteJob: List of eligible documents\n\n        loop For each document (batch 100)\n            HardDeleteJob->>BlobStorage: Delete blob\n            BlobStorage-->>HardDeleteJob: Success\n\n            HardDeleteJob->>MetadataDB: Update Document\n            Note over MetadataDB: hard_deleted = true<br/>hard_deleted_at = NOW()<br/>Status: Hard Deleted<br/>(metadata retained, blob removed)\n\n            HardDeleteJob--)EventBus: DocumentHardDeleted\n        end\n\n        HardDeleteJob->>HardDeleteJob: Generate summary report\n        Note over HardDeleteJob: Total evaluated, deleted,<br/>skipped (legal hold), errors\n    end\n" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:SequencesDoc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:errorScenarios> "User tries to delete document with legal hold -> 403 Forbidden 'Document has active legal hold'. Hard delete blob fails -> Retry next night (max 3 attempts), alert admin after 3 failures." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:eventsPublished> "DocumentSoftDeleted - User deletes document. DocumentHardDeleted - Blob permanently removed (nightly job)." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:initiatedBy> "user" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:keyDecisions> "Soft delete is immediate: user action hides document instantly. Hard delete is automated: no user permission to force hard delete. Metadata preserved: even after hard delete, metadata remains for audit." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "The nightly hard-delete portion of this sequence corresponds to docs:BatchJob_HardDeleteProcessing in documents-technical-design.ttl (not modeled as a SequenceReference here — BatchJob isn't an sd:ApiOperation or sd:DomainEvent target). This sequence's own sd:initiatedBy is 'user' reflecting its primary What/When/Who (the user-initiated soft delete); the automated hard-delete half has its own 'internal-system' sd:initiatedBy on the BatchJob itself." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "confirmed" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Soft Delete and Hard Delete Lifecycle" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:whatWhenWho> "What: User deletes document, system soft-deletes immediately, hard-deletes after retention period. When: User removes incorrect upload or document no longer needed. Who: Educator (own documents), Administrator (any document in scope) for soft delete; the system (nightly job) for hard delete." .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:Seq_StagedFileUploadForSynapseProcessing> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Sequence> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:belongsToContext> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:DocumentsContext> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:content> "sequenceDiagram\n    actor Admin\n    participant UI\n    participant DocsAPI as Documents API\n    participant BlobStorage as Staging Container\n    participant Defender as Azure Defender\n    participant EventGrid\n    participant MetadataDB as SQL Metadata DB\n    participant EventBus\n    participant Synapse as Azure Synapse\n    participant DataWarehouse as Data Warehouse\n\n    Admin->>UI: Upload bulk import file (CSV/XLSX)\n    UI->>DocsAPI: POST /api/documents/staging/upload/request\n    Note over UI,DocsAPI: {filename, size, mime_type,<br/>functional_area: staffing,<br/>import_type: employee_roster}\n\n    DocsAPI->>DocsAPI: Validate: file format (CSV, XLSX only)\n    DocsAPI->>DocsAPI: Validate: file size (max 500 MB)\n\n    DocsAPI->>DocsAPI: Generate upload_id\n    DocsAPI->>DocsAPI: Build staging path\n    Note over DocsAPI: documents-bulk-import-staging-staffing/<br/>{upload_id}_{timestamp}_{filename}\n\n    DocsAPI->>MetadataDB: Create StagingFile record\n    Note over MetadataDB: {upload_id, blob_path, functional_area,<br/>import_type, status: Scanning,<br/>uploaded_by, uploaded_at}\n\n    DocsAPI->>BlobStorage: Generate upload SAS token\n    BlobStorage-->>DocsAPI: SAS URL\n\n    DocsAPI-->>UI: 200 OK {upload_id, upload_url, status: Scanning}\n\n    UI->>BlobStorage: Upload file via SAS token\n    BlobStorage-->>UI: Upload complete\n    UI-->>Admin: \"File uploaded, scanning...\"\n\n    Note over Defender: Scan staging file in-place\n    Defender->>BlobStorage: Scan blob for malware\n    Defender--)EventGrid: MalwareScanningResult\n\n    alt Scan clean\n        EventGrid->>DocsAPI: Webhook: Clean\n        DocsAPI->>MetadataDB: Update StagingFile status = Uploaded\n        DocsAPI--)EventBus: BulkFileUploaded\n        Note over EventBus: {upload_id, functional_area,<br/>import_type, blob_path}\n        DocsAPI->>UI: Notification\n        UI-->>Admin: \"File uploaded, processing will begin shortly\"\n\n        Note over Synapse: Synapse subscribes to BulkFileUploaded\n        EventBus->>Synapse: BulkFileUploaded event\n\n        Synapse->>Synapse: Trigger appropriate pipeline\n        Note over Synapse: Based on functional_area + import_type\n\n        Synapse->>BlobStorage: Read file (using Managed Identity)\n        BlobStorage-->>Synapse: File content\n\n        Synapse->>Synapse: Parse and validate data\n\n        alt Processing successful\n            Synapse->>DataWarehouse: Insert/update records\n            Synapse--)EventBus: BulkFileProcessed\n            Note over EventBus: {upload_id, status: Success,<br/>records_processed}\n\n            EventBus->>DocsAPI: BulkFileProcessed event\n            DocsAPI->>MetadataDB: Update StagingFile\n            Note over MetadataDB: status: Processed,<br/>processed_at, records_count\n\n            DocsAPI->>UI: Notification (webhook/SSE)\n            UI-->>Admin: \"Import complete: 150 records processed\"\n\n        else Processing failed\n            Synapse--)EventBus: BulkFileProcessed\n            Note over EventBus: {upload_id, status: Failed,<br/>error_details}\n\n            EventBus->>DocsAPI: BulkFileProcessed event\n            DocsAPI->>MetadataDB: Update StagingFile\n            Note over MetadataDB: status: Failed,<br/>error_message\n\n            DocsAPI->>UI: Notification\n            UI-->>Admin: \"Import failed: invalid data format on row 23\"\n        end\n    else Scan infected/failed\n        EventGrid->>DocsAPI: Webhook: Malware/Error\n        DocsAPI->>BlobStorage: Delete infected/failed blob\n        DocsAPI->>MetadataDB: Update StagingFile\n        Note over MetadataDB: status: Scan Failed / Infected\n        DocsAPI->>UI: Notification\n        UI-->>Admin: \"Upload failed due to security concerns\"\n    end\n\n    Note over BlobStorage: Auto-cleanup after 7 days\n    loop Daily cleanup job\n        DocsAPI->>MetadataDB: Query old staging files\n        Note over MetadataDB: WHERE uploaded_at < NOW() - 7 days\n        MetadataDB-->>DocsAPI: Old file list\n\n        loop For each old file\n            DocsAPI->>BlobStorage: Delete blob\n            DocsAPI->>MetadataDB: Update StagingFile\n            Note over MetadataDB: blob_deleted: true\n        end\n    end\n" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:SequencesDoc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:errorScenarios> "Invalid file format -> 400 Bad Request before upload. Malware detected -> File deleted, status Infected. Synapse pipeline failure -> Status Failed, file remains for retry. Synapse timeout (>30 min) -> Alert admins, file remains for manual investigation." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:eventsPublished> "BulkFileUploaded - File scanned clean, ready for processing. BulkFileProcessed - Synapse publishes after processing (consumed by Documents)." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:initiatedBy> "user" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:keyDecisions> "All staging files scanned: no exceptions for 'trusted internal sources'. Browser-based upload: file uploaded via SAS token directly to staging container. Scan in-place: Defender scans staging files where they sit. Event-driven decoupling: Documents domain doesn't know about Synapse pipelines. Synapse reads directly: Synapse uses Managed Identity to access staging containers. Auto-cleanup: files deleted after 7 days regardless of processing status." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "confirmed" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Staged File Upload for Synapse Processing" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:whatWhenWho> "What: User uploads bulk import file to staging area, Synapse pipeline processes. When: District uploads employee roster CSV, EPP uploads candidate enrollment file. Who: District Admin, EPP Admin." .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:SequencesDoc> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:SourceDocument> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:docType> "sequences" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:section> "abox-tests/mied/documents/documents-sequences.md" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:StagingFileAggregate> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Aggregate> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:CapabilityDoc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:description> "Tracks a bulk-import file (CSV/XLSX) staged for downstream Synapse pipeline processing, independent of the Document/BulkOperation lifecycle used for user-facing document management." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:emits> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:BulkFileUploadedEvent> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:hasState> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:StagingState_Failed> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:hasState> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:StagingState_Infected> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:hasState> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:StagingState_Processed> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:hasState> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:StagingState_Scanning> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:hasState> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:StagingState_Uploaded> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:invariants> "Staging files are scanned for malware with no exceptions, same as any other upload. Staged blobs are automatically deleted 7 days after upload regardless of processing status. A BulkFileUploaded event is published only on a clean scan, which is what triggers the downstream Synapse pipeline." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "functionalArea is constrained to {staffing, epp, proflearning} per documents-api.yml's uploadToStaging request schema." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:rootEntity> "StagingFile" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:StagingState_Failed> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:StateDefinition> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:isTerminal> true ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:name> "Failed" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:StagingState_Infected> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:StateDefinition> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:isTerminal> true ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:name> "Infected" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:StagingState_Processed> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:StateDefinition> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:isTerminal> true ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:name> "Processed" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:StagingState_Scanning> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:StateDefinition> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:isTerminal> false ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:name> "Scanning" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:StagingState_Uploaded> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:StateDefinition> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:isTerminal> false ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:name> "Uploaded" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:StoragePolicy> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:ValueObject> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:description> "Blob container naming, path structure, access tier defaults. Read-only, managed by infrastructure." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:name> "StoragePolicy" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:TP_AzureDefenderIntegration> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:TechnicalProcess> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:TechnicalDesignDoc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:implementationNotes> "Known platform limitations and mitigations: 2 GB Defender file-size cap (mitigated by the domain's own 50-500 MB category limits, always well under it); 2,000 files/min scan-rate limit per storage account (mitigated by throttling/queuing bulk uploads with progress indicators); 10,000 GB/month default scan cap (monitored at 75% threshold, alerts admins, blocks uploads if exceeded — scanning simply stops until next month if the cap is hit); service-unavailable (blocks ALL uploads per docs:Rule_MalwareScanBlocking, no fallback scanner, by design). Provisioning: Defender enabled at the Azure subscription level (Microsoft.Security/pricings, DefenderForStorageV2 subplan, OnUploadMalwareScanning extension with a configurable monthly GB cap) plus a dedicated Event Grid Custom Topic in the same region as the storage account, with 'Send scan results to Event Grid topic' and 'Override Defender for Storage subscription-level settings' both enabled so the application's webhook endpoint receives results directly." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:steps> "Automatic trigger on any blob upload to a protected storage account container; MDAV scan engine runs in-place (2-10 sec typical for <50 MB, 60 sec max timeout); result delivered via Event Grid webhook (must handle the Event Grid validation handshake on first subscription, tolerate duplicate deliveries, return 200 OK even on internal processing failure, and validate the webhook signature); result also written to blob index tags (Malware Scanning scan result / scan time) as a secondary, non-realtime channel used for compliance reporting and administrative filtering, not for the primary processing path. scanResultType values: 'No threats found' (mark Available), 'Malicious' (delete blob, mark Infected, alert security), 'Error' (delete blob, mark Scan Failed, notify user to retry), 'Not scanned' (exceeded scan cap / unsupported format / too large — delete blob, mark Scan Failed). A background job independently monitors documents stuck in Scanning status and marks them Scan Failed if no webhook arrives within 60 seconds, covering the case where Event Grid delivery itself fails." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Azure Defender for Storage Integration Mechanics" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:TP_BlobStorageAccessPatterns> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:TechnicalProcess> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:TechnicalDesignDoc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:enforcedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:DocumentAggregate> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:implementationNotes> "Container naming: documents-{category-slug} (e.g. documents-credential-supporting-docs). Blob path structure: {year}/{month}/{attachment-type}/{attachment-id}/{document-id}_{sanitized-filename}, with year/month in UTC for timezone independence. Authentication via Managed Identity only — no storage account keys in application configuration. SAS tokens are read-only and 15-minute expiry for downloads. Error handling: upload retries use exponential backoff up to 3 attempts; quota-exceeded conditions alert admins and block new uploads; capacity/transaction-count/egress-bandwidth metrics are monitored continuously." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:steps> "Upload: browser requests upload -> API validates and creates metadata with status=Scanning -> API generates a write-only SAS token -> browser uploads directly to the target container -> API receives the Defender webhook -> API updates status. Download: browser requests download -> API checks status=Available in SQL -> API generates a read-only SAS token (15 min expiry) -> browser downloads directly from blob storage. Delete: mark soft delete in SQL immediately -> nightly job hard-deletes the blob after the retention period expires (see docs:BatchJob_HardDeleteProcessing)." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Azure Blob Storage Access Patterns" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:TP_DmzQuarantinePattern> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:TechnicalProcess> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:TechnicalDesignDoc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:implementationNotes> "Alternative NOT adopted as the primary pattern — documented for regulatory contexts requiring infected files never exist in production storage, or multi-tenant isolation needs. Adds a blob-copy operation (~$0.004 per 10,000 copies) and ~1-2 seconds of latency versus the scan-in-place pattern actually implemented." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:steps> "1) API uploads to a quarantine container (not production). 2) Metadata created (status=Scanning). 3) Defender scans in quarantine. 4) On clean scan, API copies the blob to the production container and deletes the quarantine copy, then updates status to Available. 5) On malicious/error result, the quarantine copy is deleted and status set to Infected/Scan Failed." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "DMZ/Quarantine Malware Scanning Pattern (Alternative, Not Adopted)" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:TP_FilenameSanitization> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:TechnicalProcess> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:TechnicalDesignDoc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:enforcedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:DocumentAggregate> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:implementationNotes> "Edge cases: a filename consisting only of special characters (e.g. '***.pdf') sanitizes to a default 'document.pdf'; a file with no extension (e.g. 'README') is preserved as-is; multiple extensions (e.g. 'file.tar.gz') are all preserved; Unicode filenames (e.g. '文档.pdf') are preserved via UTF-8. The original, unsanitized filename is always retained separately in metadata per docs:Rule_OriginalFilenamePreservation — sanitization only affects the blob storage path, never what the user sees in the UI or on download." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:steps> "1) Remove special characters: / \\ : * ? \" < > |. 2) Replace spaces with underscores. 3) Remove leading/trailing periods. 4) Preserve file extension (last '.extension'). 5) Truncate to 255 characters (preserving the extension). 6) Convert to UTF-8 encoding." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Filename Sanitization Algorithm" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:TP_ScanInPlaceFlow> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:TechnicalProcess> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:TechnicalDesignDoc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:enforcedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:DocumentAggregate> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:implementationNotes> "Recommended pattern per documents-technical-design.md, chosen over the DMZ/Quarantine alternative for lower latency and cost (no blob-copy operation), at the cost of a brief window (2-10 sec) where an infected file exists in the production container before deletion — mitigated by the database status check blocking downloads while status=Scanning. Background job marks documents Scan Failed if no webhook is received within 60 seconds." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:steps> "1) UI requests upload, API validates size/permissions and creates metadata (status=Scanning). 2) API generates a write-only upload SAS token (15 min expiry). 3) Browser uploads directly to the target blob container. 4) Azure Defender detects the upload and scans in-place, writing blob index tags. 5) Defender publishes a MalwareScanningResult event to Event Grid. 6) Event Grid delivers a webhook to the Documents API. 7) On 'No threats found', status -> Available; on 'Malicious', blob deleted and status -> Infected; on error/timeout, blob deleted and status -> Scan Failed." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Scan-in-Place Malware Scanning Flow" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:TP_StorageTierLifecycleManagement> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:TechnicalProcess> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:TechnicalDesignDoc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:enforcedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:DocumentCategoryAggregate> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:implementationNotes> "Documents' own responsibility is limited to specifying container names/blob paths at upload time and exposing tier information in metadata for UI display (e.g. 'Archived - retrieval may take up to 1 hour') — it does NOT manage or trigger tier transitions itself; that is entirely infrastructure-managed, matching the domain's own explicit scope exclusion ('Storage tier transition logic -> Azure Blob Storage Lifecycle Management'). Category-specific overrides are possible via separate containers with custom policies (example named in source: 'Active Employment Records' with longer Hot-tier retention) but the concrete override parameters aren't specified — see docs:Question_CategorySpecificTierOverrideCriteria." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:steps> "Azure Blob Storage Lifecycle Management policies (infrastructure-as-code, e.g. ARM templates/Terraform — not application code or an admin UI) transition a blob through Hot (0-1 year, active/frequent access), Cool (1-3 years, 30-day minimum duration, infrequent access), and Archive (3+ years, 180-day minimum duration, rare access, ~10x cheaper storage but requires rehydration to read — priority rehydration under 1 hour at higher cost, standard rehydration up to 15 hours at lower cost) tiers, evaluated daily by the Azure platform using per-container blob-prefix-matching rules." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Storage Tier Lifecycle Management" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:TechnicalDesignDoc> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:SourceDocument> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:docType> "technical-design" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:section> "abox-tests/mied/documents/documents-technical-design.md" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:UT_Document> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:UbiquitousTerm> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A file uploaded by a user, stored in Azure Blob Storage, with associated metadata tracking its lifecycle and permissions." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Document" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:describesConcept> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:DocumentAggregate> .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:UT_DocumentAttachment> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:UbiquitousTerm> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The business entity to which a document is attached (e.g., credential application ID, staffing roster ID, professional learning session ID); replaces the overloaded term 'context'." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Document Attachment" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:describesConcept> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:DocumentAggregate> .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:UT_HardDelete> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:UbiquitousTerm> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Permanently removing a document blob from storage after the retention period expires or a legal hold is released." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Hard Delete" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:describesConcept> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:DocumentAggregate> .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:UT_LegalHold> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:UbiquitousTerm> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Flag preventing hard delete of a document regardless of retention policy, typically applied for litigation or investigation." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Legal Hold" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:describesConcept> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:DocumentAggregate> .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:UT_RetentionPolicy> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:UbiquitousTerm> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Configurable rule specifying how long documents in a category must be preserved before eligible for hard delete (e.g., 7 years, 90 days, indefinite)." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Retention Policy" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:describesConcept> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:DocumentCategoryAggregate> .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:UT_SoftDelete> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:UbiquitousTerm> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Marking a document as deleted without removing the blob, preventing user access while preserving data for recovery or audit." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Soft Delete" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:describesConcept> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:DocumentAggregate> .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:UT_StagingArea> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:UbiquitousTerm> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Temporary storage location for bulk import files awaiting processing by downstream systems (e.g., Synapse pipelines)." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Staging Area" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:describesConcept> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:StagingFileAggregate> .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:epp:AarState_Approved> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:StateDefinition> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:isTerminal> true ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:name> "Approved" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Final state is set by the Credentialing domain, not by EPP." .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:epp:AarState_Denied> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:StateDefinition> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:isTerminal> true ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:name> "Denied" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:epp:AarState_RecommendedByEPP> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:StateDefinition> ;
