	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:section> "abox/mied-v3/fdd-review/13-epp-admin-users/wireframes/addendum-b-worklist-management-credentialing-data-screen.png" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:external:AzureBlobStorageSystem> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:ExternalSystem> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:hasApi> true ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:integrationNotes> "Primary storage backend for all document blobs. Accessed via Azure SDK using Managed Identity (no storage account keys in application config). Documents generates time-limited SAS tokens (15 min) for browser-based direct upload/download; the API server itself never proxies file bytes." .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:external:AzureDefenderForStorageSystem> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:ExternalSystem> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:hasApi> true ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:integrationNotes> "Malware scanning for all uploaded blobs, scan-in-place (no quarantine container). Delivers results asynchronously via Azure Event Grid webhooks to POST /webhooks/defender-scan-result. NO fallback scanner — per documents-capability.md's Malware Scan Blocking rule, ALL uploads are blocked if Defender is unavailable. Known platform limitations (documents-technical-design.md): 2 GB file size cap, 2,000 files/min scan rate limit, 10,000 GB/month default scan cap, 60-second scan timeout." .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:external:AzureSynapseSystem> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:ExternalSystem> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:hasApi> false ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:integrationNotes> "Reads bulk-import staging files directly from Azure Blob Storage staging containers using its own Managed Identity (no direct API calls between Documents and Synapse — event-driven decoupling via BulkFileUploaded/BulkFileProcessed). Synapse pipelines process staged CSV/XLSX files and write to the data warehouse; staged blobs auto-delete after 7 days regardless of processing outcome." .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:external:BulkFileProcessedEvent> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:DomainEvent> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Published by Azure Synapse (ext:AzureSynapseSystem), not by Documents. Documents subscribes to update the corresponding StagingFile record." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:payloadHighlights> "upload_id, status (Success|Failed), records_processed, error_details" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:trigger> "Synapse pipeline finishes processing a staged bulk-import file" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:external:CEPASSystem> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:ExternalSystem> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:hasApi> true ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:integrationNotes> "State of Michigan Treasury's Centralized Electronic Payment Authorization System. Three distinct integration surfaces: (1) HTTPS GET redirect with AES-256-GCM encrypted query string for payment initiation, (2) HTTPS GET redirect return with SHA-1 hash-validated query string for payment confirmation, (3) synchronous REST API (POST /api/v1/payment/cancel) for refunds, (4) daily fixed-width posting file retrieved via SFTP (through the File Transfer Service) for reconciliation. MiEdWorkforce never handles PCI-sensitive card data — all card processing happens on CEPAS itself." .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:external:CEPISystem> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:ExternalSystem> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:hasApi> true ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:integrationNotes> "CEPI (Center for Educational Performance and Information) User Lookup Tool — fallback source of authorized user contacts when a recipient isn't found in internal identity." .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:external:CTEISSystem> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:ExternalSystem> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:hasApi> true ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:integrationNotes> "Career Technical Education Information System (CTEIS, MDE-OCTE) — state system for CTE student course enrollment/outcomes. Currently uses PIC-validation REP services (GetPersonnelByDistrict/GetPersonnelByPIC/GetPersonnelByCoreFields/GetCompleteAssignmentCodeList); the FDD's own text confirms these are 'the same set of service endpoints that will be used by many of the other integrations including MSDS/TSDL, MEGS+, NexSys' — see the consolidated coverage-gap Annotation below, not three/four independent ones." .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:external:EEMSystem> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:ExternalSystem> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:hasApi> true ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:integrationNotes> "Michigan's Educator Entity Management (EEM) system is the upstream source of record for all organization data (Buildings, Districts, ISDs, EPPs, Nonpublic Schools, Professional Learning Sponsors). MiEdWorkforce does not call EEM directly — CEPI is building a CEDS JSON-LD API on top of EEM specifically for MiEdWorkforce's requirements, and the Organizations capability is the sole integration point: it pulls from CEPI via a nightly Azure Synapse pipeline, materializes a local read-only replica plus hierarchy, and serves all other mied domains from that replica. Per organizations-capability.md, no other domain integrates with EEM (or CEPI) directly — every other domain that needs organizational context depends on the Organizations capability instead. Read-only: MiEdWorkforce never writes back to EEM/CEPI. Field contract, delta-vs-full-snapshot feed shape, auth mechanism, and SLA/rate-limit are all still being finalized with CEPI (see Question_CepiApiContractUnconfirmed below). NOTE: communications-capability.ttl's own Dependencies describe Communications calling EEM directly for external educator contact data when a recipient isn't in internal identity — in tension with the 'sole integration point' framing here. Flagged in both files; not resolved by this conversion." .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:external:FTSSystem> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:ExternalSystem> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:hasApi> false ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:integrationNotes> "Michigan's File Transfer Service — state SFTP infrastructure used to retrieve the daily CEPAS posting file. payments-capability.md notes 'FTS upgrade in progress impacts integration; current documentation may be outdated.' General SFTP/file-transfer capability is owned by the documents platform capability per payments-capability.md's own Scope section, but this specific daily-reconciliation retrieval is Payments' own direct dependency per its Dependencies table." .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:external:MSDSTSDLSystem> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:ExternalSystem> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:hasApi> true ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:integrationNotes> "Michigan School Data System (MSDS) Teacher Student Data Link (TSDL) — connects student courses to the teacher of record via PIC/Unique ID validation (GetPersonnelByUniqueId, based on the existing REP TeacherInformation/GetPersonnelByPIC API). MSDS itself queries the underlying database directly today rather than calling REP APIs; the FDD notes future data-model changes may remove the PIC/Identity dependency in favor of Local Course/Section IDs, not yet defined." .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:external:MiDataHubSystem> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:ExternalSystem> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:hasApi> true ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:integrationNotes> "Michigan DataHub (MiDH, midatahub.org) — a state-level ecosystem exchanging Ed-Fi-standard data between district SIS/HR systems and state systems, for state/federal reporting. MiEdWorkforce sends staffing data outbound via the existing CEPI Public Services 'SendToHub' endpoint (JSON, opt-in per district); no inbound 'ReceiveFromHub' endpoint exists yet on either side. Ed-Fi Data Standard, not CEDS — requires mapping. See Question_DataHubFlowDirectionDisputed for a live, unresolved dispute over whether the outbound direction is even needed as framed." .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:external:MiKeySystem> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:ExternalSystem> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:hasApi> true ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:integrationNotes> "Centralized identity management system providing Unique ID/PIC assignment through probabilistic demographic matching; integrates eScholar's COTS Uniq-Id with a SOM-developed Internal Services gateway (audit/event grid). Real-time triggers: citizen account creation/update, single employee adds, demographic updates, Link ID requests. Data exchanged inbound: demographics (name, DOB, SSN, sex, race/ethnicity, alternate names), resolution commands (CREATE_NEW/USE_EXISTING/CANCEL/LINK_IDS). Outbound: Unique ID, match result (Match/No Match/Near Match), potential match candidates (see solution-integrations.md section 2). Referred to as 'identity-resolution' in iam-domain.md's own Dependencies table." .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:external:MiLoginSystem> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:ExternalSystem> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:hasApi> true ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:integrationNotes> "Primary authentication platform for Michigan citizens and state workers (Citizen/Business/Worker identity provider types); provides identity verification only, no authorization/permissions. Protocol: OpenID Connect / OAuth 2.0 authorization code flow. Token claims: email, uniqueSecurityName, displayName, name, preferred_username, userType, email_verified, realmName, tenantId. IAM performs all authorization internally based on the resulting identity claims (see solution-integrations.md section 1)." .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:external:Microsoft365GraphSystem> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:ExternalSystem> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:hasApi> true ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:integrationNotes> "Microsoft Graph API (C# native library recommended over raw SMTP, since simple auth no longer works for SMTP), POST https://graph.microsoft.com/v1.0/me/sendMail, application-registration + RBAC authentication, two-way data direction. Per 'Interface Design document - Microsoft 365 (Outlook).docx': used for sending FROM dedicated @michigan.gov mailboxes for genuinely two-way correspondence, distinct in purpose from SendGrid's one-way alert/notification channel ('as opposed to alerts or notifications'). Data classification explicitly 'Internal (should not include PII since email is not a private communication method)' — a real, load-bearing constraint on what this channel may carry, distinct from anything asserted about ext:SendGridSystem." .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:external:NASDTECSystem> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:ExternalSystem> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:hasApi> true ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:integrationNotes> "National Association of State Directors of Teacher Education and Certification (NASDTEC) Ed ID Clearinghouse — interstate registry of educator discipline/misconduct. Nightly REST pull from GET /v1/clearinghouse/people (https://www.nasdtec.org/api), incremental by current-month TransactionDate. Records stored locally for search/reference; matched to Michigan educators via Mi-Key. See abox-tests/mied/solution-integrations.md section 6." .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:external:NexSysSystem> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:ExternalSystem> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:hasApi> true ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:integrationNotes> "MDE MEGS+/NexSys — consumes MiEdWorkforce staff-by-district data (TeacherInformation API) for Title I Part A Comparability reporting. One-way send only; no inbound requirement. Same underlying REP-derived personnel-lookup shape as ext:CTEISSystem/ext:MSDSTSDLSystem." .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:external:PowerBISystem> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:ExternalSystem> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:hasApi> true ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:integrationNotes> "Microsoft Power BI Service. Reporting acts as a secure server-side broker: it validates authorization, resolves embed parameters, and calls the Power BI REST API (POST /GenerateToken against a workspaceId/reportId, and GET /reports/{reportId} at registration time to validate the report exists) using a service-principal credential stored in Azure Key Vault, accessed via managed identity. The client never receives the service-principal credential, only the resulting embed token. Licensing model (Embedded A-SKU vs. Premium P-SKU vs. Per-User Pro) is unresolved — see rpt:Question_PowerBILicensingModel. Per solution-integrations.md section 15, PowerBI is also used platform-wide (Phase 4) for data-quality/administrative dashboards against the transactional DB and/or CEPI CEDS Data Warehouse, largely unspecified ([NEEDS INPUT] markers throughout that section) — this ExternalSystem node models Power BI generally; the embed-token/report-catalog integration is Reporting's own specific, fully-described usage of it." .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:external:RapBackSystem> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:ExternalSystem> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:hasApi> true ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:integrationNotes> "Michigan State Police (MSP) Rap Back / CHRISS. Bidirectional: (1) MSP pushes daily webhook notifications to POST /webhooks/rapback when a fingerprint-flagged individual has a criminal-activity hit; (2) PPR staff pull the full rap sheet on-demand via a SOAP 1.2 call to CHRISS's GET_RAPBACK operation (https://chriss.state.mi.us/CHRISS_SUBSCRIPTION_PORTAL/SubscriptionService.asmx), display-only, NEVER stored — only retrieval metadata (who, when) is logged. See abox-tests/mied/solution-integrations.md section 4." .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:external:SendGridSystem> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:ExternalSystem> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:hasApi> true ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:integrationNotes> "State's negotiated DTMB messaging account. Outbound: POST https://api.sendgrid.com/v3/mail/send, 10,000 req/sec confirmed limit (communications-capability.md Open Question #1, resolved 2026-08-27), implemented as an in-memory queue at 9,500 req/sec. Inbound: webhook POST to /api/webhooks/sendgrid for delivery status (Processed/Delivered/Bounced/Deferred/Dropped), HMAC SHA256 signature validation. Circuit breaker opens after 10 consecutive failures (5-minute cooldown)." .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:external:UniqueIdAssignedEvent> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:DomainEvent> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Emitted by Mi-Key/the external identity-resolution capability, not by an Aggregate modeled in this file — no sd:emits is asserted. IAM subscribes to auto-create the citizen's Individual-scope authorization." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:payloadHighlights> "userId, uniqueId, miLoginId, assignedAt" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:trigger> "Mi-Key resolves a citizen identity submission to a Match or No-Match (new Unique ID created)" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:fdd32:Fdd32Doc> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:SourceDocument> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:docType> "fdd" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Covers Features 32.1-32.16 (the document's own subtitle: '32.0 Technology, Standards and Auditing (32.1-32.16)'). Authors Vidhya Punniyamoorthy, Sean Strom, Fernando Montenegro (DTMB); reviewed by Sean Strom (Technical Owner, 5/22/2025); approved by Beth Dontje (MDE) and Caitlin Groom (CEPI), both 08/05/2025 — but comments.xml contains dated entries through 2026-01-13, well after that signoff date (same pattern already noted in the FDD 29 review: the signoff table isn't 'nothing changed after this')." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:section> "functional-design-docs/32 - Technology, Standards & Auditing/32 - Technology standards and Audit.docx" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:fdd32:Req_32_10> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:NonFunctionalRequirement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:fdd32:Fdd32Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Addendum: 'User stories are not required...' Overlaps materially with every domain's own real, converted sd:Dependency/sd:ExternalSystem modeling (Mi-Key, CEPAS, CEPI, Pearson MTTC, SendGrid, Rap Back/CHRISS are all real, already-modeled external integrations using REST/SOAP/webhook mechanisms) — those ARE the concrete instances of this NFR being satisfied, just not centrally cited from one node. Not linked via sd:satisfiedBy since no single existing node represents 'the platform's integration-capability posture' as a whole; the individual Dependency nodes are domain-scoped facts, not evidence for this cross-cutting NFR node specifically." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "32.10" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "The solution must allow for integration with State-hosted and non-hosted data sources; industry standards for data exchange (REST APIs, SFTP) must be supported and preferred, with reasonable effort to support legacy/custom SOM solutions." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Integration with State-hosted and non-hosted data sources (Integration Capability)" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:fdd32:Req_32_11_1> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:UserStory> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "MiEdWorkforce will adhere to CEDS for all personal and certification information. Data must be stored in a CEDS-compliant format. CEDS data, including extensions, must be consistent with other MDE/CEPI systems. The conversion process ensures all identified data from MOECS and REP systems is migrated as needed throughout the development lifecycle." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:fdd32:Fdd32Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Two distinct asks bundled in one story. The CEDS-COMPLIANCE half is partially, piecemeal corroborated: sd:cedsAlignment is asserted across 8+ domain files (communications, credentialing, documents, epp, iam, organizations, payments, proflearning, profpractice, reporting, staffing) on individual fields/aggregates. The MOECS/REP MIGRATION half is a genuine, unqualified coverage gap: no MigrationBatchJob/Sequence, no legacy-system-import concept, and no 'MOECS-derived identifier' resolution exists anywhere in mied-v3 — credentialing-domain.ttl's own Open Question #35 (credential_number's 'PV'/'CC-K' prefixes, likely legacy-MOECS-derived) and proflearning-domain.ttl's Open Question #13 (a possible legacy-MOECS Sponsor ID) both independently flag pieces of exactly this same undocumented migration, from two different domains, without a resolution in either. No sd:satisfiedBy asserted given how central and unaddressed the migration-process half is; see the coverage-gap Annotation below." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "32.11.1" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a Data Governance Specialist, I want MiEdWorkforce to adhere to the Common Education Data Standards (CEDS) for all personal and certification information so that data consistency is maintained across CEPI systems." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "CEDS adherence for personal/certification data, migrated from MOECS/REP" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:fdd32:Req_32_11_2> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:UserStory> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "All legacy data available in the new application or an appropriate platform (cloud storage, offline database, etc.). Application fully functional with migrated data. Where possible, legacy data (past applications, messages sent) is replicated. An appropriate platform (e.g. Azure cold storage) is used for long-term retention. Retention covers long-term history (e.g. credential issue date + 99 years, or decades of employment data)." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:fdd32:Fdd32Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "No sd:satisfiedBy: docs:RetentionPolicyVO/docs:DocumentAggregate model a real, granular retention-policy mechanism, but it is scoped to DOCUMENTS specifically (with category-level policies), not the broader 'historical educator/employment/application data, wherever it lives' this story describes, and no retention duration anywhere in mied-v3 approaches the 99-year figure named here. A structurally similar but not equivalent mechanism — noted, not claimed as satisfying." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "32.11.2" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a MiEdWorkforce User, I want all legacy data to be available in the new application or an appropriate platform (e.g., cold storage) so that I can reference historical information for my professional records." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Legacy/historical data availability and long-term retention" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:fdd32:Req_32_12> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Requirement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:fdd32:Fdd32Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Addendum: 'User stories are not required, as this feature serves as a guideline rather than a functional deliverable.' HLS scenario 3's own stray fragment ('All configuration items work as expected Needs work') was flagged by a reviewer comment (id 23, Handley: 'IDK why this phrase is here. \"Needs work\"') as apparently unintentional leftover text, not a real acceptance criterion — noted, not modeled as its own requirement." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "32.12" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "The Contractor must provide an implementation/engagement exit plan ensuring SOM always retains an operational system, with or without further Contractor updates (subject to licensing/contract terms). The system must be built compatible with SOM standards (or easily migrated/reconfigured if not). Pre-launch validation includes: all user types can log in; security scans (DAST, Tenable, SAST, SCA) show no critical/high/medium vulnerabilities (or a documented remediation plan); a basic configuration audit; interface testing; a basic security audit (no default passwords, no backdoors, no open-by-default networking); a smoke test." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Vendor exit plan, environment compatibility, and pre-launch security/integration validation" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:fdd32:Req_32_13> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:NonFunctionalRequirement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "Addendum, verbatim: 'The user stories defined under Epic 2 - Reporting represent the detailed functional implementation of the high-level requirements originally outlined in this Feature 32.13 - Reporting (Epic 32 - Technology Standards and Audit).'" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:fdd32:Fdd32Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "This is the one Feature in this FDD that explicitly hands off its own detailed requirements to another FDD by name. Both abox/mied-v3/GAPS.md's FDD-02 entry and the FDD-29 review's own GAPS.md entry independently flagged 'Technology Standards and Audit requirements (32.13)' as an unconverted dependency at the time each of those passes ran — this pass closes that loop: 32.13 is satisfied by the entirety of rpt:ReportingContext's own conversion (reporting-capability/api/permissions/sequences/technical-design.ttl, reviewed in fdd-review/02-reporting/02-reporting.ttl), not by any node specific to this file. The Power-BI-as-embedded-analytics-platform decision this Feature announces is corroborated concretely by rpt:Op_GenerateEmbedToken (Power BI GenerateToken API integration) — confirms the cross-reference holds in both directions, it was not just an assumption." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "32.13" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:reporting:ReportingContext> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "Solution must integrate with analytics tools such as Power BI and SAS. All MiEdWorkforce data (any storage format/platform/online status) must be accessible via the reporting platform, with reasonably performant queries; legacy reports must be available in the new system; new data must be easy to expose for reporting without new development; reports reference data from multiple sources including historical. Reporting must not interfere with system performance (long-running queries against separate, synchronized storage). Periodic/tunable reports supported. Reporting permissions consistent with the rest of the system; report creation/viewing embedded in MiEdWorkforce." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Analytics/reporting-platform integration (Power BI / SAS)" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:fdd32:Req_32_14_1> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:UserStory> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "Administrator can view history of batch jobs for which they have access. History includes prior versions of the job. History displays configuration changes. Detailed logging of administrative activity related to batch jobs is maintained." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:fdd32:Fdd32Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "No satisfiedBy: sd:BatchJob (a Sequence subclass) is used across 7 domains for individual scheduled processes, but no CROSS-CUTTING batch-job-administration surface (a place to view run history, prior configuration versions, or admin activity logs across all of them) exists anywhere — each domain's own BatchJob instances describe what the job DOES, not an admin UI/API for managing its schedule or history. See the consolidated coverage-gap Annotation below (shared with 32.14.2-32.14.6, all facets of the same missing capability)." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "32.14.1" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a MiEdWorkforce Administrator, I want the ability to view the history for all batch jobs run for a feature so that I maintain full audit controls and accountability." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "View batch job run history for audit/accountability" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:fdd32:Req_32_14_2> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:UserStory> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "Administrator can view all current batch job schedules. Can only view schedules for jobs where they have read-only or full access. Multiple job types (email notifications, file transfers, etc.) are viewable when appropriate." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:fdd32:Fdd32Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "32.14.2" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a MiEdWorkforce Administrator, I want to be able to view all current batch job schedules (including various job types, such as email notifications and file transfers) for which I have at least read-only access, so that I can monitor the scheduled processing activity." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "View all current batch job schedules with read access" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:fdd32:Req_32_14_3> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:UserStory> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "Administrator can add schedules for batch jobs. Cannot see jobs for which they are not authorized. Cannot add schedules for jobs where they only have read-only access. Scheduling-system authentication consistent with other MDE/CEPI systems (ADM accounts, SSO login)." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:fdd32:Fdd32Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "32.14.3" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a MiEdWorkforce Administrator with appropriate permissions, I want to be able to create and add schedules for batch jobs, so that I can manage automated processing within the system while respecting security access rules." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Create/add batch job schedules with appropriate access" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:fdd32:Req_32_14_4> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:UserStory> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "System supports the State Administrator's ability to run ad hoc batch jobs. Administrator can manually trigger a batch run outside the automated schedule." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:fdd32:Fdd32Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "32.14.4" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a MiEdWorkforce Administrator, I want the ability to manually trigger and run ad hoc batch jobs outside of the regular schedule, so that I can execute necessary processes immediately upon need." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Manually trigger ad hoc batch job runs" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:fdd32:Req_32_14_5> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:UserStory> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "Administrator can remove schedules. Administrator can modify schedules. Can only modify schedules for jobs where they have full access." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:fdd32:Fdd32Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "32.14.5" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a MiEdWorkforce Administrator with full access to a job, I want to be able to modify or remove existing batch job schedules, so that I can adjust processing timing and configuration as needed." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Modify/remove batch job schedules with full access" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:fdd32:Req_32_14_6> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:UserStory> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "Administrator can cancel running jobs. Can only cancel running jobs for which they have full access." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:fdd32:Fdd32Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "32.14.6" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a MiEdWorkforce Administrator with full access, I want to be able to cancel running batch jobs when necessary, so that I can stop erroneous or unwanted processing immediately." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Cancel running batch jobs with full access" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:fdd32:Req_32_14_7> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:UserStory> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "System must successfully detect when a scheduled batch job fails. Admins and business owner(s) must receive a notification of the failed job. Detailed logging of system/administrative activity related to the failure must be maintained to aid troubleshooting." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:fdd32:Fdd32Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Shares the same missing-admin-surface gap as 32.14.1-6 (see that Annotation) for the detection/logging half. The notification half has a genuinely still-open, separately-tracked question: comment thread 36->1682393414 (Punniyamoorthy: 'Need to add the notification format and the content' -> Caswell, 2026-01-02: 'Agreed. I'm not sure we officially determined what type of notification a user should receive. Can we confirm that?') shows this was flagged during drafting and remained unanswered as of the most recent comment — not just unbuilt, but unspecified. See Question_BatchFailureNotificationContentUndefined below." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "32.14.7" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a MiEdWorkforce Administrator or Business Owner, I want to receive a notification when a scheduled batch job fails, so that I can quickly initiate troubleshooting and remediation." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Notify admins/business owners on batch job failure" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:fdd32:Req_32_15_1> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:UserStory> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "Admin with Credential permission can create/maintain the worklist per credential type (Permit, Special Education, School Counselor, School Administrator, Renewal license, Educator (Standard/Professional/Interim Teaching), School Nurse, School Social Worker, Annual Career Authorization, Additional Endorsements, Candidate Tracking). Users with the right access can access/process the worklist as defined for that type." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:fdd32:Fdd32Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Credentialing's own routing/worklist logic (Rule_ManualReviewTriggering, PPR-flag-based routing per the FDD 29 review's Req_29_2_8) matches the underlying mechanism well, but per-credential-type NAMED worklists with distinct admin-configurable access are the same still-open gap credentialing's own cred:Question_WorklistAssignmentScope already tracks (FDD 5/FDD 13's per-user, not just per-role, worklist assignment) — cross-referenced, not re-raised as a new Annotation here." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "32.15.1" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:CredentialingContext> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:Rule_ManualReviewTriggering> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As an Admin with Credential permission, I want to create and maintain worklists specific to each credential type (e.g., Permit, Special Education, School Counselor), so that users with the appropriate access can process the worklist items as defined by the credential type." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Create/maintain worklists per credential type" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:fdd32:Req_32_15_2> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:UserStory> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "Administrator can create/manage the Identity management worklist. Users with the right access can access/process it. Business rules governing worklist processing are maintained per Business Rule Management (4.0)." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:fdd32:Fdd32Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Good match: iam:IdentityResolutionRequestAggregate's RequiresResolution status IS the Identity Administrator's worklist queue (iam-domain.ttl's own notes describe staffing/citizen flows both routing into it). The 'Business Rule Management (4.0)' cross-reference names a capability with no bounded-context home anywhere in mied-v3 (see GAPS.md's existing FDD-29 entry on this same gap) — not re-raised here, already on record." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "32.15.2" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:iam:IdentityResolutionRequestAggregate> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:iam:Rule_CitizenNearMatchResolution> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As an Administrator, I want to create and manage the worklist related to Identity management so that tasks related to user identity verification are centrally processed." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Create/manage the Identity Management worklist" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:fdd32:Req_32_15_3> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:UserStory> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "State admin setup can configure/allocate privileges to manage Worklist assignments. MiEdWorkforce provides role-based worklist access/assignment per business process. Any change in user access/worklist configuration is captured under audit log." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:fdd32:Fdd32Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "The general role/authorization-allocation mechanism is satisfied by IAM's RBAC model. Two things are NOT: (1) a distinct, per-worklist-item privilege grain (view/process/reassign/configure, as opposed to IAM's own role-bundle-of-permissions model) isn't modeled generically — each domain's own worklist (e.g. profp:PPRWorklistAggregate's AssignedReviewers) handles this internally rather than through a shared cross-cutting concept; (2) the 'captured under audit log' clause assumes a working audit-log capability that does not exist — see Question_AuditCapabilityAssumedButStubOnly below (shared with 32.15.9, which makes the identical claim)." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "32.15.3" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:iam:RoleDefinitionAggregate> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:iam:UserAuthorizationAggregate> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As an Administrator, I want the system to allow me to configure and allocate privileges to manage Worklist assignments for users, so that I can ensure role-based worklist access is maintained, and all configuration changes are captured under audit controls. Reference additional user stories as part of business specification #5 System Administration - Credentialing, feature 5.5: Manage Worklist Assignment." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Configure/allocate worklist-management privileges, with audit controls" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:fdd32:Req_32_15_4> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:UserStory> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "Administrator can create/manage the EPP worklist. EPP users with the right access can access/process it as defined." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:fdd32:Fdd32Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "EPP's own working assumption ('Worklist' as a filtered view, not a separate aggregate — epp-domain.ttl's own header) covers the base case; epp:Question_WorklistAssignmentScope (Open Question #11) already tracks the exact same per-user-not-just-per-role assignment gap this story's 'right access' phrasing implies — cross-referenced, not re-raised." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "32.15.4" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:epp:EppContext> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:epp:Perm_ApplicationsView> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:epp:Perm_ApprovalsView> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As an Administrator, I want to be able to create and manage the worklist specifically for Education Preparation Providers (EPP), so that EPP users with the right access can process their workflow items. Reference additional user stories as part of business specification #13 Educator Preparation Providers, feature 13.3: Work list." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Create/manage the Education Preparation Providers (EPP) worklist" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:fdd32:Req_32_15_5> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:UserStory> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "Administrator can create/manage the Professional Learning worklist. Users with the right access can access/process it as defined." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:fdd32:Fdd32Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "ProfLearning models its own worklist as a filtered view over ApplicationReviewStatus/RequestStatus, same working assumption as EPP's. plrn:Question_ConfigurableWorklistStatuses (Open Question #12) already tracks a possible gap between that assumption and FDD 14.3's own admin-configurable-status language — cross-referenced, not re-raised." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "32.15.5" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:proflearning:ProfessionalLearningContext> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As an Administrator, I want to be able to create and manage the worklist related to Professional Learning, so that authorized users can access and process relevant items. Reference additional user stories as part of business specification #14 Professional Learning feature 14.3: Worklist." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Create/manage the Professional Learning worklist" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:fdd32:Req_32_15_6> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:UserStory> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "Administrator can create/manage the Professional Practice and Rapbacks worklist. Users with the right access can access/process it as defined." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:fdd32:Fdd32Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Good match on both halves: profp:PPRWorklistAggregate is a real, fully modeled worklist aggregate (AssignedReviewers/RoutingRules/PriorityRules/etc.), and Rap Back-triggered disclosures (profp:RapBackNotificationReceivedEvent, sourced from ext:RapBackSystem) flow into the same PPR review process rather than a separate queue — consistent with this story treating 'Professional practice and Rapbacks' as one combined worklist, not two." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "32.15.6" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:external:RapBackSystem> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:profpractices:PPRWorklistAggregate> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As an Administrator, I want to be able to create and manage the worklist related to Professional practice and Rapbacks, so that authorized users can access and process these specific case types." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Create/manage the Professional Practice and Rapbacks worklist" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:fdd32:Req_32_15_7> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:UserStory> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "Administrator can create/manage the Staffing data collection worklist. Users with the right access can access/process it as defined." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:fdd32:Fdd32Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "No satisfiedBy: unlike EPP/ProfLearning/ProfPractice, staffing-domain.ttl models no worklist concept of its own at all — not even a filtered-view working assumption. staffing-domain.ttl's own header explicitly disclaims owning several adjacent worklist-like concerns (the Identity Administrator worklist belongs to IAM), but nothing fills the gap for staffing's OWN data-collection worklist this story describes. Genuine, unqualified coverage gap — see the Annotation below." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "32.15.7" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As an Administrator, I want to be able to create and manage the worklist related to Staffing data collection, so that users responsible for staffing data can access and process relevant worklist items." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Create/manage the Staffing data collection worklist" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:fdd32:Req_32_15_8> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:UserStory> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "System allows the user to access their role-based worklist from the dashboard. Worklists are accessible from the user Dashboard based on user access permissions. The dashboard defines role-specific rules to access the worklist." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:fdd32:Fdd32Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "No satisfiedBy: dash:DashboardsContext is a stub-only bounded context (same as it was for FDD 29's Req_29_1_8 and FDD 11/16's Req_11_7) — this is the same cross-cutting dashboard-widget-surfacing concern those two prior passes already found, now independently reconfirmed a third time from a Technology Standards FDD rather than a feature FDD, which raises confidence this Dashboards-stub gap is real and central rather than a one-off. Out-of-scope for any individual domain to build, per the established precedent." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "32.15.8" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a MiEdWorkforce User with appropriate permissions, I want to be able to access my specific role-based worklist directly from the dashboard, so that I can immediately view and process my assigned workflow items." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Access role-based worklist from the Dashboard" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:fdd32:Req_32_15_9> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:UserStory> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "Role matrix lists security roles from User-Management (1.0). Changes take effect immediately. Updates are logged for audit." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:fdd32:Fdd32Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Same partial-match shape as 32.15.3 (general role/privilege allocation satisfied by IAM's RBAC model; the specific view/process/reassign/configure GRANULARITY per worklist is not a distinct modeled concept; 'logged for audit' assumes a capability that doesn't exist — see Question_AuditCapabilityAssumedButStubOnly below, shared target with 32.15.3)." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "32.15.9" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:iam:RoleDefinitionAggregate> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a State Administrator, I need to allocate view, process, reassign and configure privileges to roles so that only authorized staff can act on a worklist." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Allocate view/process/reassign/configure worklist privileges to roles, with audit logging" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:fdd32:Req_32_16_10> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:UserStory> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "User can view previously uploaded documents. Can only view documents for which they have read-only/modify permissions. RBAC enforces this. System maintains access logs recording document views. User is prevented from viewing without proper permissions." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:fdd32:Fdd32Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Direct match, including the access-logging half — another case where 'access logs' is a real, modeled capability (docs:DocumentAccessLog, docs:DocumentViewedEvent, subscribed to by adt:AuditContext) rather than an assumed one." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "32.16.10" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:DocumentAccessLog> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:DocumentViewedEvent> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:Op_DownloadDocument> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a MiEdWorkforce User, I want to be able to view documents previously uploaded only for which I have read-only or modify permissions, so that I can confirm document contents while adhering to system security controls." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "View previously uploaded documents per permission, with access logging" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:fdd32:Req_32_16_11> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:UserStory> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "System supports document processing for worklist management. When viewing worklist items, relevant documents are viewable directly from the worklist. Viewing from the worklist still adheres to RBAC/permissions. System supports document retrieval specifically for worklist processing." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:fdd32:Fdd32Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "No satisfiedBy: this requires a worklist-to-document LINKING concept (a worklist item knows which document(s) it references, and can hand off to Documents' own view/permission machinery) that doesn't exist on either side — documents-capability.ttl's own DocumentAggregate has no notion of 'the worklist item that references me,' and none of the domain-specific worklist aggregates (profp:PPRWorklistAggregate, credentialing's routing model) declare a Documents-facing relationship either. Documents' underlying view/permission mechanism (docs:Op_DownloadDocument, RBAC) is real and would need no new work; only the cross-domain LINK itself is missing. Genuine, narrow, well-defined coverage gap." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "32.16.11" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a User processing a worklist item, I want to be able to view relevant documents attached to that item directly from my worklist, so that I have the necessary information for efficient task processing." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "View worklist-attached documents directly from the worklist" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:fdd32:Req_32_16_1> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:UserStory> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "System allows integration with malware scanning tools. Integration supports ransomware/virus/spyware threat identification. All uploaded documents are vetted before being saved." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:fdd32:Fdd32Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Direct, strong match — Azure Defender for Storage integration with NO fallback scanner (documents-capability.ttl's own Malware Scan Blocking rule: ALL uploads blocked if Defender is unavailable) is a materially stricter posture than this story's own 'vetted before storage' ask, not a gap." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "32.16.1" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:DocumentMalwareDetectedEvent> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:MalwareScanResultVO> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:Seq_DocumentUploadWithMalwareScanning> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a System Administrator, I want the system to allow for integration with malware scanning tools (including ransomware, virus, and spyware scanners) so that all uploaded documents are vetted before storage." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Malware-scan all uploaded documents before storage" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:fdd32:Req_32_16_2> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:UserStory> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "Administrator can access a document administration page. Page allows listing/viewing documents across the system. Administrator can only view documents for which they have proper read-only/modify permissions. RBAC and access logs are implemented. System supports document retrieval/management for auditing purposes." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:fdd32:Fdd32Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Good match, and one of the few places in this FDD where 'for auditing purposes' is actually backed by a real capability (docs:Op_GetAuditLogs/docs:DocumentAccessLog) rather than an assumed one — contrast with 32.15.3/32.15.9's unbacked 'audit log' language (see Question_AuditCapabilityAssumedButStubOnly)." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "32.16.2" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:DocumentAccessLog> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:Op_GetAuditLogs> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:Op_SearchDocuments> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:Perm_AdminViewAll> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As an Administrator, I want to be able to access a document administration page to list and view documents across the system, so that I can perform auditing and management tasks based on my permissions." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Document administration page for cross-system list/view/audit" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:fdd32:Req_32_16_3> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:UserStory> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "System implements bulk upload functionality. Administrators/Power users can upload multiple documents simultaneously. Bulk upload is implemented where appropriate for business use." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:fdd32:Fdd32Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "32.16.3" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:Op_InitiateBulkUpload> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:Seq_BulkDocumentUpload> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As an Administrator, I want the ability to upload multiple documents simultaneously (bulk-upload), so that I can efficiently load large quantities of files into the system where appropriate." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Bulk-upload multiple documents" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:fdd32:Req_32_16_4> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:UserStory> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "Administrator can mark multiple documents for removal. System prevents bulk removal when legal holds are in place. System prevents bulk removal when retention schedules are in place." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:fdd32:Fdd32Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Direct match — documents-capability.ttl's own invariant ('If any item in bulk delete violates retention policy, entire operation marked Partially Failed') is a more precise version of this story's 'respecting restrictions' ask." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "32.16.4" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:Op_BulkDeleteDocuments> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:Seq_BulkDocumentSoftDeleteWithValidation> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As an Administrator, I want to be able to mark multiple documents for removal (bulk-remove), while respecting restrictions like legal holds and retention schedules, so that I can manage document inventory effectively and compliantly." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Bulk-remove documents respecting legal holds and retention" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:fdd32:Req_32_16_5> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:UserStory> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "Administrator can request an override when attempting to delete a restricted document. Business Owner(s) can review and approve override requests. The override request process is auditable." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:fdd32:Fdd32Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Strong match, including dual-approval for high-value overrides (documents-capability.ttl's own invariant: legal holds/retention >5 years require dual approval) and a 7-day approved-override expiry — both go beyond what this story's acceptance criteria explicitly ask for, in a good way. 'Auditable' here IS backed by real content (docs:Rule/invariant 'All override actions logged to compliance audit system'), another exception to the Question_AuditCapabilityAssumedButStubOnly pattern found elsewhere in this FDD." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "32.16.5" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:Op_ApproveOverrideRequest> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:Op_ExecuteOverrideRequest> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:Op_RequestRetentionOverride> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:Seq_AdministratorRequestsRetentionOverride> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As an Administrator, I want to be able to request an override of document removal restrictions, and as a Business Owner, I want to be able to review and approve those override requests, so that necessary exceptions to retention rules can be managed and audited." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Request and approve document-removal-restriction overrides" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:fdd32:Req_32_16_6> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:UserStory> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "Retention rules implementable at a granular level for all document types. Legal holds implementable at a granular level for all document types. Different document types support different storage backends/policies." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:fdd32:Fdd32Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "32.16.6" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:LegalHoldVO> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:Op_ApplyLegalHold> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:Op_ReleaseLegalHold> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:RetentionPolicyVO> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As an Administrator, I want record retention rules and legal holds to be implemented at a granular level for all document types so that we ensure compliance with SOM guidelines." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Granular retention rules and legal holds per document type" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:fdd32:Req_32_16_7> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:UserStory> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "User can replace a previously uploaded document. Can only replace when permitted by system permissions. Old document is appropriately discarded on replacement. New document becomes the current version, saved in the appropriate store." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:fdd32:Fdd32Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "32.16.7" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:Op_RequestDocumentReplacement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:Rule_DocumentReplacementVersioning> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:Seq_DocumentReplacementAndVersioning> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a User who has previously uploaded a document, I want to be able to replace the uploaded document only when permitted, so that the system maintains the most current file version while discarding the old document appropriately." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Replace a previously uploaded document" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:fdd32:Req_32_16_8> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:UserStory> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "Version controls are supported for uploaded documents. Replacing a document maintains version controls. Historical document-submission records can be retrieved. Historical records are preserved for auditing/retrieval." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:fdd32:Fdd32Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Direct match, with a concrete detail this story doesn't name: docs:DocumentVersion caps at a maximum of 10 versions per document — a real constraint worth knowing about relative to this story's unqualified 'preserved' language, though not a contradiction (10 versions comfortably covers ordinary replacement patterns)." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "32.16.8" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:DocumentVersion> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:Rule_DocumentReplacementVersioning> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a User, I want the system to maintain version controls when I replace an uploaded document so that historical submission records are preserved." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Version control across document replacements" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:fdd32:Req_32_16_9> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:UserStory> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "User must log in before uploading. Uploaded document is saved in the appropriate store. Different storage backends/policies apply per document type/category. All uploads are vetted by malware scanning before storage. Storage includes appropriate security measures (e.g. strong encryption). Backend is fully integrated with the UI/UX platform. Business approves the storage solution if multiple native/cost-effective options exist." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:fdd32:Fdd32Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "32.16.9" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:Op_RequestDocumentUpload> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:satisfiedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:Seq_DocumentUploadWithMalwareScanning> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a MiEdWorkforce User logging into the appropriate section, I want to upload a document, so that the document is saved correctly in the appropriate document store according to its category." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Upload a document into its correct category/store" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:fdd32:Req_32_1> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:NonFunctionalRequirement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:fdd32:Fdd32Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Addendum: 'User stories are not required, as this feature serves as a guideline rather than a functional deliverable.' Comment thread 3->4 (Montenegro/Carney, 2025-04-01, both resolved) narrows this Feature's actual scope: an early draft's 'Application' language was ambiguous between narrow (backend) and broad (whole app, including UI/UX already covered by the FDD's own dedicated UI/UX Business Specification) readings; Carney's resolution — no merging of RFP-published Business Specification numbers, no content duplication, this Feature should focus on non-UI/UX application standards specifically, with UI/UX referenced rather than restated — is why the visible text reads as governance-process language rather than concrete UI/UX criteria. 'Wiki-Application standards.pptx', named inline right after this Feature's HLS table, appears to be the actual governing document for the standards this Feature points at; skipped per CONVENTIONS.md's pptx exclusion (prose standards content, not structured reference data)." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "32.1" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "The system must maintain interface and behavior standards: application behaviors consistent with SOM UI/UX standards unless business needs require differences (documented); all SOM standards required and followed unless specifically overridden by business need; deviations from cybersecurity standards require explicit, documented business approval; all deviations from SOM standards must be linked to business needs, requested/approved by business owners, and documented for use during the ATO (Authority to Operate) process." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Application interface/behavior standards conformance" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:fdd32:Req_32_2_1> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:UserStory> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "The system must adhere to State of Michigan Digital Standards. The application is made available for DTMB eMichigan review." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:fdd32:Fdd32Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "No satisfiedBy: no graph node models a pre-launch digital-standards review gate or its outcome anywhere in mied-v3 — this is a release/QA-process requirement, not a domain-model concept, and none of the 11 domains' own technical-design files describe an eMichigan review step." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "32.2.1" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As a Developer, I want the application to adhere to State of Michigan Digital Standards so that we ensure compliance before the application can go live." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Developer adherence to SOM Digital Standards before go-live" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:fdd32:Req_32_2_2> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:UserStory> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:acceptanceCriteria> "The system is accessible and operational on mobile devices. The system operation is verified with a particular focus for educators and non-certified staff. The design must comply with the State of Michigan digital standards (which covers mobile functionality)." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:fdd32:Fdd32Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "No satisfiedBy: responsive/mobile-web behavior is a UI-implementation concern this ontology deliberately doesn't model at the design-node level (no domain's own conversion describes a distinct mobile UI/UX pattern) — consistent with how the whole solution design treats UI mechanics generally (wireframes describe screen CONTENT, never responsive layout behavior)." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "32.2.2" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "As an Educator or Non-Certified Staff, I want the system to be accessible and operational on my mobile device so that I can manage my profile and credentials easily." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Mobile accessibility for educators and non-certified staff" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:fdd32:Req_32_3> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:Requirement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:fdd32:Fdd32Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Addendum, verbatim: 'It has been determined that this feature is no longer considered necessary.' Confirmed still current by a 2026-01-02 comment thread (id 30/1291395255, Punniyamoorthy asking 'Need to confirm with Brandy' -> Caswell/Brandy replying 'Previously confirmed that this feature was no longer needed. If that is still the case, please feel free to resolve this comment.') — the rejection was re-verified, not just carried forward stale. IRONY WORTH FLAGGING: this Feature's own body text is the single clearest generic statement anywhere in this document of what a real audit capability would need to do (soft-delete over hard-delete, admin change review, historical reconstruction) — and it was the one Feature explicitly killed, while six OTHER stories in this same FDD (32.14.1, 32.14.7, 32.15.3, 32.15.9, 32.16.2, 32.16.5, 32.16.10) go on to casually assume 'audit log'/'audit controls' exist as a working platform capability. See Question_AuditCapabilityAssumedButStubOnly below." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "32.3" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "The system is able to mark data as inactive or 'delete' in accordance with required audit and retention schedules. Administrator users can review recent actions and data changes; in general, no data should be permanently deleted (soft-deleted/marked for deletion instead, except purely transactional data, erroneous uploads, or business-preapproved exceptions); where appropriate, historical data should be reconstructable. Data retention governed by SOM data retention guidelines; certain log formats may be required by DTMB for SIEM/monitoring/cybersecurity compliance (e.g. Dynatrace)." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Mark data inactive/'delete' per audit and retention schedules (soft-delete, historical reconstruction, admin change review)" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:fdd32:Req_32_4> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:NonFunctionalRequirement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:fdd32:Fdd32Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "No satisfiedBy: no single graph node represents 'the platform's primary datastore/persistence architecture' as a decision — each domain's own technical-design file describes its OWN storage choices independently (e.g. communications-technical-design.ttl's Cosmos DB hot-storage-for-email-content decision, which is domain-scoped, not a statement about the platform's PRIMARY educator-information store this Feature is actually about). orgs:OrganizationsContext's own CEPI/CEDS-JSON-LD integration (organizations-capability.ttl) is the closest existing evidence of the JSON-LD direction actually being pursued, but that's specifically about the Organizations capability's own EEM/CEPI read replica, not the platform's core IDS. sd:cedsAlignment is asserted on individual fields across 8+ domains, which is the CEDS-adherence half of this NFR being honored piecemeal — but there is no central node asserting 'MiEdWorkforce's core data model is CEDS IDS (or CEDS JSON-LD)' as a platform decision." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "32.4" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "The system must utilize the latest CEDS Integrated Data Store (IDS) as the primary database for storage and retrieval of educator information. The current CEDS IDS is SQL Server based; the standard's administrators and the State are evaluating converting to a NoSQL DB with a JSON-LD schema, likely Azure Cosmos DB. The state retains the right to determine the final data model (CEDS IDS vs. CEDS JSON-LD). Modifications to the data model must be State-approved. The IDS must be upgraded to the latest available version at launch (likely CEDS-IDS-14.x), without data loss (SOM-approved if loss is possible); SOM must approve any IDS-to-JSON-LD migration." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "CEDS Integrated Data Store (or CEDS JSON-LD) as primary educator-information datastore" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:fdd32:Req_32_5> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:NonFunctionalRequirement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:fdd32:Fdd32Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Addendum: 'User stories are not required, as this feature serves as a guideline rather than a functional deliverable.'" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "32.5" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "The system must be maintainable after delivery using the State's preferred frameworks: latest .NET LTS at delivery time (likely 10); source code in C#, ANSI SQL/T-SQL, JavaScript (TypeScript preferred); if Angular/Vue/similar SPA technology is used, latest State-supported LTS version." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Software framework/language currency (Frameworks)" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:fdd32:Req_32_6> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:NonFunctionalRequirement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:fdd32:Fdd32Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Addendum: 'User stories are not required...'" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "32.6" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "Technology used must be industry-standard; open-source software must be State-approved for use; the solution must allow integration with State-hosted and non-hosted data sources." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Industry-standard, State-approved open-source technology (Industry Standards and Open-Source Approval)" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:fdd32:Req_32_7> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:NonFunctionalRequirement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:fdd32:Fdd32Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Addendum: 'User stories are not required...' HLS scenario 3 additionally expects a software Bill of Materials (BOM) report and documented terms for both paid and non-paid licenses." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "32.7" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "Technology used must be appropriately licensed (Contractor-owned or public domain); all licensing requirements documented and submitted for business-owner review regardless of cost." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Software licensing compliance (Licensing)" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:fdd32:Req_32_8> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:NonFunctionalRequirement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:fdd32:Fdd32Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Addendum: 'User stories are not required...' No satisfiedBy: none of the 11 domains' own technical-design files document a platform-wide vulnerability-remediation SLA, credential-rotation mechanism, or scan-result distribution process — each domain's own security notes (e.g. payments-technical-design.ttl's circuit-breaker configuration, iam-technical-design.ttl's RBAC caching) are architectural details, not evidence of THIS specific NFR being satisfied." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "32.8" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "Technology used must support a mechanism for quick updates, especially security-related ones, relative to industry vulnerability categories (e.g. OWASP-defined) and remediation speed; results of scans/security audits made available to appropriate SOM employees on an ongoing basis; no backdoors/security bypasses/default credentials, all credentials available to SOM administrators and rotatable at all levels without new development." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Rapid security-update mechanism (Security Updates)" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:fdd32:Req_32_9> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:NonFunctionalRequirement> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:fdd32:Fdd32Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Addendum: 'User stories are not required...' HLS scenario 5 additionally expects application health dashboards (running processes, CPU/network load, error messages, exception logs) integrated with SOM logging platforms (Dynatrace, QRadar, Azure App Insights)." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:requirementId> "32.9" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:statement> "Software-application-generated errors must be reported in near-real-time and be addressable (correctable by administrators) in suitable online and/or batch options." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:title> "Near-real-time, admin-addressable error reporting (Error Reporting)" .

