<urn:solutiondesign:instance:iam:Fdd01Doc> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:SourceDocument> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:docType> "fdd" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Covers Features 1.1-1.8 (User Management: MiLogin Citizen/Business/Worker integration, User Group Management, User Search, User Roles, Account Registration, User Authorization Reports (deferred), and 'Emulate system for specific users and entities'/impersonation). Authors Beth Dontje, Caitlin Groom, Vidhya Punniyamoorthy, Molly Chapman (creation 5/9/2025); approved by Beth Dontje (MDE) and Caitlin Groom (CEPI) 08/08/2025 per the signoff table — but comments.xml contains dated entries through 2026-04-15/2026-04-27, well after that signoff date, meaning the document continued to be actively revised after its nominal approval (same pattern already noted in the FDD 29 pass)." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:section> "functional-design-docs/01 - User Management/1 - User Management.docx" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:iam:Fdd01RoleMatrixDoc> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:SourceDocument> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:iam:Fdd01Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:docType> "brd" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "The one confirmed workbook exception per CONVENTIONS.md — explicitly named and cited by the FDD's own business-spec text. 'All User Roles' sheet: 19 rows, columns MiLogin Type | Group | Role | ~35 per-function access levels (Read/Edit/No). Review comments elsewhere in the FDD (ids 22/23/52/62) repeatedly caveat that this matrix is 'up-to-date but subject to change after upcoming role matrix discussions' and 'will evolve' — treated here as a live, not-yet-final reference artifact, not an authoritative source to reconcile role-by-role against iam:Entity_Role. Its own column structure (a 'Group' column distinct from 'Role') is corroborating evidence for Question_NoUserGroupLayerContradiction below." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:section> "functional-design-docs/01 - User Management/MiEdWorkforce Role Matrix-Revised.xlsx" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:iam:Fdd15Doc> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:SourceDocument> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:docType> "fdd" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "One folder, 11 numbered sub-documents (15.1-15.13, several sharing a combined document per feature grouping: 15.6/15.11/15.12, 15.7/15.14/15.15), covering the Mi-Key identity-resolution integration end to end: Business/Citizen identity request and update flows, Near Match resolution, Link/Split/Retire ID, Person Search, Bulk/API identity processing, the Identity Administrator worklist, and identity-specific email/comms configuration. Authored primarily by Caitlin Groom, Molly Chapman, Lindsey McCann, Liz Breckel, Vidhya Punniyamoorthy, Beth Dontje across 8/2024-8/2025; several sub-docs (15.3, 15.8, 15.10) carry unusually extensive self-authored Gap Analysis sections comparing the FDD against an underlying BRD, already naming several of the gaps this pass independently confirms." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:section> "functional-design-docs/15 - User Management - Identity Management Integration/" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:iam:GetUserContextOperation> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:ApiOperation> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:accessType> "internal-service" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:exposedBy> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:iam:IamContext> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:method> "GET" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "CONFIRMED GAP (cross-domain consistency pass): iam is now really converted in abox/mied-v3/iam/iam-api.ttl, and it exposes no single combined identity+permissions+scope endpoint. The closest real operations are iam:Op_GetUser (GET /users/{userId}, user details only) and iam:Op_GetEffectivePermissions (GET /permissions/effective, permissions/scope only, requires a separate call) — no single call returns all three, so no rename was made. Path was originally inferred — documents-capability.md's Dependencies table names iam as the source of 'User identity, permissions, organizational scope' via REST API, but no concrete endpoint is documented anywhere in the Documents source set, and no documents-sequences.md diagram shows this call actually happening." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:path> "/users/{id}/context" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:scopeSensitive> false ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:summary> "Returns a user's identity, permissions, and organizational scope." .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:iam:IamContext> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:BoundedContext> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:iam:DomainDoc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:displayName> "Identity & Access Management" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:hasAggregate> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:iam:IdentityResolutionRequestAggregate> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:hasAggregate> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:iam:InactivityPolicyAggregate> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:hasAggregate> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:iam:RoleDefinitionAggregate> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:hasAggregate> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:iam:UserAuthorizationAggregate> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:identifier> "iam" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:kind> "CoreDomain" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Explicitly does NOT own: user authentication (MiLogin SSO, external), the probabilistic matching algorithm and Unique ID master record itself (Mi-Key, external), Educational Entity Master data (external-eem), functional permission definitions for other domains (owned by those domains), or employee roster membership/employment status (staffing owns the roster; IAM owns only the identity-resolution request lifecycle that staffing triggers). Boundary rule: Mi-Key identity matching/resolution is a single external-service integration and a single business capability, modeled once in IAM regardless of which actor or domain triggers it (citizen self-service or business-user-initiated via Staffing) — other domains never maintain their own matching state machine." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:purpose> "Controls who can access MiEdWorkforce and what they can do within it. Manages the complete lifecycle of user authorizations--from initial account creation through role assignment, scope management, and eventual deactivation--ensuring that users have appropriate, auditable access to education data and system functions based on their organizational role and scope." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:status> "documented" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:subscribesTo> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:CredentialIssuedEvent> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:subscribesTo> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:CredentialRevokedEvent> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:subscribesTo> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:CredentialSuspendedEvent> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:subscribesTo> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:organizations:LeadAdministratorChangedEvent> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:subscribesTo> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:organizations:OrganizationDeactivatedEvent> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:subscribesTo> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:organizations:OrganizationSyncCompletedEvent> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:subscribesTo> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:proflearning:CoordinatorAssignedEvent> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:subscribesTo> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:profpractices:PPRClearanceAssessmentChangedEvent> .

