	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:docType> "wireframe" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Confirmed by viewing: same table in edit mode (dropdown Degree selector, blank third row for new entry) — 'LIST ALL DEGREES EARNED' heading. Corroborates staff:EducationHistory's district/citizen manual-entry path." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:section> "abox/mied-v3/fdd-review/22-employee-assignment-details/wireframes/wireframe-02-education-history-editable-legacy.png" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:staffing:Wireframe22_03> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:SourceDocument> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:staffing:Fdd22Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:docType> "wireframe" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Confirmed by viewing: legacy Evaluation Outcome update screen showing 'Note: Updates can only be made to previous 5 years of data', a per-school-year Type of Credential/Assignment Codes/Effectiveness Rating panel, and a 'Change To' dropdown (Highly Effective/Effective/Ineffective/Minimally Effective). The 5-year note corroborates staff:Rule_EvaluationOutcomeAppealWindow's district-side window; two further near-duplicate screenshots advancing through this same save flow (image4.png, image5.png in the source docx) were viewed but not individually extracted." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:section> "abox/mied-v3/fdd-review/22-employee-assignment-details/wireframes/wireframe-03-evaluation-outcome-update-legacy.png" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:staffing:Wireframe22_04> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:SourceDocument> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:staffing:Fdd22Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:docType> "wireframe" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Confirmed by viewing: modern MiEdWorkforce 'File upload' screen, File Type dropdown defaulted to 'Identity', accepting only .doc/.docx/.pdf up to 1MB via a drag-and-drop control. Not captioned or referenced anywhere in the surrounding text. Its file-type/format shape (Identity-document upload, office-doc formats) does not match the Business Specifications section's own description of BULK Employee Roster file upload (Excel/CSV/XML formats) — these read as two distinct upload surfaces (a per-record supporting-identity-document upload vs. a bulk roster-data file upload) that the FDD's placement of this image doesn't clearly disambiguate. Not raised as a standalone Annotation given low impact (neither capability is targeted by a numbered 22.x story — Feature 22.4 explicitly defers file-upload stories to FDD 21.5) but noted here for traceability." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:section> "abox/mied-v3/fdd-review/22-employee-assignment-details/wireframes/wireframe-04-file-upload-identity-doctype.png" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:staffing:Wireframe22_05> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:SourceDocument> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:staffing:Fdd22CompanionDoc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:docType> "wireframe" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Confirmed by viewing: ISD-scoped 'Audits' worklist (Kent ISD), Search box, Collection dropdown (Fall 2025), sortable/filterable School District column, paginated (1-10 of 6115 items). This is Feature 21.7's own worklist (an FDD-21 concern) — extracted here only because it sits in the same companion document as Feature 22.6, and its layout is directly structurally reused for Req_22_6_1's SOM-scoped worklist (see Wireframe22_08)." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:section> "abox/mied-v3/fdd-review/22-employee-assignment-details/wireframes/wireframe-05-isd-auditor-audits-worklist.png" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:staffing:Wireframe22_06> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:SourceDocument> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:staffing:Fdd22CompanionDoc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:docType> "wireframe" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Confirmed by viewing: 'Data Collection Report' tab for a district, with a large placeholder panel literally labeled 'Power BI Charts?' (a live open question in the design itself, not yet a firm decision) followed by FIVE named sub-panels: Employees Not Appropriately Assigned, Employees with No Assignment, Changes to Employee Roster, Changes to Positions, All Employees — plus an attestation checkbox and 'Submit to State' button. This is 5 of the 7 sections Req_22_6_2's acceptance criteria names ('Required Positions with No Assignments' and 'Buildings with No Appropriate Positions' are NOT shown in the wireframe) — see Question_DistrictReportSectionsIncomplete below." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:section> "abox/mied-v3/fdd-review/22-employee-assignment-details/wireframes/wireframe-06-district-data-collection-report.png" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:staffing:Wireframe22_07> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:SourceDocument> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:staffing:Fdd22CompanionDoc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:docType> "wireframe" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Confirmed by viewing: 'Employee Information' side-drawer (Name, Certificate #, Certificate Type, National Board Certified, Renewal Status), an Endorsements table (Subject/Grade, Institution, Nullified), a Certificate History table (App#/Iss. Date/Exp. Date/Status, two rows both Expired), an Assignments table (same App#/date/status column shape — appears to reuse the Certificate History row shape rather than showing actual staffing assignment data, possibly a mockup placeholder issue rather than intentional), a Remarks table (Comment/Created by/Date Created) with an 'Add Comment' action, and a highlighted red 'Add to Investigation' panel/button. Corroborates Req_22_6_3's acceptance criteria field list closely, but ALSO shows an 'Add to Investigation' capability with no backing narrative anywhere in either document's numbered stories or Business Specifications prose — an undocumented UI affordance, not raised as its own Annotation given it's a single unexplained button, but noted for visibility." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:section> "abox/mied-v3/fdd-review/22-employee-assignment-details/wireframes/wireframe-07-employee-details-drawer.png" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:staffing:Wireframe22_08> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:SourceDocument> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:staffing:Fdd22CompanionDoc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:docType> "wireframe" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Confirmed by viewing: SOM-scoped 'Appropriate Assignment Reports & Audits' worklist — identical layout to Wireframe22_05's ISD-scoped Audits worklist (Search, Collection dropdown, sortable/filterable columns, same 6115-item pagination placeholder data). Direct visual match for Req_22_6_1's acceptance criteria." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:section> "abox/mied-v3/fdd-review/22-employee-assignment-details/wireframes/wireframe-08-som-auditor-appropriate-assignment-worklist.png" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:staffing:Wireframe22_09> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:SourceDocument> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:staffing:Fdd22CompanionDoc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:docType> "wireframe" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Confirmed by viewing: district-side 'Fall 2025 Collection > Documents' tab showing a 'Need to Upload Documents' banner and a Documents table with exactly the two example document types staffing-domain.ttl's own staff:DocumentRequest description names verbatim ('Master Teacher Schedule', .xlsx, Uploaded; 'Attendance for Daily Substitutes', Not Uploaded) plus a Submit button. Strong direct corroboration of Req_22_6_4/22_6_5 and staff:Op_RequestAuditDocumentation." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:section> "abox/mied-v3/fdd-review/22-employee-assignment-details/wireframes/wireframe-09-audit-document-upload-request.png" .

