	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:docType> "wireframe" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Confirmed by viewing: an individual's full Demographic Information detail (name/DOB/SSN/gender/race/tribal affiliation, address, contact, 'Account Information History' table, 'Apply for Certificate' link). Broader detail view than any single Addendum story describes; general corroboration of staff:EmployeeRecord's field shape, not tied to one Requirement." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:section> "abox/mied-v3/fdd-review/24-request-for-id-collection/wireframes/wireframe-07-employee-demographic-detail.png" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:staffing:Wireframe24_8> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:SourceDocument> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:staffing:Fdd24Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:docType> "wireframe" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Confirmed by viewing: 'ID Collection Request #122456' Near Match Resolution screen — side-by-side Submitted Record vs. two Potential Matches (90%/83% match scores), differing fields highlighted, an Action dropdown defaulted to 'Create as New ID'. Directly corroborates Req_24_3_1's side-by-side/highlight/match-score acceptance criteria and Req_24_3_3's 'Request New ID' path." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:section> "abox/mied-v3/fdd-review/24-request-for-id-collection/wireframes/wireframe-08-near-match-resolution-create-new.png" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:staffing:Wireframe24_9> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:SourceDocument> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:staffing:Fdd24Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:docType> "wireframe" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Confirmed by viewing: same screen, Action set to 'Match and Link ID's' with a Primary-ID selector, a checkbox to also link the second potential match, and a required justification textarea. Directly corroborates Req_24_3_2's 'select an existing record' / 'Use this Potential' acceptance criteria — the actual control is a Match-and-Link action, closer to iam's LinkId request type than a bare single-selection, a nuance the FDD's own prose doesn't spell out (see Req_24_3_2's notes)." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:section> "abox/mied-v3/fdd-review/24-request-for-id-collection/wireframes/wireframe-09-near-match-resolution-match-link.png" .

