<urn:solutiondesign:instance:staffing:Wireframe5> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:SourceDocument> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:staffing:Fdd10Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:staffing:Fdd18Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:docType> "wireframe" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Confirmed by viewing: Step 2 of 3 (Select Employee) — search box, 'Only show appropriately certified & endorsed employees' toggle, a live PPR-flag blocking banner ('Record_Name has a PPR Flag/Disclore and cannot be assigned to this position'), and a Certificate/Endorsement Yes-indicator table. Direct match for staff:Seq_AssignEmployeeToPosition's PPR-block branch and 18.1.5's acceptance criteria." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Confirmed by viewing: same form fully populated (an already-uploaded 'Agenda for Submitting SCECHs.pdf', Display Name filled in) — the pre-existing/edit state of the same 10.2.1/10.2.2 flow. None of these three wireframes show a 'preview' affordance distinct from re-opening the uploaded file itself — see Req_10_2_1's notes on the preview-before-publish acceptance criterion." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:section> "abox/mied-v3/fdd-review/10-staffing-admin/wireframes/support-materials-add-file-details.png" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:section> "abox/mied-v3/fdd-review/18-roster-of-positions/wireframes/wireframe-05-add-filled-spot-step2.png" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:staffing:Wireframe6> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:SourceDocument> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:staffing:Fdd18Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:docType> "wireframe" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Confirmed by viewing: Step 3 of 3 (Confirm and Add to Assignment) — employee name, Certificates table (name/expiration), Endorsements table (name/grade band). Direct match for staff:Seq_AssignEmployeeToPosition's Step 3 and 18.1.5's final acceptance criterion." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:section> "abox/mied-v3/fdd-review/18-roster-of-positions/wireframes/wireframe-06-add-filled-spot-step3.png" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:staffing:Wireframe7> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:SourceDocument> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:staffing:Fdd18Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:docType> "wireframe" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Confirmed by viewing: Assignments tab with a red 'Filled and Unfilled FTE do not meet the Approved FTE amount' banner and four stat cards (Filled/Vacant/Frozen/Total & Approved FTE) with red accent bars — direct visual match for 18.1.4's FTE health indicator." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:section> "abox/mied-v3/fdd-review/18-roster-of-positions/wireframes/wireframe-07-assignments-fte-health-warning.png" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:staffing:Wireframe8> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:SourceDocument> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:staffing:Fdd18Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:docType> "wireframe" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Confirmed by viewing: Filled Spots table with two rows for the same employee (different SCED courses) — direct visual match for 18.1.6's 'if multiple filled spots exist, display them in a list format' criterion." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:section> "abox/mied-v3/fdd-review/18-roster-of-positions/wireframes/wireframe-08-filled-spots-list.png" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:staffing:Wireframe9> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:SourceDocument> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:staffing:Fdd18Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:docType> "wireframe" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Confirmed by viewing: three-row Filled Spots table with one employee's Meets Requirements column showing 'Partially' (not just Yes/No), plus a second red banner ('Assigned employees do not meet the requirements for the position') with a 'See Recommendations' link. This is the direct evidence for the 18.1.7/18.1.8 coverage gap below: staff:Op_ValidatePlacement's responseSchema is a flat boolean (meetsRequirements: true/false, missingCredential?/missingEndorsement?), with no three-state Yes/Partially/No concept and no Recommendations-modal-shaped output anywhere in staffing-domain.ttl/staffing-api.ttl." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:section> "abox/mied-v3/fdd-review/18-roster-of-positions/wireframes/wireframe-09-recommendation-banner-partially.png" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:staffing:WireframeAddendumA21> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:SourceDocument> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:staffing:Fdd21Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:docType> "wireframe" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Confirmed by viewing: higher-fidelity 'Roster of Employees' page (Current/History tabs, Search, Add Employee dropdown, filter and download icons, Unique ID/Name/Start Date/Position/Building/Credentialed/Employment Status columns, '1-10 of 6115 items' pagination) — direct visual match for 21.1.1." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:section> "abox/mied-v3/fdd-review/21-roster-of-employees/wireframes/addendum-a-roster-of-employees-list.png" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:staffing:WireframeAddendumB21> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:SourceDocument> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:staffing:Fdd21Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:docType> "wireframe" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Confirmed by viewing: 'Demographic Information' tab for an existing employee (Joe Jonas) with Personal Information (Unique ID, Legal First/Last Name, DOB, SSN+confirm, Gender, Race/Ethnicity, Tribal Affiliation), Contact Information (address, MiLogin email/phone), and an 'Account Information History' table — matches 21.1.2's field list closely. Fields shown as populated/editable form fields here, consistent with this being the post-match 'existing employee' path rather than 21.1.3's from-scratch entry." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:section> "abox/mied-v3/fdd-review/21-roster-of-employees/wireframes/addendum-b-demographic-information.png" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:staffing:WireframeAddendumC21> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:SourceDocument> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:staffing:Fdd21Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:docType> "wireframe" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Confirmed by viewing: 'New Account Created! Thank you for submitting your information. We have created a new account for you.' confirmation screen with a 'Continue to Details' button — matches 21.1.3's 'processing page' -> 'confirmation page' -> 'user profile page' flow for a from-scratch new-identity submission." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:section> "abox/mied-v3/fdd-review/21-roster-of-employees/wireframes/addendum-c-new-account-created.png" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:staffing:WireframeAddendumD21> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:SourceDocument> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:staffing:Fdd21Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:docType> "wireframe" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Confirmed by viewing: 'Employment' tab, Current Employment/Employment History sub-tabs, an entity card with 'End Employment'/'Add Assignment' actions and a per-entity assignment table (Assignment/Meets Requirements/SCED Course Title/Start Date/Allocation/Status) — direct match for 21.1.3's 'Under the employment tab..., the business user...can end the employment, or quickly add assignments' and 21.1.2's Current/History employment tabs." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:section> "abox/mied-v3/fdd-review/21-roster-of-employees/wireframes/addendum-d-employment-tab-assignments.png" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:staffing:WireframeAddendumE21> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:SourceDocument> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:staffing:Fdd21Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:docType> "wireframe" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Confirmed by viewing: 'Data Collection & Submission' page, 'Submit New Collection'/'Past Submissions' tabs, a 'Fall 2025 Data Collection' card with a 'Start Employment Data Submission' button and a 'Due in 17 Days' badge — direct match for 21.3.1's landing description, including the automatically-updated collection-period label." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:section> "abox/mied-v3/fdd-review/21-roster-of-employees/wireframes/addendum-e-data-collection-submission.png" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:staffing:WireframeAddendumF21> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:SourceDocument> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:staffing:Fdd21Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:docType> "wireframe" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Confirmed by viewing: 'Fall 2025 Collection' Step 1 of 2, a 'Data Contains Errors' banner, then SEVEN sections matching 21.4.1's acceptance criteria almost verbatim in name and order (Employees Not Appropriately Assigned / Employees with No Assignment / Changes to Employee Roster / Required Positions with No Assignments / Buildings with No Appropriate Positions / Changes to Positions / All Employees) — each rendered as a filterable/downloadable placeholder table. NOTABLE: the large content area above these sections literally renders the text 'Power BI Charts?' as a placeholder — i.e. even the wireframe itself does not commit to how this section is actually rendered (a real Power BI embed vs. these placeholder tables vs. something else), which is evidence the reporting mechanism for this feature was still an open design question at wireframe time, not just an unstated implementation detail. See Req_21_4_1's notes." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:section> "abox/mied-v3/fdd-review/21-roster-of-employees/wireframes/addendum-f-quality-review-dashboard-sections.png" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:staffing:WireframeAddendumG21> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:SourceDocument> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:definedIn> <urn:solutiondesign:instance:staffing:Fdd21Doc> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:docType> "wireframe" ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:notes> "Confirmed by viewing: an 'Employee Information' drawer (Name/Certificate #/Certificate Type/National Board Certified/Renewal Status, an Endorsements table, a Certificate History table, an Assignment table, and a Remarks/comments section with Add Comment) opened from the roster list — direct match for 21.3.1's 'click on the Employee's Name hyperlink to open the drawer' description. This drawer surfaces Credentialing-owned data (certificate #, endorsements, certificate history) inline in a Staffing screen — a cross-domain UI composition, not a missing Staffing capability; cred:Op_GetEducatorCredentials (already converted in credentialing-domain.ttl, and already staffing's own documented dependency target for placement validation) is the natural backing call, though staffing-domain.ttl does not itself model a drawer/projection node for this composed view." ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:section> "abox/mied-v3/fdd-review/21-roster-of-employees/wireframes/addendum-g-employee-details-drawer.png" .

<urn:solutiondesign:instance:starr:StarrSystem> a <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:ExternalSystem> ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:hasApi> false ;
	<urn:solutiondesign:ontology:integrationNotes> "STARR (external state college-course data system) is synced into MiEdWorkforce via an automated Synapse Pipeline, populating STARR_COURSE_RECORDS for college-course SCECH-credit eligibility. Not a live REST call or a literal human file upload; the ontology's 'file-upload' mechanism value is used as the closest fit for this batch-sync pattern." .
